window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":3901,"title":"Chapter 3901: Chapter 3900: Foundation V","paragraphs":["The hum of the Early Sacred Living Infinity Tower of Osmont never ceased. Its weavings echoed within Noah’s core of Existence, an unrelenting pulse that matched his breathing, that devoured the complexity of the sacred Eel flesh he continued to consume. With every beat, it rose higher, inscribing the Glyph of Infinity across its surface!","Prompts passed across his vision as this continued.","|The Early Sacred Living Infinity Tower of Osmont is 2% closer towards the Second Stage, The Sacred Totem.|","|The Ventryalis – The Primal Root Atrium of Echoes, the first part of the Heart of an Early Creature, is less than 1% completed.|","A part of him scoffed inwardly.","One tower. Just one, out of more than one hundred and fifty possible Towers of Osmont, stood formed at the First Stage.","And of the ancient, archaic heart his Lineage demanded, not even one part had finished taking shape!","But still, something was happening.","He could feel his Complexity and Purity erupting like roaring floods, tens of thousands of Source Units rising every second within him.","It wasn’t natural. It wasn’t normal.","Others had needed to commit atrocities to reach this stage.","He thought of Master Hannibal, who had consumed entire Fold Dwellers and gnawed on them with guiltless precision just to push his quotient forward. That was the brutal truth for most Fold Dwellers. Progress came at cost- bloody, bitter, and loud.","And then... there were the Foldless Ones.","Living Existences like Moiraine.","She stood not far from him, her golden hair shimmering with dusted light as she traced runes in the sand, her posture fluid and elegant as always.","He turned his head slightly toward her, his voice smooth but heavy with presence.","\"If you compare yourself to the most powerful Originus Venerant Fold Dweller... how would the difference feel?\"","She blinked.","Moiraine’s gaze lowered to the sand beneath her bare feet. For a moment, the air between them shimmered with restrained power.","\"Sir Osmont,\" she said softly, \"the difference would be like this sand. I could fold it or crush it between my toes without a thought.\"","Her words landed with a silence that carried weight, and yet Noah’s lips curved into a small, knowing smile.","That was what he expected.","There were tiers even among Living Existences.","Normal Living Existences, Prime Living Existences, and Honored Ones! The path stretched further still.","He gave a faint nod. \"Okay. What about other Living Existences. Are their hierarchies similar?\"","Moiraine shifted slightly, one hand brushing the air as sand at her feet rose up- nine great runes spinning in place, each one burning with faint impressions of power. Her fingers moved like a conductor commanding a symphony of Runes.","\"For the most part, yes. Living Origins, Living Laws, Living Concepts, Living Elementals- they follow a structure similar to ours. Each has 81 Dukes that sit atop their governance councils- what we call the Kleos Living Council.\"","Her eyes narrowed slightly as one of the sand runes sparked crimson and splintered into jagged branches.","\"Though... the Living Spirits and the Living Temporals insist on their own structure. They always had to be different. Difficult. Over the eons, they abandoned the Kleos Hierarchy.\"","She paused before speaking again, her voice clipped with distaste, yet controlled.","\"The Living Spirits follow the Trine Accord. Three Supreme Spirits control their entire dominions. Below them, 64 Kleos Spirits act as emissaries across the other Living Councils.\"","She shifted, another rune forming like a wheel spinning backwards through time.","\"The Living Temporals are more erratic. They follow a Living Continuum Spiral- one Supreme Sentinel governs for a single Epoch, which they define how long it is themselves, before stepping down or... disappearing. Beneath them are nine Living Temporal Pillars who hold up a supposed Living Temporal Weave of Existence that holds the fabric of all Transcendent Folds together. Its utter bullshit as far as I know. They’re powerful, but more fragmented. Petty. Always caught in loops of their own making.\"","Noah listened, arms crossed, chest still bare as the breeze combed through his vibrant hair.","His shadow stretched long and clear beside Moiraine’s, the weight of his presence forcing the sand beneath his feet into faint depressions.","\"Tell me more,\" he said.","Moiraine turned, raising both hands now as more sand danced to her command.","\"The Nine Living Existences,\" she said, her voice smooth as honey, \"are allied. Mostly. Their forces cross into each other’s Transcendent Battlefront Folds. You’ll find Living Laws inside the Origin Folds. You’ll find Living Concepts working alongside Living Spirits.\"","Her tone didn’t change. She was delivering information. Calm. Precise.","\"In the Battlefront Folds near the Loom,\" she continued, \"Living Existences rarely step in first. Too much risk. The Loom is cloaked by swirling Paradox. That Paradox distorts everything, and there are many Inevitabilities that cannot be discovered even by the senses of Living Existences. So... they use Fold Dwellers to trigger response.\"","The sand she was using rose higher, forming the figures of Fold Dwellers- small, detailed likenesses of men, women, titans, fairies, dragons, slimes.","Around them, titanic forms shimmered into existence- Living Existences!","Moiraine’s fingers twitched, and suddenly, black spirals of sand exploded around the Fold Dwellers...they were silhouettes of Inevitabilities!","\"When an Inevitability senses a Fold Dweller moving across a doorway to the Loom... it strikes. And when it does, the Living Existences sense the disturbance in that period of time. Then they arrive. Then they fight. Because Inevitabilities are hard to be sensed even by Living Existences, this manner reduces casualties while still making progress.\"","Noah’s eyes didn’t blink. \"So Fold Dwellers are bait.\"","Moiraine didn’t flinch. \"Yes, Sir Osmont. They are.\"","She paused again, gaze steady. \"In return, Sponsors offer them treasures, titles, or elevation to the ranks of Living Existences if they accrue enough merit. Some survive. Most don’t.\"","The sand changed. The little Fold Dwellers fought, some overwhelmed by the black tide of Inevitabilities, others holding on until towering reinforcements arrived.","\"But if the sponsor isn’t watching,\" she said softly, \"if they’re too far, too late... the Fold Dwellers die. Quickly. Sometimes even slowly. Those who are weak are erased before help comes.\"","Noah exhaled slowly in understanding.","This was the cost of their path.","The price to be paid for complexity!","If he were normal like everyone else...he would have had to do something similar!","Moiraine looked toward him again, her tone darker now.","\"When a Living Paradox nears the Loom... Inevitabilities form on their own.\"","Her hands dropped to her sides.","\"The Paradox surrounding the Loom is dense. Our very presence provokes its weavings. That is why the other Existences despise us. Because of us, Inevitabilities multiply each day and only continue to increase as over time, it has gotten harder and harder to make any progress towards the Loom.\"","Her voice didn’t rise, but the emotion was buried there. Just beneath the polish. She looked utterly magnetic as she spoke about this, her golden white hair flickering in the wind.","\"And so we are blamed. Every death, every Fold Dweller and Living Existence consumed, every door left burning, is another weight and blame we carry!\"","HUUM!","The sea wind blew gently, golden grains falling slowly around her feet."]},{"number":3902,"title":"Chapter 3902: Chapter 3901: Foundation VI","paragraphs":["\"The tragedy is,\" Moiraine said slowly, her voice cool and bitter as sea mist drifting over jagged stone, \"if we, the Living Paradoxes, didn’t summon the very Inevitabilities the deeper we dwell in the Doorways to the Loom... we would have already carved entire dominions into it.\"","She stood with her back straight, her hands folded at her waist as if delivering a war strategy before a council of kings. The light above the Early Veiled Shore cast long gold shadows behind her, but she remained radiant, as if the light came from her and not the sky.","\"We are in harmony with Paradox, Sir Osmont,\" she said with care, \"Our nature aligns with it. We could wield it, shape it, bend all of existence around its contradictions. We should have flourished.\"","She turned her eyes toward him now- measured, burning behind the civility.","\"But every step we take draws out more Inevitabilities instead. They rise from the Loom like antibodies to purge us. And so...\"","Moiraine’s voice tightened with restraint.","\"That is why you mattered. A Paradox... but without the taint. You would have been an impossible sword that could plunge through the Loom’s folds without drawing out Inevitabilities. You were meant to cut through the unknown and open paths that none of us could!\"","Her chin dipped ever so slightly, her jaw tightening.","\"Now Diviticus will take that role.\"","Noah looked back at her, silent.","The corners of his lips curled just slightly.","\"Let her try.\"","...!","The words weren’t spoken too loud. They didn’t need to be. They boomed from his expression, from the stillness in his existence, from the command of his presence as he bit into another sliver of sacred Eel!","She had half of his drop of Blood. Half! But...would she always be able to control it...when his complexity rose to unfathomable levels?!","\"...\" He stayed quiet and kept this thought to himself.","Moiraine pressed on, recovering her poise like silk smoothing back into place.","\"We use more Fold Dwellers than anyone. Because of the Inevitabilities. Because we need to.\"","Her tone was calm and practiced.","\"Even the Nullvein Gravewake Folds... they’re monitored. Oryzarakh, Kelezar, and many others rotating. Always watching. The most powerful Fold Dwellers in those regions were given commands.\"","Her eyes narrowed.","\"Find the Keys.\"","She stepped forward and circled her fingers in the air. Sand lifted in spirals, forming delicate representations of different shaped objects.","\"Wonders are born from the folds, and some become Keys. Keys to Doorways leading to thr Loom that haven’t been touched. Which means no Inevitabilities. Yet.\"","Her voice dropped.","\"We crave such Doorways. We instruct leaders of Fold Dwellers to hunt them, guard them... die for them.\"","A slow exhale escaped Noah’s lips, his eyes growing distant as memories flickered across his vision. The Chronosect. The Time Sentinels. Their desperation as they looked for Keys.","A Key.","He raised his right hand and opened his palm.","A gray rectangular object lay there, dull and silent.","Moiraine’s eyes widened.","\"A key like this?\" Noah asked, his voice deep, deliberate.","She moved forward, her aura pulsing with golden arcs of Authority as she reached out and examined the object with surprise. \"Yes... this is...\"","HUUM.","Before she could finish, the very air around the key began to twist.","Living Paradoxical Authority streamed from the atmosphere of the Early Veiled Shore, as if summoned by instinct alone. It wove itself into the dull gray metal, igniting lines across its surface one by one.","Moiraine’s eyes pulsed. \"This...\"","Noah took another bite of the eel as if nothing unusual was occurring. His gaze didn’t leave the glowing Key.","\"It’ll be active soon. We will plan for something then.\"","...!","He swallowed, wiping his fingers slowly as he turned his attention inward.","There was now...","5% progress on the Infinity Tower of Osmont.","Still far from the Sacred Totem stage. But momentum was building.","He turned toward the glass woks scattered across the sands, and already- his mother stood across the way, her eyes waiting, her finger pointing.","\"These five,\" Amelia Osmont called out, her tone light with the satisfaction of a master chef. \"They’re ready.\"","Before Noah could move, Moiraine lifted her arms with a grace that belonged to queens. Golden light flowed from her palms like rivers of sunlight, shooting out to the five woks and carrying them effortlessly through the air toward them.","Noah offered a nod of approval, already preparing to continue devouring thr Early Living Marine Lifeforms.","Then, he froze.","Because...","HUUM!","A low, vibrating tremor pulsed across the Early Veiled Shore.","It wasn’t booming, so much as it was felt and sensed by them!","Waves of Authority- auras, terrifying and ancient, swept across the fabric of the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence. The auras did not hide. They did not attempt stealth. They mads themselves clear across the Nullvein Gravewake Folds!","The Early Veiled Shore was at the center of the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence...which was located in the collapsed folds of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds!","Any daring Living Existences that spread their auras out across the Nullvein Gravewake Folds...would be felt by Living Existences within the Infiniverse!","And this was exactly what happened now.","The blatant auras of Living Paradoxes- Dozens of them, flashed wildly!","Moiraine’s body straightened as her eyes pulsed with solemnity. Her head snapped to the horizon. \"Sir Osmont...\"","Noah did not flinch. He began devouring again.","\"They won’t find the land of an Early Creature,\" he said simply. \"Not unless I want them to.\"","His voice cut through the still air, calm and authoritative. Not merely reassurance, but fact. As if the reality of his words bent existence into alignment!","He didn’t turn to face her. He didn’t need to.","This was his shore.","His domain.","The privileges of an Early Creature ran deep.","Even the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence, massive and folded inward, veiled the Early Veiled Shore at its center. Unless he wished it... none could find it.","But still, their message rang out.","They had come.","Living Paradoxes. Dozens of them. Their auras blared unashamedly across the Nullvein Gravewake Folds!"]},{"number":3903,"title":"Chapter 3903: Chapter 3902: Fishing in Troubled Waters! I","paragraphs":["Moiraine’s hands curled into fists. Her golden eyes shimmered with frustration and anger.","\"For them to bring this many,\" she said, her tone sharpening with fury, \"for them to parade their forces across the Folds searching for you... they truly don’t understand!\"","Her voice dropped to a whisper that carried the weight of paradox!","\"They don’t understand that they offend an Early Creature!\"","She turned to him, and for a moment, her poised visage gave way to something fierce and righteous. Like someone that wanted to kill!","\"These fools...\"","\"...\"","Noah remained still, letting the moment stretch as the fires of Paradox burned brighter across the gray key in his hand.","He said nothing.","But within him, the Infinity Tower of Osmont pulsed once again.","And in the stillness of the Veiled Shore, his heart beat louder than the war drums of Existence even as Living Paradoxes arrived to search for him.","But they would find nothing.","He would observe their fruitless efforts, and he would continue elavating in power at the same time as he looked for opportunities!","The auras of Paradoxes still pressed on the edges of the Early Veiled Shore like trembling tides at the edge of a sacred island.","Noah stood steady as the waters near his feet stilled despite the noise beyond, as if the very reality surrounding the Veiled Shore deferred to his presence.","Then, at this critical moment, Liora came.","Her steps were heavy and urgent, the kind of urgency that could bend existence to her will. Her usually composed features were tight, lips pale, eyes sharp with a frantic dread as she felt the auras of Paradoxes.","This dread...was not for her.","\"Sir Osmont,\" she said quietly, too quietly, like something inside her might shatter if she raised her voice. \"My father... Bob...\"","Noah’s gaze turned down to meet hers.","The moment froze. Her face, drawn in worry. Her hands clenched tightly together.","He studied her for a breath.","Then, without a word, he turned away and looked toward the waters of the Early Veiled Shore.","\"I will perceive what he is doing.\"","His voice was calm as if he wanted to reassure.","Liora nodded quickly, her eyes glassy.","Noah didn’t speak again.","He closed his eyes.","And sank.","Absolute Fictional Transcendence bloomed!","—","The Paradoxical Prison was not a place that should still exist.","Yet here it was, suspended in an impossible corner of fractured Existence. Obsidian skies yawned endlessly above, the air cracked like cooling stone. Black seas groaned below, rolling with dark chains and floating fragments of shattered coffins- each one a remnant of containment, punishment, or loss.","In this place, silence ruled.","Except for one.","In the crumpled remains of a coffin wedged beneath two rusted spires, the figure of Bob hunched forward in humanoid form. His body shook from the internal pressure of something unspeakable. Around him, the chains were his own as they did not bind. They pulsed!","A resonance formed between him and it.","The Inevitability!","It had no true shape. Only a pressing weight and intention that pulsed like an alien heart. It was hunger and simplicity. It wanted. It would have...endlessly","Bob had bound himself to it entirely by choice.","He used every scrap of treasure- every glimmer of possibility from the treasures and Imitated Everythings that Altheon had passed down through Thauron. He had taken what was never meant to be taken- what was not his!","And it had worked.","Almost.","He could feel it. The edge of control. The Inevitability was listening. It didn’t understand, but it obeyed, because Bob had given it a language as it fed actively on Thauron and his Origin!","If he gained that control...","He could have reached out to his daughter.","To Liora.","To hold her. To whisper that he was sorry. That he had never truly left her, not even once.","But that chance, that slim breath of mercy- was severed.","BOOM!","A pulse of golden-red light tore through the black skies.","And the Living Existence that was none other than Oryzarakh stepped into the prison!","When he saw the Prison he used to oversee every now and then...he was shocked and then enraged!","His form burned like a wrathful sun, his eyes molten jewels, his steps shaking the very shackles of this place. His presence screamed Authority- coiled, ancient, and unforgiving!","HUUM!","The moment his aura unfurled, it sought dominion.","It sought answers.","But even as it waved its aura out, it did not sense anything!","After all, Inevitabilities were hard to find by even the most powerful Prime Living Existences!","But the Inevitability itself was a hungry creature.","Its focus snapped like a beast sighting prey.","Bob felt the instant change in the prison.","The Inevitability pulsed. Twitched. Hungered.","It wanted to lash out. It wanted to taste the blaring light of a Living Existence. To devour it. To grow.","\"No...\" Bob whispered. His voice reached into the soul of the thing.","\"You will stay calm. I will give you what you want. But not now. Not yet!\"","He wasn’t pleading.","He was bartering.","The Inevitability paused.","Its hunger dimmed.","Not erased, but banked.","Bob exhaled harshly as his eyes shone with decisiveness. Then, he flared his aura.","A flicker of white-gold light burst from his form. Not grand. Not defiant. Just enough.","He had become a Living Origin. And now he was calling out to the other Living Origins it felt in thr Nullvein Gravewake Folds!","It was reckless.","He knew that.","But the risk was better than Oryzarakh’s wrath unraveling everything when he Inevitability found him in this prison.","\"WHO?!\"","The bellow came like a hammer shattering silence as his flaring aura did not go unnoticed.","Oryzarakh’s eyes turned.","And locked onto the coffin.","Onto him.","The Living Paradox surged forward.","But...","HUUUUM!","The very sea of the Paradoxical Prison split open.","From the sundered waves rose blinding light, white and gold crashing like judgment. A blade of brilliance pierced the veil of this prison.","BOOM!","And from it... wings.","Radiant wings expanded across the shattered sky, trailing halos of interwoven reality and memory.","They shimmered with Living Origin Authority!","It was...","Altheon who had descended!","His form was blinding. His halo was forged from glory. His gaze was sharp!","He saw Oryzarakh.","He saw the torn coffin.","He saw Bob.","And something ancient in him raged.","\"You dare imprison a Living Origin?!\"","...!","A Tower of Authority exploded behind him, tall and brutal, glowing with marks of verdict.","Oryzarakh shifted, black light sharpening around him.","The two stood across from each other- power meeting power.","And below them, broken, bloodied, but alive- Bob smiled bitterly as like a cockroach, he looked for any avenue to survive!"]},{"number":3904,"title":"Chapter 3904: Chapter 3903: Fishing in Troubled Waters! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes flickered open slowly, a serene stillnes blanketing his expression as the threads of countless events coiled and settled behind his gaze.","He had watched Bob.","He had seen the desperate threading of his path, the weaving of a fate too fragile to name!","The paradoxical prison, the inevitability tethered to him like a beast of hunger, the rising flames of Living Origins now converging. A thousand threads of consequence, trembling under a single breath!","He inhaled.","Around him, the warm, dense scent of cooked Early Living Marine Lifeforms swirled in the air- a fragrance laced with purity and incomprehensible complexity. Another piece of seared flesh from the sacred wok rose into his hand as his gaze shifted calmly.","Moiraine stood like obsidian-gilded marble, composed and glorious. The golden waves of paradox etched into her form gleamed faintly in the glowing atmosphere of the Shore, her body still as if awaiting nothing but his will.","Beside her, Liora’s expression was pinched in worry, her fingers wringing at the hem of her robe. Her eyes searched his face, desperate for anything to hold onto.","\"He’s hiding his inevitability well,\" Noah said quietly, the weight in his voice like the turn of existence itself. \"There are Living Origins near him as he’s seeking their protection. If they take him in, he might survive.\"","Might!","His words didn’t offer comfort, not entirely. There was no certainty in the word might.","The waters of the budding shore reflected golden horizons. And beneath those ripples, Noah sensed the shocks of the battle.","All Fold Dwellers would feel them today!","Tremors.","The paradoxical prison, once sealed in iron black stillness, had erupted. Two colossal powers had come to blows. Living Origin and Living Paradox! The battle cracked the veil of silence that had shrouded that space for an unknown number of years!","He felt it.","So did Moiraine.","Her voice was low, lethal. \"The Honored Living Golden Paradox is here. I can feel him. Even now, I would maybe last some time against him. His might is... suffocating.\"","...!","Noah nodded.","Above the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, the golden lights turned. The suns of the Foldless Ones focused upon the rippling epicenter of chaos. And from beyond, more Living Origins stirred- drawn by Altheon, converging like blades to a throat.","Noah exhaled slowly.","A war was about to bloom in the folds. Not a war he could fight in. Not with strength.","But he was not bound by strength.","He was an Early Creature.","And Early Creatures did not fight wars in the same way others did.","He turned his gaze to Moiraine.","\"How long would it take you to bring down a standard Living Origin, if they were alone?\"","She tilted her head slightly. The light haloed her cheekbones, and her voice slipped out smooth and precise. \"One breath.\"","\"Prime Living Paradox?\"","\"One second.\"","\"Honored?\"","She hesitated. Then, firmly: \"I can survive. I cannot win.\"","Noah’s lips curved into something that could almost be a smile.","\"Good,\" he murmured. \"A chance may come. If it does, and only if you are confident it can be done unseen, in an instant, without risking being found out, you may strike.\"","...!","She nodded once, her expression solemn. \"Understood, Sir Osmont.\"","---","In the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, the air pulsed with paradox.","Wings unfurled.","Nine of them, layered in spirals of golden origination and irreversible contradiction, each feather etched in Living Authority. And above them, nine halos blazed like suns trying to burn through the very fabric of the Fold.","The Honored Living Golden Paradox hovered in place, a sovereign born from a concept beyond time. His eyes were black voids outlined in radiant luminance, his voice quiet, yet thundering.","\"They seek it too,\" he said.","His words sent ripples across the reality of the Folds, dozens of Living Paradoxes bowing their heads before him.","\"This Existential Anomaly...the Living Origins know he survived their first attack. But the Living Origins would not step foot into these folds unless they were sure and confident it was here too. Scour every Fold. Tear apart every Wheel. Search the memories of every Fold Dweller if you must.\"","He turned.","His gaze bled golden.","\"The rest of you, come. We will deal with these arrogant interlopers ourselves.\"","And they moved.","The Foldless Ones shot out like unraveling spears, chasing echoes of Origin across the Nullvein Gravewake Folds!","Out of those sent to search out.","A Living Paradox of black-gold radiance, six half-formed wings stretching behind him in silent motion. His body shimmered like molten obsidian wrapped in paradoxes that had never come to pass.","His destination? The nearby locus of time where he sensed many Wheels swirling.","It turned out to be...","The Chronosect of Threadbound Folds.","A vast geometry unfolded beneath him. Clockwork architecture formed from interwoven Wheels of Existence, surrounding a heart where statues of Sentinels of glorious musings of time moved like glyphs in perpetual dance. It was silent here, but for the ticking of an existential metronome.","He floated towards these complex meshwork of Wheels and the counltess lives they held.","But as he did so...","...!","He felt it.","The pulse of something ancient.","Something final.","His paradoxical weavings, always in a state of being and unbeing, froze.","Froze!","They trembled.","He had never felt such a thing as he could not identify it until it was too late!","True death.","He turned his head.","The air had gone still.","Then..","A whisper of white-gold light bloomed.","A paradox collapsed in on itself!","Above him, she appeared.","Moiraine.","Her robes unfurled like banners of living paradox, her presence calm, her eyes set with that surgical certainty that knew precisely where to cut.","Her voice barely moved the air. \"Embrace your contradiction.\"","Her hands drew out vast seas of impossible elegance.","She did not call out an ability or anything- simply pure paradox as she forced someone lesser...to collapse.","A line appeared across his neck. Clean. Silent. Terrifying.","His existence twisted. Not in resistance, but in acceptance. His paradoxical essence began to fold in on itself, no longer able to sustain what he was.","A single blink later, he was beheaded.","He was always beheaded, he had been beheaded, and he would have been beheaded...hundreds of times.","All his anchors and lives, lost in an instant!","No echo followed. No sound. Only the shuddering sigh of reality correcting itself!","Moiraine reached out.","The remnants of the Paradox, the weavings, the fading light- all gathered in her palm.","And in another blink, she was gone!"]},{"number":3905,"title":"Chapter 3905: Chapter 3904: Fishing in Troubled Waters! III","paragraphs":["An instant.","That was all she needed.","Moiraine vanished like a breath stolen by Existence itself!","In the space where she had stood, a Glyph of the Protagonist shimmered into existence, its intricate lines gleaming with radiant white-gold brilliance.","It pulsed with the authority of a Living Origin and scattered waves of white gold authority in this region as if to say- a Living Origin was here and responsible for this!","Existence groaned right after.","A low, grating sound like reality being bent backward screamed out into the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","And where the Living Paradox had been only moments ago, there was now only ruin. From its fractured death, horror emerged.","It was...","An Inevitability, malformed and twisted, began to bloom from the frayed threads of its paradoxical existence. It stood tall and eerie, flanked by multiple rising disfigured humanoid things- Living Collapses!","Their skin was a stretched, bleeding white, their movements jerking as if their bodies were unsure if they were meant to stand or slither. Bone cracked outward in grotesque angles.","\"Sin!\"","\"SIN!\"","They chanted with horror and victory.","One Living Collapse turned its head, and its face tore in half as if trying to form expression, only to fail. The air warped around them, screams blooming and dying in the same breath.","Then came the boom.","A thunderous golden light shattered across the Folds as the Honored Living Golden Paradox descended, his nine wings flaring out behind him in a blaze of majesty and fire. Nine halos floated behind his head in perfect geometric balance, each one carved with paradoxical truths, each one humming with a song of order and collapse.","He landed with fury in his eyes as he looked around!","\"In an instant!\" he growled.","He looked down upon the site where one of his own had been felled. He saw the budding Inevitability. He saw the Living Collapses, their bodies crawling out of the unraveling paradox. He saw the death of one of his flock!","And his eyes went still.","\"Liar’s Paradox,\" he spoke with booming coldness.","The authority in his voice reshaped the weavings of existence.","The Inevitability, barely born, shrieked without sound. The Living Collapses spasmed, their grotesque limbs clawing at an unseen force. And then, they vanished in the pure severance of presence. They were never there. Not anymore.","Only the golden blood on the ground bore witness.","Liar’s Paradox. A philosophical construct weaponized into an existential truth. It meant that if something existed that should not, its very assertion of existence became false. And if wielded by one with enough Paradoxical authority, enough power to enforce that contradiction, the contradiction won.","To lie about reality... was to change it.","The Honored Living Golden Paradox looked upon the crystalline remnants left behind- glimmering shreds of Living Origin Authority now laid bare. His voice fell coldly as he turned to the Living Paradoxes surrounding him.","\"A coward strikes among us. An Honored Living Origin, skulking in shadows, targeting our weakest. From now on, you will move in groups of ten. No one walks alone. Should a Living Origin show themselves, do not engage- signal and await reinforcements.\"","His words struck like commands of reality. The others nodded, their eyes grim.","And then...","Purple light shimmered.","From the massive concentric wheels of the Chronosect of Threadbound Folds, figures began to descend. Time Sentinels, draped in violet robes and trailing threads of stilled seconds, emerged with hesitant reverence.","Behind them, the Tower Master, a stooped figure of Originus Venerant realm bowed so deeply it seemed he might fracture.","\"To what honor do we owe the presence of Foldless Ones this day?\" he asked, voice thin and filled with reverence.","The Honored Living Golden Paradox descended slowly, his feet never touching the specks of Origin as he hovered before the Tower Master. His gaze was pure disdain.","\"Did you see anything?\"","The Tower Master trembled.","\"We felt the presence of an honored Foldless One, nothing more.\"","His words were pitiful. Empty.","With one motion, the Honored Living Golden Paradox flicked his fingers.","Time halted.","The Time Sentinels collapsed. One by one, their forms disintegrated into long, thin threads of unraveling time. The Tower Master gasped, his hands reaching upward as if in prayer- and then his body collapsed, his eyes still open in silent terror as he fell into dust.","\"Useless!\" said the Honored Living Golden Paradox.","His aura roared outward in gold and black flame, seeping into every Wheel of Existence nearby, unraveling the protections the Chronosect had painstakingly built as he searched.","If he was annoyed, he would simply kill.","For why would one bother or worry when looking at those that were akin to mere ants?!","---","In the Early Veiled Shore, the waters hummed.","Noah watched them, serene.","A single ripple moved across the sands as the air twisted.","Then, she appeared!","Moiraine!","Elegant. Burning. Breathless.","Her black and gold robes billowed softly as she descended in spirals of paradoxical light. In her arms, wrapped in the firm embrace of golden Authority, was the beheaded corpse of a Living Paradox. It left her and struck the ground with a muted boom, the sands darkening to a glimmering gold as blood spilled.","Noah’s gaze did not move immediately. He stood still, a piece of a Marine Lifeform caught in the breeze dangling from his hand. His other hand raised, shading his brow as he watched her approach.","Moiraine stood tall, though her breath was just barely uneven.","\"I kept it under an instant, Sir Osmont.\"","He smiled.","\"Yes,\" Noah said, his voice smooth and rich, like smoke curling through velvet. \"You did.\"","He stepped forward. The corpse was enormous, even in death. Its wings were crumpled, its face still twisted in confused disbelief. The clean line of beheading gleamed with the finality of paradox undone.","Noah crouched before it, his fingers grazing the golden blood.","He spoke softly, more to the body than to anyone else as he sighed.","\"Perhaps you believed yourself to be a function of purpose. That your authority made you vital. That your life held meaning in how you served.\" He tilted his head, voice low. \"But that was illusion.\"","He stood again, slow and measured, looking down with the weight of understanding pressing behind his eyes.","\"Your death, however,\" he continued, \"has value. In that stillness, in that severance- you finally matter. You, a Living Paradox, finally matter.\"","And the air pulsed.","A prompt shimmered into view!","|The Early Veiled Shore has discovered the corpse of a lifeform that can be designated as an Early Living Land Lifeform.|","|Its corpse is equivalent to 75 Sacred Bodies of Early Living Marine Lifeforms. Would you like to devour it?|","Noah smiled. A warm, chilling smile!","He didn’t answer. Not yet.","Instead, he looked to Moiraine. She stood with her back straight, her golden eyes reflecting nothing but loyalty and shadowed brilliance. Her presence alone made the winds of the Early Veiled Shore swirl tighter.","A Foldless One.","And now, a terrifying weapon that he could direct and swing!","He then looked back at the body.","And nodded!","...!"]},{"number":3906,"title":"Chapter 3906: Chapter 3905: Glorious! I","paragraphs":["The sands of the Early Veiled Shore pulsed, golden blood sinking like ink into memory.","The decapitated body of the Living Paradox, a monument to what once reigned with unchallenged terror, was slowly, almost reverently, being pulled beneath the surface.","The dunes beneath Noah’s feet shifted with intent, as if the very shore were breathing him in, syncing to his tempo. Lines of gold veined out like living roots, pulsing with light as they commected to him.","And then came the surge.","HUUM!","A wave of complexity, immeasurable and ancient, poured into him like floodwaters breaching a crumbling dam. It roared, crashing through every line of his existence!","|Your body is taking the converted nutrients of something equivalent to 75 Sacred Bodies of Early Living Marine Lifeform.|","A second prompt shimmered into place right after the first, etched in pure blue light.","|The Early Sacred Living Infinity Tower of Osmont is accepting all complex nutrients. Advancement towards the Second Stage, The Sacred Totem, is accelerating...|","Within him, in the deep, unfathomable layers of his existence, the Infinity Tower of Osmont shone. A luminous spire of stellar blue etched with glyphs that moved like rivers, its structure larger, more defined than ever before. Along its side, the Glyph of Infinity seared itself into the foundation, spinning with terrifying glory!","And more than this...","|Due to accelerated nutrient absorption, the forging of the Ventryalis, The Primal Root Atrium of Echoes, is proceeding at 300% normal rate.|","...!","Noah’s chest rose slowly, the weight of what surged into him elevating everything!","A single death of a Living Paradox. One decisive moment- and the ripples it birthed changed everything.","From beside him, Liora stepped closer, her voice trembling with hope after she saw the decimated Living Paradox be absorbed into the sand.","\"Sir Osmont... I know not the power Sister Moiraine wields, and I don’t wish to overstep, but... could she not overcome the Inevitability my father is bound to? If you send her-\"","Noah turned.","She didn’t finish her sentence.","She didn’t need to. The moment she met his eyes, her voice quieted.","He studied her- young, determined, naive. A daughter with a thread of desperation woven into every breath. And yet, the sentiment... was noble.","\"Your father,\" Noah said, voice even, sharp enough to slice reality, \"made his choices. Intervention now would only muddy the current he’s trying to ride. Could kill him. Might ruin everything he’s built. Trust him. He’s obsessed as he won’t die easily. Do not ask about this again.\"","His tone softened, just slightly.","\"Do you understand?\"","Liora looked down, nodding. Then she raised her eyes again, firmer this time. \"Yes.\"","Noah gave her a single nod in return. \"If you want to help him... tend to the affairs here. Rise. Surpass him even. I’ll keep you updated if anything drastic happens with him.\"","The girl stepped back, bowing her head before she turned and walked toward the others working the Glass Woks- those simple stations now sacred in their utility.","Noah turned back to the sands of complexity still flowing into him, his thoughts measured. The Infinity Tower was stabilizing rapidly.","\"Moiraine,\" he said as he sensed his continued and heavy elevation, \"how does it feel to kill one of your own?\"","Moiraine stood tall beside the blood-stained sand, her presence pristine, her posture immaculate.","She smiled faintly.","\"Like butchering a chicken,\" she said smoothly. \"A chicken that forgot its place. That forgot what it means to breathe the same air as an Early Creature.\"","Noah’s eyes pulsed in amusement.","She took a step closer. \"You might not grasp the gravity of your existence yet, but to those of us who’ve lived and ruled for eons, you’re akin to... an Ancestor. A sacred memory made manifest. Anyone raising their hand against you... they’ve forgotten what it means to exist. And I’ll remind them, one corpse at a time. Their Paradoxical Lineage means less than dust beside your distinction.\"","WAA!","Noah let the silence settle before replying.","\"Is that so?\"","Moiraine nodded.","\"And you take my orders as an Early Creature seriously?\"","\"To the utmost.\" Her voice was reverent.","\"Good,\" Noah said. \"Here’s an order. Never again call me Sir Osmont.\"","Her face tightened, a flicker of surprise flashing before she nodded. \"Understood, Sir Noah.\"","Noah stared at her.","\"Don’t call me Sir Noah either.\"","Another beat. \"Understood, Sir.\"","He blinked. A sigh left his lips like a long, patient exhale from an exhausted existence. \"You’re doing this on purpose.\"","\"No, Sir,\" she replied with polished composure.","He shook his head and turned away as another prompt appeared, interrupting their exchange.","|The Early Sacred Living Infinity Tower of Osmont has attained its Second Stage: The Sacred Totem.|","|A Basic Achievement of an Early Creature has been unlocked. Expanded functionality within the Early Veiled Shore is gradually becoming available.|","A Tower resounded!","HUUM!","A radiant cerulean light burst forth from Noah’s body as it was measured. Controlled. Regal!","It cascaded across the Early Veiled Shore, soaking into the glassy waters and golden sands, washing over every lifeform cooking, eating, building. The world beneath his feet, the reality tethered to his name, bent to his growth.","In that moment, the Early Veiled Shore breathed him in deeper as his blue light covered everything!","And it was just starting!","|Your Complexity Quotient and Purity Quotient have both been increased by +2,000,000.|","It was not a whisper of growth, not some subtle shift in inner potential. It was a real!","A thunderous, unseen boom that echoed through every layer of his form as if his very Existence had been waiting for this moment to ignite! The golden sands beneath his bare feet thrummed. They recognized him finally and truly as the Tower blazed.","A searing pulse raced along the left side of his chest, the heat exalting. Then came the light. Cerulean, soft and impossibly sharp at once, it traced itself upon his skin with methodical reverence. The shape of the Glyph coalesced- a looped twist of geometric elegance, infinite yet contained.","His chest, apart from from forehead, held another Glyph!","|You have gained the Basic Early Living Existential Glyph of Infinity.|","...!"]},{"number":3907,"title":"Chapter 3907: Chapter 3906: Glorious! II","paragraphs":["The blooming Glyph burned on his chest like a searing brand!","But it came with unfathomable potential!","|Glyph of Infinity- The infinite does not mean without end. It is the truth of boundaryless purpose, of uncounted beginnings. Through this glyph, you now hold the mark of what cannot be measured. Without energy, without authority, you may impose the concept of limitlessness. A command need not be uttered. Thought alone now bends what should not bend. With this glyph, one can silence collapse, reverse inevitability, and loop an enemy’s death infinitely. This is your inheritance.|","The words etched themselves not into his very will. He exhaled, and even the air trembled!","And then the change deepened.","|The remaining nutrient of the absorbed Early Living Land Lifeform is permeating across your existence. Multiple Early Sacred Living Towers of Osmont are experiencing accelerated growth and nearing completion.|","The light around him flared again.","|The First Stage of the Early Sacred Living Quintessence Tower of Osmont, the Foundation Vein, has been completed.|","|Your Complexity Quotient and Purity Quotient have both been increased by +500,000.|","From within the radiant haze, a new Tower shimmered into being behind the blue glory of Infinity. It was colorless- yet within that absence of hue was the very presence of all things. The Tower of Quintessence shimmered with an ancient clarity, not seeking attention, but demanding reverence. Like something primordial had stirred.","Moiraine, standing near the edge of the shallow tides, did not speak. Her eyes held something Noah rarely saw from her- wonder.","He’s beginning to feel old...this was the thought she had!","He was not more complex, but the air from him felt old. Early!","But he wasn’t done. Not yet.","|The First Stage of the Early Sacred Living Paradox Tower of Osmont, the Foundation Vein, has been completed.|","|Your Complexity Quotient and Purity Quotient have both been increased by +500,000.|","A third tower flared, flickering with conflicting colors that bled into and out of each other. Its form was never constant, like a Tower constructed from half-remembrances and forgotten certainties. The Tower of Paradox.","Then came the final surge.","|The First Stage of the Early Sacred Living Origin Tower of Osmont, the Foundation Vein, has been completed.|","|Your Complexity Quotient and Purity Quotient have both been increased by +500,000.|","The Tower of Origin stood behind the others like a primordial elder, as if it had been present long before his birth, merely waiting for his body to remember its existence.","The momentum of his growth should have staggered him. But Noah stood tall, arms slightly parted, letting the waves of complexity and purity crash into him. Around his ankles, the gold-drenched sand pulsed, then stilled.","Another prompt bloomed right after!","|The remaining nutrients of the Sacred Body of the Early Living Land Lifeform have been utilized by the Early Veiled Shore. When attempting the requirements for advancement, the battle against the Record of an Early Creature will now be slightly lowered in difficulty, and may not result in instant death and failure.|","Noah’s eyes narrowed as he read. The corner of his mouth lifted in that familiar curve of a smile.","\"Ho?\" he murmured, glancing down at the sands. \"You’re learning how to keep me even more intrigued.\"","The land was responding to him more like a willful entity more than a passive realm, and he couldn’t help but feel charmed by it.","But advancement... no. That step was still too great. A Record of an Early Creature wasn’t some illusion to test oneself against. It was a testament of power so absolute that it had scarred Existence itself!","He was not ready. Not yet. He knew this very well! And knowing that wasn’t fear. It was strategy!","His eyes turned toward the cerulean titan that was now the Second Stage of the Tower of Infinity. The Sacred Totem. Within it, power moved like weavings of glory.","He could feel the possibilities coiling beneath his skin. There was more he could do now!","He stepped forward. Each motion was deliberate, weighted, the embodiment of calm command.","And as his fingers curled slightly at his side, the words that followed were not grand. They were not shouted. They did not need to be.","They were simply the truth of what came next.","\"Establish the first Sacred Totem of the Early Veiled Shore.\"","The winds stilled.","And the very air seemed to lean in, listening.","HUUM!","The prompt bloomed with resplendent finality.","|The Sacred Totem of Infinity is being forged in the Early Veiled Shore.|","Cerulean light spilled outward like slow rainfall across existence. Behind the three trees at the center of the Early Veiled Shore, the ground trembled, shivered, and then began to rise.","The land itself molded upward, folding in on its own essence as if guided by hands. Sand fused with stone, roots of the strange glowing trees binding together into what began to form the base of a tower- tribal and ancient in design, primal in presence.","Noah stepped forward.","His obsidian pants shimmered with soft starlight, each step silent on the golden-grain sands. His chest remained bare, crystalline under the moonless sky, etched with the glow of the Glyph of Infinity- a faint symbol pulsing over the left side of his chest like a second heart.","Moiraine’s eyes, always sharp and knowing, followed his figure. The others turned as well, drawn by the tranquil rumble of the rising monument. It was as if the land itself was pulsing and lifting something sacred for its keeper!","The structure that emerged seemed carved of memory and purpose, and built from the musings of the Early Veiled Shore. Blue luster cloaked its surface- stone and sand conjoined by will, smoothed by time. It rose with elegance, a temple crowned by a singular relic.","A bell!","It was blue and ancient beyond measure. Hanging freely within a small arch at the tower’s peak, it bore a weathered sheen as if it had once tolled for the beginning of existence. Its form was modest, yet there was an undeniable grandeur in the way it sat- perfectly still, as if daring Existence to ask what it could summon.","|The first Sacred Totem has formed within the Early Veiled Shore.|","...!"]},{"number":3908,"title":"Chapter 3908: Chapter 3907: Glorious! III","paragraphs":["A Sacred Totem had formed, and it flashed its brilliance gloriously!","|The Sacred Totem of Infinity awaits to have its Sacred Bell rang for the first time in order to release the call to Early Living Land Lifeforms. Chances of attraction are exceedingly low. The likelihood of summoning an Early Living Land Lifeform increases depending on the distinction of the Sacred Totem. Unique conceptual foundations significantly improve rarity and response rate.|","Noah stared at the prompt, lips curling faintly as he was ready to get started!","\"Ring the Sacred Bell of Infinity,\" he commanded.","And...!","Silence.","|The Sacred Bell of a Sacred Totem can only be rang physically with the hands of the Early Creature.|","...!","Noah exhaled slowly, his smile becoming sharp.","So that was how it had to be.","He approached, steps echoing softly as he reached the newly born tower. The base held a staircase spiraling upward along the interior wall, illuminated with glowing etchings that pulsed with every footfall. Moiraine, Liora, even Ruination anf others watched from below, silent reverence in their eyes. To them, this was no casual act, and instead something else entirely!","Each step bore weight. Not metaphorical- actual resistance pushed against him as if the tower itself tested his resolve. His body ached from the climb, yet his mind remained crystalline, focused. Complexity bloomed in his bones, each movement actually making him stronger, each breath another step in the ascent.","He reached the summit soon enough as...","The bell loomed before him.","Close up, it glowed faintly with swirling stellar wheels trapped within its curves. Beside it, a rope of woven cerulean threads and silver anchors waited for his touch. He reached out with one hand, then paused- and then both hands wrapped around it, and instantly...resistance struck.","As if he could not pull this rope down!","The Glyph of Infinity on his chest flashed. Then, the Glyph of the Protagonist pulsed. Muscles trembled, arms flexing as he pulled down with everything he was. The rope moved slowly, infinitely heavy!","And then...!","DING!","It rang.","A singular tone.","Deep.","Endless.","It reverberated through the folds of the Early Veiled Shore, through the sands, through the water, through the stillness! A sound older than sound, more profound than truth!","|The Sacred Bell of Infinity has been rung for the first time. An incredible achievement! From its ringing, immense waves of complexity erupt as another Glyph of Infinity is forming within you.|","Blue shockwaves spread from the bell tower’s peak, washing over the entire shore.","Below, Moiraine lifted her gaze. His mother and wives, too! And beyond, the Infiniverse and Ruination paused what they were doing, gazing upward as their bodies glowed faintly.","Another prompt bloomed.","|All those who hear the ringing of the Sacred Bell of Infinity, regardless of their power or complexity, will experience a single Early Sacred Living Epiphany that will either allow their complexity to surge by 25%, or broaden their weavings of complexity by incorporating the heavy musings of Infinity into what they are.|","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes narrowed, watching as glyphs of soft cerulean appeared above each of their heads- symbols wrapped in cloud-like halos as if the land itself had offered them a vision.","And still, the bell rang.","|The tolling of the bell has been deemed to be... Exceptional!|","Another prompt shimmered before his eyes.","|The bell has been rung, and depending on the myriad of factors of the Sacred Totem of Infinity, an Early Living Land Lifeform may be attracted... or may not be attracted. It may not be rung again for some time.|","He stood in the stillness of that final toll, the wind pressing against him at the tower’s peak. The sea remained silent. The skies seemed to hold their breath.","And Noah Osmont, Early Creature of the Budding Veiled Shore, simply waited.","He did not need to hope.","He had already done all he could!","The wait.","The tolling of the Sacred Bell of Infinity echoed long after its chime had faded, reverberating like a question cast into the breathless silence of the Early Veiled Shore. Noah stood atop the tower still, the cerulean Glyph of Infinity etched across the left side of his crystalline chest pulsing like a quiet star.","The air held its breath. The winds of the Veiled Shore dared not stir. And Noah waited.","Waiting- such a strange, neglected virtue!","A thing scorned by the impatient, misunderstood by the impulsive.","Yet to Noah, it was neither shameful nor passive. He knew that many were addicted to the immediacy of fire, to the flash of power and sudden culmination.","No one knew how to wait anymore. But waiting, truly waiting, was its own kind of strength. In waiting, one revealed whether they could bear the weight of their desire without drowning in it.","In waiting, one measured their stillness and strength by anticipation.","For the patient, sometimes...a second was enough.","BOOM!","A sound thundered through the thick, ever-churning mists that framed the borders of the Early Veiled Shore.","Noah turned his gaze toward it, his expression unreadable. A new prompt formed before his eyes, glowing cerulean!","|In the Earliest Folds, it was common for Early Creatures to wait days, months, even years after tolling the bell of their Sacred Totems before any Early Living Land Lifeform would answer. Yet for some... mere seconds sufficed. It all depended on the sweetness of the Bell’s call.|","|The ringing of the Sacred Totem of Infinity has been deemed unfathomably exceptional. An Early Living Land Lifeform has responded. Will you grant it entry?|","Noah’s lips curled into a smile. \"Yes.\"","The mists trembled again.","BOOM!","A beam of white light surged forward from the gray mists- so bright, even the cerulean glow of the Sacred Totem seemed to dim in reverence. The radiance took form, and then form took shape. What emerged was not some titanous beast, nor a celestial horror.","No, what emerged... was a goat.","A goat!","But not just any goat.","It trotted through the mist as if it parted before its will, its steps soft and deliberate, its hooves clicking gently upon the grainy golden sand.","Its coat shimmered with such pureness of white it threatened blindness to all who stared too long. Each strand of its fur glowed like liquid snowlight, its eyes crystalline pools of ancient clarity. Yet those eyes... they narrowed. Sharpened.","Arrogance shimmered within them like a well-polished mirror!","Endless arrogance!"]},{"number":3909,"title":"Chapter 3909: Chapter 3908: Glorious! IV","paragraphs":["The goat moved with the casual superiority of a sovereign among lesser beings. Its gaze flicked over the figures gathered along the Shore.","It scoffed at the Emperor Penguin.","Snorted at the crouched forms of other Existences here!","It passed Moiraine, and for a moment, its proud expression eased into something approaching approval. It gave a tiny nod, as if saying, \"You, at least, know your worth.\"","It reached Ruination and the Infiniverse- two pillars of burgeoning power- and for them, the goat’s eyes gleamed as it gave a regal nod of respect. But that arrogance remained. It was not a creature interested in flattery!","Its attention fixed forward, to the tower.","The goat came to a halt before the Sacred Totem of Infinity, its crystalline eyes lifting to meet Noah’s. It said nothing. Yet its expression said everything- the bell had been acceptable!","More than acceptable!","HUUM!","With something bordering on bliss, it nudged the blue-gleaming tower walls, letting out a soft, self-satisfied grunt.","|The Eminent Early Living Land Lifeform, Heidrun, has answered the call and arrived at the Early Veiled Shore.|","|Land Lifeforms are categorized by rarity: Basic, Refined, Eminent, and Kleos.|","Noah’s eyebrows lifted. Eminent.","He leapt from the peak of the tower, descending like a star trailing darkness and starlight. He landed gently before the goat, who tilted its head upward, meeting his gaze with that same imperious expression.","He smiled as waves of information bloomed!","|Name: Heidrun","Designation: Eminent Early Living Land Lifeform","Rarity: Eminent","Lineage: Ancestral Echoes of Yrdifrost Lore: In the lost and earliest Chapters of the Folds, Heidrun was revered by Early Creatures as a terrifying conduit of nourishment. Her kind were rare beyond measure, said to dwell near the Loom where Totems gathered in reverent silence. The appearance of even one Heidrun would send shockwaves through Early Creatures. Entire Domains would offer up Marine Lifeforms, Early Sacred Herbs, and other Land Lifeforms to trade for one. The Reason was for....The Sacred Mead of Existence.","Sacred Mead of Existence: Heidrun can produce a golden-white mead imbued with the distilled essences of Complexity and Purity. One sip fortifies the soul, purifies the body, elevates existence, and enhances the forging of any weavings related to Early Creatures by an unquantifiable amount for the next day. Its effect on those lesser than Early Creature is so profound that having more than a drop can be deadly...","Existential Infusion: When near Early Creatures, Heidrun’s aura causes their internal Hearts or Existence to experience accelerated refinement.","Passive Boon – Glorious Stubbornness: Immune to all forms of compulsion and influence. Will only respond to those it deems \"sufficiently majestic.\"","Disposition: Arrogant. Discerning. Prideful. Loyal only to those it deems worthy.|","Noah slowly exhaled. His gaze lingered on the words \"sufficiently majestic\" for longer than necessary.","The goat... Heidrun, huffed. Her nostrils flared in response, the arrogance in her expression somehow intensifying.","He chuckled.","\"Welcome to the Early Veiled Shore,\" he said, voice smooth and resonant, his tone carrying the full gravity of someone who bore the burden of dominion.","The goat said nothing. Merely lowered her head. And with unspoken grace... stayed.","The first Sacred Totem had been tolled. The first Land Lifeform had answered!","The Early Veiled Shore... was no longer merely budding. It was beginning to blossom!","The bell’s toll still echoed softly, diffused across the sands and mist of the Early Veiled Shore like a hymn from another time.","And in that fading chime, Noah and the goat stood face to face.","Neither moved.","The goat, resplendent in its arrogance, gleamed under the blue light of the Sacred Totem. Its pure white coat shimmered with a terrifying luster, and its head was held high, nose tilted upward, eyes half-lidded with the judgment of a creature that had seen kingdoms rise and fall and found them all wanting. It looked at him as if he were some passing curiosity.","Noah... merely smiled. Calculated, amused, and infinitely patient.","He glanced at the glowing panel that hovered before him, filled with glorious script and glorious revelations. The Sacred Mead of Existence, a liquid sought after even in the Earliest Folds. That was what he desired right now!","\"Produce some Sacred Mead for me,\" he said simply.","And...!","There was a pause.","The goat blinked. Its pupils were as clear as quartz, cold and unbothered. Then, almost comically, it turned its head toward the tower behind it with a look that could only be interpreted as baffled offense.","Can you believe this guy?","Then came the haughty huff.","And another prompt.","|To obtain Sacred Mead of Existence from the Early Living Land Lifeform: Heidrun, one must hand milk it directly from its glorious udders.|","Noah blinked.","The goat shifted proudly, displaying its side. It was offering access, yes- but it made its expectations clear. If he wanted the Sacred Mead of Existence, he’d have to put in the work!","Noah chuckled at this surreal reality!","He turned, voice slightly louder. \"Someone get me a bucket!\"","There was a moment of stunned silence, the sound of shuffling feet, and then the elegant form of Moiraine approached. She held a crystal-clear Glass Bucket delicately in both hands, her voice composed, tone resolute.","\"Sir,\" she said with practiced calm, \"this is beneath your station. Let me handle it.\"","Her poise was the kind of thing that made existence listen. But Heidrun’s eyes narrowed.","The moment Moiraine stepped near, the goat snorted.","A violent gust erupted from its nose, a blast of concentrated complexity that caught Moiraine full in the chest and sent her flying backward, her body tumbling across the sand and into the lapping edges of the shore.","BOOM!","Gasps rang out, but Moiraine merely rose from the shallows with wet hair and narrowed eyes. She looked back toward Heidrun with startled respect. She wasn’t angry, only intrigued and shocked!","|The Early Living Land Lifeform: Heidrun possesses the Quality of Glorious Stubbornness. It is Immune to all forms of compulsion or influence and will only respond to those it deems sufficiently majestic.|","....!","Moiraine...was not deemed sufficiently majestic!","She jumped up and appeared beside Noah again, wiping the dampness from her brow. She offered him the bucket solemnly and seriously. \"Sir, please.","\"...\"","He took it.","He set it gently beneath the goat, who now seemed positively glowing with satisfaction.","With a sigh, Noah knelt upon the rising golden sand. The mound beneath him shaped itself softly to his weight. His bare chest reflected the tower’s glow, a crystalline sheen rippling across his form as his hand reached forward and grasped.","The udder was firm, warm.","And the moment he squeezed...","HUUM!","Golden liquid of unfathomable clarity gushed out in radiant arcs.","It filled the glass bucket with glowing swirls that looked less like milk and more like liquefied starlight. The scent of it struck immediately- a rich, honeyed aroma filled the air, thick with something more profound than sweetness.","The atmosphere of the Early Veiled Shore changed.","The weight of the air grew denser. The Towers of Origin within every being present began to hum. Complexity surged. Purity twined in elegant spirals. The very weavings of existence thickened with each drop that fell!","The concentration was so terrifying that in the next moment...","PAH! PAH!","Kazuhiko, the Emperor Penguin, Liora, and many others lost consciousness as their bodies fell down onto the sand, their existences unable to handle the terrifying concentration of the Sacred Mead of Existence!"]},{"number":3910,"title":"Chapter 3910: Chapter 3909: Glorious V","paragraphs":["Many were knocked unconscious!","Of those that remained awake, their Existence buzzed as their complexity and purity exploded upwards in a somewhat controlled manner!","Instantly, a second Basic Early Living Existential Glyph of Ruination began to form on the body of Ruination.","On the Infiniverse, an unknown reaction seemed to occuring with her as like blooming singularities, the Basic Early Living Existential Glyphs of Manadynamics, Continuity, and Dreams all bloomed simultaneously- her eyes vibrating with terrifying brilliance as one must not forget...the Early Veiled Shore...was locaded within her.","In her center.","Literally.","So what would it mean for her when the Early Veiled Shore continued to unlock its wonders?","Moiraine almost dropped to her knees on the side as her entire existence felt like it was quivering, her already tremendous complexity and purity...shockingly rising faster than it ever had before.","Her eyes trembled as within their depths, she could not help but howl out against the foolishness of Diviticus and her Mentor!","How foolish were they to have actually gone against this being?!","HUUM!","The bucket shone.","So did the eyes of those shocked who remained conscious as the shocking process seemed to just be getting started!","Noah kept milking as he mads sure his Mother, Son, Adelaide, and all others were okay.","He then stared at Heidrun with quiet wonder. \"Where do you come from?\" he asked calmly. \"Do you know where others like you dwell? Do you know where the Early Creatures might still be?\"","...!","Heidrun shimmered, its arrogant eyes lazing around.","The goat’s only response was a dignified snort.","A new prompt answered him instead.","|Very little additional records can be obtained regarding the origins of the Early Living Land Lifeform, Heidrun, at this moment.|","...!","He nodded.","It figured.","The milk flowed. The Sacred Mead of Existence flowed!","Until...","BZZT!","Noah blinked.","The udder resisted his grasp. Heidrun stepped back with a final, triumphant shake of her glimmering coat. Her eyes gleamed. Then she turned and began to trot away.","|Heidrun has produced as much Sacred Mead of Existence as she desires at this time. If you wish to collect more in the future, present her with her favorite delicacy.|","Noah remained sitting, the golden bucket pulsing before him. Heidrun strutted away, her expression smug, tail flicking with casual power as she returned to bask beneath the Sacred Totem’s glow.","He stared after her, shaking his head.","Then, he laughed!","It slipped out slow and full. His smile widened, eyes lifting to the skies as the breeze kissed his face.","\"You know,\" he said quietly, to no one and everyone, \"I’ve always wanted to be a farmer.\"","HUUM!","And for the briefest moment in the folds of existence, under a sparkling sky and upon golden sand that pulsed with ancestral might, Noah Osmont felt as if he truly were...a farmer.","All it required was to find and unlock the wonder that was the Early Veiled Shore!","The bucket of Sacred Mead of Existence glowed faintly where it sat in the golden sands, its surface calm and still, as if aware of its own impossible worth.","Noah’s gaze remained locked on it, his expression unreadable but deeply contemplative.","Unimaginably contemplative!","Around him, the sand of the Early Veiled Shore shifted softly, humming with an unseen rhythm, and below his bare feet, he could feel the tremor of something glorious moving.","Inside his being, Towers began to shudder.","A subtle quake of acceleration.","The early Towers of Osmont that would have taken a great deal of to form a single vein or layer now pulsed with progress. More than that, deep within the core of his existence, the Ventryalis, the Primal Root Atrium of Echoes, moved.","It had been crawling before.","Crawling despite everything he’d done, despite all the complexity he’d built, all the purity he’d burned through!","Now, it surged...just from him breathing the scent released by the Sacred Mead of Existence!","1%... 2%... 3%...","Every second, his Ventryalis inched forward in its completion, as if the golden milk in that bucket was reaching into him, humming softly to the rhythm of something quintessential!","And he hadn’t even tasted it yet.","Around this time...","BOOM!","The air above the Early Veiled Shore rippled.","Noah’s eyes lifted, glazed with distant starlight as he turned his gaze toward the faraway battlefield, where he could sense it- faintly but clearly.","The clash between Living Origins and Living Paradoxes in the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","A silent war, loud only to those whose perception could reach across threads of Existence.","His voice was quiet, low, more to himself than anyone around him, but heavy with thought.","But Moiraine listened in her stupor and fascination.","Any others who could listen, listened.","\"There is...a strange cruelty to the weavings of Existence,\" he murmured, contemplative!","\"A war wages not far from here. A war of truths and contradictions, of beings locked in endless opposition. They struggle, bleed, scream with purpose, chasing absolutes. And yet, here... here, something unimaginable has bloomed quietly...\"","HUUM!","His existence buzzed with unknown epiphanies as his complexity and purity surged!","While Living Paradoxes and Living Origins hurl their authority and philosophy at one another, they cannot see it. Perhaps they never would!","Life moved differently for many. Some beings run, some stand still.","Some, like Noah, walked into forgotten places!","He didn’t win a war or claim a throne to have what he had now. He simply made a series of choices... to seek. To wander. And somehow, that led him here.","His eyes were unimaginably bright as his voice echoed out, mainly to himself.","\"Sometimes, what matters most is simply where we choose to stop walking.\"","WAA!","His hand gripped the handle of the bucket.","\"If only...they could understand that.\"","The Sacred Mead pulsed with light, the milky golden liquid shimmering like starlit honey. Just the scent of it, just the nearness, had propelled his Towers forward.","What would a taste do?","He lifted the bucket slowly. It felt heavier than its size should allow. An existential weight, not a physical one.","Then, with the silence of inevitability, he drank.","A gulp.","Roughly...two hundred droplets of the Sacred Mead of Existence slid down his throat.","And...","Oh!","BOOM!","The air bent around him.","His body jerked with such violent force that a ripple of golden and cerulean light burst out in all directions!","Only his status as an Early Creature kept his frame from disintegrating outright. Even still, he staggered half a step, and a low exhale escaped his lips.","He was burning.","Gloriously burning with multicolored, and yet dull, archaic light!","He was ascending!","Within him...","|The Ventryalis – The Primal Root Atrium of Echoes, the first part of the Heart of an Early Creature, is going towards a glorious completion from the exposure to the droplets of the Sacred Mead of Existence.|","|A Profound and Quintessential change is occurring within your existence due to the consumption of something unimaginably complex.|","|81 Drops of Blood of an Early Creature have been generated in the Ventryalis!|","|162 Drops of Blood of an Early Creature have been generated in the Ventryalis!!|","|324 Drops of Blood of an Early Creature have been generated in the Ventryalis!!!|","His heart...it was forming!","The Heart of an Early Creature, a beating construct of power, of lineage, of age.","The air changed.","HUUM!","An old sound. A trembling weight passed through the folds of the Early Veiled Shore. All life paused!","Moiraine stepped back, breath caught in her throat!","Even Heidrun, the arrogant goat whose pride exceeded the sky, turned toward him.","She stared at Noah in silence.","And then, finally- nodded.","Affirmation.","As if to say, yes.","Now you are beginning to become what you were always meant to be. What you should be!","The aura of age swelled from Noah like thunder without sound, like stars being born in the lungs of a dead universe! Like Omniverses being born in dry frequencies of the Wheel!","And it did not stop.","Oh, it did not stop!"]},{"number":3911,"title":"Chapter 3911: Chapter 3910: Choices! I","paragraphs":["How exactly did one quantify age or oldness?","Some would claim it came through wrinkles carved onto the flesh like glyphs, the slow decay of joints and bone, or the graying of hair kissed by countless suns.","Others would say that it was measured in experiences- a ledger of moments, some sweet, others shattering, that shaped the weight of one’s existence.","Others believed age was the accumulation of self-reflection, of pain endured with grace, of love accepted and lost, of wonder that never faded.","And some deeper beliefs would describe age as a layering of consciousness across dimensions, a story told not in years but in the evolution of understanding.","And then, there were those who knew age wasn’t a number at all, but a scent- musky and deep- or a gaze that saw you and every version of you, all at once.","Whatever it was, age was presence!","It was weight!","And in this moment, Noah Osmont- still, unwavering- gave off the feeling of age so deep it made the air dense.","On the sands of the Early Veiled Shore, golden light shimmered as if hesitant to drift too close.","He stood with the bucket still warm from his hand, the Sacred Mead of Existence quietly standing against its crystalline walls. His bare chest shone with a soft, ancient glow, and from beneath his skin, something pulsed.","Noah’s eyes were closed. And inward, he saw it.","The Ventryalis.","The Primal Root Atrium of Echoes.","It pulsed with solemnity, a chamber of silence and memory.","This was no ordinary part of a heart.","It resembled a chambered vault made from living obsidian vines, with glowing arteries that pulsed with multicolored light, threading outward in fractal branches like the roots of a celestial tree.","Its texture was both biological and mythical- fibers like the sinew of existence itself forming the atrial walls, while its floor resembled an endless spiral carved into living stone.","At its center, a bulbous node pulsed with a steady rhythm, each throb emitting pulses that sent soft echoes throughout Noah’s body, into the Towers of Osmont, into the glyphs shining along his bones.","It was complete.","A prompt bloomed before his closed eyes.","|The Ventryalis – The Primal Root Atrium of Echoes has been fully formed.|","|All systems within your existence are now accepting and digesting the Sacred Mead of Existence.|","|You can now freely generate 1 Drop of Blood of an Early Creature every minute.|","|You can now begin nurturing a Concept or Idea from your Towers of Osmont into your own True Absolute Existential Resistance, even before surpassing the Originus Venerant Realm as from this point forward, limitations based on Realm boundaries defined by Living Existences and those lesser than them no longer apply to you.|","...!","The prompts were overwhelming.","And there were many as even now, they werent done!","|Due to the formation of the Ventryalis, the complexity of your existence, your Glyphs, Towers, and other Collective Factors, your strength has been assigned an Age.|","|Age Assigned: 1 / 1,000 |","|Note: The Age system for Early Creatures measures their authority, complexity, and presence relative to the foundational archetype of an Early Creature. An Age of 1 / 1,000 signifies a nascent but True status.|","Noah opened his eyes, the bucket still in hand, its golden milk reflecting a dancing starlight.","He smiled faintly.","He was given an age.","An age of an Early Creature!","And it turned out...he had not even reached 1 years old! He was a thousandth. 0.001!","This was fantastical and terrifying to think about as if Age was a measure of strength, how terrifying would Early Creatures be at this moment?","Would their Age continue rising with the passage of time, or if an Early Creature had their power stall at 100 years of age, even a million years later, they would still be 100 years of age?","...!","There were too many unknowns as he couldn’t say for sure!","He sighed with power and solemnity as he also thought about the other boons just now obtained.","A completed Ventryalis. The generation of a Drop of Blood of an Early Creature a minute! The forging...of his own type of Resistance based off a Tower of Osmont!","There were many boons as others could not be seen individually and could only be observed collectively!","His vision changed once more as a summarized panel shimmered before him.","[Noah Osmont] (Early Creature – 810 Drops of Blood) Age: 1 / 1,000","|Early Living Existential Glyphs: Protagonist x1 (Basic), Infinity x5 (Basic)|","|Complexity Quotient (CQ): 18,225,000 (22,000,000) SU|","|Purity Quotient (PQ): 19,220,000 (23,000,000) SU|","|True Sources with Towers of Origin Constructed: 0|","|True Sources with Towers of Osmont Constructed: 6|","|Average Lattice Quantity Per Tower: 3,000,000+|","|Total Existential Dimensional Lattices: 455,000,000+|","|Collective Total Resistance: 1002%|","He exhaled slowly, setting the bucket beside him as his entire being- his blood, his breath, his very thoughts- began to align in silent, seismic shifts.","Within his chest, the Ventryalis pulsed as more and more systems synchronized with its ancient rhythm.","The forming Heart. The Early Atlas of the Folds. The Towers that stretched across the unseen weavings of his existence!","His Existence was growing more complex by the moment!","Time.","All he needed was time.","He had made his choices. Not rushed into endless battles. Not clawed up realms for validation. No, he chose to sit. To learn. To grow.","But growth...was never quiet.","HUUM!","The sound shuddered through the folds, subtle at first, then sweeping across the golden shore in a tangible pulse.","He lowered the bucket gently back to the sand.","|Another wave of Early Living Marine Lifeforms has been detected approaching the Early Veiled Shore. Their purpose remains the rectification of population discrepancy.|","On the distant shores where the sacred waters shimmered, new bubbles had begun to surface. Multicolored light arced across the surface in elegant weaves, and the murky depths below pulsed with forming life.","Noah turned toward Moiraine, who stood silently not far behind him. Her posture was one of steady poise, even though she was looking towards him with even greater awe!","His voice carried gently, but firmly.","\"Moiraine. Could you see to that?\"","Her head lifted, her shoulders straightened as she stepped forward.","\"Yes, Sir.\"","Her eyes lingered a second too long, reverence gleaming in their depths. Then, she was gone, the sand barely disturbed beneath her feet.","Noah remained where he was.","Still.","Calm.","Time would carry the rest!","And as time flowed, so did the weavings of those entangled!"]},{"number":3912,"title":"Chapter 3912: Chapter 3911: Choices! II","paragraphs":["In the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","Where once stood a Paradoxical Prison, there now churned a battlefield!","The ancient structure shattered like glass under the weight of too many truths contorted into lies. Now, the broken remnants of that prison framed a war of extremities as Living Paradoxes clashed with Living Origins.","And the Paradoxes were winning as they had sheer numbers- led by Oryzarakh!","Booming layers of twisted brilliance erupted from over a few dozen Paradoxes, each hurling immense Authority- Living Paradoxical weavings formed from hundreds of millions of Lattices. These strands undid everything in their path. They folded existence backward into the shape of confusion and doubt.","Amid this surreal deluge, a solitary light pushed against the tide. Vast. Glacial. Immense.","Vorellion.","The Ancient Living Turtle of Twelve Epochs braced its omniverse-spanning shell as nine of its heads drew in toward the center. Each of the nine bore their own radiant halos, every one layered with Purpose and Origin. As the deadly waves of Paradox neared, Vorellion’s voices murmured in unison!","HUUM!","\"Begin No Purpose.\"","A wave pulsed outward.","From the convergence of its nine heads, an impossible paradox was unknit by refusal of premise.","The very concept of the Paradoxical attack was nullified, its purpose made retroactively void!","The Authority crashed... and vanished, as if it had never intended harm, as if it had never been born.","Its origin...was ended!","The pressure lifted. The Living Origins found breathing room again.","And Vorellion’s gaze, those nine deep orbs of ancient wisdom, settled upon the young Living Origin beside them. Once jailed in this forsaken Fold, now trembling and radiant with strength.","The thought burned through its minds.","How dare they? How dare these cruel, vile beings try to cage something so new?!","HUUM!","As Vorellion was thinking this.","An oppressive tide fell upon the battlefield.","A voice followed- low and simmering.","\"I am thoroughly enraged. And in the past eon, I have not been enraged.\"","Vorellion froze. Its shell pulser. Every head recognized the pressure. The pressure of an Honored Living Paradox!","The Ancient Turtle’s power neared the threshold of Honored, but it was not there yet.","They had sent word for reinforcements of more Living Origins to this location. Some younger Living Origins had arrived already. But none strong enough.","Not yet!","Honored Gold’s arrival needed no fanfare.","The Fold itself grew silent.","He descended like a thought too heavy to hold, like light bent around him in apology. Wings and halos pulsed around him- countless, changing, contradicting. They were there and not there, infinite in number, yet none remained visible for more than a breath.","The Honored Living Golden Paradox floated forward. Calm. Cold.","His gaze swept over the battlefield. And then, settled.","\"When,\" he asked, his tone clipped with condescension, \"did the Living Origins grow balls?\"","He looked faintly, with genuine malice.","\"Do you seek more massacres in the Battlefront Folds?\"","The Origins stirred.","Altheon flared! Shaynara surged! But none stepped forward.","\"Distractions,\" Gold continued, flicking his wrist. \"You are all distractions.\"","He tilted his head.","\"And I detest distractions.\"","His voice dropped.","\"Liar’s Paradox.\"","The Fold trembled.","The Liar’s Paradox!","It was a self-referential wound in logic. An example to better understand it...was the statement- \"This sentence is false.\"","This sentance...is false.","If true, then it is false. If false, then it is true. A loop. A contradiction. A poison.","Gold shaped his own version of such a wonder!","\"The Living Origins are only alive because they are already dead.\"","...!","HUUM!","A terrifying statement was made.","Contradicting! Unfathomable!","And behind him, a golden Tower of Origin flickered- built to protect and to unravel. To enforce contradiction!","The Living Origins roared with a shocked sense of despair.","White towers erupted from behind the Living Origins in response!","But...a heartbeat later, they began to crumble.","Altheon watched comrades unravel. Shaynara screamed as she sought to hold on!","The faces of Origin turned to terror and disbelief as their essence cracked from within.","One Origin after another fell, their light snuffed by the unbearable contradiction of their own existence.","From the single statement filled with the complexity of Honored Gold!","An Honored Living Existence...was simply that powerful.","Only three remained.","Altheon. Shaynara. Vorellion.","And one more.","Bob.","The young one had not fallen in all this as one had to wonder...how?","Vorellion reeled from the massacre. Its heads shook. Each one dripping with sorrow!","It saw the perished Origins as it wanted to roar, but did not!","Then, with profound stillness, all nine heads turned to the sky.","\"For my kin.\"","It did not roar.","It simply... gave.","And it gave everything with all its heart!","Origin surged. The echoes of its purpose, the very reason for its birth, flared one last time. And then...","\"End!\"","A pulse of Origin erupted as Vorellion unmade itself- from duty. As a sacrifice.","In its unraveling, a flare was released.","A Call!","A summons for an Honored Living Origin.","Gold watched the act with distaste.","\"Pathetic,\" he said. His tone was dripping with disdain. \"Some things are best left to end. There is peace in it. A clean fade. But you cling. You flail.\"","He raised a hand.","\"Let me clean it up.\"","He reached for Altheon, who braced himself!","But then...","Gold paused.","His hand froze in midair.","His eyes narrowed.","His Authority recoiled as his expression became heavy!","\"Form the Transcendent Paradoxical Tower of Inevitability!\" he bellowed.","...!","The Fold fractured as what he sensed came down, a terrifying musing of Origin manifesting!","White light descended like thunder on silk. An unmistakable brilliance.","A woman walked through the light.","Her legs emerged first, fair and radiant. Then her dress, a flowing garment of sparkling white, stitched with stellar jewels. Her hair, long and white, shimmered like the threads of destiny.","Her voice rang, clear and amused.","\"Whatever could have pulled an Honored Living Paradox here?\"","Gold’s expression soured as he sensed...","Royalty.","\"Do the Living Origins have so many forces now that they send a Royal Living Origin to lesser Folds?\"","The woman smiled.","\"Royal Origin Calypso, at your service.\" she said sweetly, giving a curtsy no less regal for being unnecessary. \"And yes. I came because someone here gave me good news about a little girl I thought dead\"","Her gaze fell on Altheon.","\"One of their bodies,\" she said, her voice soft as falling snow, \"cannot perish.\"","And she smiled.","The Fold pulsed once more.","And the war reached a terrifying precipice!"]},{"number":3913,"title":"Chapter 3913: Chapter 3912: Choices! III","paragraphs":["Royal Origin Calypso stepped forward, the radiance of her form diffusing across the battlefield like a balm over open wounds.","Where her bare feet touched the twisted foldscape, the strands of reality shimmered, weaving themselves back together in gentle pulses of violet-gold light.","With a single flick of her finger, the decaying Origin of Vorellion was stilled. His unraveling ceased. The rhythm of his ancient purpose resumed, however feebly.","Her eyes swept across the field. Altheon. Shaynara. And Bob.","She lingered on the latter with the faintest spark of interest, then turned her gaze outward.","The battlefield was ruin. But not in the traditional sense of ash and flame. No, the deaths of Living Origins birthed a different kind of aftermath.","In their place stood crystallized echo-groves of trees with translucent leaves humming with fractured memory, roots that tangled through the fold beneath them, feeding on the echoes of unfinished beginnings.","White mist bled from them, curling into runes that could never be read twice the same way. And above each grove floated a single radiant sphere- the final beat of the Origin who had died, still pulsing in search of the purpose it was never allowed to complete!","Calypso exhaled a long breath. \"What a bloody waste.\"","She looked up then, eyes falling upon Honored Gold, who remained elevated above the field, unmoved and unworried. Dozens of Living Paradoxes floated around him like silent stars in orbit. Their forms flickered in and out of clarity, their Authority humming together in deep synchrony.","Paradoxes had purposefully come together.","And what happened...when Paradoxes came together?!","Calypso whistled.","\"I haven’t seen a Tower of Inevitability in a while. Did I really scare you that badly?\"","WAA!","Honored Gold said nothing. He didn’t need to. His silence was a blade. Cold. Surgical. His aura, merged with the Prime and normal Paradoxes around him, pulsed in deliberate waves, each one drawing in paradoxical authority!","They were summoning it.","They wanted an Inevitability!","Calypso tilted her head, a smile playing at the edges of her lips.","\"If I had come alone,\" she said sweetly, \"this might have actually gotten troublesome.\"","She lifted one hand into the air and pointed up.","\"Thankfully...I invited a friend.\"","The shift was immediate.","Honored Gold’s expression, previously etched in stone, cracked. His eyes flicked upward.","The Fold above them split open.","Out of the tear, a woman descended.","Or rather, she fell. Headfirst. Her body suspended upside down as though gravity had forgotten its place in the conversation. Long dark hair spilled out around her like unraveling ink across a blank page. Her skin was pale, flawless. Her features were delicate, almost too symmetrical to be natural, framed by the luminous white robe that hugged her form without ever actually touching her.","She smiled.","A bright, dangerous smile.","The aura she emanated struck silence into the battlefield.","Because it was not Living Origin Authority nor Living Paradoxical Authority!","It was...","Living Law!","A Living Law!","Unlike any other presence on the field, hers wasn’t oppressive through weight. It was clarity sharpened into a command- the promise that things would be as she declared.","She hovered midair, still upside down, spinning slowly as her eyes glinted with power.","\"I was told a treasure of the Living Laws had ended up coming from this delightful little dump,\" she said. Her voice was light, lilting, far too amused. \"Which was, if I’m not mistaken... your finding, Little Altheon?\"","...!","Altheon flinched and nodded.","The Living Law spun once more, flipping upright in the blink of an eye. Her smile deepened as she focused on Altheon.","\"You give my dear Calypso here some good news- which she still refuses to share with me- and then send me a child repeating that he only wants peace from these folds. And yet...\"","She opened her arms wide to the carnage.","\"Here you are. In the middle of everything. Just what recent entanglements have you gotten yourself into, Altheon?\"","...!","Altheon offered no reply to such a question as he truly could not say much!","\"My great friend,\" Calypso said, stepping beside her. \"Royal Law Tristesse. Should we not address the... thing?\"","She gestured up.","At the peak of Honored Gold’s golden Tower, something was emerging.","A Transcendent Inevitability.","Tentacles stretched out from the forming monstrosity- multicolored, pulsing with contradiction and hunger. Each tendril sang a note of entropy. The sound alone warped the space around it. The air bled. The folds frayed!","Tristesse glanced at it, then at Honored Gold.","\"You Paradoxes never change. Always calling forth things you think you can contain.\"","\"We are the ones most affected by Inevitabilities,\" Honored Gold replied. \"You wouldn’t understand.\"","She shook her head.","\"If you say so... you ugly fuck.\"","Her smile vanished.","In the next instant, her face turned fierce, and cold.","HUUM.","A silver tower erupted behind her.","Living Law Authority surged across the battlefield in the next moment!","\"Living Paradoxical Authority,\" she declared, her voice reverberating as if etched directly into reality, \"will not work in these folds for the next minute.\"","The moment the words left her lips, they became.","The folds accepted them.","Reality bent to follow.","Dozens of Living Paradoxes blinked in confusion. Their Authority dimmed. Their bodies flickered!","Above them, the Inevitability shrieked as it fully formed, its thousand tendrils unfurling like a flower of madness.","Tristesse looked down at them, her voice now a solemn melody.","\"Little Paradoxes... do you know what Law is?\"","She paused. Let silence fill the space.","\"Law...is the formal expression of rational will. But here, it is more than that. It is a directive of purpose, not suggestion. It is reality’s spine, and I am its marrow. When I speak, existence recalibrates. When I declare, contradiction bows. That is Law.\"","She gazed down at the trembling Paradoxes.","\"So... if I have laid down the law that you cannot use your Authority...\"","Her eyes narrowed.","\"How will you run from the Inevitability you called out yourselves?\"","HUUM!","Panic erupted.","Paradoxes scattered. With no Authority to shield them, they fled with their bare existences, trying to escape the oncoming collapse.","Only Honored Gold remained still. Wings unfurled. Eyes burning.","He stared coldly into the growing chaos.","And above, the Inevitability screamed.","A thousand tentacles lashed out.","They devoured everything as just because it came from Living Paradoxes did not mean that it would not target them!","And amidst it all, in the eye of disorder, there was one who moved unseen.","Bob.","Quiet.","Solitary, and still.","He was....","Absorbing.","Drawing in the scattered remnants of the slain Living Origins.","And from within him, something unfathomable pulsed with glee as a shielded Inevitability cheered at the ongoing chaos!"]},{"number":3914,"title":"Chapter 3914: Chapter 3913: Choices! IV","paragraphs":["Royal Origin Calypso and Royal Law Tristesse floated side by side, their visages radiant with ancient power, exuding a splendor that bent the air around them.","Each emanated a sovereign presence- Calypso cloaked in regality, Tristesse in a calculated composure that never wavered.","Around them, existence itself groaned.","The Transcendent Inevitability raged.","Its tentacles lashed across reality, multicolored strands of hunger and ruin snapping and writhing.","Living Paradoxes- once draped in wings of contradiction and shimmering halos- tried to flee. But under the suffocating silence of Tristesse’s Law, their Authorities were nullified.","Powerless, many of them were caught!","HUUM!","The Inevitability devoured without pause.","Tentacles seized them mid-flight. Their radiant forms turned gray, dulling into husks as they were reeled back toward the central writhing mass. They had summoned it. And now, they were its feast!","Tristesse stood motionless, gaze locked onto the calamity.","\"Calypso,\" she said, her voice smooth as it could be, \"remind me again- how important are these folds?\"","Calypso, every part of her frame exuding dignity, turned slowly. \"What do you think?\"","Her tone was cool, though her body radiated Living Origin Authority in steady, growing waves that pushed away the distant Inevitability.","\"These are the folds that birthed a paradox that produces no Inevitabilities. Altheon found a Fold Dweller here in possession of something tied to the Living Laws and sent him to you. And...\"","Her gaze deepened. \"He also found something that...I am personally invested in. That’s three points. All tied to these Lesser Folds.\"","Tristesse allowed a small breath to leave her. Her eyes sharpened with clarity. \"That’s enough then,\" she said, each word clipped with precision. \"If I’m here, I might as well clean house. You didn’t bring me to dance around the issue...you brought me to isolate these folds, so I will!\"","WAA!","Calypso inclined her head but said nothing. She turned, her jeweled robes gleaming like woven starlight. With unhurried grace, she surged toward the Inevitability- and Honored Gold.","\"You there,\" she called, voice laced with honeyed malice, \"weavings of contradiction and uncertainty. Ready to have your day utterly fucked?\" Her eyes sparkled. \"Do you think your Royal Living Paradoxes will execute you after today’s little failure? Or will the Inevitability devour you first?\"","HUUM!","Without waiting, she plunged forward, an ocean of Origin descending!","Tristesse, behind her, exhaled and seated herself midair, crossing her legs with a deliberateness that echoed finality.","Altheon, standing nearby with Shaynara, Vorellion, and the silent Bob, blinked and asked softly, \"Esteemed Miss... just what exactly are you doing?\"","Tristesse smiled- calm, precise, and knowing. \"Relocating these Folds,\" she said, her tone utterly rational. \"From under the influence of Paradoxes. Into territory that obeys structure, and Law.\"","Then she lifted her chin.","\"O Nullvein Gravewake Folds...\"","Her voice deepened, becoming a resonant note that stretched across eternity.","\"You were born in chaos, whispered into being by Paradox, raised beneath the shadow of ruin. But I see you. I see the strands that quiver beneath your skin. The laws you yearned for in silence. Now hear me. Obey me. Step forward. Out of contradiction, and into clarity! Come beneath the light of established Law! And be still. The Law...demands it!\"","...!","HUUM!","The Folds trembled.","From her body, silver light spilled out- an endless river of Law!","It raced across the distorted folds that were endless, chasing the broken latticework of paradox like ink over parchment. Everything shivered. Shifted!","A Law was laid down.","A Law was adopted.","A Law was followed!","Tristesse grimaced slightly, her brow twitching as strain lined her expression. But she did not falter.","She exhaled. \"It’s been... a while,\" she murmured, wiping an invisible crease from her sleeve.","Altheon and the others said nothing.","And then...","A brilliant flash of silver bloomed.","The Nullvein Gravewake Folds...disappeared. Or really...displaced!","What remained behind was madness.","The Inevitability screeched. Honored Gold, undeterred, burst forward with Authority rekindled. He clashed against Calypso’s descent, the battlefield blooming with roaring contradiction.","BOOM!","She smiled as their powers collided. \"I only needed to keep you distracted while my friend took everything from you.\"","Her voice dropped, her eyes gleaming. \"Good luck, Honored Fuck. I will tell you that you and all other Living Paradoxes won’t be living quite so comfortably in the time to come...things are changing. And that change will be hard for Paradoxes to survive!\"","WAA!","She vanished.","Behind her, Paradoxes scrambled. The Inevitability unfurled more limbs, snatching bodies and fracturing logic.","Only Honored Gold remained unshaken. He stood amidst ruin, his voice low, cold, deliberate.","\"It is not Paradoxes who will know discomfort in the days to come.\" His golden eyes narrowed. \"It is all of you. None of you... are prepared. For the Paradox that cannot produce Inevitabilities. For Diviticus!\"","...!","Paradoxical Authority surged outward like a sea as he turned to meet the thing he had summoned!","—","Elsewhere.","A new weaving of existence...but also not.","WAP!","Royal Origin Calypso appeared amidst folds that were unraveling like coiled nightmares.","But there was...a semblance of Law now. A silver light seeped through them- cool, deliberate, and orderly!","What once was chaos became silence.","Around her, the silver brilliance blanketed everything. The Nullvein Gravewake Folds had been moved.","Tristesse stood at the center, composed, radiant. Altheon, Vorellion, Bob, and Shaynara nearby.","Calypso’s voice was like a heavgly blade. \"You should have sent these folds into the care of the Living Origins. Not into the domains of the Living Laws.\"","Tristesse met her gaze with even calm and smiled.","\"We’re allies, aren’t we?\" she asked, \"What matters is not whose territory they fall under. What matters is that Paradoxes will have a harder time reaching them now. And we’ll have time to understand... why these folds drew such attention.\"","Calypso said nothing. But her eyes glinted.","Then she turned.","Her gaze fell upon Altheon. \"You. Come.\"","Altheon moved without hesitation, her Authority wrapping around them both.","As they moved away, her voice dropped. \"Tell me. Has the Young Miss arrived yet in the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds?\"","Altheon hesitated. Then nodded. \"Soon,\" he said.","He paused again. \"Though she is... not alone. She’s accompanied by a Fold Dweller.\"","Calypso stopped.","Altheon’s eyes met hers.","\"Someone known as...Noah Osmont.\"","...!"]},{"number":3915,"title":"Chapter 3915: Chapter 3914: Choices! V","paragraphs":["The air held pulsed with glory!","Royal Origin Calypso raised her brows as she asked.","\"For you to mention him, is he something to worry about?\"","Altheon’s eyes flashed with uniqueness as he seemed to deliberate something...and he then he shook his head.","He remembered the words of the Young Miss!","And so...he made a choice.","Like all others, he made a choice!","\"No, she had locked away her weavings, and this Osmont is merely an attendant of hers that protected her, so I decided to reward him by keeping him close, and the Young Miss also allowed it.\"","...!","Calypso nodded at these words as she did not give them too much weight.","She looked out across the Nullvein Gravewake Folds that were nowin a different place as she voiced out...","\"We have much to do. Honor those fallen and we shall have many more Origins scour these folds, and I will make preparations for the Young Miss.\"","...!","—","The Nullvein Gravewake Folds were no longer what they once were!","Displaced, restructured, retethered.","The silver luster of Living Law Authority bled through its every strand, a quiet verdict passed across an entire dominion of collapse.","What once trembled with contradiction and unformed potential now pulsed with structure, boundary, and definition.","The mists that once refused to part were unweaving themselves into paths- mapped and measured, no longer shrouded in aimless paradox!","It was an overwhelming presence. Regal. Final. And terrifying in the way all certainty could be!","The figures of Living Origins moved through it now, their radiant authority mingling with the silver streams of Living Law.","In these very same folds.","Far away, at the heart of the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence that was hidden from the eyes of even Living Existences!","On golden sands that pulsed with ancient possibility, the Early Veiled Shore remained untouched.","Noah Osmont sat barefoot, his arms resting over his knees, looking out across the glimmering tide as his body continued to be surrounded by multicolored waves of complexity.","The horizon of the Folds shimmered with silver threads- ghostly reflections of the very beings that sought him. Calypso. Altheon. Tristesse.","He had observed how the entire battle between them and the Living Paradoxes had unfolded, all the way to this point!","He smiled softly.","\"Choices, choices,\" he said.","Behind him, the sound of splashing water echoed. Moiraine emerged, her steps silent as she carried a crystalline container holding twenty shimmering Schrödinger’s Boxes, each holding a trembling marine lifeform bound by the earliest weavings of existence.","\"You made quick work of them,\" he remarked.","Moiraine gave a nod of awe as her body also buzzed with rising complexity.","\"I did as you commanded, Sir.\"","\"...\" Noah’s gaze lingered on the horizon.","The Folds had changed...not because of overwhelming force.","They changed because the Paradoxes failed to prepare for nuance! They were caught off guard by involvement they didn’t account for or know about!","Sigrid.","And a treasure of Living Laws that was found in these folds.","His fingers brushed over his chest, over the place where his power was continuing to bloom as another part of the Heart of an Early Creature would soon begin to form.","Two of the reasons that brought Royal Living Existences here... were related to him.","Sigrid, and the Paradox that did not produce Inevitabilities!","The third related to Living Laws he was curious about, but...","He turned his gaze to the glowing bucket beside him, its golden liquid- the Sacred Mead of Existence, shimmering like a dream made tangible.","Near it, Heidrun lay basking beneath the Sacred Totem of Infinity, her glowing fur bathed in warm celestial hues as her arrogant eyes looked content.","The Veiled Shore of an Early Creature was a place of unfathomable possibilities.","His hand hovered over the sands, and in his mind, he wondered. Could he now challenge the Record of an Early Creature?","Could he elevate the Budding Shore?!","Such a question rose as another body of his...was continuing entanglements elsewhere!","—","Elsewhere.","Across a channel carved between the Living Origin Labyrinth and the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds, rivers of white gold bent and curved endlessly- a place where direction folded upon itself and momentum was heavy!","Within one of these drifting streams, Noah and Sigrid floated side by side.","She had been talking- quiet, almost playful- about the Story of the Earliest Folds. Her voice had been confident, regal, her tone rich with what she knew.","And then she stopped.","Her body stilled as her head turned toward him sharply.","Without a word, her hands moved. A veil of white gold brilliance wrapped around them, sealing them from the ever-listening gaze of Altheon that should have been monitoring them here!","She stood in front of him then, wrapped in a flowing white robe that clung gloriously to her form. Her pale hair, split with streaks of obsidian, framed her calculating face that was no longer playful, but wary. The runic tattoos on her skin shimmered beneath the robe, burning dimly with muted authority.","\"I think... I’m in trouble,\" she whispered.","Noah’s eyes sharpened. \"Oh?\"","Her lips twisted as she breathed out, looking deeply into his eyes.","\"I was meant to become the Living Order,\" she began, her voice low and steady. \"Something I didn’t ask for. Something I hate because of all ther sacrifices made.\"","Her breath quickened , though her tone stayed cool.","\"But now... now I’m bound to you. And you’ve been marked by me. And just now, my entire existence just shuddered from sensing you. On the other side of that bond. You feel... enormous. Impossibly enormous.\"","Her words slipped out, as though she did not entirely want to know the answer to the question she was asking.","Yet she had to ask!","\"Just who are you, really?\"","HUUM!","Noah’s voice was heavy.","\"Do you really want to know?\"","Sigrid bit her lip.","She nodded once.","He lifted his hand.","She hesitated.","Then stepped forward, placing her hand into his.","His aura flowed into her like heavy gravity. It pulled at the deepest parts of her being as she began to feel...euphoria!","Her eyes trembled.","Noah’s voice was quiet.","\"What beings did Living Existences look up to? Revere?\"","Her expression faltered. Her mind moved rapidly as everything lined up! She half knew it. She thought it. But to confirm it...!","HUUM!","She whispered, her stellar eyes wide.","\"I really am in a lot of trouble...\"","...!"]},{"number":3916,"title":"Chapter 3916: Chapter 3915: Battlefronts! I","paragraphs":["The air between them thrummed with something that transcended power- it was older than authority, deeper than dominion, and more fundamental than the very concept of existence itself!","Sigrid felt her being respond to it tremendously, every fiber of her existence yearning to surrender to the pull of whatever Noah was.","Her hands trembled as she gazed at his, watching the way reality seemed to bend around his fingers like light refracted through the purest crystal. The aura that emanated from him was unlike anything she had ever encountered in all her life, all her careful observations of the Living Existences who had shaped her destiny.","What was he...really?!","The question burned in her mind even as her body betrayed her, swaying slightly toward him despite her will. Her existence- that carefully controlled amalgamation of Living Origin, Order, and purpose that had been forged in the crucible of her family’s sacrifice- hummed with an almost musical resonance that matched the rhythm of his presence.","She was in trouble! Deep, unfathomable trouble that went beyond the weavings of politics or power struggles or the machinations of Royal Living Existences!","\"Are you...\" Her voice emerged as barely more than a whisper, the words catching in her throat as she fought against the overwhelming urge to simply lose herself in the depths of his being.","\"Are you in any way similar to me? Where this distinction was given to you recently, or have you always been...an Early Creature?\"","The question hung between them like a blade suspended by the finest thread. Everything- her future, her choices, perhaps her very Existence, depended on his answer.","If he was one of the ancient beings, the true Early Creatures of legend who had walked between the Folds when the Existence was young, then she was nothing more than a moth drawn to a flame that would consume her without even noticing her passing.","Noah’s smile was gentle, as if he understood the weight of her question and the fears that drove it.","\"I only recently attained the distinction of being an Early Creature.\"","WAA!","The relief that flooded through her was so profound it nearly brought her to her knees. Her shoulders sagged as tension she hadn’t even realized she was carrying drained away!","For a moment, she simply breathed, allowing the knowledge to settle into her.","\"Why does that matter?\" Noah asked, his head tilting slightly as he studied her with those impossibly deep eyes of an Early Creature.","Sigrid looked up at him, and for yet another instance...allowed vulnerability to show in her expression.","\"I... would have found it immeasurably difficult to know how to proceed with you if you were one of those ancient Early Creatures I’d only ever heard about in legends,\" she said, her voice growing stronger with each word. \"But if, like me, this identity was forced upon you or obtained through circumstance... then we are not so different after all.\"","She paused, gathering her thoughts like a scholar preparing to recite from sacred texts.","\"You see, I feel as though I have a choice now. If you had been some primordial being from the dawn of Existence, it would have been akin to me simply playing in the palm of one of those terrifying entities I’d heard stories about. The records I knew, whether true of false, spoke of some wonders and terrible truths about the ancient Early Creatures.\"","\"That they...treated Living Existences like playthings- dolls to be experimented upon, commodities to be traded between themselves for amusement or advancement. We were cared for, yes, but only as beautiful toys are revered by children who grow bored and break them when the novelty fades.\"","HUUM!","\"They only truly respected each other. To them, everything else was lesser, decorative perhaps, but ultimately disposable. And lastly...\" Her voice dropped to barely above a whisper.","\"Early Creatures were incapable of true companionship because their core weavings traced back to the Earliest Creature itself- to Everything. To be with them was to be absorbed, to trust them was to lose oneself completely.\"","...!","She searched his face, looking for any flicker of the cold indifference she had been taught to expect from beings of such power.","\"But you... you’re not that, right?\"","Noah’s response was immediate, his voice carrying the weight of absolute certainty. \"No. I am more than capable of companionship. And respect, when mutual, is both given and received.\"","...!","His eyes held hers with an intensity that was both gentle and overwhelming, and she found herself almost lost in their depths, drowning in the promise of understanding and acceptance they offered!","She nodded.","\"But still,\" she said, forcing herself to focus on the larger picture, on the responsibilities that had been carved into her very soul through sacrifice and loss, \"all the Living Origins look at me like some answer. Some ultimate solution. They expect me to become THE Living Order and somehow fix everything that Paradox made wrong so many eons ago. But...\"","The rest of her words were cut off as Noah moved closer, his hands rising to frame her face with a gentleness that belied the quintessential forces at his command. Their faces were suddenly inches apart, and she could feel his breath against her skin.","The aura of an Early Creature made all parts of her being buzz!","\"You are bound to me,\" he said, \"You are mine. Whatever responsibility others have forced upon your shoulders, you do not have to bear that weight unless you choose to.\"","\"If you were to make the choice right now,\" he continued, his voice dropping to barely above a whisper, \"I could take you to a place where no Living Existence could ever find you. You could do whatever you wanted, be whoever you chose to be, without ever having to worry about becoming anyone’s chosen vessel or predetermined savior.\"","HUUM!","The offer hung between them like a lifeline thrown to a drowning soul!","She could see in his eyes that he meant every word, that he possessed both the power and the will to spirit her away from all of this- the expectations, the burden, the weight of an entire force pressing down upon her shoulders.","Her eyes trembled as the full implications of his words sank in.","He could do it. He really could take her away from all of this, give her the freedom she had never dared to dream of. For a moment, she allowed herself to imagine it- a life without the constant pressure of existence, without the ghost of her sacrificed family haunting her every decision, without the crushing responsibility of becoming something she had never asked to be.","But even as the temptation flowed through her veins like the sweetest poison, she steeled herself against it. Her existence, which seemed to be unbearably drawn to his, fought against her as she forced herself to speak.","\"What you offer is tempting,\" she said with a sad smile, \"If things were different, I would have gladly taken your hand and never looked back.\"","But.","Her expression grew cloudy.","\"My becoming THE Living Order... it’s not simply to become what the Living Origins want me to become. I need that power, that distinction, so that I can hold the Royal Living Origins accountable for their role in my family’s sacrifice. For standing by and watching as my entire lineage burned themselves to ash so that I might live. They must pay for their complicity in that tragedy!\"","BOOM!","Her hands clenched at her sides, and when she spoke again, her voice carried the cold and calm fury of existence.","\"I also want that power because I do want to rectify the chaos that Paradoxes and Inevitabilities have wrought upon existence. The Loom, the constant threat of collapse, all the things that drove my entire lineage to the desperate act that created me- I want to see them all undone. Not for the Living Origins’ vision of order, but for the memory of my sister, my father, my mother...those who wrongfully died to give me this chance.\"","...!","Her eyes blazed with fierce determination as she looked at him, and Noah found himself nodding slowly, understanding flickering in his gaze.","\"Then I will help you,\" he said simply, moving closer until his nose brushed against hers, until she could feel the warmth of his skin and the steady rhythm of his breathing. \"Because you are bound to me. Your goals become my goals. Your vengeance becomes my vengeance. Okay?\"","The question was soft, almost tender, but it carried with it promise beyond imagination!","Her body shuddered at his words, at the casual way he offered to reshape existence itself for her sake!","When she whispered her answer, it came out as barely more than a breath against his lips.","\"Okay.\"","The moment the word left her lips, his mouth found hers, and existence exploded into brilliance. White-gold radiance erupted around them like a Wheel of Existence being born, wrapping their figures in a cocoon of pure luminescence that pulsed with the rhythm of two existences becoming something greater than the sum of their parts.","In that kiss, in that moment of perfect unity, the fate of many things was sealed...and the foundations of new weavings of existence were laid down magisterially!"]},{"number":3917,"title":"Chapter 3917: Chapter 3916: Battlefronts! II","paragraphs":["In the channel leading to the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds.","Altheon’s awareness pressed against the barrier like fingers testing the surface of still water, his ancient mind cataloguing every ripple of power that emanated from within as he did not dare to observe anything, but could somewhat gues what was happening within.","He sighed- for any displays of emotion were beneath a being of his stature, but somewhere in the depths of his existence, duty and desire waged their war.","The Young Miss. Even now, the title carried reverence that made his very essence tremble.","She was not merely a unique Living Origin, though that alone would have commanded the devotion of many. No, she was something far more precious, far more dangerous.","The Living Order.","Not just any Living Order, but THE Living Order- the singular axis upon which the balance of all Living Existences that was broken long ago...would one day turn!","Her potential was whispered among the highest echelons of Living Origins, a promise of restoration that entire Folds had died hoping to witness. And now, in this critical moment of her emergence, she chose to enclose herself with... him.","Altheon’s luminous gaze traced the smooth curve of the barrier, behind which the Young Miss conversed with the Fold Dweller he had protected from Royal Origin Calypso’s scrutiny.","Noah Osmont. The name tasted strange in his thoughts, carrying with it an inexplicable weight that made his ancient intuition prickle with unease. There was something about that being that simply felt off!","The way he carried himself. His attitude. As if even a Living Origin like him was nothing.","The Young Miss was no child. Her mind was sharp as the edge of existence, her will forged in the crucible of unimaginable loss. She knew precisely what she was doing, had calculated every angle, every consequence. But that knowledge did nothing to ease the knot of frustration that coiled in Altheon’s core!","At this moment, when her emergence into the greater weavings of existence required the utmost care, she chose intimacy over glory. Privacy over prudence.","It maddened him.","But he...had already made his choice. And now, he could only continue!","\"Young Miss,\" he called out, his voice carrying across the flowing channels of white-gold current with the authority of eons. The words rippled through the barrier like stones cast into a mirror-still pond, yet returned to him unchanged, unanswered.","Silence!","The channel around them pulsed with its own rhythm, each fold of current breathing in and out like the chest of some slumbering titan.","Rivers of light twisted through the medium, yet within that barrier, all was still!","\"Young Miss,\" Altheon tried again, his tone carrying the weight of urgency now. \"We are arriving in the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds.\"","A heartbeat passed. Then another. Existence held its breath.","Only then did the white-gold barrier begin to fade. The light peeled away in layers, each one revealing more of the figures within until finally, Noah and Sigrid stood before him in perfect clarity.","Noah’s eyes met his with that same infuriating calm that had marked their every interaction, a slight smile playing at the corners of his mouth as if he found some private amusement in Altheon’s obvious displeasure.","His hand, and here Altheon’s luminous gaze sharpened to a razor’s edge, still held hers, their fingers intertwined with an intimacy that spoke of far more than casual conversation.","The taste and smell of her still lingered on Noah’s lips, Altheon realized with a surge of something dangerously close to protective fury.","HUUM!","The Young Miss of the Living Origins- his Young Miss, the treasure of all Living Origins, had been touched by this Fold Dweller!","When Altheon’s gaze shifted to Sigrid, however, his anger cooled into something far more measured. Her eyes held that familiar sharpness, that calculating intelligence that had marked her since the moment she awakened in the Living Origin Labyrinth.","She was not some lovesick child overcome by passion. Whatever had transpired within that barrier had been her choice, made with full knowledge of its implications.","\"Young Miss,\" Altheon said, his voice carefully neutral as his gaze pointedly fixed on their joined hands. \"Many will be observing you, even though I have informed only Royal Origin Calypso and Duke Gwendolyn of your survival. I will keep my promise and say nothing regarding your... relationship. But if you express it so openly, you will invite tremendous difficulty for yourselves.\"","The words fell between them like executioner’s blades. Sigrid’s eyes sharpened, her grip on Noah’s hand tightening as if he had just spoken of stripping away some precious privilege.","He did not know how enticing thr Aura of an Early Creature was!","Yet Noah, with that maddening serenity that seemed to be his trademark, simply released her hand.","The gesture was smooth, unhurried, as if the separation meant nothing to him. As if he understood the game they were all playing and found it amusing rather than threatening.","Altheon nodded curtly, then allowed his Living Origin Authority to burst around them in a cocoon of brilliant radiance.","The final transition was always the most jarring- the moment when one stepped from the relative safety of the channels into the true weavings of war.","\"Brace yourselves,\" he murmured, though his words were lost in the building crescendo of power.","BOOM!","Complex weavings of existence erupted around them like fireworks of pure existence, reality bending and folding as they were hurled across Existence.","The sensation was that of being turned inside out and reassembled in the space between heartbeats, every atom of their beings scattered and reformed according to the will of forces beyond comprehension.","And then, stillness!","They materialized atop a massive white triangular rune, its surface carved with intricate patterns that pulsed with the rhythm of some Existential heartbeat.","Smoke and mist swirled around their bodies, carrying with it the scent of glory and possibility.","Around them, other figures were taking shape- Master Neinoro with his pristine white robes and calculating smile, dozens of other Originus Venerant entities from Folds scattered across the breadth of existence!","But Noah’s attention was already elsewhere, his gaze lifting to take in the wonder that stretched before them with the slow glory of one witnessing new weavings of existence.","Something...gloriously new.","This...he loved!"]},{"number":3918,"title":"Chapter 3918: Chapter 3917: Battlefronts! III","paragraphs":["The sky above was a weaving of impossible beauty, stretching endlessly in all directions and shot through with rivers of sparkling white and gold light.","These celestial streams flowed like liquid starlight, weaving between and around nine massive continents that hung suspended in the void like the crown jewels of existence itself.","Each landmass was surrounded by dozens of Wheels of Existence, slowly rotating constructs of pure authority that pulsed with their own inner radiance.","Every continent thrummed with vibrant Living Existential Authority, each one a distinct note in a symphony of power that made the very air burn with potential.","Before each floating realm, massive banners unfurled, their fabric woven from light itself and bearing names that commanded reverence across all of existence!","ORIGIN. ELEMENTAL. LAW. EMOTIVE. CONCEPTUAL. SPIRITUAL. TEMPORAL. DIMENSIONAL. QUANTUM!","Nine sources of ultimate authority, representing every facet of existence save one- the Paradox that was deemed too vile and dangerous to be granted sanctuary in this place of ordered purpose.","Before each continent, floating in positions of glorious vigil, stood statues of breathtaking majesty.","These were embodiments of the Living Existences themselves, each one carved from materials that he wanted to turn into Loot!","The statue representing Origin stood with six wings of pure white marble spread in perfect symmetry, twelve halos of gold rotating slowly around a form so idealized it seemed to contain the template from which many points of beauty was measured.","Its face was serene, eyes closed as if in meditation, hands folded in a gesture that spoke of patience and boundless grace.","For Elemental, a massive spirit of living flame danced in perpetual motion, its form shifting between states of Matter, Dark Matter, and Anti-Matter with each passing moment.","The very air around it shimmered with heat, a warmth that spoke of comfort and destruction in equal measure!","The statue of Law stood rigid and perfect, its form carved from what appeared to be living silver that reflected truth itself. Sixteen wings of geometric precision extended from its shoulders in mathematically perfect angles, while eight halos of burnished platinum rotated with clockwork precision.","Its eyes were open, boring into the distance with a gaze that seemed to weigh the worth of every Existence within its sight.","Emotive swayed with graceful fluidity, its form seeming to shift between different emotional states with each breath.","Carved from what looked like crystallized tears, it bore fourteen wings that changed color with each movement- now deep blue with sorrow, now brilliant gold with joy, now crimson with passion.","The Conceptual statue defied easy description, its form seeming to exist in multiple dimensions simultaneously.","What appeared solid from one angle became translucent from another, as if the very idea of statue was being explored and redefined with each viewing.","Spiritual floated rather than stood, its form composed of what looked like condensed starlight wrapped in flowing robes of stellar dust. It looked tribal and holy at the same time!","Temporal existed in a constant state of flux, its form aging and growing young in an endless cycle that spoke to the nature of time itself. Sixteen wings stretched from its back, each feather showing a different moment in history, while eleven halos spun at different rates around its head- some so fast they appeared as solid rings, others so slow their movement was barely perceptible.","To look upon it was to feel the weight of every second that had ever passed and the promise of all those yet to come.","...!","Noah shook his head at these achievements of Living Existences as he continued looking!","Dimensional seemed to exist in multiple realities at once, its form flickering between different versions of itself as parallel possibilities played out in real time. Eighteen wings of crystalline structure extended from its back, each one existing in a slightly different dimension, while thirteen halos phased in and out of visibility as they moved between planes of existence.","The very space around it seemed to fold and unfold, creating pockets of reality that contained entire Wheels of Existence.","And finally, Quantum- a being that defied all attempts at singular description. Like some cosmic entity torn from the depths of Existence, its form was a constantly shifting mass of multicolored energy that pulsed with the rhythm of probability itself. Nine wings spread from its back, each one containing swirling Omniverses of potential futures, while fifteen halos of pure possibility spun around its head in patterns that hurt to contemplate directly.","To observe it was to feel the weight of infinite possibility pressing against the boundaries of one’s comprehension!","Noah’s gaze swept across these impossible wonders, his eyes coming down and taking in the dozens of other massive runic platforms that dotted the void around them similar to where he stood.","Each one pulsed with different Living Existential Authority- triangles, squares, hexagons, and shapes that existed beyond conventional geometry.","They were the arrival points for Fold Dwellers from across the breadth of existence, each one marked with the signature of its origin point.","And there, at the center of it all, surrounded by the nine massive continents and their statue guardians, rose a citadel that defied every attempt at adequate description.","\"Hmm...\"","Even he had to appreciate this grand construct as his eyes flashed with the authority of the Weaver of Existence, seeking its identity as it rose up before his eyes!","|Aeternitas Concordia- The Living Harmony.|","HUUM!","Aeternitas Concordia!","It stretched toward the skies! The city seemed to exist in perfect balance, its architecture a seamless blend of every Living Existence’s aesthetic sensibilities.","Nine distinct sections spiraled outward from a central core, each one bearing the hallmarks of its patron power while somehow maintaining perfect harmony with the whole.","The Origin quarter gleamed with pristine white marble veined with gold, its towers rising in elegant spires. Bridges of crystallized light connected floating platforms where beings of pure radiance moved with the unhurried grace of those who had transcended the need for haste.","Law’s domain stood in perfect geometric precision, every angle calculated to mathematical perfection, every surface reflecting immutable truths that governed existence itself. The buildings seemed to have been constructed and assembled according to principles that existed before the first stone was laid!","There were other unique areas but...","Each quarter told its own story, yet all harmonized into a symphony of purpose that culminated in the massive tower at the city’s heart.","This central tower rose impossibly high, its surface a constantly shifting amalgamation of every material, every concept, every possibility that the nine Living Existences represented.","At its peak, a light burned that was not quite light- more a crystallization of purity and complexity.","As Noah and all others marveled at this...","Altheon materialized before them in a burst of white and gold radiance, his luminous eyes sweeping over every Fold Dweller present with the weight of ancient authority.","When he spoke, his voice carried the resonance of a heavy decree.","\"Welcome to the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds. One of the largest Battlefront Folds in all Transcendent Folds.\"","He raised one hand, pointing toward the magnificent citadel that dominated the center of this impossible realm. The gesture was simple, yet it carried with it the weight of existence itself.","\"There stands Aeternitas Concordia- the Living Harmony. Within its halls, you will find your Sponsors and receive your designations. From that moment forward, you will be taken to your proper roles and granted contact with the Living Existences themselves before you begin making your way out of this place...and towards the Doorways of the Loom filled with Inevitabilities!\"","HUUM!","The implications hung in the air like incense, heavy with promise and threat in equal measure. This was the moment of transformation, the threshold between what they had been and what they might become.","\"Go,\" Altheon commanded, his voice carrying the finality of judgment itself. \"When you pass through the Living Coalition Gateway, your initial designation will be granted, and everything else will follow.\"","He looked calmly towards the Fold Dwellers with sharp eyes before he disappeared!","\"Good luck.\"","...!"]},{"number":3919,"title":"Chapter 3919: Chapter 3918: Aeternitas Concordia! I","paragraphs":["The absence left by Altheon’s departure was immediate and palpable.","Noah’s gaze swept across the impossible view of Aeternitas Concordia, his eyes catching every detail with the methodical precision of one who understood that knowledge was power, and power was survival.","From his vantage point atop the triangular runic platform, he could observe the intricate dance of arrival and ascension that played out across this realm of infinite possibilities.","Other platforms materialized in brilliant flashes of authority- some bearing entire contingents of Fold Dwellers who moved with the coordinated precision of military units, others delivering solitary figures whose very presence seemed to bend reality around them.","Each arrival told a story. The group that emerged from a hexagonal platform of crystallized time moved with the measured cadence of those who had learned to navigate temporal folds.","A lone figure stepping from a sphere of living shadow carried herself with the fluid grace of one who had danced with entropy and emerged unscathed. Another cluster, their forms wreathed in elemental fury, bore the scars of battles fought in the elemental folds.","All of them, every single one, had earned their passage here through trials within Doorways!","They were the survivors who had looked into the abyss of Imitation Mutated Inevitabilities and emerged victorious!","Soon, they would all ascend to Aeternitas Concordia and receive their designations- labels that would define their roles in the weavings of war that stretched toward the Loom itself.","Noah found himself genuinely curious about what designation awaited him and Sigrid.","Would their origins in the Nullvein Gravewake Folds mark them as outcasts from Paradoxical Folds, or would Altheon’s subtle machinations behind the scenes provide some measure of protection for the one he called Young Miss?","The thought of Altheon brought a different sort of contemplation to Noah’s mind, one that carried with it the cold clarity of long-term planning.","The Prime Living Origin had played his role admirably thus far, bowing to Sigrid’s authority while maintaining the careful facade of respectful distance for Noah.","But Noah had not forgotten that this same being had tried to kill his other self, Ozymandias, not so long ago!","Altheon had acted without knowledge of who he truly faced, yes, but ignorance was no absolution for attempted killed of he- Noah Osmont!","In his mind, the Prime Living Origin was already marked for death, a sentence waiting to be carried out when the moment was right.","For now, though, Altheon served a purpose.","He was a tool- useful, efficient, and perfectly positioned to provide protection for him and Sigrid while maintaining the illusion of propriety.","If he proved valuable enough in that role, Noah was not averse to postponing his execution indefinitely. Tools, after all, were only discarded when they broke or outlived their usefulness.","And if the day came when Altheon needed to be removed from the equation... well, Noah had Moiraine for precisely such situations.","The Living Golden Paradox had already proven her capability by eliminating one of her own kind with surgical precision. A Prime Living Origin would present no greater challenge to her particular skills!","The thought brought a slight hum to his lips, a sound of quiet satisfaction that was lost in the glorious symphony that surrounded them.","He was preparing to move toward Aeternitas Concordia, to take Sigrid and begin their ascent into whatever wonder awaited them, when a familiar voice cut through his contemplations.","\"Miss,\" came the oily tones of Master Neinoro, his approach heralded by the rustle of pristine white robes and the calculated smile that had become his trademark. \"You can always come with us to receive your designation under the Living Laws. We wouldn’t want you to experience any hardship if you travel with others and receive no designation or worse yet, be labeled as coming from Paradoxical Folds.\"","HUUM!","The audacity of this fucker was immense.","Here, in this moment of glorious significance, this insignificant creature had the unmitigated gall to waste their time with his machinations!","The ingratiating smile, the false concern, the barely veiled threat disguised as helpful advice- it was all so predictably pathetic.","Noah could see Sigrid’s annoyance building, her stellar eyes darkening.","She was preparing to deliver what would undoubtedly be a devastating verbal assault, but Noah had enough of this guy.","\"I’ve heard enough bullshit from you already,\" he said, his voice carrying the weight of absolute finality as he stepped forward.","His gaze locked onto Master Neinoro’s confident expression with the precision of a hunter sighting prey. \"So for now, stay here and do not move a step.\"","The words hung in the air for a heartbeat, deceptively simple in their construction.","Then Noah allowed a fragment of his true nature to surface- just enough to make his point with crystalline clarity!","HUUM!","The aura of an Early Creature could be expressed in many ways. When wielded with benevolent intent, it could fill even Living Existences with euphoria so profound they would weep tears of pure joy.","But when turned to darker purposes, when infused with the cold displeasure of a being whose very existence predated the concept of authority itself...","Master Neinoro froze mid-breath.","His confident smile cracked like glass subjected to impossible pressure, the carefully constructed mask of superiority dissolving to reveal the stark terror beneath.","His eyes- those calculating orbs that had gazed upon Masters of Existence with casual disdain- now trembled like leaves in an existential hurricane as they stared at Noah with the horrified recognition of prey that had finally glimpsed its predator!","And it would not even know what type of predator had locked onto it!","The effect was immediate and absolute. Every muscle in Neinoro’s body locked in place, held rigid by an instinctive understanding that to move, to speak, to even breathe too loudly might attract the attention of something that could erase him from existence with less effort than it took to blink.","Noah nodded at the sudden, blissful quiet that followed. Without another word, he beckoned to Sigrid, and together they began their ascent toward Aeternitas Concordia, leaving behind a cluster of shock and confusion!","Behind them, Neinoro’s entourage rushed to his aid, shaking him, calling his name, trying desperately to break whatever weaving had fallen over him.","Their voices carried notes of genuine alarm as they struggled to understand why their leader- a being who commanded respect across multiple Wheels and Fold Dwellings, was cowering before what appeared to be nothing more than a Paradoxical Fold Dweller!","Many of them cast wary glances toward Noah’s retreating figure, their earlier dismissiveness replaced by a caution born of witnessing power they couldn’t comprehend.","But Noah paid them no mind. His attention was already elsewhere, drawn by the complex weavings of auras that surrounded the dozens of Fold Dwellers making their way toward Aeternitas Concordia.","The stellar roadway that led to the Living Coalition Gateway was crowded with beings of incredible power and potential at the Originus Venerant stage.","Some as weak as those with 2 Million CQ and PQ, and other as strong as those exceeding 50 Million PQ and CQ!","It was there, among that clustering multitude, that Noah’s gaze fell upon something that made him stop and blink.","A figure that sparked recognition in the depths of his memory- someone who had no business being here, whose presence raised questions that demanded immediate answers.","How could there possibly be someone he recognized in this place?","Noah shook his head with calm incredulity as he studied the familiar silhouette.","There, moving with the measured pace of one accustomed to being the voice of reason in chaos, was a figure he remembered well from days ago.","Days, and yet it seemed like a while ago!","It was...","The Peacemaker!","Alexander Asmodeus, if his records served correctly!","The last time Noah had seen him, the man had been facing off against Bob with him in their native Wheel of Existence- a confrontation between powers that had seemed impossibly grand at the time but now felt quaint and weak in comparison to now.","For the Peacemaker to be here, in the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds, meant many possibilities and none.","Since he should have been a local of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds!","But Noah thought.","His mind worked with the rapid precision of a Weaver of Existence, sifting through memories and recent events with meticulous care.","Slowly. Rapidly.","And eventually...","The words of Royal Origin Calypso and Royal Law Tristesse echoed in his thoughts, fragments of conversation from the battle that had reshaped the very nature of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds.","And soon, his eyes brightened up at the only possible connection.","A treasure of the Living Laws that Altheon found within the Nullvein Gravewake Folds and sent back to them!","Could it be him? Could Alexander Asmodeus be the mysterious treasure that had drawn the attention of a Royal Living Law?","Noah’s eyes shone with the bright fire of curiosity as he adjusted his trajectory, floating toward the stellar roadway where the Peacemaker moved among the crowd of ascending Fold Dwellers.","Beside him, Sigrid noticed his change in direction but said nothing, content to follow his lead as they navigated the complex currents that surrounded them.","He was curious to know.","The threads of entanglements had brought them together once before, in simpler times.","Now, as they prepared to meet again in this place of glorious significance, Noah could only wonder what role the Peacemaker would play in the grand weaving that was slowly being woven around Fold Dwellers, Living Existences, and himself!","His curiosity, brilliant and irrepressible, demanded satisfaction. And he had never been one to deny himself!"]},{"number":3920,"title":"Chapter 3920: Chapter 3919: Aeternitas Concordia! II","paragraphs":["The stellar roadway stretched before them like a river of crystallized starlight, its surface humming with the accumulated weight of countless footsteps of those walking or floating across it.","Each step Noah took sent subtle ripples through the luminous pathway, his existence exceptionally bright compared to others as the Living Existential Authority nearby seemed to distinctly sense it!","If he ever truly released a smidge of his actual aura...","Around him, the roadway teemed with life- a procession of beings who had earned their place through trials like the Living Origin Labyrinth.","The air itself seemed to thrum with the collective might of hundreds of Originus Venerant entities, their bodies radiating the silent authority of Towers of Origin. Among them moved the occasional Primarch, their more modest power signatures making them look feeble and likely among the first to die if they ventured towards the unexplored doorways of the Loom!","But Noah’s attention remained laser-focused on one figure among the throngs, his ancient eyes tracking the Peacemaker’s measured progress through the crowd.","As he drew closer, details began to resolve themselves with crystalline clarity, each revelation adding another layer to the puzzle that Alexander Asmodeus had become.","The man was not moving alone- a fact that immediately elevated Noah’s assessment of the situation from curiosity to active interest.","’Ho?’ The thought formed in his mind with the weight of genuine surprise, and Noah felt his lips curve into a smile that held both amusement and sharp calculation.","To the left of the Peacemaker walked a figure that, at first glance, appeared to be nothing more than a laid-back teenager whose casual demeanor seemed almost comically out of place among those here.","The young man’s hands were tucked casually into his pockets, his posture suggesting the kind of easy confidence that came from knowing exactly how dangerous you were!","But Noah’s enhanced perception cut through the carefully constructed facade as beneath the mundane appearance, waves of power rippled outward, and it was not the structured authority of an Originus Venerant.","This bum was a Living Law!","Noah felt his smile deepen as information began to cascade across his vision.","The being’s name resolved itself in elegant script before his eyes as his distinction of the Weaver of Existence borrowed his heavy Complexity.","|Kaedric Voss, the Mediator of Absolute Arbitration.|","Beyond that single line of identification, everything else dissolved into question marks!","Noah’s eyes sharpened.","Why would a Living Law accompany the Peacemaker so openly? What could Alexander Asmodeus possibly possess that would warrant such protection?","Even Altheon, for all his devotion to Sigrid and her identity, maintained the pretense of distance, watching from the shadows while allowing her to move through Existence with apparent independence.","But Sigrid was no ordinary being- she was already a Living Origin who had previously shattered her Tower, but she could still survive encounters even with other Living Existences as her previous power was slowly regained!","And...all Living Existences- Foldless Ones at least, not counting those labeled as [Young] Paradoxes or [Young] Origins, existed beyond the Originus Venerant realm.","So what made the Peacemaker so valuable that he merited open protection from a normal Living Law?","Noah’s gaze further shifted to Alexander’s right, where another figure walked with the measured grace of one accustomed to command.","She was striking in the way that dangerous things often were- beautiful, but with a deadly glare.","Her gaze swept the roadway ahead with the systematic precision of royalty, every movement radiating the kind of rigid discipline that spoke to a lifetime spent in positions of absolute authority!","Noah’s weavings focused on her like a magnifying glass, and once again, information began to flow across his consciousness.","|Seraphina Valorheart, Law Maker.|","His mind supplied, the name carrying with it undertones of nobility.","Her complexity though...was nearly ninety million Source Units, placing her towards the very pinnacle of what an Originus Venerant could achieve!","Yet even she walked beside the Peacemaker as if they were...equals.","Her position, slightly ahead, taking point, scanning for threats- spoke to her role as the one currently leading.","Noah absorbed all of this information as he continued his approach, his smile widening with each new detail that fell into place.","The Peacemaker himself remained partially obscured, his true nature hidden behind veils that seemed particularly potent.","But even through those protections, he could glimpse enough to understand that Alexander had undergone changes every bit as dramatic as his own.","The man’s power signature registered at over two million in both Complexity and Purity Quotients- a staggering advancement that spoke to rapid progression.","Hid eyes pulsed sharply.","How had someone else achieved such rapid advancement within the confines of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds...or after they left not too long ago?","Noah knew that beings like Alexander and the Great Usurper carried their own heavy flows of Existence- and he had even eclipsed them both in their Wheel of Existence!","But at this moment, wasn’t the Peacemaker carrying perhaps a bit too much weight compared to before?","\"Hmm...\"","Noah went forward through the crowd. His movement was unhurried, casual, as if he were simply another traveler making his way toward the Living Coalition Gateway.","But every step was calculated, every gesture designed to close the distance between himself and the answers he wanted.","And so...","When Noah finally spoke, his voice carried across the crystalline air with the weight of inevitability itself, cutting through the ambient noise of hundreds of conversations.","\"Peacemaker.\"","HUUM!","The single word hung in the air like a bell that had been struck!","It was simultaneously a greeting, a recognition, and a challenge.","Alexander Asmodeus froze mid-step. For a heartbeat, genuine shock bloomed across his features!","It was the expression of a man who had thought himself safely anonymous, with nobody who could possibly know that distinction here!","But the shock lasted only a moment.","With little effort, he gathered his composure, turning slowly to face the source of Noah’s voice.","When his eyes met Noah’s across the crystalline expanse of the stellar roadway, they shone with their own inner light- the warm glow of genuine surprise mixed with something that might have been...relief?","\"You?\" he said.","He said!"]},{"number":3921,"title":"Chapter 3921: Chapter 3920: Aeternitas Concordia! III","paragraphs":["You.","A simple word, yet it carried within its single syllable the weight of recognition and surprise!","Noah and Alexander Asmodeus gazed at each other, their minds working in parallel streams of calculation and memory.","For beings of their caliber- an entire symphony of communication could unfold in the space between one heartbeat and the next.","For them, the mere span of an instant could potentially have hours of conversations!","Reality itself seemed to slow around them, creating a pocket of temporal stillness where minds could meet and speak without the cumbersome requirement of words.","Alexander was the first to break the silence, though silence was perhaps the wrong word for the complex web of mental communication that suddenly sprang into existence between them.","His consciousness reached, establishing a connection that nobody else could even listen to.","\"I could be surprised and shocked and ask how you are possibly here,\" he said, \"But anything is possible in the vastness of existence, so I won’t ask that. It is...good to see a familiar face from my home after all the craziness...\"","...!","There was something almost wistful in the way he said ’home,’ as if the concept had taken on new meaning since whatever occured recently!","\"But the only thing connecting us and what I could at most be curious to know is... did you manage to kill Bob? I was planning to send another body of mine back to the Nullvein Gravewake Folds to finish him off entirely for the sake of my peace, but I have been kept... busy.\"","The last word carried undertones of frustration mixed with resignation, as if Alexander had discovered that power came with its own particular set of chains.","Around them, Existence remained frozen in that crystalline moment between recognition and response.","Seraphina Valorheart’s hand had begun to move in that short instant. But the motion hung incomplete, suspended in the weavings of compressed time while their two minds communicated in an instant!","Noah’s mental manifestation- a perfect reflection of his physical form rendered in thought and intention- appeared above his head in this frozen space as he looked towards a similar mental manifestation of the Peacemaker while he replied.","\"Bob is actually a ridiculous cockroach to kill,\" he replied. \"He has survived an Inevitability, Living Paradoxes, Living Origins... he is living large with the luck of a Protagonist right now. But you don’t have to worry about him.\"","...!","The statement hung in the mental space between them, and Noah could see the exact moment when confusion flickered across Alexander’s consciousness.","The Peacemaker’s mental form leaned forward slightly, his expression shifting from casual inquiry to focused attention.","\"What do you mean? Inevitability? Why is he no longer a worry? He led to the destruction of our Wheel of Existence, and for the sake of our peace...\"","For the sake of Peace.","After he said this, his gaze flickered.","\"...ah, maybe it does not matter anymore.\"","WAA!","Toward the end, Alexander’s mental manifestation shook its head with the gesture of a man who had learned to pick his battles carefully.","\"You two at this moment may be evenly matched,\" Noah continued, his mental voice taking on the tone of someone delivering a diagnosis, \"but he is not looking for you or anyone else, just obsessively trying to survive. He won’t threaten your peace. But Little Bobby truly does not matter. As someone who had a heavy flow of existence from our Wheel of Existence, I am curious about you. I heard a treasure of the Living Laws was taken from the Nullvein Gravewake Folds, and now you appear here...\"","The effect of these words was immediate and profound. Alexander’s mental manifestation pulsed with surprise!","\"How could you have possibly found that out?\" Alexander asked, his mental voice carrying notes of alarm!","Noah’s mental manifestation smiled as he shook his head with gentle amusement, his gaze shifting to encompass the frozen figures of Kaedric Voss and Seraphina Valorheart that seemed to be moving in slow motion.","\"Are you in any trouble?\" he asked.","\"I see a Living Law beside you, and that girl whose gaze has become extremely cold the moment I called out to you. As a courtesy from someone stemming from the same folds as me, I could lend a helping hand if you need help.\"","The offer hung between them!","Alexander’s mental form went still as surprise flashed through his consciousness.","The Peacemaker’s gaze shifted to the frozen figure of Seraphina, and Noah caught the flash of complicated emotions that flickered across his features.","When Alexander looked back, his expression had grown stern, as if he was wrestling with decisions that carried consequences far beyond everything imaginable!","\"My Enneagram does not deem any malice from you and even shines differently compared to all others I’ve come across, and I trust it... even though it is the cause for my current situation...\"","He paused, seeming to weigh his words with care.","\"But it is okay,\" he finally continued, shaking his head with resignation. \"I will figure it out myself. The Living Laws...claim something at the very heart of me was or is a part of a Relic tracing back to the earliest Living Laws. And this woman beside me, Seraphina...supposedly carries the other part. They say the two of us have to join and move as one in the future, but... my heart is bound to another. Even for the sake of Peace...we will have to see.\"","HUUM!","Noah blinked, his mental manifestation processing this revelation with the fascination of someone discovering an entirely new species of problem.","When he spoke again, his mental voice carried tones of genuine curiosity mixed with barely suppressed amusement.","\"Your biggest problem was that you have to be with a second woman?\"","...!","Noah found such a problem uniquely amusing!","The Peacemaker nodded as he looked above at the distant continents and statues.","\"I know. A seemingly...stupid or useless notion to some.\"","It was simultaneously admirable and limiting, the kind of romantic idealism that spoke to nobility of spirit while potentially creating insurmountable obstacles to practical solutions.","Noah’s mental manifestation shook its head with the exasperation of facing someone who had a stubborn adherence to impractical principles.","He approached Alexander’s consciousness as his mental hand came to rest on the shoulder of the Peacemaker’s projected form.","\"Brother, I do not know much about you...\" he said with earnest sincerity, \"But you need to expand your horizons. Our hearts are big enough to love many. You would be surprised if I told you the number in my harem. If this is the biggest problem you are facing right now, I will leave you to it with that advice!\"","...!"]},{"number":3922,"title":"Chapter 3922: Chapter 3921: Aeternitas Concordia! IV","paragraphs":["Noah stepped back from the space of shared consciousness with the easy grace of one accustomed to such things.","The quickest to react was, unsurprisingly, the hidden Living Law!","Kaedric Voss moved with fluid precision, stepping forward in a motion that seemed casual but carried within it the coiled readiness of a predator suddenly alert to potential threat.","His youthful features- still maintaining that carefully constructed facade of harmlessness- sharpened as his eyes swept over Noah and Sigrid with the systematic thoroughness of a Living Law.","Simultaneously, Seraphina Valorheart’s instincts kicked into full awareness.","Her hands found Alexander’s shoulders and pulled him back slightly while her body shifted to place itself squarely between him and them!","When she spoke, her voice carried the crisp authority of someone accustomed to being obeyed without question, but it was extremely cautious!","\"Who are you?\"","...!","Noah’s response was casual, his smile deepening with what could only be described as genuine amusement.","\"I am actually someone who is rooting for you, Seraphina,\" he said, his voice carrying encouragement!","Without waiting for a response, Noah turned and began walking away, his hand finding Sigrid’s with the natural ease.","Their departure was unhurried, almost leisurely, as if they were simply continuing a pleasant stroll.","Behind them, Seraphina stood frozen in shocked confusion.","She turned to Alexander with the sharp movement of someone seeking answers.","\"Who are they?\" she whispered,\"You did not mention others knowing your identity...\"","Alexander’s response was measured, delivered with the careful neutrality. His hands rose to gently remove hers from his shoulders, the gesture simultaneously intimate and distancing as he sought to reestablish the boundaries that were there.","\"They are just some friends, nothing to worry about.\"","WAA!","Seraphina blinked, and a moment later, she tilted her head as she replied truthfully.","\"You... do not have any friends.\"","...!","\"...\" Alexander could not entirely deny this!","He offered no reply, choosing instead to release a sigh as he simply began moving forward.","Seraphina turned to Kaedric Voss.","The Living Law’s response was delivered with the lazy drawl of someone whose attention was already moving on to other concerns.","\"Yeah, yeah, I’ll keep an eye on them,\" he said, his tone carrying casual dismissiveness.","\"They are just mere Fold Dwellers.\"","...!","In the distance, Noah’s smile widened as the words reached his hearing. His gaze shifted forward, focusing on the magnificent structure that awaited them just ahead.","The Living Coalition Gateway rose before them like a monument, its archway wrought from golden brilliance that seemed to pulse with its own inner rhythm.","The light that emanated from its surface was welcoming, carrying within it the promise of recognition and purpose that had drawn countless beings across impossible distances to stand before its threshold.","Each individual or group that passed through the gateway was subjected to a gentle but thorough analysis, their very essence examined and catalogued.","Within seconds of crossing that threshold, the results of that examination would manifest in the form of a rune- one of nine possible designations that would determine not just their immediate fate but their role in the Battlefront Folds reaching towards the Loom!","Noah watched with fascination as an entire group moved through the gateway’s embrace, their forms bathed in the analytical light before being marked with the multicolored brilliance that designated them as products of the Quantum Folds.","The newly designated Fold Dwellers passed through with expressions of hopeful anticipation, their steps carrying them toward what Noah now recognized as the next stage of their journey.","Beyond the gateway lay a white circular clearing that served as a gathering point for those who had received their designations.","His distinction as thr Weaver of Existence flashed as the identity of this space bloomed!","The Circle of Convergence!","The Circle of Convergence was surrounded by nine smaller statues, each one a scaled-down version of the magnificent monuments that crowned the floating continents above.","These statues served as more than mere decoration; they were conduits through which the Living Existences could observe and evaluate the assembled Fold Dwellers, their stone eyes occasionally flashing with the light of attention as Sponsors made their selections known.","Thousands of beings filled the space around the circle- Fold Dwellers of every conceivable description mixed freely with Living Existences who floated grandly or sat on thrones surrounded by others of the same Living Existential Authority.","The atmosphere thrummed with anticipation and barely suppressed anxiety as the resources and safety of the future of many hung in the balance of decisions made by beings whose motivations were unknown!","The group designated as Quantum Fold Dwellers took their positions within the circle, their nervous energy palpable as they waited for the judgment that would determine their immediate future.","Seconds stretched as they stood beneath the watchful gaze of the statues.","But the Quantum statue remained dark, its stone eyes reflecting nothing but indifference toward those who bore its mark.","Their confidence began to waver, each passing second adding weight to the possibility that they would be left unsponsored, unclaimed, and with no patron!","Then, just as despair began to creep into their expressions, salvation arrived in the form of a voice that echoed across the Circle of Convergence with the authority of a glorious proclamation.","|The Prime Living Temporal Porana has chosen to sponsor the Quantum Fold Dwellers on the square!|","HUUM!","Relief flooded their faces, their expressions transforming from anxiety to joy in the space of a heartbeat. A multicolored coin materialized above them, its surface wreathed in Living Existential Authority that made the very air around it shimmer with possibility.","The group’s leader reached up to claim their prize with trembling hands, bowing deeply before leading his companions toward the far side of the square where a shimmering golden veil concealed what appeared to be a marketplace buzzing with activity.","Noah observed this ritual with fascination, his mind already beginning to piece together the underlying mechanisms that governed Aeternitas Concordia!","The next arrival before the Gateway was a solitary figure whose very presence seemed to dim the light around him.","Dark-haired and cold-eyed, he carried himself with the casual confidence of someone who had long since stopped caring about the opinions of others.","The sword at his side rested in a sheath shaped like the hand of a clock, its presence adding an ominous note to an already intimidating figure.","Noahs weavings already observed this being and saw over ninety-five million in both Complexity and Purity Quotients, placing him among the most formidable Fold Dwellers!","When the gateway’s light touched him, a purple rune flashed above his head, marking him as a product of the Temporal Folds.","The dark-haired swordsman stepped into the Circle of Convergence with the unhurried pace.","He had barely taken his position when the air around him began to vibrate with competing authorities.","|The Prime Living Origin Dexus has chosen to sponsor the Temporal Fold Dweller on the square!|","|The Prime Living Elemental Firan has chosen to sponsor the Temporal Fold Dweller on the square!|","|The Prime Living Concept Adyan has chosen to sponsor the Temporal Fold Dweller on the square!|","The announcements came in rapid succession, each one accompanied by the materialization of a coin that pulsed with its own unique signature of power.","Noah watched with growing interest as multiple Living Existences competed for the privilege of claiming this particular prize, their offers manifesting as tangible tokens of their attention.","The swordsman surveyed his options, and after a moment’s consideration, he reached up to claim the largest bundle- five coins that shone with purple radiance, accepting the sponsorship of a Prime Living Temporal while politely declining the others through a series of respectful bows.","A few others past and underwent similar processes, until eventually...it came time for them!","As Noah and Sigrid finally approached the gateway itself, he found his mind buzzing with possibilities of how things would unfold.","\"Let’s see.\" he murmured to Sigrid as they stepped up to the threshold.","Sigrid nodded, her expression carefully composed as they stepped forward together into the golden embrace of the Living Coalition Gateway.","The analytical light washed over them with a gentle intensity.","Then came the booming sound, drawing every eye nearby to focus on their position with magnetic inevitability!","HUUM!","The gateway flashed, its golden brilliance suddenly overwhelmed by something far darker and more ominous.","Deep obsidian light erupted from its archway like blood seeping through bandages, painting everything within sight in shades of contradiction and impossibility.","Above Noah and Sigrid’s heads, defying every expectation and shattering the careful order that had governed this place, a rune materialized in letters that seemed to burn against the very fabric of existence itself.","PARADOX!","Oh!","Paradox!","The word hung in the air like a curse made manifest, its presence transforming the Circle of Convergence from a place of hopeful anticipation into something that resembled a courtroom where the verdict had already been delivered!"]},{"number":3923,"title":"Chapter 3923: Chapter 3922: Aeternitas Concordia! V","paragraphs":["Paradox!","The blazing obsidian marking hung over Noah and Sigrid like an inescapable brand, its dark radiance pulsing through the golden atmosphere of the Coalition Gateway!","The very air around them seemed to recoil from the designation, as if existence itself was reluctant to acknowledge what they had been marked.","The Living Coalition Gateway, that magnificent archway of golden brilliance that had processed many with seamless efficiency, now trembled with uncertainty.","Noah raised his head with a widening smile, his eyes shining with an intensity that seemed to pierce through the veils to see the machinations beneath.","So... this was how they wanted to play things, was it?","Were Altheon and those behind him truly unable to alter their designations to mark them as those of Origin Folds, or was this something else?","Beside him, Sigrid’s expression became cold. Her stellar eyes lifted toward the skies as if she could see through the layers of reality to where Altheon lurked.","The moment she did so...","For only their ears to perceive, Altheon’s grand voice resonated.","|I’m sorry, Young Miss. You two were supposed to be branded with the designation of Origin Folds... I will check to see what occurred. But all other plans should still be in place.|","...!","His voice carried a brooding quality, as if something had gone awry in calculations that should have been flawless.","But Noah shook his head at those words with the weary patience of someone who had long since learned that nothing in existence...ever occurred by mistake.","Nothing!","Every twist of fate, every apparent accident, was simply another thread in the weavings of magisterial existence!","Whatever had occurred was always what the plan had been. The question was simply whose plan it truly served.","Bathed in that accursed black light, Noah reached out to take Sigrid’s hand with deliberate casualness.","Together, they walked past the Coalition Gateway as the frozen masses of shocked observers finally found their voices, their paralysis breaking like ice.","\"This...\"","\"Paradoxical Fold Dwellers!\"","The shouts echoed through the Circle of Convergence like accusations hurled at criminals, each voice carrying its own particular blend of revulsion.","As if they were looking at pieces of shit!","In the surrounding spaces where Living Existences maintained their vigils, many pairs of ancient eyes turned to regard them with expressions that ranged from cold displeasure to barely contained hostility.","Why...would so many beings gaze upon Fold Dwellers simply because they originated from realms influenced by Living Paradoxes with such profound displeasure?","The answer lay in the fundamental weavings of guilt by association.","It was, quite simply, the sin of association!","Living Paradoxes were hated with an intensity that transcended anything and everything, their very existence seen as a cancer upon the ordered structure of Existence itself.","For surrounding the Loom...that ultimate prize that beckoned to every conscious being across the breadth of existence...lay countless horrifically powerful Inevitabilities that only came to be because of Paradox!","Everyone sought the Loom.","Everyone dreamed of reaching that quintessential destination where, it was believed, lay wonders and unfathomable answers relating to THE Creature...the being from whose essence all Living Existences had supposedly sprung from in the Stories of the Earliest Folds.","But over the eons, little progress had been made toward that ultimate goal, and the blame for that stagnation rested squarely... upon the shoulders of the Living Paradoxes.","Fucking! Living! Paradoxes!","Their very nature spawned Inevitabilities like infection breeding in an open wound, each paradox they embodied giving birth to new horrors that guarded the Loom.","The constant production of Inevitabilities had only increased exponentially over the years until entire regions of Doorways had become impassable death traps.","It was why Keys to new doorways empty of Inevitabilities were always sought by Living Existences!","So even Fold Dwellers who bore no personal responsibility for the actions of Living Paradoxes...found themselves branded with the same stigma.","This...was not the first time in history that beings associated with Paradox had appeared in Battlefront Folds!","In every previous instance, such unfortunate souls had been left to wither in isolation, unsponsored and unwanted, their potential wasted.","All eyes now focused upon Noah and Sigrid with pressure that might have reduced lesser beings, but Noah simply took Sigrid forward with the unhurried confidence!","They walked to the center of the square with measured steps, their bearing radiating a calm assurance that spoke to either supreme confidence or complete madness.","The Living Existences who floated grandly around the periphery of the square or sat upon thrones that pulsed with their own inner radiance regarded this display of composure with expressions of barely contained scorn.","How dare these marked creatures display such confidence in the face of existential disapproval?","A Living Spirit, her form wreathed in threads of ethereal energy that shifted between states of existence with each breath, finally gave voice to the collective sentiment.","\"Do not take up too much time here,\" she called out with the cold precision.","\"You will not be chosen anyway...!\"","Her words died in her throat as something impossible occurred before the astonished eyes of every witness.","An obsidian coin materialized above Noah and Sigrid’s heads, its surface shrouded in a veil of Living Existential Authority so dense it seemed to bend light around itself like a miniature black hole!","A coin of sponsorship.","The voice that announced this development carried across the Circle of Convergence with the weight of glory!","|An Unknown Living Existence has chosen to sponsor the Paradoxical Fold Dwellers on the square!|","BOOM!","The announcement struck the assembled crowd like a physical blow, sending ripples of shock and disbelief through beings who had thought themselves prepared for any eventuality!","Clamor erupted from both Living Existences and Fold Dwellers alike as they struggled to process what they had just witnessed.","Who would sponsor Paradoxical Fold Dwellers?!","Even more disturbing than the sponsorship itself was the designation of \"Unknown Living Existence.\"","What level of authority was required for a being to conceal their identity even here, in the heart of Aeternitas Concordia where all pretenses were supposed to be stripped away?!"]},{"number":3924,"title":"Chapter 3924: Chapter 3923: Aeternitas Concordia! VI","paragraphs":["As Fold Dwellers stood frozen in shocked confusion, the Living Existences present began to display expressions of grim understanding.","They knew with the certainty that came from eons of experience that for one to possess the ability to veil themselves in this space, they had to be either an Honored Living Existence or a Royal one.","The implications hung in the air as they understood somwthing was afoot!","Yet even as every eye fixed upon the floating obsidian coin with expressions ranging from awe to shock, Noah regarded the offering with casual indifference. When he finally spoke, his words carried the weight of glorious tyranny.","\"A single coin seems too little for us, isn’t it?\"","...!","HUUM!","The silence that followed was so complete it seemed to have physical weight, pressing down upon the assembled multitude like a blanket woven from pure shock.","What manner of madness possessed this Fold Dweller that he would negotiate with a being powerful enough to maintain anonymity in the heart of Concordia itself and even sponsor them?!","Yet not long after Noah had spoken, the obsidian coin flared with its veiled Living Existential Authority as if responding with displeasure, and four more coins descended from the void to hover beside the first.","...!","Five coins. Very few even knew what the coins stood for, but it was now more coins than any had received of those that passed recently!","But Noah simply shook his head with the patient expression of someone who had not yet heard an acceptable offer.","\"More.\"","...!","Others watched in maddening fascination as the coins multiplied again, reaching ten in total!","Were...Fold Dwellers from Paradoxical Folds actually worth more than many knew?!","The surrounding atmosphere began to shake with an imposing presence that had barely contained fury, a terrifying aura pressing down in warning.","Noah opened his mouth to speak again, but Sigrid’s hand found his shoulder with a gentle touch, her brows raised.","He sighed with a nod, reaching up to claim the coins as if he were being forced to accept an inadequate but marginally tolerable settlement!","\"Okay, okay.\"","It was a maddening scene to observe, a complete inversion of every expectation and protocol that governed this place!","Nobody knew what to comment or how to process what they had just witnessed.","But Noah paid no attention to the sea of shocked faces that surrounded them, simply nodding with a tyrannical smile to the Living Existences who ringed the periphery of the square as he and Sigrid made their way toward the exit.","They passed through the shimmering gateway that led deeper into Concordia, leaving behind a crowd trapped in collective stupor!","—","Past the gateway, Aeternitas Concordia revealed its true nature in all its magnificent complexity.","Here, boundless waves of concentrated Living Existential Authority bloomed like flowers crafted from pure possibility, their radiance mingling with the presence of tens of thousands of Fold Dwellers and several hundred Living Existences who moved through what resembled a rising marketplace of glorious proportions.","Large golden crystalline towers stretched toward the skies on all sides, their surfaces reflecting and amplifying the ambient authority until the very air seemed to shimmer with liquid Living Existential Authority.","Through the center of this magnificent chaos ran a single golden pathway that led upward toward the ascending heights of Concordia, known as the Aureum Ascendant!","Along the sides of this golden road, peak Originus Venerant Fold Dwellers had established elaborate stalls beneath massive banners that proclaimed their wares in terms designed to capture the attention of the desperate and ambitious.","\"Wonders from the Loom!\" declared one such banner, while others advertised \"Treasures of the Loom\" or \"Items from the Loom\" in letters that pulsed with their own inner radiance.","It was, Noah realized with growing interest, an elaborate fiction.","Ridiculous lies!","None of these traders had actually reached the Loom itself.","Instead, they dealt in treasures recovered from the Doorways that led toward the Loom, artifacts torn from the grasp of Inevitabilities or discovered in the unique locations of thr Doorways.","The variety was staggering.","Scattered among these wonders, treasures that had been wrested from Inevitabilities themselves stood!","Most of these treasures could aid progression across the Originus Venerant stage, while others promised the potential to transcend that realm entirely for those who had already reached the theoretical maximum of 99,999,999 in both Complexity and Purity.","Within the pristine towers that rose above the marketplace, even more remarkable treasures could be found- even the rites that could grant the opportunity to undergo the fundamental transformation required to become a Living Existence.","It was this possibility and many more that drove many Fold Dwellers to brave the dangerous Doorways of the Loom, following the instructions of their sponsors while simultaneously seeking to accumulate enough contribution and funds to...trade for their own transcendence!","This was the culture of the Empyrean Bazaar, as this section of Concordia was called!","A place where desperation and ambition mingled, where the impossible became merely expensive and dreams could be purchased by those willing and rich enough to pay the ultimate price.","Deeper into the city’s heart, areas reserved primarily for Living Existences housed golden tower-like buildings that contained even more fantastical treasures like artifacts that could propel one’s complexity toward the exalted status of Prime Living Existence or even hint at the terrifying grandeur required to achieve Honored status.","Everything could be found here, for those with the means to acquire it.","Everything!","Noah gazed upon all these wonders with eyes that shone like stars.","In his mind, a single word echoed with the resonance of infinite possibility...Loot!!!","Glorious, profound loot spread out before him like a banquet prepared specifically for his consumption.","Yet as soon as they stepped into the Empyrean Bazaar, many nearby observers turned to regard them with expressions that ranged from dismissive scorn to open hostility.","The rune of Paradox that still blazed above their heads marked them.","To barter and trade in this location required wonders of one’s own to offer in exchange.","What possible treasures could Fold Dwellers from Paradoxical Folds possibly possess that would be worth the attention of Originus Venerant entities or Living Existences?","The question hung in the air around them, and Noah merely shook his head calmly as nothing he saw nearby had even made his heart pulse.","So he simply ignored the gazes and looked further in!","But as he did so...","BZZT!","He felt his eyes buzzing.","A unique influence buzzed within his existence as he found it tracing back to...his glorious Early Veiled Shore!"]},{"number":3925,"title":"Chapter 3925: Chapter 3924: Heidrun’s Delicacy! I","paragraphs":["In the influence of the Living Laws, where the Nullvein Gravewake Folds had been transported, reality had taken on a different quality entirely.","The silver threads of Living Law Authority wove through every particle of existence here, bringing Regulation to chaos and structure to the infinite paradoxical possibilities that had once defined these Folds.","In a hidden corner of these Folds","At the very heart of the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence lay his sanctuary. The Early Veiled Shore pulsed with an authority so ancient and fundamental that even Aeternitas Concordia could not compare!","During the time one body had been occupied with the Battlefront Folds, another body had been making tremendous progress with his weavings of his existence!","The Sacred Mead of Existence, that golden elixir he had milked from Heidrun’s divine form, had proven to be a catalyst beyond all wildest calculations.","Every process had become easier, faster, more efficient under its influence.","In what felt like mere moments but had actually encompassed what should have been hours of concentrated effort, he had successfully forged eighteen additional Towers of Osmont within his being!","Each tower was a monument to his growing understanding of what it meant to be an Early Creature, their crystalline towers standing proud.","Each completion had granted him an additional five hundred thousand Source Units in both Complexity and Purity Quotients- a progression that would have taken other beings thousands or millions of years to achieve.","The forging of these towers, combined with the countless other processes that the Sacred Mead had accelerated, had elevated his rapidly rising quotient values beyond thirty-five million.","35 Million+!","A staggering advancement from the lower twenties where he had begun this phase of his development!","On the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore, Noah’s primary body sat in meditative stillness, his form radiating the kind of peaceful authority that spoke to harmony with forces.","The glass bucket containing the Sacred Mead of Existence rested beside him, its contents shimmering with an inner light that made the surrounding air thick with Living Existential Authority.","Around him, arranged in careful positions that suggested both reverence and practical necessity, sat many figures.","Moiraine’s golden radiance had taken on new depths, her form pulsing with the kind of complexity infinitely close to what he felt from Honored Living Paradoxes!","His mother, Amelia, maintained her characteristic serenity even as waves of transformative energy washed through her existence, reshaping her very foundations with each breath.","Others had found their own ways to adapt to the terrifying concentration of authority that permeated the Shore.","The Emperor Penguin and Kazuhiko had long since succumbed to the overwhelming nature of the Mead’s influence, their forms unconscious like a few others, but slowly growing more complex as their bodies worked to acclimate to an environment that challenged everything!","The entire scene carried an air of primitive majesty that seemed to mock all things he had seen in Transcendent Folds so far.","Here were no grand citadels- just them, vibrant sands, trees, and shores of crystalline waters that reflected glory.","Simple.","Quintessential!","It truly felt like a home designed for Early Creatures, a place where the fundamental forces of existence could be shaped freely!","It was in this moment of perfect equilibrium that...","HUUM!","|10,000,000 Complexity and Purity Quotients have been utilized as the forging of the Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Tyranny has been successful.|","|10,000,000 Complexity and Purity Quotients have been utilized as the forging of the Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Loot has been successful.|","|10,000,000 Complexity and Purity Quotients have been utilized as the forging of the Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Ascendancy has been successful.|","BOOM!","Glory...was whst bloomed!","Noah’s seated form, his upper body still bare to the gentle radiance, began to shine with an archaic brilliance.","For a moment, his existence flickered as thirty million points of Complexity and Purity were consumed in the forging process!","The numbers representing his accumulated power dropped with the finality of death, the sacrifice necessary to birth something far greater than the sum of its components.","But even as those numbers decreased, three magnificent glyphs bloomed across the expanse of his back like constellations!","They etched themselves into his very essence with lines of power that pulsed with their own inner glory, each one a masterwork of runic wonder.","The Sacred Mead of Existence had made the entire process rapid and elegant, its influence smoothing the transitions and accelerating the integration until what should have been an agonizing transformation became something approaching ecstasy.","Noah had chosen Tyranny, Loot, and Ascendancy to be the first concepts elevated to Refined status!","He did this through careful calculation of what would serve him best in the trials to come.","Though his numerical complexity values had decreased, his entire existence felt immeasurably more powerful, as if he had traded crude quantity for refined quality.","Even an enemy at 50,000,000 CQ and PQ...would be smashed around endlessly by him at this moment. Or at least, this wss what he felt!","New information began to cascade across his consciousness at this time.","|Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Tyranny|:: Tyranny is not mere domination or the crude exercise of power over the weak. True Tyranny is the absolute authority to impose one’s will upon existence itself, to declare that reality shall bend because you have decided it must. It is the glorious right of those who have transcended the limitations that bind lesser beings, the sacred privilege of reshaping Existence according to personal vision rather than collective consensus. For you, to be Tyrannical is to be authentically yourself. The truest expression of your fundamental nature. From this moment forward, any time you acts in accordance with your Tyrannical essence, the processing and advancement rate of your existence will accelerate exponentially. The Glyph requires no energy to activate and can distort the very fabric of existence around enemies, imposing the weight of absolute authority upon their weavings until they submit or shatter beneath its inexorable pressure...","...!","An unfathomably heavy Glyph showed itself!"]},{"number":3926,"title":"Chapter 3926: Chapter 3925: Heidrun’s Delicacy! II","paragraphs":["After Tyranny, Noah’s mind buzzed as the latter two also expressed themselves!","|Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Loot|:: Loot is the reality that all things of value belong ultimately to those with the power and wisdom to claim them. It is not theft. It is the natural order of existence asserting itself, the strong taking from the weak, the clever outsmarting the foolish, the deserving inheriting what was always rightfully theirs. This Glyph grants the ability to silently siphon Authority from any enemy or neutral being within one mile of proximity, their power forming infinity bubbles of pure Loot that flow toward you without their knowledge. This passive acquisition continuously increases your Complexity and Purity Quotients while simultaneously weakening potential threats through gradual drain of their essential authorities. The usage of this Glyph actively can also multiply and enhance almost all loot by an unknown factor.","|Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Ascendancy|:: Ascendancy is the inevitable rise of superiority over mediocrity, the natural elevation of the exceptional above the mundane. It encompasses not merely personal advancement but the capacity to lift others through association with greatness. This Glyph instantly makes all transformations five times faster and more effective, but Ascendancy is not a solitary concept. You may select certain beings as Ascendant, sharing growth that your own existence cannot process quickly enough and distributing it to chosen recipients. When an Ascendant reaches the ten million marker in both Complexity and Purity, you receives one Ascendancy Mark of Existence that can instantly establish any Tower of Osmont without the usual requirements. Additional marks are earned at fifty million and one hundred million quotient levels. Ten Marks allow any Tower of Osmont to achieve its second stage instantaneously...","...!","Noah’s eyes shone with the brilliance of tyranny being born as he absorbed the implications of what he had gained.","There were so many applications he wanted to explore, so many experiments he wished to conduct with these new capabilities!","The Glyph of Loot alone promised to transform every encounter into an opportunity for advancement, while Tyranny would allow him to impose his will upon reality with a directness that transcended normal limitations.","But before he could fully immerse himself in exploration of these new weavings, he felt a gentle nudge that drew his attention to more immediate concerns.","Heidrun had left the warm glow of the Sacred Totem of Infinity where she usually basked in arrogant contentment.","The magnificent goat now approached him with eyes that shone with an intensity he had not seen before, her entire bearing suggesting excitement that transcended her usual imperial disdain!","As she drew near, another prompt materialized before his consciousness with the urgent glow of something requiring immediate attention.","|Heidrun senses through the weavings of your existence in Aeternitas Concordia something that is her delicacy!|","WAA!","\"Ho?\"","What could possibly capture the attention of a being as magnificently arrogant as Heidrun?","The goat’s standards were so elevated that she had dismissed even Moiraine’s worthiness with casual disdain, yet something in the distant reaches of Aeternitas Concordia had stirred her interest to the point of action.","|Heidrun wishes to borrow your eyes and show you the delicacy she can smell through your other body.|","...!","This terrifying Eminent Early Living Land Lifeform was truly unfathomable- how could a goat possibly borrow the eyes of someone as complex as himself?","More bewildering still, how could she detect the scent of her preferred delicacy through another body of his existence separated by impossible distances?!","He turned his gaze toward her lustrous form, taking in the way her pure white fur seemed to capture and reflect the golden light of the Early Veiled Shore until she appeared to be carved from compressed starlight itself.","Her crystalline eyes held wonder as he saw something that might have been anticipation within them!","After a moment’s consideration, he nodded.","In the next instant, Heidrun’s eyes blazed with an inner radiance that seemed to pierce through the very fabric of Existence itself!","---","In Aeternitas Concordia, Noah’s head snapped to attention with the sharp precision of someone suddenly influenced by an external will.","The movement was so abrupt, so completely divorced from his previous casual observations, that Sigrid’s eyebrows rose in silent question.","But before she could voice her concern, Noah had already begun moving with purpose, his steps carrying him forward along the golden pathway.","He could feel Heidrun’s influence like a gentle pressure behind his eyes, her consciousness offering subtle suggestions that guided his gaze here and there across the magnificent expanse of the Empyrean Bazaar.","The sensation was neither invasive nor uncomfortable- more like having a knowledgeable guide whisper directions in his ear while navigating unfamiliar territory.","Taking Sigrid’s hand with unconscious familiarity, Noah allowed himself to be led past the throngs of Fold Dwellers who continued to regard them with expressions ranging from curious disdain to outright hostility.","Their Paradoxical markings made them pariahs in this place, unwanted reminders of the chaos that had made progress toward the Loom so achingly difficult!","The guidance eventually brought them before one of the first massive tower-like buildings that rose from the golden pathway.","But it was not the tower itself that captured their attention- it was the incandescent garden that sprawled across its ground floor, a carefully cultivated paradise that seemed to pulse with its own unfathomable glory!","At the center of this botanical wonder sat a brilliant golden throne, its surface wrought from what appeared to be crystallized sunlight.","Upon this seat of power lounged a Living Elemental whose very presence transformed the air around him.","Golden flames danced around his form like loyal pets, their movements synchronized to the rhythm of his breathing as he reclined with the casual arrogance of absolute authority!","But it was the grass beneath the throne that made Noah’s enhanced perception suddenly flare with interest.","The vegetation was unlike anything he had encountered, with each blade shimmering with a gold-green radiance!","|Auric Vitae Grass|:: This extraordinary vegetation originated from an unknown Doorway Domain leading toward the Loom, discovered growing in the corpse of an Inevitability that had been infused with pure life force before its destruction. The grass carries within its cellular structure the concentrated essence of thr inevitability existence itself, refined into something approaching perfection. Proximity to Auric Vitae Grass accelerates all forms of progression by a factor of three, while consumption grants the extraordinary ability to exchange portions of one’s Complexity Quotient for Purity Quotient and vice versa- a transformation that allows for unprecedented flexibility in personal development...","WAA!","Noah’s eyes shone!"]},{"number":3927,"title":"Chapter 3927: Chapter 3926: Quintessential Tyranny! I","paragraphs":["As Noah looked at the green gold grass, he felt Heidrun’s weavings buzzing as if she was excitedly saying this was what she wanted!","While he and Sigrid stood before the grand building, their interest apparently obvious enough to draw attention, the Living Elemental seated upon his golden throne slowly opened eyes that burned with fires of dignity and glory.","His gaze swept over them with the casual dismissiveness of someone examining insects that had wandered too close to a flame, and when those burning orbs settled upon their Paradoxical markings, his expression shifted to one of open scorn.","With a wave of his hand that carried all the authority of displeasure, he addressed them in tones that dripped with condescension.","\"Go looking around elsewhere,\" the Living Elemental, whose name Noah saw above his head in letters of flame that read |Pyrion Aureus, the Goldfire King|, declared with the casual cruelty of someone stepping on ants.","\"The grasses aren’t for sale, nor could something like you even afford them.\"","BOOM!","In the surrounding areas, Fold Dwellers further back began to smile amongst themselves with the mean-spirited joy of witnesses to public humiliation, while Living Existences occupying more prominent positions in the grander golden buildings barely spared a glance before returning to their business, as if Noah and Sigrid truly did not understand that they would receive nothing here.","But Noah did not move a single step backward!","Instead, his response was to calmly and coldly step forward, his gaze sweeping over the Auric Vitae Grass with the systematic thoroughness of someone conducting an appraisal.","He approached the golden barrier that protected the building until he stood directly before it, his presence suddenly radiating something that made the very air around him shimmer with dangerous potential.","His eyes flashed with the terrifying authority of the Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Tyranny, and in that moment, Noah felt the overwhelming desire to put its immensity to practical use.","He wanted to be authentically himself- to embrace the Tyrannical nature that was his truest expression!","Purple light flickered in the depths of his pupils as he prepared to speak.","\"Not for sale?\" His voice carried across the garden with the weight of quintessential judgment, each word precisely articulated and heavy with implications!","\"In existence, everything is for sale. Authority is for sale. Fold Dwellers are for sale. Treasures are for sale. And even Living Existences like you... are for sale.\"","...!","HUUM!","\"That is a truth very few understand in existence,\" Noah continued, his voice gaining momentum like an avalanche gathering speed!","\"Even someone like you may have forgotten it in your comfortable delusions of permanence and untouchability. But the fundamental weavings of existence remain unchanged by your ignorance. Everything is for sale. The only question, the only question that has ever mattered...is a matter of price.\"","...!","Oh!","Those words!","Those eyes!","That expression!","Oh!","His words drew the attention of everyone within hearing range, their imposing nature cutting through casual conversations and dealings to focus every available mind on this unprecedented display of audacity!","Fold Dwellers stared in incredulous fascination while Living Existences began to regard him with expressions that ranged from shocked disbelief to growing fury!","Before his eyes, visible only to him, a prompt flashed with the brilliant urgency of glory.","|The processing and advancement rate of your existence has accelerated exponentially for the next hour due to your unbound Tyranny!|","WAA!","Even as the notification faded, Noah could feel his other body on the Early Veiled Shore explode upward in power, his very essence responding to the authentic expression of his fundamental nature.","But his focus remained fixed upon the shocked Living Elemental before him, whose golden flames had begun to flicker with the irregular rhythm of barely contained rage.","Pyrion Aureus was momentarily frozen by the tyrannical words, his mind struggling to process the reality of a mere Fold Dweller speaking to him in such terms!","But as the implications settled into his consciousness as his expression began to change, golden flames threatening to spill from his form and burn everything within reach!","Yet even at such a critical juncture, Noah continued his tyrannical words, his gaze fixed upon the Living Elemental with the steady intensity of someone delivering a lesson to a particularly slow student.","\"Are you a petulant child?\" he asked with calm precision.","...!","\"Because petulant children throw fits when they don’t get their way. Petulant children need to be coaxed to calm down, their tantrums managed through careful application of patience and understanding.\"","His head tilted slightly, as if genuinely puzzled by what he was observing.","\"But you claim to be a Living Existence, a being who has transcended the limitations that bind lesser entities to cycles of death and instability. So why, exactly, are you acting like a fucking child?\"","...!","BOOM!","The profanity struck the air like a physical slap, its casual delivery somehow more shocking than if he had screamed it!","\"You displayed your wares here to sell them,\" Noah continued with relentless logic, his voice never rising above conversational levels.","\"And it should not matter who stands before you with the desire to purchase them. At this moment, this is not a Fold Dweller trying to buy something from a Living Existence. This is a customer attempting to conduct business with a seller. That is the extent of our relationship here, nothing more, nothing less.\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"Since I am the customer in this transaction, you should be groveling at my feet, trying desperately to convince me to buy your products rather than taking my business elsewhere. So tell me, O seller, why are you not already down on your knees where you belong?\"","BOOM!","|Unbound Tyranny!|","|Glorious Tyranny!|","|The processing and advancement rate of your existence has accelerated even further exponentially for the next half a day due to your unbound Tyranny!|","The words struck Pyrion Aureus like existential blows, each syllable igniting the golden fires that surrounded him until they erupted in all directions!","The Living Elemental rose from his throne with movements that spoke to barely contained violence, his presence suddenly radiating pressure that made the very foundations of Existence tremble in response.","Distant Fold Dwellers began dropping to their knees as waves of power far exceeding the Originus Venerant realm washed over them, their bodies unable to withstand the concentrated fury of a being whose nature was forged from elemental wonder.","Other Living Existences in the surrounding golden buildings turned to stare at Noah with expressions of deadly intent, their collective attention focusing on him like predators!","A mere Fold Dweller, a creature marked with the stigma of Paradox, actually thought he could speak to them in such terms?!","The audacity was beyond comprehension, crossing lines that had been established again and again!","Like a slumbering titan finally roused to wakefulness, Pyrion Aureus began walking away from his throne, each step sending tremors through the golden barrier that protected his domain.","His eyes blazed with livid fury as they fixed upon Noah, who stood with his hands clasped behind his back in a pose of casual confidence, regarding the approaching Living Existence as if he were utterly certain that nothing harmful would befall him!"]},{"number":3928,"title":"Chapter 3928: Chapter 3927: Quintessential Tyranny! II","paragraphs":["Even as the terrifying Living Elemental advanced upon him, Noah maintained his position with the unshakeable composure of someone who understood the true mechanics of power.","His stance remained relaxed, hands still clasped behind his back in a pose of casual confidence that bordered on the absurd given the circumstances.","And why would he be bothered by this display of theatrical intimidation?","The weavings of his situation were crystal clear to anyone with the wisdom to perceive them.","Beside him stood Sigrid, a Living Origin and the Living Order herself in the process of reclaiming her power!","She was someone who could stand against any normal Living Existence with confidence. She was bound to him, which meant that when calculating his True Power, her capabilities were included in the equation!","The concept of raw and true power remained even now!","But even if she were somehow removed from consideration, there was still Altheon observing from his elevated position.","The Prime Living Origin might harbor his own agenda, but his protection of Sigrid extended to anyone she chose to stand beside.","And beyond even Altheon’s watchful presence, there was the mysterious sponsor who had provided those obsidian coins- a being powerful enough to maintain anonymity even in the heart of Aeternitas Concordia itself!","The simple truth was that nobody here possessed the authority to touch them without facing consequencesal!","His true power had never been as high as it was right now when everything was put in the picture.","And Noah knew it with the certainty!","So rather than displaying any concern for the approaching elemental fury, he gave Pyrion Aureus only the most casual of glances before allowing a yawn to escape his lips.","He looked around the immediate area with the bored expression of someone whose attention had already moved on to more interesting subjects.","But his apparent disinterest masked a focused observation of something far more significant than the posturing of an offended Living Existence!","Deep within his being, the Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Loot had begun its silent work, its authority radiating outward in waves that touched every conscious entity within its considerable range.","His eyes took on a golden glow as he observed something that only he could perceive, countless infinity symbols connected by streams of pure authority, flowing toward him like tributaries feeding a mighty river!","And he...was a quintessential river!","The Glyph operated with surgical precision, drawing minute portions of authority, including Living Existential Authority from every being within a mile of his location.","It made no distinction between power levels or affiliations.","Fold Dwellers and Living Existences alike found themselves unknowingly contributing to his advancement, their energy siphoned away in quantities so small they might not notice the loss for days or even weeks.","What seemed unfathomably minuscule to beings of their stature was, when accumulated across hundreds of sources, a treasure trove of advancement!","The golden bubbles that flowed toward him carried more than mere power too!","|+3 Weavings of Living Origin Authority.|","|+2 Weavings of Living Spiritual Authority.|","|+1 Scattered Knowledge of the Daeni Passageway towards the Loom.|","|+1 Scattered Records of types of Inevitabilities.|","|+1 Scattered Records of Aeternitas Concordia.|","The diversity was staggering!","Pure authority flowed alongside crystallized memories.","Noah smiled and nodded with genuine appreciation for the elegant efficiency of his new capability, though to external observers, his reaction appeared to be nothing more than the casual acknowledgment of something amusing in his surroundings.","But to those watching this confrontation unfold, his behavior painted an entirely different picture.","Here was a Fold Dweller so daring, or so foolish, that he refused to even look at the Living Elemental approaching him with murderous intent.","Instead, he glanced around the area and smiled as if he found something entertaining in his impending destruction.","Further back along the golden pathway, Seraphina Valorheart’s expression had grown heavy with concern as she leaned closer to Alexander Asmodeus and whispered, \"That is a friend of yours? He seems about to die...\"","She had witnessed enough battles to recognize when someone was about to be obliterated by forces beyond their ability to resist. Yet the Peacemaker simply shook his head with calm certainty.","He might not know much about Noah’s capabilities or resources, but there was something in those nonchalant eyes that reminded him of his own expression when he was utterly confident in his plans.","The look of someone who had calculated all variables and found them acceptable.","\"He won’t die,\" Alexander replied calmly.","Kaedric Voss raised an eyebrow at this declaration, his youthful features showing skeptical amusement at what appeared to be either supreme confidence or complete delusion.","Pyrion Aureus had finally closed the distance, his golden flames crackling with Living Elemental Authority as he loomed over Noah’s still form!","\"You seem to be good at talking, so the first thing I will do... is take away your ability to talk.\"","...!","The threat was booming! But as Pyrion began to gather his terrifying pressure and Living Existential Authority, all of the surrounding existence itself seemed to take notice of the impending violation!","HUUM!","An undoubtedly complex pressure descended upon the surroundings like the weight of judgment itself, accompanied by a voice that carried the chilling brilliance of absolute authority.","\"Fighting is discouraged in Aeternitas Concordia.\"","...!","The words struck the assembled crowd with heavy force, causing the eyes of Living Existences throughout the area to flash with recognition and shock!","That voice, that unmistakable weaving of power refined...belonged to an Honored Living Existence!","An Honored Living Existence moved to protect him!","Noah continued to act as if he had heard nothing at all, his attention apparently focused on observations that existed entirely outside the current confrontation.","But his apparent indifference only deepened the mystery that surrounded him as...was an Honored Living Existence actually protecting this Fold Dweller from Paradoxical Folds?","In the distance, both Kaedric Voss and Seraphina Valorheart turned to Alexander Asmodeus with expressions that had shifted from casual concern to profound seriousness.","When Seraphina spoke again, her tone carried entirely different implications.","\"That...IS a friend of yours???\"","Alexander watched the unfolding scene with calculating eyes but chose not to reply immediately!"]},{"number":3929,"title":"Chapter 3929: Chapter 3928: Quintessential Tyranny! III","paragraphs":["Alexander wanted to see exactly what else would occur in this increasingly complex situation as he watched like many others!","Pyrion found himself trapped in a position that would have been comical if it weren’t so politically dangerous.","His expression reflected the weight of someone who had been publicly disrespected but now faced the impossible choice between maintaining his dignity and avoiding offense to a being who was an Honored Living Existence!","The realization that this seemingly insignificant Fold Dweller possessed backing at the Honored level transformed the entire dynamic of their interaction.","His golden flames dimmed slightly as calculation overtook personal fury, though the transition was clearly painful for someone accustomed to absolute dominance within his sphere of influence!","Noah allowed the silence to stretch just long enough to be uncomfortable before speaking with the same nonchalant tone.","\"I am here to buy. Will you sell?\"","WAA!","The Living Elemental controlled himself at these words as he breathed out.","\"What...can you even offer?\" Pyrion demanded, his voice carrying undertones of frustration and barely contained resentment. \"I will only sell for something of equivalent value that I need, or something even more valuable!\"","Things had to be of equal value!","What could a Fold Dweller from Paradoxical Folds possibly possess that would interest a Living Existence who had access to treasures from across the Doorways of the Loom?","For this challenge, Noah smiled with the expression of someone who had been waiting for exactly this moment to arrive.","He closed his eyes briefly, his consciousness reaching across impossible distances to touch upon the wonders that were there on the Early Veiled Shore.","The place that contained treasures that would drive Living Existences to madness with desire!","He didn’t even consider the Sacred Mead of Existence- that golden elixir was something that even Early Creatures sought after!","If he brought even a single droplet to this place, even if he diluted that droplet into Early Sacred Waters by a factor of a million, it would cause a commotion that would draw attention from across the breadth of existence itself.","Instead, his awareness settled upon the multiple Glass Woks that dotted the Shore, each one filled with Early Sacred Waters and the cut up bodies of Early Living Marine Lifeforms.","The sight of them brought a smile to his lips as he selected one particular Wok with cut up meat whose contents would serve his current purposes perfectly, and it disappeared from thr Early Veiled Shore.","The musings of Early Creatures were very obscure. He knew something as minor as a bit of Sacred Water and pieces of an Early Living Marine Lifeform...would be a good tool to utilize without causing issues!","Entanglements, yes.","He was also doing it with a certain goal in mind as it related to...Sigrid!","When Noah opened his eyes again in Aeternitas Concordia, he waved his hand casually.","A Glass Wok materialized in the space before him, its crystalline surface reflecting the golden light of the surrounding towers while steam rose from its contents in spirals that seemed to carry their own inner radiance.","Within the vessel, surrounded by Early Sacred Waters that pulsed with their own gentle luminescence, rested the prepared form of an Early Living Marine Lifeform whose complexity had been refined through utter wonder!","The moment the Wok appeared, the very weavings of Existence nearby trembled in response to its presence!","BOOM!","The concentration of Living Existential Authority in the immediate area exploded upward in a cascade of transformation that left everyone present struggling to process what they were experiencing.","A glorious scent spread outward from the Wok like ripples across the surface of still water, carrying with it essences so profound and complex!","Every being within range, Fold Dwellers and Living Existences alike felt their very existence buzzing with want and need. A need bordering on obsession.","The effect was immediate and universal. Fold Dwellers who had been gazing with fascination suddenly found themselves rising to their feet in shock, their attention captured by sensations that promised transformation beyond their wildest dreams!","Living Existences who had been observing the confrontation with detached amusement now stared at the Wok with expressions of barely contained hunger and shock!","But none were affected more profoundly than Pyrion Aureus himself.","None.","The Living Elemental’s body began to shake as his existence buzzed in ways it never had before.","Every fiber of his being was screaming that he needed to acquire the contents of that vessel, that his very survival depended upon gaining access to whatever miraculous substance it contained.","\"I’ll take it! I WILL take it! We trade!\"","His eyes blazed with astonishment and greed as the words erupted from him without conscious thought.","The careful negotiations and measured considerations were swept aside by the overwhelming urgency of his need!","But Noah simply shook his head with the patient expression of someone who had expected exactly this reaction.","As he began to speak, a simple bowl materialized in his hands, a vessel that seemed almost mundane compared to the glorious Wok that had captured everyone’s attention.","\"Impatience,\" Noah began, \"is the mark of those who have never learned to distinguish between want and need, between desire and necessity. You look at what I offer and immediately demand everything, like an Inevitability... tasting the sweetness of a Living Existence for the first time.\"","His tone carried the kind of gentle condescension that made his words cut truly fucking deep!","\"With such qualities, this hasty grabbing, this inability to consider consequences or negotiate with wisdom...you may find yourself dying much sooner than later. Existence...has little patience for those who cannot exercise patience themselves.\"","BOOM!","Noah lifted the bowl slightly, its simple ceramic surface somehow managing to capture and hold the attention of everyone present.","\"No, my offer to you is not this entire Wok. You... will get a single bowl. You will accept this bowl. You will thank me for getting this mere bowl.\"","...!","The pronouncement struck the assembled crowd like a shattering Wheel of Existence!","A single bowl!","The magnitude of what he was withholding, the vast majority of whatever miraculous substance the Wok contained, sent tremors of shock through beings who had never been denied anything they truly desired.","Pyrion Aureus trembled at such words, his golden flames flickering with the irregular rhythm of desperation.","Yet even as his rational mind recoiled from the words, his existence continued to buzz with tremendous yearning for even that reduced portion!","He wasn’t alone in his reaction.","Multiple Living Existences had begun moving forward through the surrounding areas, their eyes shining with the same desperate hunger as they calculated whether they might be able to negotiate for their own portions of this incredible treasure!","Noah observed Pyrion’s hesitation with calm patience, then allowed disappointment to color his expression as if watching a promising creature fail an important test.","\"Have you learned nothing from me, Little Elemental?\" he asked with reproach. \"You hesitate? Even now, faced with an opportunity that may never come again, you allow doubt to cloud your judgment?\"","The purple light of Tyranny began to shine around Noah with tremendous intensity as he his musings of Tyranny reached unprecedented levels!"]},{"number":3930,"title":"Chapter 3930: Chapter 3929: Quintessential Tyranny! IV","paragraphs":["What was more tyrannical than lecturing and talking down on someone so much more powerful?!","\"Let me educate you about hesitation,\" he continued, \"Hesitation is the luxury of those who believe time is infinite, who assume that opportunities will always present themselves again if the first offer is declined. But existence operates according to different weavings entirely.\"","WAA!","His gaze swept across the assembled crowd, ensuring that his words reached every being within hearing range.","\"Those who delay, who spend precious moments wondering if they should act rather than acting decisively, invariably find themselves losing the most critical opportunities of their existence. Existence does not wait for the hesitant. It rewards the bold, elevates the decisive, and abandons the cautious to watch from the sidelines as others claim the prizes they were too afraid to reach for!\"","HUUM!","The weight of his words seemed to press down upon everyone present like a physical force!","Even though he was a mere Fold Dweller.","But he seemed to hold such an astonishing imposing demeanor!","\"So choose now, Little Elemental. Will you be the one who acted when action was required, or will you be the one who hesitated until the moment passed and left you with nothing but regrets?\"","The confrontation had transformed from a simple trade negotiation into something approaching a lesson!","At such a critical juncture, the Living Elemental gritted his teeth and forced the words out with conflicting emotions","\"Deal! I will take the bowl!\"","The declaration echoed across the golden pathway, marking the moment when desire finally overcame caution and need triumphed over pride!","Noah smiled and nodded with the satisfaction of someone whose careful planning had achieved exactly the desired result.","With a casual wave of his hand, he caused the Wok with its shocking scent that had drawn Living Existences from across the immediate area, to disappear back into his weavings, leaving only the simple bowl floating in the space between them.","\"Pack it up for me,\" Noah said with the tone of someone concluding a routine transaction.","Pyrion Aureus nodded without taking his eyes off the bowl, his attention so completely focused on his prize that he seemed unaware of anything else in his immediate environment.","With a snap of his fingers, he caused the entire garden to collapse inward upon itself, the Auric Vitae Grass and all the carefully cultivated beauty of his display being drawn into a treasure that looked like an Elemental Wheel of Existence that he produced!","The compressed treasure had the gardeb in it and pulsed with its own inner light as he presented it to Noah, who allowed the bowl to float across the intervening space toward its new owner with unhurried grace.","The moment the trade was completed, Pyrion’s expression transformed into one of pure joy.","He instantly wrapped the bowl in high concentrations of Living Elemental Authority, creating layers of defense that would have been sufficient to protect one’s progeny!","His eyes darted around the immediate area as if he were worried that other Living Existences might attempt to take his prize by force.","\"Do you need anything else?\" he asked with the eager tone of someone hoping to extend a profitable relationship. \"I have many things found across the Doorways of the Loom on the higher floors...\"","He pointed to the building behind him as he spoke.","His words sparked immediate reactions from the Living Existences who had been drawn to the area by the scent of Noah’s offering!","They began gathering around Noah and Sigrid with eyes that shone brightly, several of them speaking up simultaneously to declare their own readiness to trade for bowls of his miraculous treasure!","\"I have a Panacea of Inevitability that will instantly grant a hundredth of the whole complexity of the Originus Venerant stage...\"","\"I have 3 Sparks of Everything!\"","...!","Their voices rose grandly!","And yet...","Noah looked at all of them with the calm, cold assessment of someone who had just witnessed the fundamental hypocrisy of power reveal itself freely.","When he spoke again, his voice continued its weavings of Tyranny!","\"How could I possibly trade with such esteemed Living Existences when I am merely a Fold Dweller from Paradoxical Folds?\" he asked, his tone dripping with mock confusion as he gestured toward the obsidian marking that still blazed above his head.","\"You all still see that, right? Nothing has fundamentally changed about my nature or my origins, correct? I am still the same being who was deemed unworthy of your attention mere moments ago, still a sinner by association, still marked with the stigma of Paradox, still everything you found so distasteful when I first appeared before you.\"","His voice began to rise, taking on the booming quality of someone delivering judgment from a position of absolute authority!","\"Or does having something you desperately want suddenly make all of that acceptable now? Does possession of treasure somehow cleanse the stain of my origins, transform my fundamental nature, erase the sin of association that made me so unpalatable to your great weavings of Existence?!\"","BOOM!","\"Tell me, O enlightened ones! which is the truth? Was I unworthy when I possessed nothing you wanted, or am I suddenly acceptable now that I have something you need? Because the weavings of my existence haven’t changed. The only variable that has shifted...is your perception of what I might offer you in return for your temporary tolerance.\"","...!","|Quintessential Tyranny!|","|The advancement of your existence has accelerated even further exponentially and quintessentially for the next day due to your unbound Tyranny!|","His weavings of existence buzzed with interminable glory.","In the Early Veiled Shore, his main body became surrounded by seas of multicolored brilliance as a Tower of Osmont was completed right away, and another Tower started forming right after!","In the small region of Concordia where he and Sigrid stood...the golden pathway fell silent!","Utterly and completely silent as no Living Existence said anything, but their eyes burned with a chilling light as nobody...liked to be talked down and pointed of their faults like this, or have their hypocrisy laid out so blatantly.","So now, as dozens of Living Existences surrounded Noah and Sigrid, how would this situation resolve itself?!"]},{"number":3931,"title":"Chapter 3931: Chapter 3930: A Duke! I","paragraphs":["The atmosphere was heavy!","The assembled Living Existences were staring at Noah with expressions that ranged from controlled anger to calculated assessment.","His words were tyrannically heavy, forcing beings of immense power to confront their own hypocrisy!","Then, cutting through the charged atmosphere with absolute finality, came a single word.","\"Disperse.\"","HUUM!","The command resonated with such overwhelming authority that Existence itself seemed to shiver in response.","Many present instantly recognized the voice as belonging to a terrifyingly powerful Honored Living Existence, but this time the source felt different.","It was not descending from the skies, but immediate and present.","Something already here.","They had never even sensed his approach!","Through the rapidly forming corridor of retreating figures strode a being whose very presence altered the fundamental nature of the space around him.","He was fully adorned in sleek silver armor that appeared forged from liquid starlight, each plate perfectly fitted while emanating waves of Living Spiritual Authority so pure they made the surrounding air shimmer.","His head was entirely covered by the same silver plating, shaped into the magnificent form of a bull. The craftsmanship was unfathomable, each curve designed to project both terrifying majesty and absolute regality!","In his hands, he carried a radiant cylindrical staff that pulsed with inner light.","All Living Existences quieted and began dispersing according to his command, their eyes reflecting shock.","A few among them clearly understood that an Honored Living Existence of this particular bearing was someone connected to...Royalty.","To the Royal Living Existences!","The armored figure’s attention settled upon Noah and Sigrid, but there was something peculiar in his focus.","He seemed to be entirely ignoring Sigrid, his gaze fixed upon Noah as if he were the only being present who truly mattered.","|Your Sponsor has requested you.|","The words entered their ears freely.","The bull-headed figure then tapped his cylindrical staff against the golden pathway, and existential light erupted around them.","The illumination wrapped around Noah first, then seemed to remember Sigrid as an afterthought, the light extending to encompass her a full second later.","As if she had been forgotten. As if she were nobody compared to Noah.","They disappeared in a flash of radiance that left afterimages burned into the observers!","The surroundings fell into immediate hush as the assembled Living Existences looked at each other. Silent communications began flowing between them.","Who the hell was that Fold Dweller?","\"Find out everything you can on him,\" came whispered instructions. \"Keep tabs, but be careful since a Royal Living Existence is involved! Likely a Royal Living Spirit!\"","The commands spread through the crowd, each being understanding they had witnessed something that would require careful investigation!","The image of...Noah Osmont was burned into their minds like a brand!","---","Across Concordia.","In its deeper corners!","There was...a tower among many towers.","The crystalline golden tower that served as their destination appeared unremarkable from the outside, its architecture following the same principles that governed most structures throughout Aeternitas Concordia.","But appearances were often carefully constructed lies in a place where power danced in patterns too complex for most minds to follow.","WAP!","Noah and Sigrid materialized within a white-gold hall whose dimensions seemed to shift.","The space was simultaneously vast and intimate, its walls stretching toward infinity while maintaining the atmosphere of a private meeting chamber.","The Honored Living Existence who had transported them stood beside them before beginning to walk toward the far end of the hall. There, rising from the polished floor, stood white steps that led to an elevated throne.","But it was not the throne itself that captured Noah’s attention.","It was the figures arrayed along those steps like living statues carved from pure authority.","Three Honored Living Existences stood on one side, while two occupied the other, their combined presence creating an atmosphere so dense with power that lesser beings would have been crushed by proximity alone.","Their escort moved to join the group of two, bringing the total to six Honored Living Existences serving as guards for whoever commanded such protection!","The woman seated upon the white throne was glorious to look at. Her stellar dark hair seemed to contain Wheels within its depths.","Her tan skin radiated warmth that spoke to utmost glory!","Terrifying waves of Living Origin Authority cascaded over her skin like liquid starlight. But it was her eyes that truly captured Noah’s attention.","They resembled dozens of stacked Wheels of Existence, each one rotating at different speeds and containing the compressed essence of entire weavings of existence!","The moment Noah and Sigrid materialized within the hall, those impossible eyes focused upon them.","WAP!","In an instant that defied perception, the woman flashed from her throne to appear directly in front of Sigrid, her movement so swift that even Noah’s enhanced senses could barely track it.","But he did nothing as he did not sense danger!","She embraced Sigrid with desperate intensity, her arms wrapping around the younger woman with tenderness that seemed...off given the overwhelming power she radiated.","\"I am sorry.\" she whispered with heavy emotion, her voice carrying genuine regret. \"I did not agree with them... I am sorry!\"","The repetition carried the weight of someone who had been carrying guilt for a long time.","This terrifying entity was actually apologizing!","But Sigrid’s response was delivered with coldness.","\"Let go of me, O Duke Gwendolyn,\" she said with calm authority.","BOOM!","Duke.","A fucking Duke!","One of the eighty-one Dukes of the Living Origins. Beings whose collective authority governed the fate of countless Wheels of Existence!","Noah’s eyes flashed with sharp focus. When he attempted to examine Duke Gwendolyn, he encountered barriers his abilities could not penetrate. Her weavings of existence operated on an entirely different level, so refined that even identifying her name was beyond his current capabilities!","He could observe the work of his Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Loot as it drew bubbles of authority from the six Honored Living Existences, their power flowing toward him in quantities too small for them to notice. But from Duke Gwendolyn herself... nothing.","Her existence was closed off entirely, protected by barriers even a Refined Glyph could not penetrate.","Hearing Sigrid’s cold words, Duke Gwendolyn sighed.","She released her embrace slowly, holding Sigrid’s shoulders for a moment before letting go and reappearing upon her throne with the same impossible swiftness.","Her expression returned to one of utmost regality and calmness, the brief crack in her composure sealed behind layers of authority as she focused her attention upon Noah.","She looked him up and down as if gauging everything about his nature, his potential, his worthiness to stand in her presence. Her eyes became somber at a certain point in this examination, as if she had discovered something that both impressed and concerned her.","When she spoke, her voice carried the weight of absolute authority.","\"You are an unexpected variable in all of this, and you seem to be unfathomably profound. I was planning many things to not draw attention to the Young Miss here, and there was an intervention early at the Coalition Gateway that I am still tracking down the one responsible, but you... were exceptional enough just now that nobody even gazed at the terrifying wonder standing beside you. For that, you have my thanks.\"","...!","A Duke of the Living Origins had just expressed gratitude to a Fold Dweller from Paradoxical Folds.","But Noah’s gaze remained calm even while facing such a terrifying being!","He simply nodded as he spoke out.","\"Of course. After being labeled Paradoxical and drawing attention, I knew I needed to do something to take the eyes off Sigrid. So I put the spotlight on myself. Used a treasure even Living Existences cannot ignore. Everyone will focus on me and ignore the prize right beside me. I saw all of this and planned for it so...no need for the thanks!\"","WAA!","Duke Gwendolyn’s eyes widened slightly, her gaze focusing on Noah with renewed intensity as she began to understand that this unexpected variable might be even more significant than she had initially calculated!"]},{"number":3932,"title":"Chapter 3932: Chapter 3931: A Duke! II","paragraphs":["After Noah’s tyrannical words, the Duke and six Honored Living Existences regarded him with expressions of cold calmness.","The temperature in the hall seemed to drop several degrees as their collective displeasure made itself known through subtle fluctuations in the ambient authority that permeated every surface.","In the silence that followed, Sigrid began to stroll around the hall with unhurried grace, her movements carrying the fluid confidence of someone entirely comfortable here!","She approached an arched window veiled with Living Existential Authority, its surface opaque to outside observers while remaining transparent to those within.","Through this one-way barrier, she could gaze out into the sprawling magnificence of Concordia without revealing her presence to the countless beings moving through its golden pathways.","\"I do not plan to return to the Heart of Origin,\" she said with the calm finality of THE Living Order making a decision that had been long considered and carefully weighed.","The Heart of Origin.","It was a place countless weavings of distance away from their current location, nestled in the very heart of the Transcendent Origin Folds where the Royal Living Origins and the Council of Living Origin resided in splendor that defied description.","It was the seat of power for their entire hierarchy, the place where decisions were made that affected the fate of infinite weavings of Existence!","\"I will not return,\" Sigrid continued, her voice steady as it could be.","\"For the sake of fully returning to my power, and to awaken Order, I plan to go across the Battlefront Folds and experience Existence truly. I feel that if I go through existence and impose my own Order in regions of chaos, this will act like infusing blood into my Heart of Order.\"","Duke Gwendolyn’s expression shifted to one of deep concern as she processed these words.","\"I heard Altheon mention this, but... it is dangerous. You are far too important. A single Inevitability that you cannot see, sense, or handle, and you would be dead.\"","The weight of that possibility buzzed.","The silence that followed was heavy!","It was at this moment that Noah moved with deliberate purpose, walking across the hall to stand behind Sigrid before openly taking her hand in his.","The action was simple, intimate, and absolutely tyrannical in its implications!","The Honored Living Existences immediately buzzed with Authority, their forms radiating displeasure at this display of familiarity between him and their precious Young Miss!","Duke Gwendolyn’s frown deepened as she observed the casual way Noah intertwined his fingers with Sigrid’s.","Noah held Sigrid’s hand as if examining its structure, his attention apparently focused on some detail that only he could perceive. When he looked up to meet Duke Gwendolyn’s gaze, his expression carried the calm gaze of a ruler that had gone through too much!","\"Do you know...what Order is?\" he asked with the calm precision.","Duke Gwendolyn’s response was delivered with stern authority. \"Why don’t you enlighten us? I saw that you were a talker out there...\"","Noah smiled and continued.","\"Order is not the mere absence of chaos, nor is it the rigid imposition of arbitrary rules upon unwilling subjects. True Order is the recognition of natural hierarchies, the understanding that some beings are meant to lead while others are destined to follow. It is the wisdom to see patterns where others see randomness, to find purpose where others find confusion.\"","His gaze swept across the assembled Honored Living Existences before returning to fix upon Duke Gwendolyn with laser intensity.","\"If Order herself, THE Living Order, tells you that she must go through existence and experience the chaos so that she can correct it, then perhaps the appropriate response is not to question her judgment but to listen with the respect her nature demands. She understands her own requirements better than any external observer ever could.\"","HUUM!","The weight of his words seemed to press down upon everyone present!","Heavy silence followed his declaration, broken only when Duke Gwendolyn looked between him and Sigrid with an expression that had grown profoundly serious.","\"Things are not how they used to be,\" she said, her voice taking on the sharp cadence of someone delivering unwelcome news.","\"As always, everything revolves around Paradox. Paradox has always been powerful, dangerous, unpredictable. But...just minutes ago, Paradoxical Weavings did something that reminded us all exactly why the Loom is surrounded by Paradoxical energies in the first place.\"","Noah and Sigrid listened with calm attention as Duke Gwendolyn continued.","\"There is a place where Living Existences jointly exist within the Transcendent Temporal Folds. A unique environment called the Nexus of Living Convergence, surrounded by such chaotic temporal weavings that a cloud of Paradox appeared around it naturally over the years. In that place, for eons, the Coalition of Living Existences kept a treasure. A Treasure that had made us unfathomably powerful over the years, with only thr topmost Living Existences knowing about it!\"","Her expression grew darker as she recalled the details.","\"Because that place was fortified like the environment around the Loom, it had Paradoxical weavings all around it. Any Paradoxes who approached would cause Inevitabilities to bloom, preventing any progress. They would be attacked by the very forces their nature summoned, and we would detect their presence and join the assault. For countless eons, Paradoxes never made their way inside. Until... today!\"","BOOM!","Noah listened with careful attention, though internally he felt a flash of surprise. Had the Paradoxes moved so quickly?","Duke Gwendolyn’s voice took on the urgent quality of majesty.","\"In the last hour, that place was compromised. Suddenly, groups of Honored Living Paradoxes and Royal Living Paradoxes led a surprise assault where somehow, they passed through the weavings of Paradox without producing Inevitabilities!\"","WAA!","The implications of that statement were staggering.","\"It took all Honored Living Existences and Royal Living Existences there by surprise, and there were heavy casualties. The Living Paradoxes took away the treasure that had been protected there for eons. A treasure that has made the Coalition of Living Existences... unfathomably powerful!\"","Noah remained silent as Sigrid asked with cold curiosity. \"What was the treasure being protected there?\"","Duke Gwendolyn’s reply came with the weight of existential significance: \"A Corpse!\"","...!","Noah’s eyes became sharp as understanding began to dawn. Internally, he felt a deeper chill as he asked: \"Whose corpse exactly?\"","Duke Gwendolyn looked at him silently for a long moment, as if weighing whether to reveal information that could reshape their understanding of everything.","Finally, she spoke with quiet finality.","\"The Corpse...of an Early Creature!\"","...!","Oh.","Oh!!!"]},{"number":3933,"title":"Chapter 3933: Chapter 3932: Power Must Be Taken! I","paragraphs":["The corpse of an Early Creature!","The moment Duke Gwendolyn spoke those words, the entire hall became eerily silent.","A hush that seemed to press against the walls themselves, as if Existence was holding its breath!","Everybody was silent. The six Honored Living Existences stood like statues carved from concentrated authority, their forms radiating power yet somehow diminished by the weight of this revelation.","Noah’s eyes buzzed with countless complex thoughts as he turned to look through the veiled window toward distant Concordia.","The golden pathways and crystalline towers that had seemed so magnificent moments before now appeared somehow smaller, less significant when measured against the implications of what he had just learned.","His mind moved with the swift precision of someone calculating variables that could determine the fate of existence itself.","The Living Existences had possessed the corpse of an Early Creature for eons. The questions that arose from this single fact alone were heavy.","How had this corpse come to be? How had one of his kind died? Where were the others who should have prevented such a catastrophe?","The very concept of a dead Early Creature seemed to violate fundamental laws of Existence, yet here was evidence that such an impossibility had occurred.","At this moment of profound contemplation, Duke Gwendolyn continued.","\"Altheon brought us news of the Paradox that does not produce Inevitabilities. The one known as both Ozymandias...and Aetheron. We did not get the chance to eliminate this being, and now it is as if his capability has been shared with the most powerful Living Paradoxes.\"","Her voice carried the weight of someone delivering a report from a war that was already lost.","\"In the lead of the assault was someone we know to be called Honored Diviticus in our records, with her authority parting the dense concentrations of Paradox and preventing the rise of Inevitabilities while she allowed other Paradoxes to move freely through what should have been an impenetrable barrier!\"","...!","\"The already powerful Living Paradoxes had gained something fundamental when they acquired the essence of the Paradox that produces no Inevitabilities, and now with the Corpse of an Early Creature, who knows what tremendous power they will wield. The Coalition of Living Existences needs THE Living Order as another weapon in their arsenal.\"","HUUM!","Another weapon in their arsenal.","The Living Existences still possessed depths of power that remained hidden, terrifying mysteries that could reshape the fundamental nature of existence.","Yet even they recognized the need for more weapons in the coming conflict.","Another silence descended upon the hall, heavier than the first. Noah continued to reflect on how events had unfolded, the chain of causation that led back to his own actions with uncomfortable clarity.","Because of him, a terrifying progression of events seemed to be accelerating beyond anyone’s ability to control.","He had inadvertently given Living Paradoxes wings. They were now more powerful than ever, all because Diviticus had obtained half a drop of his blood. Half a drop!","The magnitude of power contained in such an infinitesimal amount of his essence was both humbling and terrifying.","As he contemplated this reality, his mind flashed with possibilities. If half a drop could grant such capabilities to Living Existences...","\"...\"","Duke Gwendolyn observed Sigrid’s expression during this revelation, noting that the same determination remained etched across her features even after learning of these catastrophic developments.","She sighed with the weight of someone accepting an inevitable outcome.","\"If you still wish to proceed even after knowing all this, then your safety will be paramount. If you are to move anywhere, you must have protection. Someone moving closely with you who will also help you understand how to best weave your existence. If you wish to move freely, I will have to form a team around you to traverse the Doorways of the Loom!\"","Toward this proposal, Sigrid showed no complaints, her expression remaining steady as she contemplated the paths that lay ahead.","Noah continued gazing toward Aeternitas Concordia, his mind thinking about countless variables while simultaneously paying attention to developments of his existence elsewhere entirely!","---","Elsewhere.","On his Early Veiled Shore, Noah’s main body experienced utmost peace and serenity while sitting upon the golden sands that pulsed with glory.","The crystalline waters lapped gently at the shoreline, their sound creating a symphony of tranquility that spoke to forces older than Living Existences.","But this peace was interrupted by a goat currently staring at him from mere inches away from his face.","\"...\"","A goat!","Heidrun’s vibrant eyes blazed with fiery intensity as she gazed at him with an expression that clearly communicated her expectations.","She was looking as if saying.... Well? Where are the delicacies?!","Noah smiled at her imperious demand and produced the miniature wheel that the Living Elemental had used to compress his entire garden.","The compressed space contained the precious cargo that had drawn Heidrun’s attention across impossible distances.","The Auric Vitae Grass!","Noah gazed at the green-gold vegetation within the miniature construct, each blade shimmering with potential.","\"I could give this to you to eat all of it, and then we would have to go through the trouble of looking for something like it again. How about planting it here so that you can have an endless supply?\"","WAA!","Heidrun’s eyes pulsed with approval as the goat nodded her head with the regal satisfaction of someone whose wisdom had been properly acknowledged.","|Heidrun tremendously approves of this idea and knows the perfect plot for the Auric Vitae Grass.|","Her head whipped around across the Early Veiled Shore, the Budding Shore, as if she were inspecting what would be the perfect location for something like this!","A prompt had bloomed before Noah consciousness, and before he could process its implications fully, another appeared with information that made him pause.","|To plant something and grow it in the Early Veiled Shore, especially something as unique as the Auric Vitae Grass stemming from Doorways of the Loom, something critical is required to allow its anchor and eventual growth.|","...!"]},{"number":3934,"title":"Chapter 3934: Chapter 3933: Power Must Be Taken! II","paragraphs":["The next prompt contained requirements that made even Noah shake his head at the level of difficulty associated with maintaining an Early Veiled Shore.","|A vital catalyst to allow for the anchor and growth of the Auric Vitae Grass is the Blood of an Early Creature. For the amount of Auric Vitae Grass on hand, approximately 18 Drops of Blood would be required.|","Noah read these prompts with the resignation!","But the benefits provided by the Early Veiled Shore were far too critical to abandon over concerns about cost- costs which werent truly costs as he could recover them in a short period of time!","So he went ahead.","\"Let us proceed with the planting of the Auric Vitae Grass,\" he voiced aloud, his words carrying the weight of Existential command.","What occurred next was a scene of such primal beauty that it seemed to belong to the earliest epochs of existence itself.","The palm of his right hand opened like a flower blooming in reverse, and eighteen drops of dull crimson-gold blood flowed forth with the stately grace of liquid starlight.","Each drop pulsed with its own inner radiance, containing within its molecular structure the compressed essence of what it truly meant to be an Early Creature.","These drops moved through the air with purposeful intent, flowing toward an empty area close to the crystalline waters of the Shore but positioned further inland where the golden sands met the roots of the ancient trees. They arranged themselves into a perfect square formation before sinking into the ground with the weight of Existence being fulfilled.","The moment his blood touched the earth, transformation began.","The golden sands of that region shifted and changed, their very nature being rewritten by the influence of Early Creature essence.","A glorious plot of fertile land rose from the Shore itself, its surface shining with white and gold radiance that spoke to potential beyond normal understanding.","HUUM!","The soil seemed ready to nurture wonders that existed beyond the comprehension of lesser realms!","New prompts appeared before Noah, detailing the process.","|The Auric Vitae Grass must be planted in bundles of nine, with each bundle representing a complete cycle of growth and renewal. This work must be done physically by the Early Creature or a single helper stemming from the Early Veiled Shore, as the direct contact between your essence and the grass is required for proper integration with the Shore’s unique environment.|","Noah accepted these requirements with calm understanding. He expanded the miniature wheel to its full size, revealing the vibrant green-gold grass exactly as it had appeared in the garden surrounding the Living Elemental in Concordia.","The sight of it made the air itself seem to thicken with concentrated possibility.","The process that followed carried the weight of ritual he never expected to be doing!","Noah took his first bundle of nine grass shoots and approached the transformed plot with movements that seemed to echo ancient ceremonies.","As he began to plant, the Early Living Existential Glyphs across his body began to shine with soft radiance, their light casting patterns across the waters Shore.","His bare upper body glistened with Existential perspiration that caught and reflected the light of the Glyphs, creating an image of primal beauty as he worked the fertile soil with his hands.","Each movement was deliberate, precise, carrying the weight of someone performing sacred work that would echo across existence.","As he planted the first bundle, his consciousness filled with new information.","|The Early Sacred Living Farming Tower of Osmont has fully formed due to the unique circumstances of this planting. Your connection to the agricultural mysteries of Early Creatures has deepened beyond normal parameters.|","...!","His hands suddenly became filled with verdant crystalline waves of light that pulsed in harmony with the planted grass!","The radiance spread from his fingers into the soil, creating connections between his essence and the growing vegetation that transcended normal botanical understanding.","Another prompt followed immediately!","|The growth and cultivation of all Early Sacred Herbs will now be five times faster than normal rates. The Early Veiled Shore has been recognized as a true agricultural home worthy of Early Creature cultivation.|","It was a glorious scene!","As Noah continued his sacred work, Heidrun approached with an expression of determination that transcended her usual arrogance.","She carefully took nine bundles of the precious grass in her mouth, exercising tremendous self-control to avoid consuming the delicacy she so craved.","Her movements carried the dignity of someone participating in a ceremony whose importance she fully understood.","Together, they worked in harmony that spoke to the deepest connections between Early Creatures and the Land Lifeforms who had chosen to serve them.","Noah’s hands moved with practiced precision while Heidrun positioned her bundles with careful attention to spacing and depth.","It was a glorious scene that seemed to capture the very essence of what the Early Veiled Shore was meant to represent!","An Early Creature and an Eminent Early Living Land Lifeform working together in harmony while around them, Moiraine and others maintained meditative positions or slept peacefully as their complexity continued to rise through exposure to the Shore’s concentrated authority!","The entire weaving of existence carried an air of primitive and magisterial authenticity that mocked the elaborate constructions and schemes of the Living Existences.","Here was power in its purest form, not wielded through elaborate hierarchies or complex machinations, but expressed through the simple act of nurturing growth in soil that had been blessed by the blood of an Early Creature.","As they worked, the Shore itself seemed to pulse with approval, its weavings pulsing with their movements in a symphony of cultivation!","The process of planting continued with the measured rhythm of sacred ritual, each bundle of nine Auric Vitae Grass shoots finding its place in the transformed soil with precision that spoke to ancient agricultural wonders!","Noah moved with unhurried grace, his hands working the blessed earth while Heidrun contributed her own careful plantings, the goat’s usual arrogance tempered by the solemnity of their shared task!"]},{"number":3935,"title":"Chapter 3935: Chapter 3934: Power Must Be Taken! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 3934: Power Must Be Taken! III","When the final bundle had been placed and the last of the golden soil patted into place around tender shoots, Noah and Heidrun stood at the edges of their green-gold plot with expressions of peace and contentment.","The work had been satisfying in ways that transcended normal accomplishment, connecting them to weavings that predated the concept of existence itself.","It felt unfathomably and magisterially peaceful in a way that could not be fully described!","Heidrun’s excitement was palpable as she gazed upon their handiwork, her crystalline eyes reflecting satisfaction that went beyond mere anticipation of future meals.","This was farming in its purest form, the nurturing of something that would provide sustenance and wonder for ages to come!","She could the see the future, and it was filled with glorious green gold grass!","And as if responding to their completion of this sacred work, new information began flowing across Noah’s mind.","|Auric Vitae Grass Growth Cycle- Complete maturity achieved in 1 hour from initial planting. Current planted specimens are already at 95% maturity due to the enhanced conditions of the Early Veiled Shore and the direct involvement of Early Creature essence in the cultivation process.|","|The Optimal harvest window begins at full maturity and extends for 24 hours before gradual decline in potency. During harvest, Seeds of the Auric Vitae Grass will naturally generate within the root systems and can be replanted immediately for continuous cultivation cycles.|","|Each harvested plot will yield triple the originally planted amount due to the Early Veiled Shore enhancement effects. Recommended replanting ratio: One-third seeds for expansion, two-thirds for immediate cultivation of new plots. This process allows for exponential growth of cultivated area over time.|","|The Early Sacred Living Farming Tower of Osmont provides passive growth acceleration. With proper timing and resource allocation, the Shore can support unlimited expansion of agricultural operations while maintaining optimal yield rates across all cultivated plots.|","HUUM!","Noah breathed in the sweet scent of growing grass as gentle winds carried the aroma across the Shore.","The shoots swayed with hypnotic rhythm, their movement synchronized to Glyphs that seemed to echo the heartbeat of existence itself!","He reached out to stroke Heidrun’s head with casual affection, and the normally imperious goat allowed the gesture freely, her arrogance somehow enhanced rather than diminished by her willingness to accept praise from one she deemed worthy.","After savoring this moment of agricultural triumph, Noah walked away from their plot toward the scattered figures who populated his Early Veiled Shore.","Some sat in meditative positions while others slept peacefully, but all of them radiated the gentle glow of beings whose complexity continued to rise through exposure to the concentrated authority that permeated every grain of sand!","As he approached them, Noah pulled upon the Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Ascendancy, feeling its power respond to his will like a perfectly tuned instrument awaiting the touch of a master.","He remembered the words that had described its function with perfect clarity.","He could select certain beings as Ascendants, sharing growth that his own existence could not process quickly enough.","When an Ascendant reached the ten million marker in both Complexity and Purity, he would receive one Ascendancy Mark of Existence that could instantly establish any Tower of Osmont without the usual requirements!","Additional marks would be earned at fifty million and one hundred million quotient levels, while ten Marks would allow any Tower of Osmont to achieve its second stage instantaneously!","The implications were gloriously staggering.","Not only could he accelerate the advancement of those around him, but their progress would directly contribute to his own development in ways that created exponential growth patterns!","“All those here shall be Ascendants,” he uttered with calm certainty.","HUUM!","The Glyph of Ascendancy blazed to life with hues of white and gold that seemed to contain within their radiance the compressed essence of unlimited potential.","Above the heads of Moiraine, Adelaide, Barbatos, Henry, his mother, Liora, and many others, the same hazy glow of the Glyph appeared like crowns of light marking them as chosen recipients of his excess growth.","The connection formed instantly, creating pathways through which he could share the overwhelming development his existence generated!","And... the one thing that nearly caused his body to explode due to its potent weavings was the Sacred Mead of Existence that continued to accelerate every process beyond normal parameters.","Noah approached the crystal bucket containing the milky gold liquid that had already transformed his capabilities beyond recognition.","Without hesitation, he lifted it to his lips and took another gulp, consuming five hundred drops this time with the casual confidence of someone who had grown accustomed to handling forces that would destroy his other self just minuted ago!","His existence erupted with multicolored lights of primal and tribal grace as his complexity scaled upward once again.","The radiance that emanated from his form carried patterns that spoke to the earliest epochs of existence, when power flowed in lands and folds thst even Living Existences had not walked through!","Behind him, those he had marked as Ascendant experienced their own transformation. Their eyes fluttered as waves of shared advancement washed through their beings, their Complexities and Purities jumping by tens of thousands every second as they received the overflow from his accelerated development!","Noah nodded with satisfaction as he observed their progress, then focused his attention on one particular figure among the blessed recipients of his generosity.","Moiraine sat upon the golden sands like a statue carved from concentrated authority, her gorgeous white-gold figure utterly otherworldly in its perfection.","The radiance that surrounded her form seemed to bend light itself, creating patterns that hurt to observe directly for those weaker, yet drew the eye with magnetic inevitability.","“Moiraine,” Noah called with the calm authority of absolute command, a plan already unfolding in his mind as he thought about what the Living Paradoxes had managed to accomplish with Diviticus!","Her eyes fluttered open, glazed with burning complexity as the effects of shared advancement continued to course through her existence!","4/5"]},{"number":3936,"title":"Chapter 3936: Chapter 3935: Power Must Be Taken! IV","paragraphs":["Chapter 3935: Power Must Be Taken! IV","She rose with fluid grace and came to stand beside Noah like a loyal soldier awaiting orders, this extremely powerful Prime Living Paradox displaying the kind of devotion that would have shocked anyone who understood her true capabilities!","Noah looked at her with the steady gaze as he spoke calmly.","“The Paradoxes have begun to move with Diviticus in the lead,” he said without preamble. “She has obtained something from me that allows her to pass through Paradoxical weavings without producing Inevitabilities. Using this capability....she led an assault on a heavily defended location and succeeded in stealing something the Coalition of Living Existences had protected for eons. A treasure that made them unfathomably powerful.”","Moiraine’s expression shifted to one of stern seriousness as she processed these words.","Her golden eyes blazed as she asked!","“What did they steal?” she asked this with the precise diction of someone who needed to understand every detail of a rapidly evolving situation!","“The corpse...of an Early Creature,” Noah replied with calm finality.","HUUM!","The shock that crossed Moiraine’s features was immediate!","She then showed anger.","As if she was expressing...how dare they?!","Both the Living Paradoxes and other Living Existences- how dare they desecrate a body of an Early Creature?!","She could not imagine it if it was the body of Noah before her that Living Existences held in their hands for eons.","It was true desecration!","Noah watched her reaction with approval before continuing.","“If a bit of myself taken by Diviticus can achieve all this, I will give a lot more of myself to you. Become...an Honored Living Paradox that does not produce Inevitabilities.”","BOOM!","The words were heavy.","Heavy!","Moiraine’s shock deepened as she stared at him with wide eyes, her voice barely above a whisper when she responded: “I could never...”","But Noah cut through her protest instantly, carrying the purple brilliance of Tyranny calmly here!","“You will,” he said with imposing authority. “Let me tell you about power, so that you can always remember its fundamental nature.”","Heidrun raised her head from thr distance and blinked as if she were wondering what the pristine Early Creature was saying now.","“Power... is not a gift to be bestowed by benevolent masters upon grateful others. Power is not charity dispensed by those who have it to those who lack it. Power is a force of nature that must be seized by those who possess the strength and will to claim it!”","HUUM!","” It can never be truly given because the act of giving implies that the recipient remains dependent upon the giver’s continued goodwill.”","His gaze fixed upon her with laser intensity, each word carefully chosen to cut through layers of conditioning and understanding!","“Right now, I want to give you power. I could force you to take it, could overwhelm your resistance and impose advancement upon your existence whether you desired it or not. But if I did that, you would never truly possess power. You would simply be a conduit for mine, forever limited by your own failure to choose greatness when it was offered freely.”","The silence that followed was burning with possibility, heavy with the weight of decisions that would echo across existence!","“So tell me, Moiraine,” he continued with calm tyrannical authority, “do you want power? Will you take the power I offer not as a gift but as something you claim through your own will and desire?”","His words struck her gloriously, each syllable resonating through the deepest foundations of her existence.","Moiraine’s eyes pulsed with growing firmness as understanding dawned, as she recognized that this moment would define her future capabilities along her fundamental nature as Living Paradox!","She stepped forward with decisive movement and knelt before him, her voice carrying the weight of absolute commitment when she spoke.","“I want it!”","WAA!","Noah nodded with the satisfaction.","His palm opened like a flower blooming in reverse, and drops of blood began flowing forth by the dozens, each one pulsing with the compressed essence of what it meant to be an Early Creature.","“Then take it.” he commanded with tyrannical authority that seemed to reshape the very air around them.","The very Early Veiled Shore shining around them!","One hundred dull crimson-gold drops of Blood flowed toward Moiraine like liquid starlight given purpose and direction.","They sank into her body through her skin and mouth, each drop carrying with it transformative power that would have destroyed lesser beings even as it elevated her beyond previous limitations.","In an instant, she began to radiate a terrifying flow of power that made the surrounding air shimmer with barely contained Living Existential Authority.","But Noah was not finished with his generosity!","Even as the Blood worked its transformation upon her cellular structure, he took the bucket of Sacred Mead of Existence and scooped a mouthful of the golden liquid.","He brought it toward Moiraine’s mouth with careful precision, allowing five hundred droplets of the miraculous substance to flow past her lips.","...!","HUUM!","The reaction was immediate and overwhelming.","A terrifying eruption of complexity instantly exploded outward from Moiraine’s form, engulfing everything within sight in waves of transformative energy that spoke to forces beyond normal comprehension!","The very foundations of the Early Veiled Shore trembled as they absorbed and channeled power, while those marked as Ascendant found their own advancement accelerating beyond all previous parameters!","The golden sands beneath their feet pulsed with rhythm that echoed the heartbeat of existence itself, while the crystalline waters reflected light that had never existed before this moment!","In the distance, the newly planted Auric Vitae Grass swayed in harmony with forces that could never have been observed before.","This...was transformation in its purest form, the reshaping of a being’s fundamental nature through the application of power that existed beyond the normal categories of possibility!","And at its center stood Noah, Early Creature and an architect of tyrannical advancement, watching with satisfied eyes as his actions created ripples that would reshape the balance of power across all levels of existence.","Diviticus took half a drop of his blood? Okay!","Okay!","Let’s see what Living Existences could be raised with a hundred drops.","If that was not enough, then he would do it with 1,000 Drops of Blood!","He could go utterly crazy...in ways no Living Existences understood!","5/5!","Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]},{"number":3937,"title":"Chapter 3937: Chapter 3936: A Twitch! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 3936: A Twitch! I","Noah stood surrounded by incandescent waves of light that pulsed with the rhythm of glorious transformation, his enhanced perception focused entirely upon the changes occurring within Moiraine as his Blood and Sacred Mead of Existence worked their fundamental alterations upon her very essence.","The combination of the Blood and Sacred Mead of Existence created reactions of magisterial tyranny, reshaping her capabilities and her nature as a Living Existence!","She seemed to barely be holding on as her complexity and purity surged upward in exponential curves.","Her form trembled with the effort of containing forces that pressed against the boundaries of what her existence could accommodate!","Then, in a moment that marked the crossing of an invisible threshold....","BOOM!","Her aura changed with the finality of a Wheel of Existence being born.","It became more pressing, heavier, carrying an undeniable weight that spoke to authority operating on entirely different principles than anything she had possessed before!","Where once her presence had been impressive, it now commanded attention. Deserved attention! Undoubtedly!","Noah smiled brilliantly as he observed this transformation, recognizing familiar patterns in the oppressive nature of her new aura.","From her, he now sensed a similar sense of suffocation that he had experienced when encountering beings like Honored Diviticus and Honored Gold.","She had crossed a fundamental threshold, ascending beyond the normal categories that defined Prime Living Existences.","But her transformation was only beginning.","Her figure began to rise from the golden sands of the Shore, her feet leaving the crystalline surface while her body maintained perfect stability in the air above.","Her eyes and mouth opened simultaneously, releasing streams of dull crimson-gold light that formed into tendrils which descended back toward the earth before wrapping around her form like ceremonial garments woven from pure authority!","...!","The sight was magnificent and terrifying to observe!","New information began cascading across Noah’s consciousness as existence itself buzzed.","|The Ascendant Moiraine is undergoing existential evolution from a Living Existence to an Arch Living Existence, a transformation that expands the very boundaries of what she can become.|","|Her possible weavings of existence have been fundamentally expanded. She can now achieve things that were previously impossible, transcending limitations that bound her previous form.|","|An Arch Living Existence is capable of holding two Living Existential Authorities simultaneously if proper conditions are met. Living Existential Authority density and depth of complexity and purity is increased by factor of five. Glyph formation rates accelerated by 300%. Resistance to existential manipulation increased exponentially. It is possible to exceed the 100% cap of a resistance through the aid of an Early Creature.|","WAA!","The implications were gloriously maddening.","An Arch Living Existence represented a complete departure from normal progression of Living Existences!","The beams of crimson-gold light shooting from her eyes and mouth began sinking back into her form, their energy transforming as it merged with her essence.","The result was spectacular beyond description...nine blazing dull crimson-gold halos materialized around her head, each one bearing a pair of archaic wings that moved with their own subtle rhythm.","The halos...had wings!","When her eyes finally opened, they carried a terrifying glow of power that was fundamentally different from anything Noah had observed in other Living Existences.","Noah observed her advancement and nodded with contentment.","|The Ascendant Moiraine has long ago exceeded the ten million and one hundred million markers, but has achieved such vast advancement in complexity and purity since being designated as an Ascendant that fifty Ascendancy Marks of Existence have been obtained from her transformation alone.|","|From other Ascendants present in the Early Veiled Shore, an additional twenty-five Ascendancy Marks of Existence have been generated through shared advancement.|","...!","The set of prompts were glorious ones.","Quintessential ones!","A total of seventy-five Ascendancy Marks of Existence obtained in a single moment of transformation!","Noah’s eyes shone as he contemplated the possibilities that such a number represented.","Seventy-five marks meant he could either establish seventy-five new Towers of Osmont at their first stage, each granting five hundred thousand in both Complexity and Purity, or advance seven existing towers to their second stage, gaining two million in each quotient...plus a Basic Early Living Existential Glyph for each type of Tower.","The choice between breadth and depth carried significant implications for his future development.","Well, he said future but really, it would mainly matter in the next few hours...or a day or two at most!","More first-stage towers would provide steady growth and diversification of capabilities, while advancing existing towers to their second stage would create...Sacred Totems that could potentially attract additional Early Living Land Lifeforms like Heidrun.","After a moment of deliberation, Noah’s eyes flashed with glorious tyranny as he made his decision.","The reason became clear as his gaze shifted toward Heidrun, who continued to observe her newly planted green-gold grass with imperial satisfaction and arrogance!","What was the reason he currently possessed an Eminent Early Living Land Lifeform? The answer lay in the Sacred Totem of Infinity that had drawn her across impossible distances to answer his call!","“Use the Ascendancy Marks of Existence to advance the Quintessential Tower, the Ascendancy Tower, the Protagonist Tower, the Loot Tower, Tyranny Tower, Paradox Tower, and Origin Tower,” he commanded with cold precision.","HUUM!","He gave the command, and things began to unfold.","His existence buzzed with glory as changes began occurring! His muscles undulated as if an utterly terrifying foundation was continuing to be forged within the architecture of his very essence, each fiber of his form adapting to accommodate new levels of Existence.","|The following Early Sacred Living Towers of Osmont are being advanced to their Second Stage completion: Quintessential Tower, Ascendancy Tower, Protagonist Tower, Loot Tower, Tyranny Tower, Paradox Tower, and Origin Tower. New Sacred Totems will soon be born.|","His body exploded with waves of immensity that made the surrounding air shimmer with barely contained authority!","The transformation was visible in every line of his form, from the way his skin seemed to glow with inner radiance to the manner in which his very presence began warping the space around him.","Towers formed.","And very soon, Sacred Totems would also form!","At this moment of his own fundamental elevation, Noah looked toward Moiraine, who remained suspended in her ongoing transformation.","Her new eyes, shining with dull crimson-gold radiance, regarded him with expressions of shock and even grander respect.","“We are not done,” he said with calm finality.","Her newly transformed eyes pulsed with power as she felt her Existence tighten with anticipation and perhaps a touch of caution.","“What...else could Sir be thinking of?” she asked carefully.","Noah tapped out with his finger and sent a concentrated burst of information directly into her consciousness.","When the transfer was complete, he spoke.","“A certain amount of complexity and purity will form either a Basic, Refined, Eminent, or Kleos Glyph. An Eminent Glyph requires one hundred million Complexity and Purity Quotients, while a Kleos Glyph demands one billion. Form as many Eminent and Kleos Glyphs as you can manage.”","...!","Moiraine’s seriousness was visible in every line of her elevated form as she nodded with newfound understanding.","She thought.","And she then moved!","Her weavings of Existence began to transform, preparing to sacrifice vast quantities of complexity and purity for even grander power.","|The Arch Living Existence, the Ascendant Moiraine, can form up to Eminent Glyphs with her current distinction and proximity to an Early Creature serving as catalyst for the process.|","|The Ascendant Moiraine has sacrificed an initial ten billion CQ and PQ to simultaneously form one hundred Eminent Early Living Existential Glyphs of Paradox.|","...!","Even Noah felt a moment of surprise at the magnitude of what she was doing right off!","One hundred Eminent Early Living Existential Glyphs!","What followed was a sight that would have driven Fold Dwellers to their knees in reverence or terror.","One hundred points of singularities bloomed across Moiraine’s body like Wheels being born in miniature, each one marking the genesis of a Glyph whose power would reshape her weavings of Existence.","The moment this process began, Moiraine alone released such a terrifying archaic air of age that the very sands of the Early Veiled Shore began to resonate!","The crystalline waters at the shoreline reflected her radiance while the three ancient trees swayed in response!","Even Heidrun momentarily stopped her calm observation of the green-gold grass plot, her imperial composure cracking as surprise and what appeared to be recognition flickered through her crystalline eyes!","The goat’s reaction spoke to depths of knowledge and records in its lineage that stretched back to epochs when such transformations were more common, when Early Creatures did such actions easily and without evem sparing much thought.","Moiraine’s transformation continued to unfold with terrifying beauty, each Glyph that formed upon her body adding new layers to her already overwhelming presence!","Looking at her suspended form, radiant with the light of one hundred newly formed Glyphs, Noah laughed with Tyranny and glory, his voice carrying across the Shore.","“Continue! Continue! You shall be one of my finest designs!”","The words rang across the Early Veiled Shore like a proclamation!","In the distance, the newly planted Auric Vitae Grass swayed in rhythm, while the crystalline waters witnessed everything.","They witnessed!","1/3"]},{"number":3938,"title":"Chapter 3938: Chapter 3937: A Twitch! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 3937: A Twitch! II","As Noah observed his own transformation and the elevation of Moiraine in the Early Veiled Shore, the reverberations of their advancement would eventually ripple across the vast expanse of Existence itself.","Eventually.","But they were not the only ones experiencing fundamental change in this moment of existential significance.","Existence is vast, unexplored, and filled with wonder beyond the comprehension of most conscious beings.","What many commonly know and understand represents but a mere fractional facet of the true Weavings of Existence that stretch across infinite possibilities.","In these grand unexplored territories dwell countless entities who are exceptional in their own right, masters of their own fables, beings whose choices carry weight that affects far more than they could ever imagine.","And in the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, a countless distance away from the conflicts and revelations unfolding elsewhere, such choices were being made that would reshape the very foundations upon which some parts of existence operated!","—","In the Heart of Paradox, nestled within the deepest regions of the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, lay a domain of wonder.","Stellar obsidian and gold rivers of Living Paradoxical Authority flowed through the landscape in patterns that hurt to observe directly, their currents carrying contradictions that made reality itself seem uncertain of its own nature.","At the center of this impossible realm stood a massive statue that dominated the horizon with its sheer presence.","The figure was carved from materials that existed in states of perpetual contradiction, its form both solid and ethereal, ancient and newly forged.","In its hands, it held a weapon that defied rational description....an obsidian infinity symbol whose very existence seemed to challenge the fundamental weavings governing reality.","The robed statue wore a crown that pulsed with its own inner radiance, its features carved into the likeness of a terrifying Paradoxical Emperor whose gaze overlooked everything within this domain.","There was something unsettling about those stone eyes, as if they contained awareness that transcended the merely artistic, consciousness trapped within unchanging material that watched and judged with paradoxical patience!","Yet where its gaze fell now, thousands upon thousands of terrifying Living Paradoxes circled a certain area with wills of power that made the surrounding air shimmer with barely contained authority.","The assembly was unprecedented in its scope and significance- thousands of Prime Living Paradoxes formed outer rings of observation, while close to one hundred Honored Living Paradoxes occupied positions of greater prominence.","Among these Honored beings stood Gold, his form radiating the particular brand of ancient authority.","But even he, for all his accumulated power and wisdom, showed deference to the ten figures who commanded the ultimate positions of authority in this gathering.","Duke Elagabalus sat grandly upon an obsidian throne constructed from hundreds of miniaturized Wheels of Existence, each one pulsing with its own rhythm of contained reality.","His terrifying obsidian-gold hair flowed like liquid metal around his shoulders, while his crimson-gold robe seemed to absorb and reflect light Paradoxically!","Above his head floated a three-pointed crown that pulsed with authority so concentrated it made the surrounding space bend subtly around its presence.","Beside him and arranged in careful formation sat nine other entities, each occupying thrones of different colors and materials but all sharing the same fundamental nature...they were Dukes, ten of the eighty-one beings who collectively governed the fate of all Living Paradoxes across existence.","Their presence here spoke to the significance of whatever had drawn them together in this place of ancient power!","All of their attention was focused upon a single object that lay before them like a sacrifice offered to forgotten wonders.","Near Duke Elagabalus stood none other than Diviticus, though her visage now shimmered with an extremely brilliant white grandeur that spoke to fundamental changes in her nature and status.","She seemed untouchable, wrapped in a unique authority that made even the assembled Dukes regard her with respect!","Many of the gathered Paradoxes looked toward her with expressions of awe.","But...what commanded their collective attention was a body- the corpse they had stolen from the Coalition of Living Existences through audacious assault and impossible capability.","It was the preserved remains of an Early Creature, a being whose death should have been inconceivable yet whose body lay before them as undeniable proof that even the mightiest could fall!","The corpse was massive in scale, perhaps ten times the size of any Living Paradox present, its proportions telling of the fundamental differences between Early Creatures and the beings who had evolved in their wake.","The most striking feature was the wound that had ended its existence- a diagonal cleave that ran from shoulder to waist, cutting through flesh and bone with such precision that no trace of energy remained to indicate what force could have delivered such a devastating blow!","Yet when even Honored Living Existences gazed upon that wound, they felt their hearts shake with the understanding that if such a strike were directed toward them, they would crumble like dust!","The corpse appeared humanoid in its basic structure. Around its waist was wrapped what appeared to be clothing fashioned from animal hide, though the materials were unlike anything that existed in current reality.","The garment suggested primitive origins yet radiated an aura of authority that made it clear this being had needed no external symbols to command respect!","Its upper body lay bare, revealing the full extent of the massive wound while simultaneously displaying the fundamental differences between Early Creature physiology and that of lesser beings.","Apart from the diagonal cut that had ended its existence, the skin and muscle appeared completely drained of blood, their color faded to a gray that spoke to death in its most absolute form.","Yet paradoxically, even in death, the corpse carried waves of life that far exceeded even the Royal Living Paradoxes present!","It was as if death itself had been unable to fully claim this being, leaving behind something that existed in the space between existence and nonexistence.","All across its body, one could observe indentations and excavations where countless entities had worked over eons to extract samples of skin, muscle, and bone.","Also prominent...were thousands of terrifying Glyphs that seemed broken and carved out, with each shattered Glyph causing any Honored Living Existence who looked at it to feel a sense of oppression! From a simple one...of the thousands of broken Glyphs!","The Coalition of Living Existences had clearly been harvesting from this corpse for an unimaginable length of time, each extraction representing attempts to understand or replicate the fundamental nature and power of Early Creature existence.","Most shocking of all was the absence of the heart, clearly removed through careful surgical precision by something far more powerful than a Living Existence!","2/3"]},{"number":3939,"title":"Chapter 3939: Chapter 3938: A Twitch! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 3938: A Twitch! III","The network of vessels that remained revealed blood cells that defied conventional understandingz they appeared as gray, lifeless Wheels of Existence, suggesting that even in death, the corpse’s circulatory system operated according to principles that transcended understanding.","The archaic air that emanated from the corpse created an atmosphere of wonder mixed with terror.","Its head retained features that might once have been noble or beautiful, though death had transformed them into something terrifying.","The eyes were blacked out, creating endless abysses that seemed to stare into dimensions that existed beyond current reality!","Its hair remained wild and untamed, dark gray strands that held their original configuration despite the complete absence of life!","Every Living Paradox present gazed upon this impossible sight with eyes that shone with mixture of hunger, fear, and desperate hope.","In the heavy silence that followed their collective observation, the voice of Duke Elagabalus echoed across the gathering with the weight of glorious proclamation.","He looked toward Diviticus with an expression that combined respect with calculation, his words carrying implications that would reshape the hierarchy of their entire weavings of existence!","“I do not think my proposition of making Honored Diviticus a member of the council and granting her the rank of Duke will meet with any complaints now. Through her aid, we were able to obtain something we could only envy for eons!”","HUUM!","All eyes turned to regard both the speaker and the subject of his declaration, the magnitude of what had been achieved finally settling into their weavings with proper weight.","Duke Elagabalus smiled toward Diviticus with satisfaction that bordered on pride. “Duke Diviticus, why don’t you be the first to study the corpse that the Coalition of Living Existences has been feeding from all these eons so they could match our power? The rest of the council will call for it to be veiled and hidden away soon!”","Duke Diviticus!","DUKE!","No longer merely Honored, but elevated to one of the highest ranks their weavings could bestow. She might not yet possess the accumulated strength that typically accompanied such position, but the title she now held carried authority that transcended mere power!","She nodded with eyes that shone with anticipation and calm glory.","As she approached the massive corpse, she felt waves of awe and veneration washing over her being.","The corpse lay motionless, yet her very existence pulsed with wonder and interminable glory at simply being in its presence. She moved forward with careful steps until she stood before the massive form, its scale making her feel insignificant despite her newly elevated status.","With trembling hand, she reached out and touched a single finger of the corpse...just the finger alone, which was itself larger than her entire torso.","It should have been something simple, a mere contact between living flesh and dead tissue.","And yet in the next moment, the impossible occurred.","HUUM!","The surface of the corpse instantly began buzzing and trembling!","...!","The finger she had touched twitched once...a single, involuntary movement that lasted no more than a heartbeat.","A twitch. Just one twitch.","Goodness, just one twitch!","But it was so terrifying in its implications that the instant this movement was seen and felt, every Living Paradox present was overwhelmed by primal terror. .","No matter what distinction they held, no matter how much power they had accumulated or how many conflicts they had survived...Prime, Honored, Royal, Duke...every single one scattered into lights of pure panic and fled for their existence.","Instantly!","From observing that one twitch!","They ran with the desperate urgency of beings who had suddenly realized they stood in the presence of something that could erase them from reality without effort!","Light-years disappeared in seconds as they put distance between themselves and the source of their terror, their only thought being escape from whatever force could make a dead Early Creature respond to touch.","Duke Diviticus found herself among those who fled, her newly elevated status providing no protection against the instinctive horror that had seized her Living Existential Authority!","She ran until she was light-years away before managing to stop and look back, her enhanced perception confirming that the twitch had been singular...after she had released contact, the corpse had returned to its previous state of absolute stillness.","“...”","She breathed heavily with shock that made her entire form tremble, her heart pulsing with rhythms that spoke to terror mixed with unprecedented shock.","Slowly, carefully, she began to return, her eyes wide with the knowledge that she had just witnessed something that defied every understanding of existence.","One by one, the thrones of Dukes began to reappear in the distance, their occupants peering from afar with expressions of shock and profound seriousness.","Only when they confirmed that the corpse had returned to complete motionlessness did they dare to approach again, their movements cautious as prey animals checking for predators.","Immense silence followed their gradual return, heavy with weavings that none of them fully understood but all recognized as monumentally significant.","In this moment of utter shock and tension, Duke Elagabalus fixed his gaze upon the still-trembling Diviticus.","His eyes flashed sharply as understanding began to dawn, and he turned to command one of the Honored Living Paradoxes behind him.","“Touch the corpse,” he ordered with stern authority that brooked no argument.","The Honored being was initially hesitant, his earlier terror still fresh in memory, but the duke’s unwavering gaze left no room for refusal.","He approached the massive form....and hesitantly made contact with its surface.","Slowly!","This was how much Living Existences revered and feared Early Creatures!","The moment stretched as every observer held their breath, ready to scatter again at the first sign of movement.","But...nothing happened. Nothing at all.","Duke Elagabalus and others stared in shock as the implications became clear, their collective attention turning toward Diviticus with expressions that mixed awe with growing excitement.","Before anyone could voice their thoughts, she was already floating toward the corpse again, her own curiosity overcoming her earlier terror.","She went forward again and reached out. This time, she touched the toe of the massive foot with deliberate precision.","And once again, the impossible occurred.","HUUM!","A booming flash of terrifying aura erupted from the point of contact as the toe twitched with the same involuntary response that had sent them all fleeing moments before.","Diviticus released contact immediately, her face showing a complex mixture of shock, terror, and exhilaration that spoke to discoveries!","Glorious discoveries!","She turned to look at the other Dukes and Honored Gold, and in their shared expression of fear mixed with tremendous excitement, they all recognized that they had stumbled upon a terrifying finding.","A finding that seemed to be uniquely centered around Duke Diviticus and her interaction with this corpse of an Early Creature!","What was this?! What could they do with this?!","Oh!","3/3 Next chapter titles Oh! I & II & III & IV & V"]},{"number":3940,"title":"Chapter 3940: Chapter 3939: Oh! I","paragraphs":["Communication exists in countless forms throughout the vast expanse of existence.","Words spoken aloud carry meaning from one consciousness to another.","Actions taken with purpose convey intentions that transcend mere verbal expression.","Symbols and gestures create bridges between minds that might otherwise remain forever isolated!","Through these varied methods, understanding flows between beings like water finding its natural course.","Yet...there exist rare and precious moments when communication transcends all conventional boundaries.","Instances when harmony reaches such perfect resonance that even without words or symbols, without deliberate action or conscious thought, mere gazes become sufficient to convey the deepest truths.","In these extraordinary circumstances, eyes speak volumes that entire libraries could never contain, and understanding passes between beings with the immediacy and speed of light!","At this moment in time, within the Heart of Paradox surrounded by rivers of obsidian and gold authority, such a unique phenomenon was occurring.","In the aftermath of their collective flight from the impossible twitch of dead flesh responding to living touch, the assembled Living Paradoxes had returned to find themselves witnesses to something that challenged every assumption they held about the nature of existence itself.","The massive corpse of the Early Creature lay before them unchanged, yet the knowledge of what they had witnessed transformed everything about how they perceived both it and the being who had triggered its response.","Initially, their gazes carried expressions of pure shock mixed with exhilaration that bordered on euphoria.","Duke Elagabalus and Diviticus exchanged looks.","Honored Gold’s ancient eyes blazed with recognition of possibilities that stretched toward horizons he had never dared imagine.","The fact that Diviticus could cause a corpse of an Early Creature to react while others could not meant that something within her current status, some fundamental aspect of what she had become, allowed for this unprecedented interaction.","All of this understanding passed between them through nothing more than shared glances, their expressions communicating complex chains of reasoning without need for verbal confirmation.","Shock gave way to joy as they recognized the magnitude of what they had discovered, the potential that lay before them like an unopened treasure vault whose contents could reshape the balance of power across all of existence!","But then, without a single word being spoken, their collective expressions began to shift.","From exhilaration to confusion, the change occurred with such synchronicity that it might have been choreographed by unseen hands.","Each face reflected the same troubling question that had begun to surface in their minds like a bubble rising from deep waters.","Why would Diviticus alone possess this capability? What was it about her transformation that created such a unique reaction?","Nobody uttered these questions verbally or even formed them as conscious thoughts, yet they all looked at each other with perfect understanding of the uncertainty that had begun to gnaw at their earlier certainty.","The confusion painted itself across their features with unmistakable clarity, creating a moment of shared bewilderment that needed no explanation.","Then, as if guided by the same invisible force that had synchronized their confusion, their faces began to change again. From puzzlement to dawning realization!","Diviticus looked directly at Honored Gold, her gaze carrying the weight of recognition. The only reason she possessed this unprecedented capability was because she had consumed the body of Ozymandias.","She had obtained half a drop of his blood, and somehow that infinitesimal portion of his essence had granted her the ability to not produce inevitabilities and to interact with an Early Creature’s corpse to cause it to twitch!","Simultaneously, every Living Paradox present arrived at this same conclusion through their own chains of reasoning.","And right after this moment of collective understanding, their expressions underwent another synchronized transformation.","From realization to somber gravity, the change reflected minds grappling with implications that threatened to overwhelm their ability to process.","Oh.","They all looked at each other with the same terrible awareness dawning behind their eyes.","There were precious few reasons why the being that Diviticus had partially devoured could possess something that would react with the body of an Early Creature!","Either Ozymandias had carried some inheritance or connection to an Early Creature, or...","\"...\"","Oh!","The alternative was too enormous, too terrifying in its implications to fully contemplate.","The moment such possibilities began to surface in their consciousness, their faces collectively drained of color!","Without speaking a word, without exchanging so much as a gesture, they all felt the same chill settling into their bones as the unthinkable began to seem not merely possible but probable.","Diviticus began to pant, her breathing becoming rapid and shallow as the weight of realization pressed down upon her like a physical force!","She looked between Honored Gold and Duke Elagabalus, her head shaking in small, desperate movements that spoke to denial so profound it bordered on panic.","This expression of rejection spread through their ranks like a contagion, each face reflecting the same desperate need to reject what their minds were trying to tell them!","Even without words, they communicated their shared refusal to accept the possibility that Ozymandias could have been an Early Creature himself!","No. He had to have been someone with an inheritance. A bearer of some treasured connection. Maybe.","Their wordless communication continued as emotions cycled through them with the inexorable rhythm of grief itself.","Denial gave way to anger as the gathered Paradoxes turned their gazes toward Diviticus with expressions that held her responsible for consuming something that might have been infinitely precious.","The accusation in their eyes was clear- she was the one who had devoured him, who had potentially destroyed something irreplaceable.","But anger could not be sustained in the face of honest self-reflection.","Their expressions shifted to something approaching bargaining as they recognized, each in their own way, that any of them would have done the same thing given the opportunity. The blame could not rest solely on her shoulders when they all would have made identical choices.","\"...\"","Oh!","Depression followed as surely as night follows day.","Their gazes became haunted as they contemplated what they might have lost, what connection to Early Creature heritage might have been severed forever through their actions.","The weight of potential tragedy settled upon them like a shroud woven from regret and missed opportunity.","They looked at each other with expressions of shared numbness, each face reflecting the same dazed incomprehension of beings who had discovered that their greatest triumph might simultaneously be their most catastrophic failure.","Throughout this entire emotional journey, not a single word had been spoken.","Yet everyone understood each other with perfect clarity, their shared experience creating a harmony of communication that transcended all conventional boundaries!","At such a moment came... acceptance mixed with a desperate form of bargaining, hope clinging to rational explanation like a drowning man grasping for a savior.","It was Duke Elagabalus who finally broke the heavy silence that had settled over them like a funeral pall. His voice carried conviction born from desperate need to believe his own words.","\"That Ozymandias could not have been an Early Creature. Otherwise, he would not have come to us as merely an Originus Venerant. Even weaker than that. Early Creatures at birth would be many times grander than any Honored Living Existence. The very concept defies logical possibility. So it cannot be possible. It is not possible.\"","...!","Oh?!"]},{"number":3941,"title":"Chapter 3941: Chapter 3940: Oh! II","paragraphs":["Duke Elagabalus spoke with such firmness that for a moment, the weight of doubt seemed to lift from their collective consciousness.","There was immense silence as his words settled into their minds, but Diviticus and others nodded with gazes full of desperate hope.","Duke Elagabalus continued with growing confidence, his voice taking on the tone of someone who had found solid ground in a landscape of shifting possibilities.","\"It is likely that he obtained an inheritance or treasure relating to an Early Creature. Perhaps a drop of blood from some ancient source, and that is what Diviticus obtained half of. Which means we must find Ozymandias at all costs. If he possesses such a treasure, it belongs with us. There is no harm being...friendly. Inviting him to our ranks truly.\"","...!","Oh!","Their eyes blazed with collective acknowledgment as they seized upon this explanation like salvation itself.","All of them worked together to push down and deny the alternative possibility, burying it beneath layers of rational argument and desperate hope.","It was not possible that Ozymandias had been an Early Creature. It did not make sense given what they had observed. So they denied it, cast it aside, refused to give it space in their thoughts.","Denial became their shared truth, their collective protection against possibilities too vast to accept.","Duke Elagabalus looked toward the massive corpse that had started this entire chain of revelation, his expression brightening with newfound purpose.","\"If from that inheritance, Diviticus truly holds half a drop of Early Creature blood, let us see if you can use your existence to reanimate and control this corpse that reacts to you. Perhaps you could act as its missing heart, become the vital force that gives it motion and purpose.\"","His voice grew stronger as the possibilities multiplied in his mind.","\"If you achieve this, then the Living Paradoxes will have a genuine Early Creature fighting on our behalf. At that time, what worries would we have? What force in all of existence could stand against us?\"","They looked at each other and nodded with expressions that mixed hope with determination.","Their collective gaze spoke volumes about their shared decision to embrace this path forward, to transform potential catastrophe into ultimate triumph.","Right.","It had to be this way.","It had to be possible!","It had to!","Oh!!!","—","Time passed, as it always did, being the single terrifying construct that no being could stand against.","When one contemplated all the cold and vile entities across existence and considered their kill counts, nobody could surpass the numbers that were naturally claimed by time itself.","Empires crumbled, stars died, Omniverses perished, Wheels of Existence underwent Breakings, civilizations rose and fell... all according to its inexorable rhythm!","Yet time also brought progress, advancement, and the steady accumulation of power that transformed the possible into the inevitable.","In the Early Veiled Shore, with the passage of time came accomplishments that defied the normal boundaries of what beings could achieve.","Progression unfolded here according to principles that existed beyond the understanding of others, each moment bringing transformations that would have taken others lifetimes to accomplish!","The scene that greeted Noah’s enhanced perception was one of sublime beauty touched with power that made the very air shimmer with possibility.","Moiraine’s visage descended slowly through the golden atmosphere of the Shore, her feet finally touching the crystalline sands with the gentle grace.","Her nine winged halos rotated around her head with subtle movements, each wing bearing patterns that hurt to observe directly yet drew the eye with magnetic inevitability!","Her skin shone with white-gold radiance that seemed to emanate from within rather than reflecting external light, creating an aura of otherworldly beauty that marked her as something fundamentally different from other Living Existences.","But it was the addition of the Eminent Early Living Existential Glyphs of Paradox that truly transformed her appearance into something that belonged to the earliest epochs of Existence!","The golden glyphs covered her body in intricate patterns that made her look like an archaic tribal being touched by unknown authority, each marking pulsing with its own weaving while contributing to a greater symphony of power.","Around her form, tendrils of Paradox swirled passively like storm clouds burning with potential destruction, their movements suggesting barely contained forces that could erupt at any moment to reshape existence according to her will!","Currently, five hundred swirling Eminent Early Living Existential Glyphs of Paradox adorned her being, each one representing a sacrifice of one hundred million in both Complexity and Purity Quotients.","The numbers were staggering- fifty billion units of power refined into permanent enhancements that would reshape her capabilities forever!","To understand the magnitude of what she had achieved, one needed to comprehend the demarcations of power that governed existence itself.","The peak of Originus Venerant entities stood at 99,999,999 in both Complexity and Purity.","Spilling past this threshold, one entered the realm of power that most normal Living Existences wielded, ranging from one hundred million to nine hundred ninety-nine million.","From one billion to ninety-nine billion marked the varying power levels of Prime Living Existences, while Honored ones exceeded the one hundred billion marker in both quotients!","Moiraine, the glorious Ascendant, the Arch Living Existence who had transcended normal categories through Noah’s gifts and her own determination, was now firmly established among such beings!","Noah sat upon the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore, his expression one of calm satisfaction as he observed her descent. The smile that played across his features carried the particular joy of someone whose careful investment had yielded returns beyond his most optimistic projections.","Before him, new information began cascading across his consciousness as the Early Veiled Shore recognized and catalogued the implications of what had been achieved!","|By experiencing the advancement of the Arch Living Existence, Moiraine, and witnessing her formation of multiple hundred Eminent Glyphs, you have understood Eminent Glyphs on a fundamental level. The requirement to form your own Eminent Glyphs has been reduced from 100 Million to 75 Million.|","Oh?!"]},{"number":3942,"title":"Chapter 3942: Chapter 3941: Oh! III","paragraphs":["The implications were significant!","Through observation and proximity to her transformation, his own understanding had deepened to the point where he could achieve similar feats with greater efficiency. It was yet another demonstration of how the Early Veiled Shore facilitated advancement through shared experience and collective growth.","Another prompt appeared with information that made him turn to survey his domain.","|Seven additional Sacred Totems have been enacted in the Early Veiled Shore, manifesting the completed Second Stage Towers of Osmont.|","Noah’s gaze swept across the landscape as he observed the newly manifested structures scattered throughout different areas of the Shore.","Each Sacred Totem bore similar fundamental architecture to the original Totem of Infinity, yet each possessed its own unique characteristics that spoke to the distinct nature of the Tower it represented.","Different colors dominated their crystalline surfaces, while ancient-looking bells crowned their peaks with designs filled with quintessential glory.","The sight was magnificent, speaking to accumulated power that had been refined into permanent monuments to his advancement.","Yet even as he admired their beauty, another prompt appeared that tempered his satisfaction with practical limitations!","|Until the Early Veiled Shore advances from its current Budding status, it cannot support another Early Living Land Lifeform as the ringing of any bells will not call forth anything. The Early Living Land Lifeform, Heidrun, has occupied an immense breadth of existence provided by the Shore for Land Lifeforms. Additional capacity requires fundamental expansion of the Shore itself.|","...!","Oh...","The Sacred Totems were built and ready to serve their purpose, yet he could not ring their bells to call forth terrifying creatures like Heidrun until the Shore itself evolved to accommodate such expansion!","He shook his head at this limitation with rueful amusement, recognizing that even in a realm of impossible wonders, certain boundaries still applied.","As Noah’s gaze moved across the Sacred Totems, it naturally fell upon other figures who populated his domain, each representing their own remarkable journey of advancement and transformation.","Ruination and the Infiniverse no longer competed to exceed one another in complexity, their rivalry having evolved into something more cooperative as they focused on becoming more complex both for themselves and for him.","Ruination had made tremendous advances despite her relatively modest baseline complexity and purity, which remained less than one million.","Less than 1 Million!","Yet...she shockingly held eleven Basic Early Living Existential Glyphs of Ruination alongside two Refined Early Living Existential Glyphs of Ruination!","The combination equated to more than thirty million in effective Complexity, creating a situation where even if a being appeared before her with thirty million actual complexity and purity, with only a single Refined Glyph...she would be able to defeat them with casual ease!","The Infiniverse presented an entirely different case study in advancement.","She had not generated massive waves of power or undergone dramatic eruptions of authority, yet among all those present, with the sole exception of Moiraine, she was the one who had advanced the most.","Her progress was monstrous in its scope, achieved through methods that were...a bit off compared to others!","She possessed Refined Early Living Existential Glyphs of Manadynamics, Infinity, Continuity, Dreams, and Entropy alongside five Basic Glyphs, with nine million in raw complexity and purity to spare.","Her total accumulated power had already exceeded sixty million!","Yet she had not generated terrifying waves or grandiose eruptions because she possessed something that very few could even fathom.","At this moment, the Early Veiled Shore was entrenched at her core, positioned at the center of the Infiniverse Wheel itself. Its advancement and the continuing wonders that bloomed within its boundaries would affect her in ways that even Noah did not fully comprehend at this moment.","She was not merely advancing alongside the Shore; she was evolving in harmony with it, their development intertwined in ways where the effect was not fully known!","His mother, Henry, and others were steadily progressing past the ten million marker in Complexity as everyone advanced according to their own weavings and capabilities.","The shared benefits of his Ascendancy designation ensured that all members of his inner circle experienced growth that would have been impossible under normal circumstances!","As for himself...Noah’s entire visage carried an air of primal and archaic power that made the surrounding air shimmer.","His skin and muscles pulsed with heavy glows of brilliance! The combination of Sacred Mead of Existence consumption and the exponential acceleration provided by the Refined Glyph of Tyranny had created progression rates that surpassed even True Severed Adaptive Power of Existence.","His tyrannical monologues had not been mere displays that were useless- they had served as catalysts for the Glyph of Tyranny, accelerating his advancement through authentic expression of his fundamental nature, and truly...it felt good to talk down to hypocritical beings every now and then!","Through additional Ascendancy Marks of Existence, he had successfully forged more than fifty additional First Stage Towers of Osmont.","Combined with his three Refined Glyphs and twenty Basic Glyphs, plus the complexity and purity gained from tower construction itself, he now held 47 million in both CQ and PQ.","When he considered all factors together... he was already approaching the peak of Originus Venerant!","...!","Oh!","Already!","Had it even already hit one full day since he attained the Early Veiled Shore?!","The speed of his advancement defied every normal expectation, compressed into timeframes that should have been impossible yet had become reality through the wonders of the Early Veiled Shore.","It was a moment that required profound silence and contemplation.","All of this terrifying progression had been made possible by the Early Veiled Shore and the unique opportunities it provided!","As Noah reflected upon these accomplishments, a familiar presence silently appeared before him.","Heidrun stood with shining arrogant eyes that bore into his with the imperious expectation that had become her trademark.","She blinked once, as if asking what exactly he was doing when there were obviously more important matters demanding attention.","Her head nudged toward the vibrant plot of green-gold grasses, the Auric Vitae specimens they had planted with such care and ceremony.","Above the cultivation area, a glorious archaic aurora of light swirled in a crescendo of power that spoke to processes reaching their ordained completion!","New information began flowing across Noah’s consciousness soon after.","|The Auric Vitae Grasses have reached full maturity and are ready for harvesting. Optimal harvesting window has begun.|","|Harvest Yield: Current mature grasses will yield 300% of originally planted amount due to Early Veiled Shore enhancement effects. Total harvestable material: 2,700 individual shoots of varying potency grades.|","|Seed Generation: Each harvested grass shoot will produce 3-5 viable seeds for replantation. Estimated total seed yield: 10,800 seeds capable of establishing new cultivation plots.|","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":3943,"title":"Chapter 3943: Chapter 3942: Oh! IV","paragraphs":["Noah read prompt after prompt, and they did not even seem close to being done as more came even before one fully enjoyed the grandeur of the prompt before it!","|Replantation Process: Seeds may be planted immediately following harvest in prepared plots enhanced with Early Creature blood. Germination rate in Shore conditions: 98%. Time to maturity: 1 hour under current enhancement levels.|","|Plot Expansion: Additional cultivation areas may be established at any time through sacrifice of Early Creature blood. Recommended ratio: 18 drops per standard cultivation plot. Maximum sustainable plots limited only by available Shore territory.|","|Sacred Storage: Harvested crops may be stored within Sacred Totems, which will further enhance their weavings of existence for as long as they remain in containment. Enhancement rate: 5% potency increase per day of storage, maximum enhancement: 500%.|","|Quality Grading: Harvested materials will be automatically categorized into Standard, Superior, and Pristine grades based on Shore influence during growth. Higher grades provide exponentially greater benefits when consumed.|","|Processing Options: Raw consumption provides immediate but temporary benefits. Processed materials may be refined through Sacred Totem exposure, Early Creature alteration through cooking, or combination with other Early Sacred materials for permanent enhancement effects.|","|Manual Harvesting Required: Manual harvesting can be done by an Early Creature, an Early Living Land Lifeform, or Arch Living Existence to maintain optimal potency. Automated harvesting is possible through thr sacrifice of one drop of Blood, but it reduces effectiveness by 75%.|","...!","Oh!","Noah smiled at the comprehensive information provided by the Shore’s systems, each prompt revealing new layers of complexity to what had initially seemed like simple agricultural work.","He rose from his seated position and reached out to stroke the lustrous coat of the arrogant Heidrun, her fur carrying warmth that seemed to be burning brighter as she looked at thr vibrant green gold grasses!","His gaze shifted toward Moiraine, whose transformation into a terrifying Honored Arch Living Existence wielding hundreds of Eminent Glyphs represented one of the most significant achievements so far. Yet...her first action after ascending to such overwhelming power would be to help manually harvest crops in the Early Veiled Shore!","There was something profoundly appropriate about this!","As Noah approached the cultivation plot with Heidrun beside him and Moiraine moving to join them, the Early Veiled Shore itself seemed to pulse with anticipation.","As he moved and began to harvest the grass by hand, he looked around and wondered...nothing too crazy was going on out there in the meanwhile, right?","\"...\"","Such a thought only rose once before he shook his head with a smile and returned to his task of harvesting.","Acting as an Early Creature- as a Farmer in this Early Veiled Shore had granted him a more rapid progression than what any grand battles or war would have.","Doing things in the Early Veiled Shore would actually allow him to progress the fastest!","The harvest began with quintessential glory.","Noah positioned himself at one edge of the cultivation plot while Moiraine approached from another angle, her newly transformed presence making the very air shimmer with contained authority.","Between them, Heidrun stood with the imperious confidence of someone who had never failed at any task she deemed worthy of her attention.","Glass containers materialized around the edges of the plot, their crystalline surfaces designed to preserve the unique properties of whatever they contained.","For her first attempt at harvesting, Heidrun approached a particularly vibrant cluster of green-gold shoots with the focused intensity of someone proving a point.","Her jaws opened with careful precision as she grasped the grass with movements that should have been flawless in their execution.","But...by the time her mouth moved toward the designated container, the Auric Vitae Grass had long since disappeared down her throat!","...!","Oh!","Her eyes shone with pleasure and contentment that she couldn’t quite suppress, the taste of the delicacy overwhelming her intentions with pure sensory bliss.","Yet almost immediately, guilt flickered across her crystalline gaze as she realized what had occurred.","She looked toward Noah with an expression that mixed embarrassment with determination, noting how he remained focused on his own harvesting work without judgment or criticism.","In that moment, Heidrun made a decisive promise to herself: she would successfully harvest a bundle without consuming it.","Her second attempt began with even greater resolve.","She approached another cluster with movements that carried the dignity of someone who had learned from previous mistakes.","Her jaws closed around the grass with deliberate control, every fiber of her being focused on the simple task of transportation.","But once again, by the time her mouth reached the container, the grass had vanished into her stomach!","She released a tremendous sigh of contentment that spoke to satisfaction beyond conscious control, her body betraying her intentions through pure instinctive response to the incredible delicacy.","But this...","How could she fail at such a fundamental task? Her! An Eminent Early Living Land Lifeform whose capabilities should have transcended such simple difficulties!","She could do this. She would do this!","And so she continued to try, each attempt ending in the same inevitable conclusion despite her growing determination to succeed at what should have been elementary work.","Noah, meanwhile, had fully immersed himself in the harvest with the focused attention. He moved with unhurried precision, his hands working the blessed soil while his mind contemplated the larger implications of what they were accomplishing.","As he worked, his thoughts turned to the limitations that currently constrained the Early Veiled Shore.","Those boundaries had served their purpose during the initial development phase, but now they represented obstacles to greater achievement.","The Shore possessed infinite potential that remained locked behind arbitrary restrictions!","His eyes began to shine with growing intensity as understanding formed into decision. The time had come to push beyond current boundaries, to attempt advancement that would elevate the Shore to new heights!","As his hands continued their careful work, new information began flowing across his consciousness.","|Harvest Quality Assessment: Current collection consists entirely of Standard Quality Auric Vitae Grass. Environmental factors and harvesting technique have maintained baseline potency without enhancement or degradation.|","The assessment continued as both he and Moiraine worked with methodical precision, their combined efforts gradually filling container after container with the precious green-gold vegetation.","After helping to harvest more than half of the available crop, Noah nodded with satisfaction at their progress. He turned to Moiraine, whose delicate yet serious approach to the work showed how seriously she took it.","\"Finish up,\" he said with quiet authority, his gaze shifting toward Heidrun, who had completely failed in all her attempts at harvesting.","The goat now lay upon the golden sands with a noticeably enlarged belly, her normally arrogant expression transformed into something that resembled drunken contentment from consuming hundreds of the precious grass shoots.","Noah shook his head with amusement at the sight before turning his attention to more pressing matters. His gaze swept across the radiant expanse of the Shore as he voiced his next intention!","\"I shall sacrifice more blood to expand the number of cultivation plots- 5 more.\"","HUUM!","New prompts appeared soon after!","|Five new cultivation areas require 90 drops of Early Creature blood for proper enhancement and soil preparation. Enhanced plots will provide increased yield compared to original specifications.|","Noah nodded his agreement without hesitation!","His palm split open with the practiced ease of someone who had grown accustomed to such sacrifices, and ninety dull crimson-gold drops flowed forth like liquid starlight. They moved with purposeful intent toward empty areas of the Shore, each drop carrying within its essence the concentrated power needed to transform golden sands into blessed agricultural territory.","The blood sank into the golden sands, and immediately the transformation began.","Five additional plots of fertile land rose from the Shore itself, their surfaces shining with the same white-gold radiance that marked areas touched by Early Creature essence.","Satisfied with this expansion, Noah turned back to Moiraine, who continued her delicate work with the serious concentration of someone who understood the importance of precision in all things.","\"When you are done harvesting,\" he instructed, \"you can begin planting the seeds here and on the other plots.\"","Moiraine, this terrifying being whose power now ranked among Honored Arch Living Existences, simply nodded with the respectful attention of a devoted follower.","\"Yes, Sir!\" she replied without the slightest trace of resentment at being assigned such humble work, even looking at it as something sacred!","Noah’s expression grew more serious as he surveyed the Shore that had become his sanctuary and foundation for advancement beyond normal limitations.","When he spoke again, his words were tyrannically heavy.","\"I wish...to fulfill the final condition for the advancement of the Early Veiled Shore.\"","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":3944,"title":"Chapter 3944: Chapter 3943: Oh! V","paragraphs":["The Shore had served them well in its current Budding state, but the limitations imposed by this initial phase had begun to constrain their potential for growth.","Too many restrictions remained in place, preventing them from accessing capabilities that lay just beyond their current reach.","He had Sacred Totems, but he could not call anymore Early Living Land Lifeforms!","He needed more plots of land to grow more and different Sacred Herbs.","He needed many things that the current level of the Early Veiled Shore was limited by.","He needed to advance to the Blooming Shore, regardless of the risks such transformation might entail!","The moment he voiced this intention, radiant archaic light began flowing around the entire Early Veiled Shore like aurora made manifest.","The very air seemed to thicken with anticipation as ancient weavings recognized the significance of what was being attempted!","HUUM!","New information cascaded across his consciousness.","|The final condition for Budding Shore advancement to Blooming Shore status is being challenged. Initiating trial protocols that have remained dormant for an unknown number of years.|","...!","|Shore Memory Gate manifestation imminent. Transference across multiple weavings of existence will commence, targeting a distant Lost Basic Record of an Early Creature.|","|Trial Designation: You will be assigned a random Record Body of an Early Living Marine Lifeform that closely matches your current level of power, with your power, complexity, glyphs...being carried over in addition to whatever power the Marine Lifeform holds. Success requires survival of the full encounter with the Early Creature present in the Lost Basic Record. Failure results in permanent termination of advancement potential.|","|Due to the extremely low probability of success, limited aid is permitted. Three summons of Early Living Land Lifeforms or other Lifeforms from the Early Veiled Shore are authorized, each manifestation lasting exactly five seconds before forced return.|","|Early Creature Record Threat Assessment- The Early Creature in this trial operates according to complete authenticity parameters. No limitations have been imposed on its capabilities. Survival probability approaches zero even for beings of Honored status. Simple endurance from luck and other factors represents the absolute limit of possible achievement.|","|Trial Duration: Objective survival time set at one minute.|","...!","Oh!","Oh goodness!","Noah reviewed the prompts with growing seriousness, understanding that what he was about to attempt represented a trial designed to test beings whose power dwarfed even the mightiest Living Existences.","Yet the potential rewards justified any risk, promising advancement that could elevate the Shore beyond all current limitations!","In a portion of the Early Veiled Shore, the golden sands began rising to form an archway that pulsed with its own inner radiance.","The Shore Memory Gate took shape with geometric precision that hurt to observe directly, its surface reflecting memories of events that had shaped the weavings of existence of distant possibilities.","Noah cast one final glance at his companions.","Moiraine continued her harvesting work with methodical precision, while Heidrun remained sprawled upon the sands with her expression of drunken satisfaction.","In the distance, others maintained their meditative positions, their advancement continuing through the passive benefits of the Shore’s unique environment.","\"Hoo...\" He breathed out and himself ready.","Without further hesitation, Noah walked toward the Shore Memory Gate and...disappeared into its radiant embrace!","The sensation of traversal was unique.","He felt himself moving across records so massive and fundamental that they dwarfed the accumulated knowledge of entire Folds, their weight pressing against his consciousness like the attention of unknown creatures!","These were memories that could cause even Living Existences to question their significance in the grand scheme of existence.","And after what felt like eons compressed into seconds, blinding blue light began to flash around him as new information flooded his awareness.","|Arrival confirmed at the Blooming Shore of Early Creature designated Thal’dorven the Primordial Fisher. Current location: Early Sacred Waters at depth of 400 fathoms.|","|Record Body Assignment: Refined Early Living Marine Lifeform - Designation: Prismatic Tide Serpent. Current capabilities include enhanced mobility, water manipulation, and moderate defensive adaptations.|","|Early Creature Thal’dorven the Primordial Fisher will begin harvesting activities within the next 30 seconds. Survival objective: Endure presence and activities for one minute duration. No additional objectives required.|","...!","Oh!","The Early Sacred Waters around him shimmered with authority so concentrated it made his borrowed body vibrate!","Dozens of other gorgeous and gloriously powerful Refined Early Living Marine Lifeforms swam in careful formations around him, their movements speaking to intelligence.","But despite their beauty and obvious power, all of them carried expressions of deep apprehension, as if they understood with perfect clarity that they would soon become ingredients for something far greater than themselves.","At their head swam a being that commanded attention through sheer presence alone.","An Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeform!","The Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeform resembled an anglerfish, but elevated to proportions and beauty that defied normal categories.","Its bioluminescent lure pulsed with patterns that spoke to deep-sea mysteries older than recorded history, while its form combined predatory grace with otherworldly elegance.","An Eminent Early Living Existential Glyph of Water blazed upon its sleek hide, surrounded by hundreds of Refined Glyphs of Water that created patterns of power visible even in the depths of these sacred waters.","When it opened its magnificent jaws to release a roar that sent reverberations across the aquatic realm, the sound carried challenge and defiance directed toward an Early Creature they could not yet perceive.","...!","Noah wanted to smack it right away.","Why the hell was it trying to die so quickly, he just needed a minute!","The moment that roar echoed through the depths, reality itself seemed to pause in recognition of what was about to unfold.","Then came the response that would test every assumption Noah held about the nature of power and survival.","An utterly terrifying aura bloomed and swept over everything with the inexorable force of judgment!","Just from this preliminary manifestation of presence, Noah felt five of his Basic Glyphs buzz and dim as if they were being shattered by the sheer weight of attention from something that existed beyond normal categories of existence.","Two Marine Lifeform had their bodies buzz as they went limp.","From...an aura alone.","Oh!","This 1 minute survival...was about to feel like eons, and that was if he survived the next few seconds!","Oh!!!"]},{"number":3945,"title":"Chapter 3945: Chapter 3944: Brutal! I","paragraphs":["A day could feel like passing seconds when immersed in the flow of meaningful work, yet a second could sometimes stretch into eons when faced with the prospect of imminent annihilation.","When confronted with an utterly terrifying force that existed beyond all normal categories of power, surviving a single minute seemed not merely difficult but fundamentally impossible, as if Existence itself had decreed that certain thresholds should never be crossed by lesser beings!","The aura of the Early Creature swept outward like a tide of compressed authority, carrying with it the weight of existence itself distilled into pure presence.","In the next moment, Noah felt his entire being freeze as comprehension dawned with horrifying clarity! From above, descending through the Early Sacred Waters with inexorable purpose, came what appeared to be a spear.","But as the object drew closer, its true nature became apparent.","This was no weapon of war, but something far more mundane and yet infinitely more terrifying in its implications. The thin implement carried a hook at its end that seemed to exert magnetic attraction on the very essence of existence itself, seeking to impale consciousness and drag it upward like the most common of catches.","It was a fishing hook.","A fishing hook!","Simple, utilitarian, and absolutely unstoppable in its descent toward the assembled Marine Lifeforms.","Noah watched in horrified fascination as the hook descended through the crystalline waters, its presence causing reality itself to bend around its path.","All around him, the Refined Early Living Marine Lifeforms froze as if time itself had stopped flowing through their bodies!","Only the magnificent Eminent creature that led them retained the ability to move, its superior nature allowing it to struggle against forces that rendered lesser beings helpless as caught fish.","But even the Eminent being’s resistance proved futile. The hook wove through the waters with casual precision, its path predetermined by intelligence.","It pierced through three of the Refined Marine Lifeforms with the ease of a needle passing through silk, then sprang upward with its harvest secured upon the barbed point.","Noah’s eyes buzzed with seriousness as he witnessed Refined Early Living Marine Lifeforms, beings whose power exceeded that of many Originus Venerant entities whose complexity ranged between ten and twenty million in both quotients, plucked from their element like goldfish caught by a child’s first fishing rod!","The casual nature of their capture spoke to power disparities so vast that normal categories of measurement became meaningless!","Within his borrowed body, the Refined Glyphs and Towers of Osmont that defined his accumulated strength began to resonate with alarm.","He could not even move when the fishing line descended, his existence locked in place by forces that recognized no resistance. A force that overcame his 1002% collective Resistances!","The only reason he had survived this initial harvest was pure chance, the random fortune that had placed him outside the hook’s predetermined path.","The difficulty of this Record was beyond anything he had imagined.","Even Honored Living Existences might struggle against the Early Creature whose casual fishing expedition could erase beings of tremendous power with no more effort than gathering ingredients for an evening meal!","At this moment of paralyzing realization, the fearsome Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeform released a roar that sent shockwaves through the sacred waters.","Its magnificent voice carried rage and defiance as it witnessed its companions being harvested like common livestock, the sound echoing wit weavings that spoke to fury!","The creature began rising toward the surface, its powerful form cutting through the water with movements that defied the crushing pressure of the Early Creature’s presence.","Behind it, the remaining Marine Lifeforms followed with the desperate urgency of beings who understood they were swimming toward their doom yet had no alternative.","Noah’s initial instinct was to remain hidden in the depths, to avoid drawing attention that could only result in his immediate destruction.","The logical choice was to let the others face whatever horror awaited above while he sought shelter in the darkest corners of these sacred waters.","But the moment this thought formed in his consciousness, his existence began buzzing with the unmistakable sensation of enormous danger approaching.","His enhanced intuition, honed through countless trials and elevated by the gifts of the Early Veiled Shore, screamed a warning that isolation would mean death.","If he remained behind while the others ascended, he would be hunted down and eliminated with even greater ease than those who had already been caught.","This was a terrifying realization that he trusted without question. He began rising alongside the other Marine Lifeforms, his borrowed body moving with reluctant urgency toward whatever awaited them at the surface!","As they emerged from the Early Sacred Waters, Noah’s enhanced perception took in everything he could observe in a single comprehensive sweep, as if time itself had frozen to allow him to catalog the impossible wonders that stretched before them.","First and most shocking of all, he saw the Early Creature itself.","Thal’dorven the Primordial Fisher!","He sat upon a sand dune with the casual posture of someone engaged in the most routine of activities.","The being’s appearance was simultaneously humanoid and utterly alien, ancient beyond measure yet carrying the vital presence of something that had never known decay or diminishment.","Its upper body was laid bare, revealing skin of burnished bronze that seemed to contain within its surface the accumulated light of countless suns!","Every muscle was gloriously defined and sculpted according to principles of perfection that transcended normal physical development.","The Early Creature’s lower body was covered by what appeared to be an animal skin skirt, yet even this simple garment shone with multicolored light that suggested construction from materials harvested from Eminent or Kleos Early Living Lifeforms!","The casual display of such precious materials as common clothing spoke to resources and capabilities that dwarfed anything Noah had previously encountered.","It showed the wonder and absolute mystery surrounding Early Creatures!","What truly captured his attention, however, was the expression of absolute calm and apathy that marked the Early Creature’s features as it attended to its fishing rod!"]},{"number":3946,"title":"Chapter 3946: Chapter 3945: Brutal! II","paragraphs":["With movements that carried no more emotional weight than preparing a simple meal, Thal’dorven removed the Marine Lifeforms caught upon his hook, using hands that moved with casual precision to snap their necks before tossing the bodies into a bucket placed conveniently beside him.","The sight was simultaneously mundane and horrifying, speaking to a perspective that viewed beings of tremendous power as nothing more than ingredients for dinner.","Did Noah...not look at Basic Early Living Marine Lifeforms just like this?","\"...\"","As his gaze swept beyond the Early Creature, Noah began to observe the fantastical layout of this Blooming Shore that served as Thal’dorven’s domain.","The realm stretched across horizons that seemed to exist beyond normal spatial limitations, each area dedicated to different aspects of cultivation and development that made his own Shore seem primitive by comparison.","Vast plots filled with radiant Sacred Herbs created patterns across the landscape, their arrangement suggesting knowledge accumulated over eons of experimentation and refinement.","Each plant pulsed with its own inner radiance!","Massive and complex Sacred Totems rose from strategic positions throughout the Shore, their bells towering five times higher than anything Noah had managed to construct.","The structures hummed with authority so concentrated it was visible as distortions in the surrounding air, their presence suggesting capabilities that transcended his current understanding of what such monuments could accomplish.","Groves of trees bearing vibrant fruits created areas of concentrated life that made the very atmosphere shimmer with barely contained vitality.","Each piece of fruit appeared to contain within its flesh the compressed essence of advancement itself, promising transformations that could elevate any being fortunate enough to partake of their bounty!","Throughout this impossible garden moved five unique Early Living Land Lifeforms, their presence adding layers of complexity to an already overwhelming display of accumulated resources.","Four appeared to be of Refined status, while the fifth was clearly Eminent, its size alone dwarfing anything he had previously encountered.","The Eminent Land Lifeform resembled a crystalline stag whose antlers branched into patterns that burned to observe directly, each point containing compressed Folds that pulsed with their own weavings!","Its mere presence seemed to stabilize the Shore itself, suggesting symbiotic relationships between Early Creatures and their chosen companions.","Additional features dotted the landscape with the kind of primitive grandeur that spoke to an entity that had achieved perfection through simplicity rather than complexity.","After absorbing this impossible wonder in what felt like both an instant and an epoch, Noah’s attention snapped back to more immediate concerns as he noticed the timer for his survival trial.","Forty-five seconds remained.","The countdown felt simultaneously too long and impossibly brief, each passing moment bringing him closer to either triumph or absolute annihilation!","He looked ahead as the Marine Lifeforms around him began roaring their defiance, their voices combining into a chorus of challenge directed toward the Early Creature who had dared to treat them as mere prey.","Their combined might created waves of authority that would have impressed even Honored Living Existences, yet their display seemed to have no more effect than children shouting at a mountain!","Children trying to topple an elephant!","Thal’dorven looked up at them with what might have been amusement, his expression shifting from casual indifference to something approaching mild interest.","When he smiled, the expression carried the weight of Existence aligning themselves according to his will.","In the next moment, a single Glyph appeared upon his forehead with the brilliance of a Wheel being born.","The symbol blazed with the authority of Living Law itself, its presence transforming the fundamental nature of reality in the immediate area!","The moment the Glyph manifested, a massive white hand descended from the skies above with the inexorable certainty of gravity itself.","The appendage was composed of pure Living Law given form, its fingers spread wide to encompass half of the remaining Marine Lifeforms in a grip that wanted no resistance!","Noah felt his existence freeze once again as the hand approached, but this time his paralysis was not complete. The combined effects of his accumulated power and the desperate urgency of the situation allowed him to retain just enough mobility to act, though every second of delay brought the descending hand closer to sealing his fate.","The moment those massive fingers closed around him, he would be crushed out of existence with no more ceremony than swatting an insect.","He knew this!","He understood this with absolute certainty, the knowledge burning through his consciousness like acid through flesh!","Gritting his teeth against the overwhelming pressure that sought to reduce him to helpless prey, Noah’s mind buzzed with command!","|Summon the Lifeform Moiraine!|","BOOM!","...!","In the next instant, the space around his Marine Lifeform body buzzed with the arrival of something glorious!","The illusory yet tangible form of Moiraine materialized beside him, her nine winged halos and five hundred Eminent Glyphs blazing with authority that momentarily challenged even the oppressive presence of the Early Creature.","She was shocked as she took in their surroundings, her enhanced perception immediately observing the impossible nature of their situation!","But the connection between her consciousness and Noah’s allowed her to understand the critical nature of their circumstances without need for lengthy explanation.","His voice reached her through the chaos of clashing authorities, carrying the urgency of someone whose existence hung by the thinnest of threads!","|Keep us alive for the next five seconds!|","WAA!","Her existence erupted with power as understanding crystallized into action. Without hesitation, without calculation of odds or consideration of personal safety, she roared her acknowledgment.","\"Yes, Sir!\"","...!","Valiant.","Glorious.","For him...she would give anything!","Every one of her five hundred Eminent Glyphs blazed with simultaneous brilliance as she channeled the full extent of her accumulated power against the white hand descending upon them!","The collision of forces that followed would determine whether Noah’s trial continued or ended in the crushing grip of a terrifying authority made manifest.","And with the power of an Early Creature, it was truly hard to say just how the scales would tip!"]},{"number":3947,"title":"Chapter 3947: Chapter 3946: Brutal! III","paragraphs":["At the explosive outburst of Moiraine’s power, reality itself seemed to bend around the collision of forces.","Her five hundred Eminent Glyphs of Paradox blazed with such concentrated authority that the very fabric of existence groaned under the strain of containing such tremendous energy!","The white hand, descending with the inexorable certainty of existential evolution judgment, shockingly deviated slightly in its descent.","For a breathless moment that stretched across eons, the massive appendage of Law trembled as it encountered a deviation of resistance it had not expected to find!","Moiraine’s accumulated power, refined through processes that had elevated her beyond a normal Living Existence, created a deviation that even the Early Creature’s casual authority could not immediately penetrate!","Yet the pause was brief. The white hand completed its descent, managing to grasp half of the remaining Marine Lifeforms in its crushing grip, but Noah found himself excluded from its harvest.","Moiraine’s intervention had been sufficient to deflect the targeting, though at tremendous cost to her own reserves of power.","On the shore, Thal’dorven the Primordial Fisher looked genuinely surprised for the first time since the trial began.","His expression shifted from casual indifference to interest as he observed the unexpected resistance to his authority.","At this moment of reprieve, the surviving Marine Lifeforms launched their desperate retaliation!","The magnificent Eminent creature that led them roared with renewed fury as it directed the others in a coordinated assault against the Early Creature who had dared to treat them as mere prey.","Their combined might created waves of authority that would have impressed even Royal Living Existences, yet their display seemed to barely register on Thal’dorven’s consciousness!","Moiraine materialized more solidly beside Noah, her form radiating protective determination as she positioned herself between him and any further threats. Her nine winged halos spun with increasing velocity while her Glyphs prepared for whatever horrors might come next.","And yet, as their desperate resistance unfolded, a voice boomed across the battlefield with such exotic power that reality itself seemed to reshape around its utterances.","\"That is not the power of a little fish at the Refined level or even simple Eminent level. And was that Paradox? Haha, are one of my lesser brethren attempting a shore advancement right now? You should not have allowed me to know!\"","...!","Oh?","Oh!","The voice of the Early Creature carried weight!","Heavy weight!","Each syllable resonated through dimensions, while undertones suggested depths of experience.","The sound was simultaneously beautiful and terrifying, like hearing the voice of existence itself speaking with casual amusement about the struggles of insects.","The exotic power contained within those words caused all the Marine Lifeforms, including Noah and Moiraine, to freeze as understanding dawned with horrifying clarity.","They were fucked!","Instantly, with movement that transcended normal concepts of speed, Thal’dorven appeared in front of the most powerful Eminent Marine Lifeform.","The creature that had led their desperate charge now found itself face to face with something that existed beyond all resistance.","The Early Creature tapped out with casual precision, a single finger making contact with the Eminent being’s magnificent form.","The result...was immediate and absolute.","The Marine Lifeform collapsed and began unraveling into streams of light, its accumulated power dissipating like smoke before wind as its very existence was casually negated!","Simply.","Calmly.","Horrifically!","Thal’dorven smiled with dangerous satisfaction as his gaze swept across the remaining fish, his expression carrying the particular joy of someone who had just discovered an unexpected source of entertainment.","\"Do you know that if the attempt of advancement fails from my actions, I actually get a boon from it? Now that I know, I will naturally get serious and not allow you to pass! Haha, how much time do you have left? It won’t matter as I won’t let this go for even another second. I will just wipe the rest of these weak fishes out!\"","Noah’s expression became unfathomably heavy as the full implications of their situation crystallized with devastating clarity.","At such a moment of absolute despair, Moiraine’s voice rang out with desperate defiance!","\"YAA!\"","She had two seconds remaining in her manifestation, but her eyes blazed with fierce determination as she shot forward.","She understood that her Sir was attempting something grand here, something that could reshape the very foundations of his power!","The casual joy this being took in causing his failure ignited fury within her!","She would not allow this.","Seas of golden Paradox began gathering around her form as she prepared to expend everything in a final desperate gambit.","Her accumulated power condensed into patterns of glory, wonders of a myraid weavings of Paradoxes forming!","Yet the expression on the Early Creature’s face remained placid, almost bored, as he observed her gathering might.","Above his head, with the casual ease of someone swatting an annoying insect, another Glyph appeared.","PAH!","The symbol flashed with brilliance that hurt to perceive directly, and Noah’s enhanced vision identified it with growing horror.","This was not merely an Eminent or Refined Glyph.","It was...","A Kleos Early Living Existential Glyph of Law!","Kleos!","It instantly erased Moiraine into dust, her accumulated power and tremendous advancement reduced to scattered particles that drifted away on calm winds.","Her short journey in this record came to an end as she was sent back!","The casual ease with which she was destroyed spoke to power disparities that rendered all resistance meaningless.","|The Arch Living Existence, Moiraine, has been forcefully laid to rest from this Record. Her manifestation has been terminated through absolute authority.|","The prompt that appeared carried finality that stated no argument or hope of reversal!","One of his greatest achievements, the being he had elevated beyond defined categories through careful application of gifts had been casually obliterated by forces that recognized no limit to their dominion.","The eyes of the Early Creature remained calm and apathetic as his Glyph prepared to flash again, its target now clearly focused upon Noah himself!","There would be no reprieve, no moment of hesitation, no opportunity for desperate last stands!","Yet at this moment of absolute certainty, Noah stepped forward with tyrannical fearlessness that defied every rational calculation.","He could fail.","The possibility hung before him like an executioner’s blade, carrying with it consequences that would echo across every aspect of his existence.","Failure would come with results so heavy they might crush his ambitions and his very essence.","Yet at this critical juncture, he did not call out for anyone else to manifest beside him.","When faced with the impossible, when confronted with forces that transcended every normal category of resistance, there were still ways to survive.","One such method was knowledge. And understanding how to wield it with precision!"]},{"number":3948,"title":"Chapter 3948: Chapter 3947: The Weight of Obsession! I","paragraphs":["In the moment before the Early Creature’s Glyph could flash with terminal authority, Noah spoke with calm certainty.","\"You are a Record of yourself. You are already dead.\"","...!","HUUM!","The words struck Thal’dorven with such unexpected force that his casual demeanor faltered.","The Early Creature stopped, his Living authority pausing as he focused his full attention upon this insignificant Marine Lifeform who had dared to speak truth that cut to his heart of existence itself!","In the next moment, Noah’s serpentine form began changing as his own glorious humanoid shape manifested.","His bare upper body emerged with the same primitive majesty that marked Thal’dorven, his skin gleaming with inner radiance while muscles spoke to power!","Power!","Noah stared coldly at the Early Creature as his understanding crystallized into strategy.","\"Someone of your stature should be able to sense it,\" he said with calculating precision, each word chosen to cut through layers of self-deception that even Records could maintain.","\"You are but an echo, a memory given form but no longer truly Living. The rewards you speak of gaining from my failure are illusions, phantoms of desires that belonged to the being you once were but can never be again.\"","His voice carried tyrannical authority as he continued!","\"You possess no capacity to benefit from my success or failure. You are a shadow cast by light that no longer shines, a story told by voices that have long since fallen silent. Whatever obsessions drive you now are the chains of a dead past binding a present that should not exist.\"","HUUM!","The Early Creature’s expression shifted to something that combined majesty with profound despondence, of power mingled with existential sorrow!","\"Of course,\" Thal’dorven replied, his voice carrying weavings of acceptance mixed with endless regret. \"I know that I am dead. The knowledge burns through every moment of this false existence. But understanding changes nothing.\"","His gaze grew distant as he continued, \"I still carry my obsessions, the fundamental patterns that defined who I was when life flowed through these veins. Obsession, you see, is one of the more terrifying tools anyone can possess. It transcends death, outlasts reason, persists when every logical foundation has crumbled away.\"","The Early Creature’s smile carried the weight of tragedy as he focused once more upon Noah.","\"No, I do not have to kill you. But my obsession, who I was and who I remain even as a Record, will ensure that you are killed. Because some patterns run deeper than existence itself.\"","Noah nodded with calm understanding, recognizing the fundamental nature of what they faced.","Yet even as acceptance settled over him, curiosity burned with its own form of desperate intensity.","\"Before you kill me then,\" he said with the measured tone of someone requesting a final favor, \"could you tell me more about us? About why you died? And why others are nowhere to be seen?\"","These words caused the Record of the Early Creature to have his eyes flash with genuine surprise, awareness focusing upon weavings that had not occurred to him until this moment!","\"The others are missing?\" Thal’dorven said, his voice carrying undertones of growing concern. \"This...\"","He seemed contemplative as understanding began to dawn, ancient mind processing information that challenged assumptions he had carried since his death!","Soon he shook his head with a smile that mixed sorrow with resigned determination.","\"You have already utilized your one chance to call for help from your Land Lifeforms,\" he said, returning to the immediate situation. \"And you would need to survive here for at least five minutes to elevate from Budding Shore to Blooming Shore. There is time enough for you to obtain information regarding what happened all those eons ago and connect it to whatever age this has become.\"","His expression hardened as obsession reasserted its dominion over curiosity!","\"But again, my nature will not allow that. My personality was inherently selfish and self-serving, and even in death, obsession does not change. I will gain nothing from your success, yet my Record will feel satisfied in causing your failure.\"","The Early Creature’s smile turned cold as he voiced the fundamental cruelty that drove his actions!","\"If I am dead, why should others prosper? What benefit do I gain from your advancement? The outlook is simple- I have nothing to gain from your success, everything to gain from your failure.\"","The philosophy was extremely cruel and self-serving, speaking to darkness that transcended malice!","As he spoke these words, the terrifying Kleos Glyph on his forehead flared with renewed intensity while thousands of other Glyphs materialized across his form, each one preparing to unleash forces that would end absolutely everything!","Noah shook his head with tyrannical certainty, his gaze carrying the weight of someone who had calculated possibilities beyond the immediate situation.","He had calculated much!","\"I do not have only a single chance to call a Land Lifeform,\" he said with calm precision. \"And the time I need to survive is significantly less than what you believe.\"","As he spoke, his eyes flicked upward to observe the timer that had been counting down since the trial began. Five seconds remained.","At this critical moment, brilliance flashed before him as a terrifying aura manifested with the force of existential intervention.","The resplendent white goat, Heidrun, appeared in front of Noah with such majesty that even the Early Creature paused in recognition of what he was witnessing.","Her lustrous coat blazed with inner radiance while her crystalline eyes carried determination that transcended her usual arrogance!","She positioned herself as if she would defend Noah against anything and everything, her stance speaking to loyalty that had been earned through simple kindness and respect.","After all, this man had fed her, had provided her with delicacies beyond imagination.","Even when she had failed repeatedly to harvest anything, he had not criticized or discouraged her efforts.","He was a good Early Creature!","She would save him if salvation was needed!","When Thal’dorven saw Heidrun, genuine shock crossed his features for the second time since the trial began.","His voice carried amazement that bordered on disbelief!","\"How could you possibly have something like that with a mere Budding Shore?!\"","Noah looked calmly at this being as the final seconds trickled away, his voice carrying the weight of absolute conviction.","\"Because my obsession... is greater and more quintessential than yours.\"","With those words, as the timer reached its final moment...","BOOM!","Everything became painted in brilliant gold!"]},{"number":3949,"title":"Chapter 3949: Chapter 3948: The Weight of Obsession! II","paragraphs":["Everything became painted in brilliant gold as Noah felt utterly complex radiance cover him from head to toe!","The sensation was simultaneously overwhelming and gentle.","Prompts began unfolding before his vision with the stately precision of recognition!","|You have successfully survived one minute before an Early Creature against all odds. This achievement transcends normal categories of possibility and marks you as worthy of advancement beyond current limitations.|","|All requirements to advance the Budding Shore to Blooming Shore status have been achieved. Initiation of transformation commencing immediately.|","...!","The prompts came in unending wave as Noah felt both relief and weariness!","And they continued.","|Your Early Veiled Shore will now begin advancing and expanding according to parameters established during the earliest epochs of existence. Prepare for fundamental alteration of your domain.|","|Shore expansion multiplier is 500%. Total area increase from baseline specifications will reshape the nature of your Shore.|","|Early Living Land Lifeform capacity has been increased to twenty-five beings. Current occupancy: five slots are utilized by the existence of Heidrun alone, reflecting her exceptional nature and requirements.|","|Early Sacred Herb procurement now possible through utilization of Records obtained from the Blooming Shore of the Early Creature designated as Thal’dorven the Primordial Fisher. Requirements include the sacrifice of existing Sacred Herbs plus drops of Early Creature blood.|","|Trade network access may be established- Connection to Records of other Early Creature’s Shores allows for resource exchange and knowledge acquisition.|","....!","The Prompts just continued coming relentlessly as the advancement of the shore came with utterly too many points!","And horrifically, it was not done.","Oh, it was not done!","|Early Folds Plot System Unlocked. Through the advancement to Blooming Shore status, you have gained access to the ancient practice of Early Fold Designation - a cultivation method that transcends normal agricultural limitations by creating living pocket dimensions specifically attuned to the growth of singular, incomparably precious Early Sacred Herbs.|","|You may designate up to nine (9) specialized Plots as Early Folds, each existing as a miniature living dimensional space anchored within your Blooming Shore. Each Early Fold can only cultivate one specific type of Unique Early Sacred Herb, but the herbs grown within these folds will possess potency and properties that exceed anything achievable through conventional methods.|","|Creating an Early Fold requires the sacrifice of 100 Drops of Early Creature Blood to establish the dimensional anchor, plus an additional 50 Drops to attune the fold to a specific herb type. The initial seed or sample of the desired Unique Early Sacred Herb must be provided during the designation process and will be consumed to establish the fold’s weaving of Existence.|","|Each Early Fold exists as a stable Living pocket dimension that cannot be detected or accessed by external forces, protected by the fundamental authority of the Early Creature who created it. The folds are immune to temporal manipulation, spatial interference, and existential disruption by beings below Early Creature status.|","|The most extraordinary capability of Unique Early Sacred Herbs lies in their ability to grant understanding of Lost Forgotten Principles - fundamental truths about existence that were known to the earliest beings but have since been erased from Existence itself. These principles transcend normal concepts of authority, law, or power, representing the foundational mechanics upon which all existence was originally constructed.|","|Example Lost Forgotten Principle: The Principle of Existential Primacy- The authority to declare oneself as the fundamental basis upon which other typed of existence depend on, making one’s continued existence a prerequisite for the continued existence of other things. Mastery of this principle rendered Early Creatures nigh impossible to kill by making their death equivalent to existential annihilation.|","...!","|Current Status- 0/9 Early Folds designated. Designation process available immediately upon availability of required materials and selection of desired Unique Early Sacred Herb specimens.|","...!","Sheesh!","Sheesh!!!","\"...\"","Noah had no words at the endless array of prompts.","This time, there were truly too many, and each was more profound than the other!","Noah felt the golden glow beginning to fade as the transformation completed its initial phase.","His consciousness descended back into his own Early Veiled Shore, the Memory Gate crumbling as its purpose was fulfilled.","His feet touched the familiar golden sands with the relief of someone returning home after journeying through a place of impossible danger.","Yet even as he sighed with the satisfaction of survival against insurmountable odds, his attention was immediately captured by changes occurring throughout his domain.","The edges of the mist that had always marked the boundaries of his Shore began churning with new energy, swirling patterns that spoke to expansion beyond previous limitations.","In the next moment, those boundaries exploded outward.","The Early Veiled Shore transformed before his eyes as it evolved from its Budding state into the full glory of a Blooming Shore!","The golden sands stretched in all directions, encompassing territory that dwarfed his previous domain.","Where once he had possessed a sanctuary of significant but limited scope, he now commanded a domain that approached the scale of proper Early Veiled Shore!","Six new radiant trees materialized to join the original three that had anchored his domain since its inception, their forms towering higher than before while their branches spread to create canopies.","Each tree pulsed with its own unique weaving of life-giving energy, their roots extending through dimensional space to create networks of connections!","The crystalline waters that had always marked one edge of his domain now expanded into a proper sea, its shores creating bays and inlets that suggested possibilities of even more wonders.","The water itself had grown denser with life.","Throughout the vastly expanded landscape, new features manifested with a kind of primitive grandeur!","Areas specifically designated for different forms of farming stretched across horizons. The plots where Auric Vitae Grass currently grew appeared insignificant compared to the possibilities now available.","Noah stood at the center of this transformed domain, taking in all the new features as he went over the lengthy prompts again and again!","The Early Veiled Shore had become something that approached the magnificence he had witnessed in Thal’dorven’s domain, though still primitive compared to what eons of development might accomplish.","The Blooming Shore represented potential that stretched toward horizons he could barely imagine, each new feature promising opportunities for advancement others could not fathom!","And he...was just getting started!"]},{"number":3950,"title":"Chapter 3950: Chapter 3949: The Past and the Dead! I","paragraphs":["The golden light of advancement continued to cascade across Noah’s newly transformed Blooming Shore, each wave of enhancement settling into the expanded realm.","Yet even as he stood at the epicenter of this profound transformation, even as the very fabric of his domain reshaped itself according to his will and achievement, a deeper truth swept across existence itself.","For all the magnitude of his accomplishments, for all the terrifying power he had accumulated and the impossible trials he had overcome, even he remained but a single thread in a weaving of Existence whose full scope defied comprehension!","Existence did not pause to acknowledge any triumphs.","The vast machinery of existence continued its rotation, indifferent to whether any particular being rose to greatness or fell into obscurity.","Countless eons ago, long before Noah’s name had ever been whispered into being, existence had unfolded according to its own immutable rhythms.","Its own unperceivable weavings!","Galaxies had burst into brilliant life and faded into cold darkness. Universes had expanded from singular points of density before collapsing back into the void that birthed them.","Entire Cosmos had danced their weavings across dimensions that stretched beyond imagination, each one containing within its boundaries billions upon billions of worlds, each world harboring its own stories of triumph and tragedy!","Omniverses had risen like titans from the primordial chaos, their boundaries encompassing realities so vast that the mind could not grasp their scope, only to shatter like glass when their time reached its ordained conclusion!","Wheels of Existence themselves, those fundamental constructs that served as the building blocks of Folds... had come into being and underwent Breakings and Transformations constantly.","Through all of this, existence had remained constant.","It required no single being to validate its continuation.","It needed no particular consciousness to witness its wonders.","The great machine ground on, as it always had, as it always would, producing marvels and catastrophes with equal indifference!","And yet, in the face of such overwhelming vastness, a question lingered.","What of Noah Osmont in this grand scheme of existence?","Would future beings speak of Noah Osmont with the same reverence reserved for Early Creatures? Would he even be known?","Would he become simply another story told in whispered tones, another fable shared among those who sought to understand the mysteries of power and transcendence? Another cautionary tale about the hubris of those who dared to reach beyond? Or would he not even be remembered?","The answer to this question remained shrouded in the mists of uncertainty, hidden behind veils of Quintessence!","For in the end, only time itself possessed the authority to determine which names would be remembered and which would fade into the silence of forgotten ages.","---","Across the infinite weavings of existence, in domains so distant from Noah’s transformed Shore that the light of his achievement would take eons to travel the space between them, other stories continued to unfold according to their own inexorable logic!","In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, where reality bent and twisted according to principles that defied rational understanding, a scene of deceptive simplicity played out upon a world so insignificant that its destruction would barely register as a footnote.","The world itself existed as little more than a mote of dust.","Contained within a small universe, which itself was nestled within a larger cosmos, which in turn resided within a grand Existential Domain, which was but a single component of a massive Omniverse, which finally found its place within one of the countless Wheels of Existence that formed the foundation of existence itself.","Unperceivably small!","Upon this utterly inconsequential world, in a kingdom whose borders would have seemed laughably small to beings like Living Existences, a muddy road stretched between settlements that housed creatures whose greatest ambitions involved little more than the accumulation of modest wealth and the avoidance of starvation.","The road itself bore the scars of countless seasons, its surface a treacherous mixture of churned earth and standing water that reflected the gray sky above.","Along its edges, where the grass grew thick and wild, merchants and travelers had worn narrow paths that spoke to the endless migration of those seeking better fortunes in distant lands.","Thatched-roof buildings lined the road at irregular intervals, their walls constructed from timber and stone quarried from local hills.","Smoke rose from countless chimneys, carrying with it the scent of wood fires and the simple meals that sustained populations of thousands.","Through this medieval landscape moved the procession of humanity in all its varied forms.","Farmers trudged along the muddy road with carts laden with the fruits of their labor, their faces weathered by sun and wind, their hands bearing the calluses that marked a lifetime of honest toil.","Peasants walked alongside these farmers, their clothing patched and repatched until the original fabric had become little more than a foundation for layers of practical repair.","Among these humble travelers moved figures whose very presence spoke to the rigid hierarchies that governed this simple world.","Slaves shuffled along in chains that clinked with each step, their heads bowed in submission and in the bone-deep exhaustion.","Their guards rode alongside on horseback, their hands never far from the weapons that ensured compliance with the established order.","And occasionally, carriages would roll along the road with wheels that threw mud in all directions.","Through windows of real glass, faces peered out with the casual arrogance of royalty.","It was beside this road, in a spot where the mud had pooled particularly deep and the grass grew particularly thick, that a figure sat in apparent desolation!","At first glance, he appeared to be nothing more than another casualty of a world that showed little mercy to those without means or connections.","His clothes hung in tatters around a frame that seemed diminished by hunger and exposure, their original color lost beneath layers of grime.","Yet there was something in his posture that suggested deeper truths hidden beneath!","His skin, beneath the accumulated dirt and wear of his chosen disguise, possessed a vitality that seemed to pulse with each heartbeat.","At this moment of deceptive tranquility, when the beggar sat in perfect stillness beside the muddy road while the procession of humanity continued its ancient dance around him, the very fabric of space began to distort!","BZZT!","The distortion started as little more than a shimmer in the air. But it grew with each passing second, becoming a tear in reality.","From this tear in existence descended a figure whose presence transformed the very nature of the space around him!","Duke Elagabalus materialized with slow majesty, his form radiating power.","This being of great power descended through the mundane atmosphere of a world whose greatest concerns involved the price of grain and the changing of seasons.","His ancient eyes swept across the scene below with the particular disdain.","The humans who moved along the muddy road continued their daily routines as if nothing had changed, their limited perception unable to register the presence of something that could erase their entire world from existence with less effort than swatting an insect!","Duke Elagabalus floated downward, his attention focused entirely upon the figure who sat beside the road in apparent destitution.","\"You have seen everything so far?\" he asked, his tone carrying the careful respect of one powerful being addressing another whose true capabilities remained hidden beneath layers of deliberate misdirection.","\"We were able to obtain the body of an Early Creature as I gave Diviticus the task of reanimating it. But...\"","At such a moment, the beggar smiled.","And he spoke calmly!","\"What worries you is that Ozymandias,\" the beggar said, his voice carrying none of the weakness suggested by his appearance. Each word emerged with the clarity of crystal and the weight of absolute certainty.","\"Logically, you are convinced, as you rightfully should be, that he cannot possibly be an Early Creature. This is a correct line of thought. It is only logical, but...\"","He paused, allowing the silence to stretch.","\"What of the infinitesimally small chance that he is an Early Creature? Is that why you came to bother me?\"","An immense silence settled over the muddy road, broken only by the distant sound of carriage wheels splashing through puddles and the murmur of voices engaged in the simple business of survival.","In that silence, two beings of unimaginable power regarded each other across a gulf that separated not just their physical forms but their fundamental approaches to the mysteries that governed existence itself!"]},{"number":3951,"title":"Chapter 3951: Chapter 3950: The Past and the Dead! II","paragraphs":["Duke Elagabalus felt the weight of that silence pressing against him.","\"You know already, Duke Schrodinger,\" he said.","\"You are one of the true leaders of Paradox. If there really is a possible threat of an Early Creature for the Paradoxes, only those like you can handle it.\"","The beggar’s smile deepened, and suddenly the illusion of poverty seemed as thin as morning mist.","Though his clothes remained tattered and his position unchanged beside the muddy road, there was something in his bearing that spoke of terrifying Paradoxical Authority!","Schrodinger!","Oh, Schrodinger!","\"Ah,\" Schrodinger said, \"You see, Duke Elagabalus, you have stumbled upon the very heart of what it means to exist within Paradox itself.\"","He gestured with one hand toward the road where a merchant’s cart had just struck a particularly deep pothole, sending muddy water splashing in all directions while the driver cursed with creative eloquence.","\"Consider the nature of uncertainty,\" Schrodinger continued, his eyes taking on that terrible brightness.","\"In the realm of Paradox, we exist perpetually suspended between states of being and non-being, between possibility and impossibility. Sinners. Anchored. What is Paradox, if not the acknowledgment that reality itself refuses to conform to the simple categories that lesser minds demand?\"","HUUM!","The air around them began to shimmer with barely visible energies as Schrodinger’s true nature began to bleed through his carefully constructed disguise.","\"At this very moment, Ozymandias exists in a state of quantum uncertainty regarding his fundamental nature. He is simultaneously an Early Creature and not an Early Creature, a being of existential significance and a mere Fold Dweller of limited scope. His true nature remains hidden behind the veil of observation until the moment when certainty collapses possibility into a single, immutable, magisterial truth.\"","...!","Duke Elagabalus found himself leaning forward despite every instinct that warned him against showing such open interest.","\"But surely,\" he said, \"there must be some way to determine-....\"","\"Ah, but that is where you misunderstand the beauty of true Paradox,\" Schrodinger interrupted with a gentle correction.","\"The moment we attempt to observe and categorize, we fundamentally alter the nature of what we observe. Our very act of seeking certainty changes the parameters of the equation. Until that moment of collapse occurs, Ozymandias remains beautifully, terrifyingly uncertain.\"","WAA!","When Schrodinger finished these words, Duke Elagabalus released a sigh that carried the weight of eons.","\"That does not advance any solution here,\" he said, frustration bleeding through his carefully maintained composure.","At such words, Schrodinger’s smile took on a change that transformed it from gentle amusement into something far more dangerous.","\"So what if he turns out to be an Early Creature?\" he asked with casual indifference.","\"Are you so fearful of an Early Creature?\"","BOOM!","Duke Elagabalus’s response came without hesitation, driven by honesty!","\"Yes,\" he said, and there was no shame in his admission. \"I am very much afraid of an Early Creature. Anyone with sense of logic would be. Anyone who does not fear an Early Creature knows nothing of existence!\"","...!","The admission rang across the muddy road with the clarity of absolute truth.","Schrodinger’s smile widened at these words, and he shook his head with patient amusement.","\"Fear,\" he said, \"is nothing more than the mind’s response to that which it cannot understand or control. We fear the darkness because we cannot see what moves within it. We fear death because we cannot comprehend what lies beyond the veil of existence. We fear Early Creatures because their power operates according to principles that transcend our ability to categorize or predict.\"","He paused to watch as another carriage rolled past, its wheels throwing muddy water in all directions while the occupants remained blissfully unaware of who was around them!","\"But fear, you see, is born from ignorance. Once something is truly understood, once its nature is catalogued and its capabilities mapped, fear transforms into something else entirely. It becomes respect, perhaps, or caution, or even admiration. But fear itself dissolves like mist before the sun of comprehension.\"","Duke Elagabalus remained silent, his ancient mind working to process everything.","At this moment of contemplative quiet, Schrodinger’s expression shifted to something that carried absolute confidence!","\"I do not fear any Early Creature,\" he said with calm certainty, \"because I have means to protect myself and you all if an Early Creature does ever come to light.\"","...!","Oh!","\"What?\" he demanded, his composure cracking. \"How?!\"","Schrodinger smiled as he looked out across the muddy road.","At that precise moment, a particularly ornate carriage approached their position, its wheels striking a deep pothole with enough force to send a cascade of wet mud splashing across Schrodinger’s already tattered robes.","...!","He wiped away the filth with movements that spoke to infinite patience, his expression never changing even as the royal occupant of the carriage looked down at him with an expression of supreme arrogance before proceeding along the road without a backward glance.","Schrodinger did nothing about this casual insult, his attention already returning to the matters that truly demanded his focus.","\"To understand this,\" he said, \"you would have to recollect something from the Stories of the Earliest Folds. Do you remember what happened after Paradox was locked away the first time?\"","Duke Elagabalus felt his expression shift to one of weary resignation.","\"Duke Schrodinger,\" he said, \"I have heard the Stories of the Earliest Folds countless times. I don’t want to-\"","\"And you will now listen to it again another time,\" Schrodinger interrupted, his voice taking on the stern authority of one who would accept no argument!","Duke Elagabalus fell silent, recognizing the futility of resistance when faced with such a being.","Schrodinger settled back against the muddy home, his eyes taking on the distant look of one who gazed across eons to witness events that had shaped existence itself!","When he began to speak, his voice carried the cadence someone telling...a version of a story!","\"The Creature moved across the Earliest Folds with a sense of melancholy,\" he began, \"as it found that uniquely, it missed The Living Paradox. Having been with it for so long, it found that it actually missed its company!\""]},{"number":3952,"title":"Chapter 3952: Chapter 3951: The Past and the Dead! III","paragraphs":["\"So The Creature had purpose and a beginning, but yet found itself longing for a company it knew was not good for it.","To make up for this absence, The Creature went to observe all the things born from the spread of its Everything by the Living Paradox.","And...the closest Lifeforms it enjoyed seeing, as if they were its own children, were the Early Creatures.\"","Schrodinger’s voice took on notes of paternal sadness as he continued. \"It observed them. How they were trying to find their own purpose. But they stumbled. They constantly fought with Inevitabilities, for after The Living Paradox was locked away, Inevitabilities became even more rampant throughout the Earliest Folds.\"","...!","The tragedy began to unfold as Schrodinger painted pictures with words!","\"The Creature had the now immensely powerful Living Origin and The Living Concept constantly protecting it, so it did not have to worry about such threats.","But the Early Creatures...its children, began to die in the hands of Inevitabilities!","It hurt it tremendously every time it observed this injustice, so it traversed across the Folds and called together The Living Elemental, Living Origin, Living Concept, Living Spirit, Living Dimension, Living Law, Living Temporal, Living Emotive, and Living Quantum.\"","Duke Elagabalus found himself leaning forward despite his earlier reluctance, caught up in the flow of narrative he heard many times before, but the details in this one seemed much clearer!","\"He gathered them and said he wished to protect the fruits of his Everything, and wanted to build something that would help the poor Lifeforms gain the power to fight against Inevitabilities.","Hesitant, THE Living Existences looked at each other before ultimately... they agreed to work with The Creature to create a place of refuge and potential for progression of power that they deemed...","The Early Veiled Shores!\"","HUUM!","The Early Veiled Shores...those legendary realms that existed at the very foundations of power itself, had been born from The Creature’s desire to protect its children.","\"The Creature was extremely happy at this collaboration,\" Schrodinger continued, \"as he told THE Living Existences that they would not regret this decision.","They worked for an entire eon until they designed and scattered Early Veiled Shores for Early Creatures to use as refuge and as lands to elevate their own Everything.","The Creature received his own Early Veiled Shore that was made unfathomably unique, and he found himself lost in the designs he helped to make himself as he began spending lots of time in this small, isolated domain.","In his own shore.","After he saw the Early Creatures obtained the Early Veiled Shores and could hide from Inevitabilities and even begin growing themselves, he left them to their devices, content with what he had done as he disappeared...lost in his own Shore.\"","\"...\"","But the story did not end with triumph and harmony as one somehow hoped.","\"In the meantime, the Early Creatures progressed. They grew strong over the eons and successfully became powerful enough through their Shores to fight and win against extremely terrifying Inevitabilities. But with power came... chaos.\"","The inevitable tragedy began to unfold as Schrodinger’s voice took on notes of disappointment.","\"The Early Creatures gradually began vying for supremacy, going across the Folds and beginning cycles of untold chaos.","They took under their banner Inevitabilities, Living Lifeforms, and all sorts of other Lifeforms for the sake of their Shores.","And from peace... chaos began to propagate wildly.\"","\"And because THE Living Order was destroyed in the fight against Paradox, there was no return to Order!","And without order, what could there be apart from chaos?","And so, Early Creatures lived as they wished!","Chaos spread across the Earliest Folds.","The balance that had been so carefully constructed began to crumble as those who had been saved by The Creature’s intervention turned their gifts toward conquest and domination.","The Living Law could not stand the chaos.","It went before the Early Creatures and admonished them, telling them this was not what they and THE Creature had envisioned.","But the Early Creatures did not listen.","They said the only one they would listen to was not here, and had not shown himself for eons.","The futility of trying to restore order through mere words became apparent as power without restraint...inevitably led to corruption and conflict.","So the chaos continued!","The Living Law was furious at the violation of order as it set off to the lands where Inevitabilities had first risen.","It searched for a solution in a place filed with uncertain possibilities!","There, after countless perils, it found something from the chaos of Inevitabilities and Everything... in the form of a Herb.\"","...!","Schrodinger’s voice dropped to barely above a whisper as he reached the climax of his tale.","\"A simple herb, and yet the Living Law felt an indescribable wonder from it.","It spent its Law and ordered the herb to be understood by it.","It was shocked as the herb it found... turned out to be the answer to the problem of Early Creatures!","It was a herb that could...heavily weaken and take down unruly Early Creatures!\"","HUUM!","The Story of the Earliest Folds being told by Schrodinger ended there, leaving Duke Elagabalus staring at the beggar with expressions that mixed shock with incredulity.","\"Are you saying,\" Duke Elagabalus asked, his voice barely steady, \"that you... have found what The Living Law found all those Ages ago?!\"","...!","At such a question, Schrodinger only smiled and leaned back against the muddy area, his eyes taking on that unfathomably bright brilliance.","He offered no answer, but his silence carried more weight than any words could have conveyed.","In that moment, beside a muddy road on an insignificant world in the depths of the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, the balance of power shifted in ways that would echo across existence itself.","And it was silent.","Surrounded by weak humans that knew nothing!","And somewhere, in a place beyond imagination, Noah Osmont continued his own journey toward greatness.","Isolated.","Not at all too worried about others!"]},{"number":3953,"title":"Chapter 3953: Chapter 3952: My Foundation is Complete! I","paragraphs":["The golden sands of the Blooming Shore stretched beneath Noah’s bare feet like crushed starlight given form, each grain pulsing with the accumulated authority of his recent advancement.","The sensation was intoxicating in its completeness...warm without heat, substantial without weight, alive with possibilities that seemed to whisper directly into his consciousness with every step he took across this transformed place!","He stood at the heart of his expanded domain, his upper body bare to the crystalline winds that swept across territories that had grown beyond all previous limitations.","Occasionally, as he walked through this paradise of his own design, new prompts would materialize before him.","|The Maximum Population of the Early Veiled Shore has been increased to 100.|","There were many that continued to trickle over as the land waited for him to give his directiona!","Yet among all these wonders, what captured his attention most profoundly were the connections that now existed to Records of other Early Veiled Shores...pathways that stretched across impossible distances!","Records.","Records meant that the Shores themselves no longer existed in their original form.","They had become echoes, memories given structure and substance but no longer truly alive with the presence of those who had created them.","\"...\"","Noah’s mind turned inevitably to the continuation of the Stories of the Earliest Folds that Sigrid had shared with him.","He understood now why Living Existences looked upon such beings with reverence that bordered on subservience and fear!","He thought of the chaos and wonder that Early Creatures had brought to existence itself.","And he thought of THE Living Law, driven by necessity to seek something in the chaotic birthplace of Inevitabilities...something that she had utilized to restore a semblance of balance to Existence itself.","Some called it a weapon in their retelling of the Story. Others whispered of it as a poison specifically crafted to bring low beings whose power exceeded all normal categories of measurement.","But whatever its true nature, THE Living Law had wielded it to bring about Order where chaos had threatened to consume everything.","Yet Early Creatures had not been destroyed at that time. The Stories made that much clear!","So what had happened to them? Who possessed sufficient power to erase entities whose capabilities transcended every normal limitation?","The questions burned in his consciousness, demanding answers that remained frustratingly beyond his reach.","As these thoughts churned through his mind, Noah felt the pulse of his own existence.","His progression continued to unfold according to principles that defied every normal expectation, unperceivable and quintessential in nature!","Right now, his Complexity and Purity Quotients had spilled past the sixty million marker. But when he considered his Refined and Basic Early Living Existential Glyphs alongside these raw measurements, when he calculated the true scope of his collective capabilities...","His actual power had already spilled past one hundred million.","The boundary between Fold Dwellers and Living Existences- that fundamental threshold that defined the very nature of hierarchy...had been crossed silently, without fanfare or ceremony.","When it came to his CQ and PQ, he was waiting to hit 75 Million before forming his first Eminent Early Living Existential Glyph!","But even though he had yet to reach that number, his actual power already spilled past Originus Venerant.","For him, it was not even some grand achievement worthy of celebration. The transition had occurred as naturally as breathing!","Those were their definitions and distinctions, after all. The categories that others used to measure and understand power simply did not apply to a being like him.","Standing upon the golden sands of his Shore, feeling the crystalline winds pass over his resplendent skin like the caress of infinity itself, Noah spoke with calm certainty that carried across his domain like a proclamation.","\"As of this moment,\" he said, his voice resonating through the Shore that existed beyond normal space, \"my foundation could be considered complete.\"","HUUM!","His foundation.","Everything before this moment...every trial overcome, every power gained, every impossible feat accomplished...he deemed nothing more than the laying of groundwork for what was to come!","BOOM!","The moment these words left his lips, the very fabric of existence around him began to pulse with recognition.","The Early Veiled Shore itself seemed to buzz with glory!","Moiraine, whose eyes were still blazing from the encounter of a Record of an Early Creature, watched on.","Heidrun, this glutton, had her eyes bright as she was chewing more Auric Vitae Grass freely while she nodded her head.","Golden light erupted from the crystalline sands beneath his feet, rising in spirals that wrapped around his form like coronation robes woven from pure authority.","The sensation was overwhelming and gentle simultaneously.","New information began cascading across his awareness as his existence corrected itself!","|Your existence has become more defined according to principles that predate all current understanding of power and progression. Through achievement that transcends normal categories of possibility, your own Exclusive Realms have now been designed.|","|Foundation Stage: The Early Primordial Genesis - Complete. This stage encompasses the fundamental building of power according to your own weavings of existence and Early Creature principles, establishing the basic architecture upon which all future advancement will be built. Characteristics: Complete formation of first Heart component, establishment of multiple Sacred Totems, accumulation of 100+ Million total collective complexity and purity source units.|","|The Next Exclusive Realm that will define you has been deemed by your weavings of existence as The Early Throne Ascendancy Realm- At the peak of this realm, you will attain power equivalent to a true Early Creature of the earliest epochs. Progression requirements: All 150+ Early Sacred Totems of Osmont advanced to the Fourth Stage, complete all components of the Heart of an Early Creature, and attain 10,000 Kleos Early Living Existential Glyphs. Other requirements may arise as you learn more regarding existence. This realm marks the transition from foundation to true existential significance.|","|The Third Exclusive Realm: The Early Infinity Dominion - Even your current understanding cannot grasp what lies at the peak of this realm. What awaits beyond this threshold remains shrouded in mystery that transcends current comprehension.|","...!","The information settled into his consciousness, each detail finding its proper place within the greater structure of understanding that governed his unique path toward transcendence.","Where others might have been overwhelmed by the scope of what lay ahead, he found only anticipation burning in his chest like a steady flame.","And oh, was he fucking steady!","The golden winds of his Blooming Shore carried with them the scent of infinite possibility.","Behind him, the Sacred Totems that dotted his expanded domain pulsed with sympathetic resonance, their bells remaining silent but ready to ring once more!","Noah stretched slightly as right after, his voice boomed out.","\"Alright, lets fully utilize this glorious Shore, shall we?!\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":3954,"title":"Chapter 3954: Chapter 3953: My Foundation is Complete! II","paragraphs":["The Blooming Shore stretched around him like a canvas waiting to be painted with wonders that had not been seen since the earliest epochs of existence, each feature demanding exploration and understanding!","Yet before he could delve into the mysteries of Early Folds or test the limits of his expanded capabilities, practical necessity demanded his attention.","The requirements for designating any plot of land as an Early Fold were precise and unforgiving- he would need prerequisite seeds!","Standing upon the golden sands that pulsed with the rhythm of his heartbeat, Noah raised his voice as it echoed out.","\"Initiate the opening of the trade network connected to the Record of the Blooming Shore of the Early Creature designated as Thal’dorven the Primordial Fisher.\"","HUUM!","The response was immediate and overwhelming.","In front of his eyes, reality itself seemed to fold and reshape as an illusory golden screen bloomed into existence with the majesty of a wheel being born.","The manifestation was breathtaking in its complexity, each mote of light that comprised its surface carrying information.","|Trade Network Connection Established Successfully. Resource exchange parameters now operational.|","|The accumulated treasures and cultivation achievements of an Early Creature who mastered the arts of marine cultivation and Shore development are now accessible through established trade. Exchange rates determined by relative scarcity and fundamental value across existential hierarchies.|","|Warning: All transactions are conducted with the Record of the Blooming Shore. Nature of receiving entity remains undefined. Exercise appropriate caution when engaging in exchanges involving personal essence or irreplaceable resources.|","As these words settled into his consciousness, the screen transformed before his eyes into something that resembled a glorious marketplace of impossible scope and grandeur.","At the very top of the display, written in letters that seemed to burn with their own inner fire, appeared the designation: |Vault of the Blooming Shore of the Early Creature, Thal’dorven the Primordial Fisher.|","Below this header, the screen organized itself into distinct sections that pulsed with their own unique radiance, each one promising access to resources that could reshape the nature of existence itself.","Noah’s enhanced perception observed them with growing amazement:","|Early Sacred Herbs, Early Sacred Produce, Early Living Marine Lifeforms, Early Sacred Tools, Fold Seeds, Architectural Blueprints...|","Each section glowed with a different hue, creating a symphony of light that spoke to the vast diversity of treasures that awaited his exploration.","The very sight of such abundance made his chest tighten with anticipation!","When he focused his attention upon the section marked, Early Sacred Herbs, the screen responded to his interest with eager compliance.","Suddenly, the display exploded with radiant vegetation that seemed to pulse with their own living light.","Hundreds upon hundreds of herbs materialized before his eyes, each one more magnificent than anything he had previously encountered!","Some appeared as simple flowers whose petals contained compressed Wheels of Existence, while others resembled trees whose branches stretched across dimensional boundaries.","His gaze settled upon two specimens that commanded attention through sheer presence alone.","The first was a delicate flower that seemed to be crafted from crystallized moonlight, its petals shifting through spectrums of color that had no names in any known language.","When he focused upon it, information flowed into his consciousness.","|Early Sacred Herb: Lustral Purity Blossom|","|Effect: Consumption grants exactly 50,000,000 Purity Quotient enhancement with no diminishing returns. Maximum consumption limit: 10 specimens per individual existence. Total potential enhancement: 500,000,000 Purity Quotient.|","|Exchange Requirements: 1 Eminent Early Living Existential Glyph, OR Early Sacred Lifeblood Herb (Equivalent rarity), OR 100 Drops of Early Creature Blood.|","|Note: This herb represents one of the foundational tools used by Early Creatures to establish the basic architecture required for transcendent advancement. Its cultivation requires specific temporal and spatial conditions that exist only within Plots properly maintained Early Veiled Shores. High chance of finding this herb in the Living Doorways of the Loom|","...!","A ridiculous herb that granted ridiculous boons!","Yet its cost...","His eyes flashed sharply as he measured everything.","The second specimen that caught his attention was even more extraordinary- a plant that seemed to exist in multiple weavings of existence simultaneously, its form shifting between states of being.","|Early Sacred Herb: Sovereign Law Genesis Vine|","|Effect: Consumption grants 10 Kleos Early Living Existential Glyphs of Law, permanently integrated into the consumer’s existential weavings. These Glyphs cannot be removed, replicated, or transferred under any circumstances. Low chance of finding this herb in the Living Doorways of the Loom.|","|Exchange Requirements: 10,000 Drops of Early Creature Blood, OR Weavings of 25% of an entire Blooming Shore (Irreversible transfer).|","|Warning: Recommend extreme caution before proceeding with exchange.|","Noah stared at these two resources with growing alarm, his mind calculating the implications.","He currently possessed fewer than one thousand drops of his Blood, making the requirement of ten thousand seem not just expensive but potentially catastrophic.","Even the herb requiring one hundred drops gave him pause and raised questions!","Exactly who would be the recipient of his blood? The dead Early Creature whose Record maintained this marketplace? The question caused him to freeze with caution, every instinct honed through countless trials screaming warnings about the dangers of surrendering essence to unknown entities.","The silence that followed was heavy with unspoken concerns as Noah contemplated the wisdom of such exchanges.","His blood was not merely a resource. To surrender it carelessly could invite consequences that stretched far beyond simple transaction!","Pushing aside these troubling thoughts for the moment, Noah turned his attention to the other sections of the miraculous marketplace, his curiosity driving him to explore despite his growing caution.","When he focused upon Early Sacred Produce, the screen filled with fruits and vegetables that seemed to pulse with concentrated life force.","One item immediately captured his attention, a golden apple whose surface seemed to contain swirling nebulae.","|Early Sacred Produce: Vitality Nexus Apple|","|Effect: Consumption permanently increases progression of complexity and purity rates by 1000%. Moderate chance of finding this produce seed in the Living Doorways of the Loom.|","|Exchange Requirements: 500 Drops of Early Creature Blood, OR Complete architectural blueprints for Third-Stage Sacred Totem construction.|","\"Hmm...\"","He looked, and turned away.","The Early Sacred Tools section revealed implements that defied normal categories of understanding. A crystalline hammer caught his eye, its surface reflecting dimensions that seemed to exist sideways to normal reality.","|Early Sacred Tool: Reality Forging Mallet of Thal’dorven|","|Effect: Allows the wielder to directly reshape the fundamental properties of any material or energy within their Shore. Can be used to enhance Sacred Totems beyond normal limitations or other unique constructs|","|Exchange Requirements: 500 Drops of Early Creature Blood, OR Sacrifice of 3 completed Sacred Totems at the Third Stage or higher.|","This, he also looked at and turned his eyes away from!"]},{"number":3955,"title":"Chapter 3955: Chapter 3954: My Foundation is Complete! III","paragraphs":["But it was in the Fold Seeds section that Noah encountered something that made his eyes pulse.","A single seed floated in isolation at the center of the display, its surface so dark it seemed to absorb light itself.","|Fold Seed: Genesis of Unbound Existence|","|Effect: Grants understanding of the Lost Forgotten Principle of Unbound Existence once matured inside a designated Early Fold Plot. Low chance of finding this herb in the Living Doorways of the Loom. |","|Exchange Requirements: 50,000 Drops of Early Creature Blood, OR Complete dissolution and absorption of 75% of a Blooming Shore with all its accumulated treasures and Lifeforms.|","Oh!","Noah’s expression grew increasingly grim as he absorbed the details of these miraculous resources!","A pattern was emerging that filled him with both wonder and deep concern- many of the herbs and produce listed in the marketplace could potentially be found in the Living Doorways of the Loom, those treacherous passages that led toward the ultimate prize of existence.","His instincts told him with absolute certainty that he should not exchange his blood.","There were too many unknowns, too many potential consequences that could reshape the very foundations of his existence in ways he could not predict or control.","\"What item on here will take Auric Vitae Grasses as a resource for exchange?\" he asked aloud, his voice carrying the weight of careful calculation.","A golden light flashed across the screen in response to his query, and new information materialized before his eyes like a gift offered by existence itself.","|Early Sacred Herb: Foundation Strengthening Root|","|Effect: Consumption grants 1,000,000 Complexity Quotient and 1,000,000 Purity Quotient enhancement with no diminishing returns. Can be consumed 100 times with consistent effects.|","|Exchange Requirements: 100 shoots of Auric Vitae Grass per specimen. Quality grades affect exchange ratios- Superior grade reduces requirement to 75 shoots, Pristine grade reduces requirement to 50 shoots.|","|Note: This represents one of the most fundamental cultivation aids used by Early Creatures to establish proper foundation. Regular consumption during advancement phases ensures optimal development.|","...!","Noah felt a smile spread across his features as understanding crystallized into decision.","This was an exchange he could make, a transaction that aligned with both his current resources and his long-term goals for advancement!","\"Buy,\" he declared with calm authority.","A brilliant light flashed across the screen as the transaction completed itself, and Noah felt the subtle shift in reality that marked the successful acquisition of resources that could accelerate his progression beyond normal limitations.","A multicolored root appeared in his hands, its mere existence buzzing with age and power as he analyzed it!","Not just for purposes of eating...but also whether it could he replanted in his own Early Veiled Shore!","But as the light gradually faded and the marketplace returned to its previous state, Noah came to two conclusions that would reshape his approach to the challenges that lay ahead.","First, his blood was unfathomably precious and desperately wanted by forces he did not yet understand.","The sheer scale of the exchange rates demanded for his essence spoke to value that transcended normal principles, suggesting that Early Creature blood represented something far more significant than mere biological fluid.","Second, and perhaps more importantly, the Living Doorways of the Loom contained treasures that could elevate any being to heights of power previously considered impossible.","It was why Living Existences were so fervant about it!","If he was to achieve the progression required for his Exclusive Realms, if he was to become what he truly wanted to be, he would need to seriously delve into those treacherous passages alongside the usage of his Early Veiled Shore, especially if he did not want to pay with his Blood.","The path forward was clear, even if the destination remained shrouded in uncertainty.","The Doorways of the Loom beckoned with promises of advancement that could not be ignored, no matter how dangerous the journey might prove to be!","Standing upon his Blooming Shore, surrounded by wonders that defied imagination, Noah began planning for the trials that would define his Existence as on this day, with a completed foundation, he began his first steps in his own...Early Throne Ascendancy Realm!","—","In the infinite weavings of existence, there existed a fundamental divide that touched every conscious being across all the weavings of reality.","It was a distinction so basic, so elemental, that it formed the very foundation upon which all understanding of life and death was built.","There were those who were Living, and those who were Dead.","Simple.","Straightforward.","Undeniable!","This truth echoed through every Fold, every Wheel of Existence, every domain where consciousness dared to take root.","Fold Dwellers across the vast expanse of existence found themselves categorized by this simple yet profound distinction...they drew breath and thought and dreamed, or they had surrendered these gifts to the endless silence that claimed all things in time.","Yet existence, in its infinite complexity, refused to be bound by such simple categories!","For when beings exceeded a certain level of power, when their accumulated authority transcended the normal limitations that governed them, even Dead Things became something greater.","They shed the chains of death like discarded clothing, ascending to heights where the very concepts of life and death became meaningless distinctions.","Amongst the ten Foldless Ones, the ten types of Living Existences who commanded the fundamental forces that shaped Existences itself...there was not a single entity that could be considered truly Dead.","Even those who had once known the embrace of death transcended such limitations when they achieved the heights of Living Existence, their existence elevated beyond the reach of death’s final claim.","This observation led to a question for those who dared to contemplate the deepest mysteries of existence- Where, in all the vast expanse of Existence, were the Dead?","Where, across the infinite Folds that contained countless civilizations and uncounted souls, were those who remained truly, indubitably, unperceivably dead?","Was everything Living after surpassing Originus Venerant? After becoming a Living Existence?","It was a question that very few dared to ask, for the implications of its answer touched upon truths too vast and terrible for most minds to bear!","And even fewer possessed the knowledge necessary to provide an answer that would satisfy the scope of such an inquiry.","For the dead did not simply cease to exist...they went somewhere!","They found their way to domains that existed beyond the reach of Living Existences, domains where different rules governed the nature of consciousness and purpose!"]},{"number":3956,"title":"Chapter 3956: Chapter 3955: The Rich and the Poor! I","paragraphs":["In another Weaving of Existence, removed from the familiar territories where Living Existences pursued their endless struggles for advancement and dominion, lay a domain that existed according to principles that would have driven most conscious entities to madness with their profound wrongness.","This was an unknown place, a forgotten corner of Existence where the fundamental laws that governed Existence, life, and death had been twisted into configurations that served purposes too alien for normal comprehension.","The entire domain was crafted from obsidian that gleamed with inner light that somehow managed to convey both beauty and despair in equal measure.","The obsidian stretched in all directions, forming landscapes of impossible weavings where black crystal formations rose like the bones of dead titans!","The air itself seemed thick with the weight of accumulated sorrow, each breath carrying flavors that spoke to loss on an existential scale.","At the heart of this dreary magnificence lay something that defied every expectation of what an Early Veiled Shore should represent.","Where such domains typically embodied life and growth and infinite possibility, this Shore spoke only of endings and decay and the terrible finality of death given form.","Finality!","The waters that should have sparkled with crystalline clarity were instead murky and black, their surface reflecting no light as they lapped against shores of sand that had been ground from the bones of forgotten civilizations.","Each grain carried within it the compressed essence of dreams that would never be fulfilled, ambitions that had been cut short by forces too vast to resist.","The trees that dotted this desolate landscape stood as monuments to futility itself!","Their branches reached skyward with the desperate grasping of those who sought salvation that would never come, their bark scarred by wounds that wept sap as black as midnight.","No leaves adorned their twisted limbs, no fruit offered sustenance to those who might seek shelter in their shadow.","Sacred Totems that had once rung with the music of harmony lay shattered across the blackened sands, their bells cracked and silent.","The very foundations upon which they had been built showed signs of violence so profound it had left scars in the fabric of existence itself.","Shrines that should have housed the accumulated wisdom of ages stood as hollow shells, their sacred spaces defiled by forces that recognized no sanctity!","The plots of land that should have nurtured miraculous growth lay barren and poisoned, their soil so thoroughly corrupted that nothing would ever grow there again.","At the center of this nightmare landscape sat a figure that commanded attention through sheer presence alone, despite the terrible wounds that marked its form.","The Early Creature bore the unmistakable signs of one who had achieved the heights of power, its muscled frame speaking to strength that had once commanded the respect of Living Existences.","Its bare chest was a map of violence, each scar telling stories of battles fought against forces unperceivable to many!","But it was the head that drew the eye with horrifying fascination.","A massive gash split the skull nearly in half, running from the crown all the way down to the neck with surgical precision.","The wound gaped open like a second mouth, revealing depths that seemed to contain swirling darkness rather than the biological structures that should have existed beneath bone and flesh!","Yet despite injuries that should have resulted in immediate death for any normal being, the creature blinked with eyes that burned with terrible awareness.","Before it floated a flickering obsidian screen that pulsed with the same dark radiance that permeated the entire realm, its surface displaying information that remained hidden from external observation.","In this landscape of absolute desolation, where hope had been systematically eliminated and beauty existed only to emphasize the magnitude of loss, the Early Creature’s voice echoed with authority that made the very foundations of reality tremble.","\"Blood...\" it said, each syllable dripping with hunger that transcended normal desire.","\"All I want... is Blood!\"","HUUM!","As it said so, behind him could be seen green gold grasses trying to pierce into thr black sand to give them some color, but the moment they did so, there was only a dim glow gained that seemed like it would be eaten up in a matter of hours!","Death...permeated here far too potently.","And in constrast...there were other places filled with the overabundance of life!","---","In the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds, where the struggle between order and chaos played out on a stage vast enough to contain the ambitions of many powers, the magnificent citadel of Aeternitas Concordia rose against horizons that stretched beyond imagination.","Outside this monument to cooperation between forces of Living Existences, contained within a bubble of golden radiance that bent light around its surface like a lens focused on infinity, Noah floated alongside beings whose combined Existences were far too bright!","Sigrid stood beside him with the poise of one who had never doubted her right to command the attention of the most powerful beings in existence.","Altheon maintained his position behind them with the patient watchfulness. The Prime Living Origin’s luminous form pulsed with barely contained energy, ready to defend his charges against threats that might emerge from any direction.","Three Honored Living Existences completed their immediate retinue, their presence adding layers of protection that would have made even Honored Living Existences pause before considering aggressive action!","The golden bubble that contained them existed beyond the reach of casual observation, its surface configured to deflect even the enhanced perceptions of Honored Living Existences.","Duke Gwendolyn had listened to the demands of Sigrid’s with careful attention. When she had finally agreed, it was to provide protection for their journey into the Living Doorways of the Loom, and her acquiescence had come with conditions that reflected the true magnitude of the dangers they would face!","\"If you are to truly traverse across the Doorways of the Loom,\" she had declared, \"you will go with a team composed of entities I personally select to ensure your survival.\"","...!"]},{"number":3957,"title":"Chapter 3957: Chapter 3956: The Rich and the Poor! II","paragraphs":["Sigrid had agreed to these terms without hesitation. Altheon was one, but the identity of the others who would join their expedition remained a source of curiosity.","WAP!","The distinctive sound of spatial displacement announced Duke Gwendolyn’s return to their protective bubble, her arrival accompanied by two figures whose presence immediately shifted the balance of power within their confined space.","Duke Gwendolyn herself was a vision of regality that transcended normal concepts of beauty and authority. Her stellar dark hair seemed to contain entire galaxies within its depths, while her tan skin radiated warmth.","The Living Origin Authority that cascaded over her form like liquid starlight!","But it was the two beings who accompanied her that caused Noah’s expression to shift.","The first figure resembled a titan carved from white-gold radiance, its muscled frame speaking to physical power that could have crushed Wheels with casual gestures.","The second entity presented a study in contrasts.","It appeared as a verdant fairy-like creature whose delicate features might have inspired artists across countless civilizations, yet its expression carried coldness that suggested it viewed everything in existence as fundamentally beneath its notice.","Despite its seemingly fragile appearance, the power that radiated from this being made even Noah’s eyes observe a level of authority that operated on the level of Royal Living Existences.","The casual indifference within its gaze was potent!","Duke Gwendolyn gestured toward the fairy-like entity with movements that carried the precise elegance of introduction. \"This is Royal Living Origin Thessaly, the Weaver of Reversed Existence,\" she announced.","\"Of all Living Origins, she possesses the unique capability to reverse the collapse of any existence that has occurred within a day, so long as she bears witness to the event.\"","HUUM!","To possess the ability to undo death, to reverse the fundamental processes that governed the end of existence!","Noah’s gaze remained fixed upon this being as he spoke with calm directness. \"What if someone collapses her existence? Can she also reverse this?\"","...!","An immense silence settled over their gathering at this question.","Royal Living Origin Thessaly’s expression grew even colder as her attention focused upon Noah.","Nobody spoke for several heartbeats, the tension building like pressure in a vessel approaching its breaking point.","Then, cutting through the oppressive quiet like a blade, booming laughter erupted from the titan-like entity who stood beside Duke Gwendolyn.","\"Haha!\" the being exclaimed with genuine amusement, his voice carrying a unique dialect.","\"Little Brother is funny one. Very few dare talk back!\"","His sentences were not entirely fluent as they seemed somewhat broken and simple.","Duke Gwendolyn’s expression remained cold as she turned to introduce this final member of their expedition. \"In all of existence,\" she declared with absolute certainty, \"no Royal or Honored Living Existence can take down Titano.\"","...!","Titano!","This being, whose casual manner and easy laughter suggested someone comfortable with great violence!","Titano himself seemed entirely unconcerned with the gravity of his reputation, his attention already shifting to Noah with the focused interest of one who had found something genuinely intriguing.","He walked forward with movements that carried no threat.","\"I admire you!\" Titano declared with the sincerity of one who spoke only truth in any circumstance.","His gaze shifted momentarily toward Sigrid before returning to Noah with renewed intensity. \"Brother, how you do it? THE Living Order is big thing, how you wrap her around you? How are you, supposed Fold Dweller, talking so freely to even Dukes as if equals? I really admire you for this, brother!\"","...!","His words missed some proper flow here and there, but his muscular figure and honest eyes were genuine!","Noah’s eyes shone with inner light as he regarded this being whose casual manner concealed depths of capability that could crush Royal Living Existences.","Internally, he smiled at the directness of questions, but outwardly he maintained the serious expression of one prepared to address them.","Duke Gwendolyn and her assembled retinue observed this exchange with expressions that mixed coldness with growing incredulity, while Sigrid smiled lightly and shook her head with the patient amusement.","\"Which question do you most want an answer to?\" Noah asked with the gravity of one preparing to share wisdom of Quintessence!","Titano’s gaze shifted once more toward Sigrid, his expression becoming thoughtful as he considered the relative importance of the mysteries that demanded his attention.","\"Question relating to her,\" he decided with characteristic directness. \"How you bag her down?\"","...!","Noah nodded with the seriousness of one about to deliver a lesson of fundamental importance. \"Brother, are you rich or poor in regards to existence?\"","The question seemed to catch Titano off guard, his expression shifting to one of genuine consideration as he processed implications that had not occurred to him.","\"What defines rich and poor?\" he asked after several moments of contemplation.","\"Someone poor in existence,\" Noah explained with the patience of a teacher addressing a promising but naive student, \"just has themselves and their power, nothing else. Someone rich has treasures. Things that can make Honored Ones, Royal Living Existences, and even Dukes jealous.\"","He paused to let these words settle before continuing. \"Do you have anything like that?\"","Titano’s response came without hesitation, his honesty cutting through any pretense that might have clouded the issue. \"No, brother. I only have hands that can break bones of Honored and Royal Living Existences...\"","Noah shook his head with the sadness of one delivering unwelcome but necessary truth. \"Then you are poor, brother. And the poor in existence... will have to fight tooth and nail to get anything, especially a baddie like her.\"","The lesson struck Titano with the force of heavy revelation, his terrifying eyes shining with newfound understanding as he nodded with the enthusiasm of one who had just discovered principles that could reshape his entire approach to existence!","Off to the side, Duke Gwendolyn shook her head with expressions of incredulity that bordered on disbelief.","Sigrid had a calm smile while Altheon’s gaze was cloudy, but he did not say a single thing as Titano...was a terrifying weapon of the Living Origins even he had only heard about!","And now...even this being was freely talking to the Fold Dweller, Noah Osmont!"]},{"number":3958,"title":"Chapter 3958: Chapter 3957: Advancement and Inevitabilities! I","paragraphs":["The golden bubble hung suspended in the void like a captured sun, its surface rippling with currents of Living Origin Authority that bent reality around its edges.","Within its confines, Duke Gwendolyn’s sigh carried the weight of eons as her gaze swept across the assembled beings who would determine Sigrid’s fate.","\"These are the Existences that will be traveling with you,\" she said.","\"Altheon, Thessaly, Titano, and...\"","Her eyes drifted to Noah, and in that moment, something shifted in her expression.","The stellar darkness within her gaze deepened, wheels within wheels turning as she studied him with an intensity.","She was a Duke. One of the eighty-one who sat at the pinnacle of Living Origin hierarchy.","Throughout her impossibly long life, she had catalogued and categorized every form of power, every variation of authority that dared to manifest across the infinite Folds.","She always knew what she looked at...it was not arrogance but simple fact, as fundamental to her nature as breathing was to mortal creatures!","But when she gazed at Noah Osmont, that certainty fractured.","Her mind turned through possibilities.","Perhaps he was someone intrinsically connected to THE Living Order, bound by threads of Existence so profound that even she could not fully perceive their nature.","The way Sigrid looked at him, the casual ease with which she accepted his presence...there was something binding between them!","Or perhaps he was the scion of another Duke, one of her carefully cultivated allies....","The game of Dukes was one played across Folds and ages, where a single move might take millennia to reach fruition.","The third possibility made her chest tighten as...perhaps he carried an Inheritance so profound that even Living Existences would tear apart existence to have it. What he displayed in Concordia could be part of it!","She was curious, desperately curious, about exactly what-...!","|Do not worry too much about his identity.|","Sigrid’s voice bloomed in her mind like a flower of pure thought, |Just know that he... will absolutely protect me.|","HUUM!","The mental communication carried undertones that Duke Gwendolyn had not heard from the Young Miss before- absolute certainty mixed with something that might have been fondness!","Duke Gwendolyn sighed at such words.","Things were getting more and more entangled!","Duke Gwendolyn’s gaze shifted between them....Sigrid watching with that small, knowing smile, while Noah continued his earnest instruction of Titano as if he were a sage imparting the deepest mysteries of existence to an eager disciple.","The massive titan nodded along with such sincere concentration that his entire form seemed to vibrate with the effort of understanding, occasionally interjecting with \"Yes, brother!\" and \"This makes sense!\" as Noah explained what appeared to be the fundamental principles of...finding a baddie through material wealth?","The absurdity of it- a supposed Fold Dweller lecturing one of the more terrifying weapons in the Living Origin arsenal about romantic economics should have been laughable!","Instead, it filled Duke Gwendolyn with a profound unease that settled in her bones.","She released another sigh, this one carrying the weight of responsibilities that stretched across existence itself.","Turning to Sigrid, she allowed her expression to shift from calculation to concern.","\"Young Miss,\" she began, \"things are not as peaceful as they appear. There is a Coalition of Living Existences, yes, but...\" She paused.","\"Not all are truly allied. Schemes run deep...deeper than the roots of the trees of existence, deeper than the foundations of existence itself. Power runs even deeper still as apart from those truly Living...there are also those truly Dead!\"","The golden light within the bubble seemed to dim slightly, as if responding to the gravity of her words.","\"And on top of all this,\" Duke Gwendolyn continued, her hands moving in subtle gestures that painted pictures in the air...shadows of things that should not be named directly.","\"There are the Weavings of Existence themselves, forces that even make us seek the Loom with such desperate fervor. In all of this maze of power and purpose, you must be careful. You are both a hope for the future and...\" She hesitated, then pushed forward with grim determination. \"And a weapon that many would wield without concern for your wellbeing.\"","The earnestness in her voice, stripped of all pretense, seemed to strike Sigrid. The Young Miss nodded seriously, her stellar eyes reflecting understanding of burdens she should not have to bear.","Duke Gwendolyn straightened, addressing the entire gathering now.","\"There are things you know and things you do not know. This time around, when it comes to the identity of the Young Miss, no one...absolutely no one, is to be trusted.\"","Even Titano stopped his eager nodding to pay attention!","\"Thus,\" Duke Gwendolyn declared, her words falling like hammers, \"your first Doorway to the Loom will not even stem from the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds.\"","WAA!","Noah’s conversation with Titano ceased mid-sentence, his attention snapping to the Duke with intensity.","\"Instead,\" she continued, a smile playing at the edges of her lips that held no warmth whatsoever, \"you will enter silently into a Doorway from the side of the Transcendent Paradox Battlefront Folds.\"","...!","\"What?\" Sigrid’s surprise burst forth before she could contain it, \"Paradoxical Folds?\"","Duke Gwendolyn’s smile widened, becoming something that might have been satisfaction.","\"Surprised? Yes, a Doorway through the Paradoxical Folds. Just as Paradoxes have extended their reach toward other Transcendent Folds over the eons, so have we. I have my... clone waiting for you in front of the exact Doorway you will enter.\"","For Living Origins to move through Paradoxical territory spoke to infiltrations and schemes that redefined the supposed boundaries between the great powers!","\"I chose this one,\" Duke Gwendolyn explained, \"because Inevitabilities are much easier to predict and face than other Living Existences. I know for certain there are no Living Paradoxes, Origins, Laws, or any other Living Existences within this particular Doorway. Such a thing is a much more controlled environment, regardless of its inherent dangers. And mind you, it is very dangerous!\"","She paused, allowing them to absorb this information before delivering the final assessment. \"Because the number of Inevitabilities is higher due to it being in the Paradoxical Folds, the danger level is elevated, but manageable with the current team. So you shall... go.\"","The moment the word left her lips, the bubble erupted with radiant Living Origin Authority that made reality itself sing. The light was so brilliant it seemed to burn through dimensions themselves, and then...","HUUUM!","Nothing.","Where once a few beings had stood ready, now only Duke Gwendolyn remained, her form solitary against the vast expanse of the Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds in this area.","She looked toward distant Aeternitas Concordia, its towers catching light that had traveled across impossible distances to reach this moment.","Another sigh escaped her, this one carrying dread and solemnity.","\"I wonder,\" she said to the endless expanse, \"how many beginnings will face destruction in this coming storm...\"","The question hung unanswered in the space between heartbeats, between one moment and the next, as somewhere across the impossible distances of existence...Noah materialized before a Doorway that should not exist, in a place where they should not be!"]},{"number":3959,"title":"Chapter 3959: Chapter 3958: Advancement and Inevitabilities! II","paragraphs":["The transition between Existence should have been instantaneous, a mere blink between one existence and another, but Duke Gwendolyn’s power carried them across countless weavings of Existence with such force that Noah felt every impossible fold they traversed!","Each layer pressed against his consciousness like pages in a book being riffled by an impatient reader, thousands of stories and possibilities bleeding into one another until the very concept of distance became meaningless.","When they finally materialized, Noah’s first sensation was suffocation of existence itself!","It was...familiar.","It was Paradox!","The space around them defied every natural law. Obsidian cloth hung in the air like frozen waterfalls, each drape twisting into its neighboring fabrics. The material seemed to flow upward and downward simultaneously, creating corridors that led everywhere and nowhere, passages that existed in states of being both open and closed.","It was as if someone had taken the concept of a maze and wrapped it in funeral shrouds, then set those shrouds to dancing in winds that blew from dimensions that should not exist.","The very air tasted of contradiction...sweet and bitter, thick and thin, present and absent all at once!","Out of the many Living Existential Authorities Noah commanded...Paradox truly took a special place as it seemed...natural!","Each breath Noah drew felt like inhaling possibility itself, raw and unfiltered, scraping against his enhanced perception like sandpaper made from compressed paradoxes.","But it was what lay before them that truly commanded attention.","Where space should have continued its paradoxical dance of obsidian drapery, there was instead a wound in Existence itself.","Mirror-black fissures folded in upon themselves with the wet, organic movement of a dying creature’s final breath, each crack revealing glimpses of something golden and terrible within.","The collapsed space pulsed with a hunger as it was the hunger of absence itself, demanding to be filled with anything and everything that dared exist near it.","Noah felt his body lean forward involuntarily, drawn by a pull!","It was as if every particle of his being recognized that golden depths as a destination, a final resting place where all journeys ended.","His 1002% resistances screamed in protest, holding him back from simply walking forward into obliteration, but the effort required was considerable even for someone of his power.","This...was what true danger felt like!","Floating before this wound, maintaining position with apparent ease despite the inexorable pull, was a figure encased in obsidian armor so dark it seemed to absorb light rather than reflect it.","The armor itself was a work of art, each plate had been carved with paradoxical symbols and runes.","Sigrid tensed beside him, her hand finding his with instinctive wariness. Through their connection, he felt her recognition spark into confusion, then shock as the crystalline faceplate of the armor began to separate with the sound of breaking ice.","The face revealed beneath was impossibly, undeniably familiar.","\"Duke Gwendolyn?\" Sigrid’s voice cracked with disbelief. \"How...?\"","The smile that spread across this other Gwendolyn’s features held layers of satisfaction at this response!","This was not mere illusion or projection, he could feel the authentic weight of Paradoxical Authority radiating from her form, as real and undeniable as the Origin Authority her other body commanded!","\"Everyone has their talents, Young Miss,\" Duke Gwendolyn said.","\"Mine was being capable of forming an Origin Embryo that could become anything. And so...\" She gestured to herself with armored hands that moved with deadly grace, \"I had this body become a Living Paradox.\"","HUUM!","An Origin Embryo that could become anything.","She had literally created a second self that operated according to entirely different fundamental principles!","It was not unlike what Moiraine had achieved as an Arch Living Existence, capable of holding two authorities simultaneously, or Sigrid herself who embodied both Order and Origin.","\"Come,\" Duke Gwendolyn continued, gesturing toward the hungry golden depths behind her. \"I will continue standing guard here while you all enter. What you see behind me is a Living Doorway of the Loom that has devoured everything nearby. Only someone with the complexity of an Honored Existence can resist its pull enough to enter or leave safely.\"","She paused, allowing them to absorb the magnitude of what they were about to attempt.","\"It is a dangerous domain, as chaotic as anything can be, so...\" Her gaze found Sigrid with meaningful intensity, \"You can go all out with your restoration of order. Inevitabilities are silent, deadly, and unable to be observed until they make their move. They prefer to target the weakest first, so you two...\"","Her attention shifted between Noah and Sigrid.","\"The two of you will proceed slightly ahead. Thessaly, Titano, and Altheon will remain hidden but can move instantly to ensure your safety should the need arise.\"","Noah met her gaze with eyes thst burned with Tyranny.","This Duke who wore two faces, who embodied contradiction while serving Origin, was playing a game. A dangerous one!","Sigrid nodded, her hand tightening briefly around Noah’s before she released it to maintain proper appearance. \"We understand.\"","Noah moved from Titano’s side with fluid grace, the massive being’s disappointed expression at losing his instructor almost comical given the circumstances.","As he took his position beside Sigrid, Noah offered her a smile that carried both reassurance and anticipation!","Duke Gwendolyn’s commands rang out with crisp authority.","Her final glance settled on Thessaly with particular weight, and though no words were spoken aloud, the fairy-like being’s cold expression shifted to one of absolute determination.","|Protect the Young Miss at all costs.|","The mental command might as well have been carved into the fundamental laws of existence for the weight it carried.","Then they were moving forward, allowing the Doorway’s pull to claim them.","The sensation began as pressure against his skin, gentle at first like sinking into warm water.","But as they crossed the threshold where existence ended and the Doorway began, that pressure multiplied exponentially!","Noah felt his existence compress, every atom of his being squeezed through a space that should not have been able to accommodate anything larger than a thought.","His enhanced perception screamed contradictory information...he was being stretched across infinity while simultaneously being crushed into a point smaller than zero.","...!","This was what coming close to the Loom felt like!","The golden depths rushed up to meet them, or perhaps they fell into it, or perhaps both states existed simultaneously in this place where paradox ruled.","Noah felt his various Glyphs flare with protective authority, each one fighting to maintain his coherent existence against forces that wanted nothing more than to scatter him across dimensions and reassemble him.","Then, between one heartbeat and the next, they arrived!","HUUM!","The impact of materialization in this new space hit Noah alongside prompts as he rapidly analyzed his new surroundings.","|You have entered the Living Doorway: The Paradoxical Executor of Unmaking|","|All Living Existential Authority effectiveness reduced by 50% due to paradoxical interference. The very nature of this domain rejects ordered expression of power.|","...!","|Multiplication Paradox Active: All encountered Lifeforms, Herbs, and Inevitabilities will immediately gain the effect \"Paradoxical Proliferation\" - any singular entity becomes five identical copies upon manifestation before you. These copies, if Inevitabilities or applicable lifeforms, share distributed consciousness and must be eliminated simultaneously to achieve true death.","|Entropic Storms: Periodic waves of pure dissolution will sweep through the domain at irregular intervals. These storms strip 10% of all resistances temporarily and inflict stacking deterioration.|","|Execution Pillars: Massive columns of concentrated Living Existential Authority manifest spontaneously throughout the domain. Contact results in immediate complexity reduction of 10,000,000 source units per second of exposure. Pillars provide no warning before manifestation.|","...!","Sheesh!"]},{"number":3960,"title":"Chapter 3960: Chapter 3959: Advancement and Inevitabilities! III","paragraphs":["The space they had materialized in defied common sense!","Walls of flaming obsidian gold rose on all sides...left, right, above, and below, creating a cube of scorching paradox that had no true orientation.","The flames themselves were wrong, burning with heat that froze and cold that seared, their light casting shadows that were somehow brighter than the surfaces they fell upon.","The obsidian was not solid but liquid, not liquid but gas, not gas but something that existed in states for which no words had been invented!","\"Young Miss,\" Thessaly’s voice rang out from behind them, already hidden in the veils of existence alongside Altheon, their presence undetectable yet undeniably close.","\"We are right behind and will act as soon as danger appears.\"","Sigrid nodded. \"Let me act first. If I cannot handle it, then you may make your move.\"","There was no verbal response, but Noah felt the acknowledgment silently.","Beside him, the massive figure of Titano remained visible, his presence a mountain of barely contained violence that somehow managed to be reassuring rather than threatening.","The being’s expression had shifted to one of serious contemplation.","\"Brother,\" Titano said, his voice carrying that distinctive broken cadence that somehow made his words more impactful, \"Can I stay and talk with you as we go? I have much to learn.\"","Noah couldn’t help but smile at this terrifying entity he had yet to fully figure out who spoke with such earnest sincerity. \"Sure.\"","They began moving through the doorway, each step requiring conscious effort against the environment’s attempts to unmake them. The ground beneath their feet was simultaneously solid and intangible!","Titano looked down at his massive hands, flexing fingers that Noah knew could shatter the existence of powerful Living Existences.","\"Brother,\" he said, \"All I know is how to break the bones and bodies of Living Existences and Inevitabilities. How can I get rich like you?\"","...!","The question, delivered with such brutal honesty, made Noah’s estimation of this being rise even further.","He was honest when it came to this simple being that he actually liked due to his nature.","\"It will be too hard to get rich exactly like me,\" Noah said, choosing his words with care. \"But you can use your strength to get rich. Tell me, brother, how many Living Existences have you killed so far?\"","Titano’s brow furrowed with the effort of recall, his lips moving slightly as he appeared to count on mental fingers. \"I have broken the heads and existence of fifty-five Honored Living Paradoxes.\" He paused, continuing his mental tally. \"Nine Honored Living Elementals. Seven Honored Living Origins.\"","...!","Another pause, then almost as an afterthought: \"Oh, and two Royal Living Origins.\"","HUUM!","The casual delivery of such a tremendous kill count made Noah’s expression sharpen with newfound respect, while beside them, Sigrid actually stumbled, her shock breaking through her composed exterior!","He had killed Honored AND Royal Living Origins?! Why?!","Before Titano could continue what was clearly going to be an even longer list, Thessaly materialized.","Her expression had darkened to something approaching actual anger, an emotion that seemed foreign on her fairy-like features.","\"Titano,\" she said, \"Duke Gwendolyn told you to never mention your missions to others.\"","Titano blinked with the confusion of someone who had been following rules he didn’t quite understand. \"But this is Brother,\" he said, gesturing toward Noah with one massive hand. \"The man who bagged the Young Miss. He is not among ’others,’ is he?\"","WAA!","The simple logic, delivered with such straightforward certainty, made Noah laugh.","\"Right,\" Noah said, wrapping an arm around Titano’s shoulder in a gesture that required him to reach significantly upward. \"I am a close Brother, so you can tell me anything!\"","His voice took on a conspiratorial tone. \"Why were you ordered to kill all those Living Existences?\"","Titano’s response came without hesitation. \"They were Traitors.\"","The single word hung in the paradoxical air like a death sentence already carried out. Noah nodded thoughtfully, filing away this information about the complexities within the Coalition of Living Existences.","\"Okay,\" he said, maintaining his casual tone despite the weight of what he was learning. \"What did you do with their bodies?\"","Titano blinked again, clearly puzzled by the question. \"Nothing? Broken bones and muscles are useless to Titano.\"","Noah shook his head with the patient exasperation of a teacher. \"Brother, the corpses of your enemies are one of the best ways to get rich! It is high quality Loot! If you had given me a corpse of an Honored Living Existence right now, I could make you very rich.\"","The transformation in Titano’s expression was immediate and profound.","His eyes brightened with the fervor of someone who had just discovered a fundamental truth about existence! He nodded so vigorously that the air around him displaced in visible waves, his white gold muscular skin vibrating.","\"What about Inevitabilities?\" he asked with growing excitement.","\"If you capture for me an Inevitability equivalent to an Honored Living Existence,\" Noah said, \"I’ll make you just as rich.\"","Titano’s eyes blazed with purpose as he beat his chest with enough force to create thunderclaps in the paradoxical space. \"Titano will break all Inevitabilities to get rich!\"","His booming declaration echoed through the domain with terrifying intensity, seeming to bounce off the flaming obsidian walls in ways that multiplied and magnified the sound until it became a roar of challenge.","A challenge!","A challenge that no entity within this space could possibly ignore.","The response...was immediate.","\"SKEEE!\"","The sound that answered Titano’s challenge was not quite a scream, not quite a roar, but something that existed in the space between...a harrowing cry that spoke of hunger so vast it had gained consciousness, of absence so profound it had learned to hate everything that dared to exist!","Up ahead, where the corridor of flaming obsidian gold seemed to twist into a knot of spatial impossibility, thousands of tentacles erupted into being!","They did not emerge from anywhere so much as simply decide to exist, each one a different shade of wrong- some were transparent yet cast solid shadows, others were solid yet translucent, and still others seemed to exist in states that Noah’s enhanced perception could only classify as \"probably there.\"","But what made his expression sharpen with genuine interest was not the tentacles themselves, but what his prompts immediately identified.","|A type of Inevitability has been observed : The Gnawing Absence of Purpose|","|Threat Level: Honored Living Existence Equivalent|","|Warning: Paradoxical Proliferation taking effect|","HUUM!","Before their eyes, the single mass of tentacles shimmered like heat mirages on a summer road.","Then, where one horror had been, five identical versions materialized, each one absolutely real, each one independently conscious yet somehow sharing a distributed intelligence that made them more dangerous than five separate entities could ever be.","The tentacles surged toward them with the inexorable certainty of entropy itself, each appendage seeking to unmake, to drag them into whatever nightmare of non-existence spawned such creatures.","Beside him, Sigrid stepped forward, and Noah felt the air change as Living Order began to assert itself against the chaos of this domain.","In another direction, a muscular force of nature had an excited expression as he looked towards the Inevitability while punching his chest, his booming roar echoing out as he also moved!","\"Titano! Will get! Rich!\"","...!","The tentacles surged forward with the inexorable hunger of existence denied, each appendage a different shade of impossibility!","They moved without pattern yet with terrible purpose, some phasing through the obsidian flames as if they didn’t exist, others treating the fire as solid surfaces to push against, and still others seemed to exist in multiple positions simultaneously until the moment of observation collapsed them into singular, terrible reality!","Titano’s response was immediate and gloriously simple.","\"I BREAK YOU TO GET RICH, INEVITABILITY!\"","HUUM!","The declaration boomed through the paradoxical space with such force that the flaming walls actually flickered, as if his voice alone carried enough conviction to make even this twisted domain pay attention.","Then he moved, and Noah finally understood why Duke Gwendolyn kept this being as her personal weapon and gave him missions to even kill Royal Living Origins.","There was no technique to Titano’s assault, no sophisticated manipulation of Living Existential Authority or clever application of authority.","He simply reached out with hands that had broken Royal Living Existences and grabbed the nearest cluster of tentacles with the casual certainty of someone picking flowers. The appendages, each one dense enough with paradoxical authority to crush an ordinary Living Existence into conceptual paste, tore like wet paper in his grip!","\"Break!\" Titano roared, ripping another section free with his left hand while his right pulverized three more tentacles into a spray of impossible fluids that existed in too many dimensions at once.","\"Break for richness!\"","...!","The Inevitability screamed with five overlapping voices that created a sound that should not have been possible. Each of its proliferated bodies felt the damage, sharing the pain across their distributed consciousness in ways that made them writhe with synchronized agony!","Yet for every tentacle Titano destroyed, two more seemed to manifest from the twisted space between existence and void.","The massive being didn’t care. He waded into the mass of writhing appendages like a child playing in ocean waves, each movement destructive beyond comprehension.","And again...there was not really any burst of Authority around him!","When tentacles wrapped around his arms, he flexed and they shattered!","When they tried to pierce his skin, they bent and broke against muscle that had been forged through eons of violence.","When they attempted to unmake him with paradoxical authority, he simply refused to acknowledge their attempts, his existence too stubbornly simple to be undone by complexity.","\"Brother, I am very strong, yes?!\" he called out to Noah mid-destruction, casually backhanding a tentacle thick as an ancient tree trunk into obliteration. \"Titano will break many things! Soon very rich!\"","...!","But even Titano’s terrifying might could only do so much against five bodies that shared consciousness yet acted independently.","The tentacles began to adapt, learning from each destruction, beginning to weave patterns that even his tremendous strength couldn’t simply tear through.","They were...Inevitable.","They started moving in quantum uncertainties, existing in probable positions until the moment of impact, making it impossible to grab what wasn’t definitely there!","It was at this moment that Sigrid stepped forward.","The change in the atmosphere was immediate and absolute.","Where before the air had tasted of paradox and contradiction, now something else began to assert itself...something that predated the chaos, something that remembered when existence had structure and meaning and purpose!","Her face lit up with white brilliance that had nothing to do with external light sources.","It was illumination that came from within, from the very core of what she was becoming.","Her hair, those striking strands of white and dark, began to dance in winds that existed in dimensions where order still reigned supreme.","Each strand moved with deliberate grace, creating patterns that had been perfect before paradox had ever learned to question them.","She raised her hand with the slow majesty of inevitable consequence, and in that gesture was contained the weight of every law that had ever been written, every rule that had ever brought structure from chaos, every moment when existence had chosen meaning over entropy!","Then she brought her hand down, and with perfect clarity that cut through the screaming chaos of battle, she spoke a single word.","\"Order.\"","Order.","...!","Oh, fucking Order!"]},{"number":3961,"title":"Chapter 3961: Chapter 3960: Advancement and Inevitabilities! IV","paragraphs":["What is Order?","Order is not the mere absence of chaos, though chaos flees before its presence!","Order is not simply organization, though all things organize themselves according to its will.","Order is the first word spoken when THE Creature looked upon the void!","It is the fundamental assertion that existence has meaning, that patterns have purpose, that there is a correct way for Existence to unfold!","It is the existential parent that looks upon the tantrums of entropy and says, with infinite patience and inexorable certainty...","|No.|","HUUM!","No!","Order does not destroy chaos...it contains it, shapes it, gives it boundaries within which it can exist without consuming everything. It is the frame that holds the painting, the banks that guide the river, the rules that make the game worth playing!","And in this moment, in this place of pure paradox where impossibility had made itself king, Order reasserted its primordial claim.","The moment Sigrid’s hand completed its descent, white brilliance erupted from her form with the patient certainty of dawn breaking over Existence that had forgotten the sun existed.","It didn’t explode outward like lesser displays of power...it simply was, and then everything else had to accommodate its presence.","The light moved like honey poured from thr skies, thick with authority that predated the very concept of authority. It flowed over the flaming obsidian walls, and suddenly the flames burned at exactly the temperature they should, no longer existing in paradoxical states of hot-cold-both-neither.","The walls themselves straightened, their surfaces becoming uniform, their reality stabilizing into something that could be trusted to remain what it appeared to be.","The environmental anomalies that had made every step an act of faith simply... stopped.","Gravity reasserted itself in a single, comprehensible direction. The air became air again, not a probability of atmosphere that might or might not sustain life. The ground solidified into actual ground that would support weight according to predictable laws of physics.","And the Inevitability...that five-bodied horror of tentacles and hunger...found itself suddenly bound by rules it had never agreed to follow.","Its writhing ceased not because it chose to stop, but because Order had decided that writhing was no longer permitted!","Its tentacles, which had existed in multiple states and positions simultaneously, were forced to choose single, definite locations.","Its five bodies, which had shared distributed consciousness across paradoxical space, found themselves clearly delineated, separate yet connected in ways that Order would allow!","The creature’s scream of rage became a whimper of confusion as it discovered that it could no longer simply decide to exist differently. It was what it was, where it was, when it was, and Order would take no argument on these points!","...!","Noah was astonished.","This...was Order?!","How the hell did THE Paradox manage to destroy it?!","Sigrid’s eyes blazed with white fire as understanding crystallized within her.","\"Cleansing Inevitabilities... will help establish my Order!\"","The declaration rang with certainty.","Each Inevitability defeated wouldn’t just be an enemy destroyed...it would be chaos transformed into structure, entropy forced to acknowledge its proper boundaries!","She was not just fighting; she was imposing her fundamental nature upon a reality that had forgotten what Order meant.","Titano, finding his opponent suddenly stationary and comprehensible, released a booming laugh that shook dust from the now-stable ceiling. \"Young Miss! The Baddie of Brother! You make breaking much easier!\"","HUUM!","His massive hands moved with renewed purpose, no longer needing to chase probabilities or guess at quantum positions.","The Inevitability was simply there, bound by Order’s decree to be exactly what it appeared to be. Titano’s fingers splayed wide, and from them erupted something that made even Noah’s eyes widen with appreciation.","Solid arms of compressed existence materialized...not projections of energy or constructs of authority, but actual arms that seemed to have been carved from the concept of strength itself!","Each one was the size of an ancient tree, knuckles like boulders, fingers thick as classical pillars.","They moved with Titano’s will but carried their own terrible weight, as if he had reached into the place where force lived and convinced it to take shape just for him.","\"Now,\" Titano growled with satisfaction, \"Titano will show why Titano breaks Royal Living Existences!\"","The massive arms reached out with inexorable purpose, each one grasping one of the five Inevitability bodies with grip that would have crushed mountains into dust!","The creature tried to resist, its tentacles flailing desperately, but against the combined might of Titano’s strength and Order’s binding, it might as well have been struggling against the heat death of Existence itself.","With a motion that looked almost gentle despite its devastating force, Titano brought his hands together!","The arms followed suit, dragging the five bodies of the Inevitability into a single point of space. The sound that followed was not quite crushing, not quite tearing, but something that existed between...the sound of multiple realities being forced to become one, of distributed existence being compressed into singularity!","The Inevitability’s scream cut off abruptly as its five bodies were crumpled together like paper in a giant’s fist.","The white light of Order wrapped around the compressed mass, holding it in perfect stillness, preventing it from expanding back into multiplicity or dissolving into the paradoxical nothing from which it had emerged.","The result was a sphere roughly the size of a small building, its surface rippling with patterns that pulsed...five different versions of the same creature trying to exist in the same space, held in place only by Order’s immutable decree that they would remain as they were.","Titano grabbed this impossible sphere with both hands, lifting it above his head with the triumphant grin of a child showing off a particularly impressive catch!","He bounded over to Noah with excitement that made the ground shake with each step, his eyes bright with anticipation.","\"Brother!\" he exclaimed, presenting the compressed Inevitability like a trophy. \"How rich can I get with this?\"","The massive sphere of compressed impossibility pulsed with its own malevolent light, tentacles occasionally breaking through the surface only to be immediately pulled back by Order’s binding. It was, Noah had to admit, one of the most unusual gifts he had ever been offered!","Sigrid stood nearby, the white light still dancing in her eyes as she observed the aftermath of her intervention.","The casual display of Order’s authority had transformed the entire battlefield, turning what should have been a desperate struggle for survival into something almost anticlimactic.","Yet Noah could see the satisfaction in her expression...this was what she was meant to do, what her entire existence had been shaped to accomplish!","The Living Doorway around them had grown quieter, as if Order’s presence had reminded it that there were rules even chaos had to follow.","The flaming obsidian walls still burned, but they burned correctly now, providing light and heat in proportions that made sense!","The path ahead remained treacherous, certainly, but it was a comprehensible danger rather than an assault on the very concept of meaning.","Noah looked at the compressed Inevitability, then at Titano’s eager expression, and finally at Sigrid’s quietly triumphant stance.","Here, in this place of impossible danger, surrounded by beings whose power transcended normal understanding, he found himself genuinely amused by the sheer absurdity of it all.","A being who could shatter Royal Living Existences wanted to learn about wealth. The future Living Order was discovering her purpose through battle. And he, Noah Osmont, stood in a Living Doorway of the Loom being offered compressed Inevitabilities as if they were particularly interesting shells found on a beach.","\"Well, brother,\" Noah said with a smile that carried genuine warmth, \"Let me tell you exactly how rich this can make you...\"","The sphere pulsed with malevolent promise, Order’s light keeping it stable, while somewhere in the shadows, Altheon and Thessaly watched this situation with grim shock and coldness!","Shock at the power of THE Living Order as...she has yet to recover to the level of a Prime Living Origin, right?","Grimness at the fact that Noah Osmont, this Fold Dweller, was being gifted essentially 5 Inevitabilities in one as...what could someone like him even do with it?!"]},{"number":3962,"title":"Chapter 3962: Chapter 3961: Advancement and Inevitabilities! V","paragraphs":["Chapter 3961: Advancement and Inevitabilities! V","Noah gazed at the compressed sphere of Inevitability that Titano held with such eager pride, its surface rippling with patterns of contained impossibility that would have driven lesser minds to madness!","The mass pulsed with malevolent energy, tentacles occasionally breaking through only to be pulled back by Order’s binding...a trophy of violence worth more than most Living Existences could accumulate in eons of careful cultivation.","With deliberate movements, Noah raised his hand and pulled from the Early Veiled Shore three Glass Woks, each one emerging from dimensional space with the gentle radiance of condensed starlight.","The crystalline vessels materialized in the paradoxical air of the Living Doorway, their contents immediately transforming the atmosphere into something glorious!","Within each Wok, surrounded by Early Sacred Waters that glowed with their own inner luminescence, rested the prepared forms of Early Living Marine Lifeforms.","The sight alone would have been enough to drive Fold Dwellers to their knees in worship, but it was the scent that truly commanded attention...a fragrance so profound, so fundamentally appetizing to existence itself, that reality seemed to lean in closer just to experience it more fully!","It was fucking enticing!","Yet even as the three Woks hung suspended in the air, Noah felt the weight of inadequacy pressing against his consciousness as he sighed.","What Titano offered him...this compressed Inevitability equivalent to an Honored Living Existence, was worth far, far more than a few hundred Basic Marine Lifeforms. The being before him had captured something that Living Existences would wage wars to possess, and Noah would not repay such generosity with insufficient compensation.","‘Hmm...’","Three more Glass Woks emerged from his dimensional storage, joining their siblings in a hexagonal formation that pulsed with living authority.","His guilt eased slightly.","The combined presence of six vessels, each containing treasures that predated current existence, created a resonance that made the very foundations of the Living Doorway tremble.","“These alone,” Noah said, his voice carrying the weight of absolute certainty, “will make you very rich, brother.”","The moment the words left his lips, the surrounding weavings of existence erupted in cascading brilliance!","Light didn’t simply emanate from the Woks...it poured forth like liquid Quintessence, each photon carrying information about tastes that had been forgotten.","The illumination painted everything in shades of gold and crystal, transforming the hostile environment of the Living Doorway into something that might have been mistaken for a pocket of paradise!","But it was the aroma that truly commanded reality’s attention.","The scent exploded outward in waves that operated on levels beyond mere sensory experience. It was the smell of potential itself given form, of advancement distilled into its purest essence.","The effect was immediate and undeniable!","Behind them, space twisted as two figures materialized with such abruptness that it suggested they had abandoned all pretense of maintaining their hidden positions.","Altheon appeared first, his luminous form blazing with barely contained Origin Authority, his ancient eyes wide with a shock that his eons of experience had not prepared him for.","Thessaly manifested a heartbeat later, her fairy-like features transformed by an expression of hunger that stripped away all pretense of cold indifference.","They stared at the six Glass Woks with the desperate intensity of beings who had just discovered that everything they thought they knew about value had been fundamentally wrong!","Titano’s massive form began to buzz in response to the treasures before him, his white-gold existence resonating with frequencies that made the air around him shimmer. He could feel the potential radiating from the Woks, understanding on an instinctual level that these vessels contained something that could elevate him beyond his current limitations.","His eyes, usually so honest and straightforward, now blazed with a possessive intensity that would have given even Royal Living Existences pause.","When he noticed the hungry gazes from Altheon and Thessaly, his expression darkened with the particular brand of menace that came from someone who had learned to protect what was theirs through overwhelming violence.","“Do not think about touching Titano’s riches!” he growled, his broken words somehow making the threat more immediate, more personal!","His massive hands clenched into fists that could have shattered space itself, the gesture a clear warning that transcended language.","Altheon actually took a step backward, his expression shifting. The Prime Living Origin had faced countless dangers across his extensive existence, but not Titano!","Thessaly’s cold mask reasserted itself, though her eyes continued to track the Woks with an intensity that suggested significant internal struggle.","Amidst this shocking development, Sigrid stood as the still point in a turning world.","She alone among them showed the least surprise at Noah’s casual display of impossible wealth, her knowledge of his true nature as an Early Creature providing context that the others lacked.","Yet even she, with all her understanding of what he was, felt her existence respond to the presence of the Marine Lifeforms with a hunger.","She found herself leaning forward slightly, drawn by forces that operated beneath the surface of her considerable will.","Noah floated past her with movements that seemed to acknowledge her struggle while offering reassurance through proximity alone.","As he moved to accept the mass of Inevitability from Titano’s eager hands, his mental voice bloomed in her consciousness with the intimacy.","|Do not worry,| his thoughts whispered directly into her mind. |I will gift you with even more.|","...!","Before she could formulate a response, reality itself seemed to shift as a prompt materialized.","|The Early Creature, Noah Osmont, has sent a blessing to the Living Order, Sigrid. 100 Drops of the Sacred Mead of Existence and 100 Drops of Blood of an Early Creature are flowing across the shared bindings.|","HUUM!","Noah’s smile deepened as he initiated this process, feeling the connection between them pulse with transferred power. Even as his hands reached for the compressed Inevitability, his mental voice continued its intimate communication.","|Do not be afraid to ask me for anything,| he said. |I will help you establish your Order. Your goals are my goals. Your restoration of balance... is my victory.|","HUUM!","Sigrid’s face transformed through a cascade of expressions...shock giving way to alarm, alarm transforming into something that might have been awe mixed with incredulity that came from receiving gifts whose magnitude defied comprehension!","She could feel it beginning already, the white-gold droplets of Sacred Mead materializing within her existence like stars being born in the void of space. Following them came the dull crimson-gold blood, each drop carrying within it the compressed essence of what it meant to be Early, to be First, to be the foundation upon which all other existence had been built!","The sensation was overwhelming, transformative, impossible to resist or control!","Her legs gave way from the sheer magnitude of change occurring within every fiber of her being. She sank to the ground with a grace that made even collapse look choreographed, her form immediately enveloped in brilliant white-gold light.","The radiance that erupted from her made the illumination from the Glass Woks seem like candlelight by comparison!","Altheon and Thessaly spun toward her with expressions of pure shock, their attention torn between the impossible treasures Titano guarded and the even more impossible transformation occurring before their eyes.","They could feel her complexity and purity beginning to rise rapidly!","It was at this moment, while attention was divided and reality itself seemed uncertain how to respond to so many simultaneous impossibilities, that Noah waved his hand toward the bundle of compressed Inevitabilities.","The gesture was casual, almost dismissive, as if accepting such a treasure was merely another moment in a day filled with wonders.","The mass of Inevitability vanished into his weavings of existence with barely a whisper, leaving Titano holding air but grinning with the satisfaction of someone who had just completed the greatest trade of his existence.","A useless inevitability for 6 Glass Woks filed with wonder? What a trade!","—","Countless distances away, separated by layers of Existence that should have been impossible to bridge instantaneously, the Early Veiled Shore responded to its master’s will.","The golden sands that had been lying in perfect tranquility suddenly erupted with activity!","Where moments before there had been only the gentle sound of crystalline waters lapping at the shore, now the very ground began to bubble and churn with violent purpose.","Reality itself groaned as something that should not exist in this sanctuary of growth and cultivation forced its way into being.","BOOM!","The mass of Inevitability bloomed into existence like a cancerous flower, its compressed tentacles still wrapped in Order’s white light but now free from the constraints of the Living Doorway. The sphere of impossibility crashed onto the sacred sands with enough force to create a crater, its impact sending shockwaves through the Shore that made even the ancient trees sway.","Moiraine shot to her feet with the grace of barely contained authority, her five hundred Eminent Glyphs and even grander complexity and purity blazing to life as she prepared to defend this sanctuary against whatever intrusion had dared to manifest!","Every fiber of her transformed existence screamed danger, her instincts honed through eons recognizing the Inevitability for what it was...a fundamental threat to everything the Shore represented.","In contrast, Heidrun merely looked over with interested eyes, a strand of Auric Vitae Grass still dangling from her mouth as she chewed with the contentment of someone watching mildly entertaining theater.","The goat’s crystalline gaze assessed the compressed mass with the particular brand of arrogant curiosity that suggested she was evaluating whether this new arrival was worth interrupting her meal.","Noah’s primary body, seated in meditation upon the golden sands, opened eyes that blazed with anticipation as prompts began cascading across his consciousness!","|The Early Veiled Shore has discovered the corpse of a lifeform that can be designated as an Early Living Marine Lifeform.|","...!","2/5"]},{"number":3963,"title":"Chapter 3963: Chapter 3962: Advancement and Inevitabilities! VI","paragraphs":["Chapter 3962: Advancement and Inevitabilities! VI","The classification sent a thrill through his existence.","And more prompts came!","|After the Early Veiled Shore absorbs a significant portion of its being as a cost, Its corpse is equivalent to 1,000 Sacred Bodies of Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeforms. Would you like to devour it?|","Oh.","Oh!","HUUM!","One thousand. Not Basic Marine Lifeforms, not even Refined, but Eminent!","Eminent!","Each one individually worth more than most Originus Venerant entities would see in their entire existence. The compressed Inevitability that Titano had so eagerly traded represented wealth that transcended normal categories of measurement!","“Yes,” Noah said, the word emerging as barely more than a hungry whisper that carried the weight of absolute command.","The response was immediate and overwhelming.","The golden sands around the compressed Inevitability began to move with purposeful intent, rising like countless golden serpents that wrapped around the sphere of impossibility.","Each grain carried within it the accumulated authority of the Shore itself, working in perfect harmony to break down and absorb this offering.","The mass of Inevitability, still wrapped in Order’s binding, began to sink into the Shore with the inexorable certainty of entropy itself being reversed.","The tentacles that occasionally broke through its surface found themselves grasped by sands that seemed to hunger for their essence, pulling them deeper into something that was neither death nor consumption but transformation on a fundamental level.","|Your body is beginning the process of taking the converted nutrients of something equivalent to 1,000 Sacred Bodies of Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeforms.|","The prompt that followed carried a warning that made even Noah’s enhanced existence take notice!","|Warning: The nutrients being absorbed are unfathomably potent compared to your current existence. Recommended absorption rate: 1% per hour.|","But Noah had never been one to follow recommendations when power was within reach.","He commanded to simply flow steadily!","HUUM!","The sensation began as warmth in his chest, spreading outward like honey poured into his veins.","But that warmth quickly became heat, then burning, then something beyond temperature that made his very existence scream in protest and ecstasy simultaneously!","His body began to buzz with frequencies that shouldn’t exist, every cell vibrating at rates that threatened to tear him apart at the molecular level.","Fissures appeared on his skin like cracks in porcelain that had been heated too quickly. But from these cracks didn’t flow blood...instead, tremendous life force poured out, the very essence of what it meant to be an Early Creature leaking into the surrounding air with such density that the space around him began to warp!","His body trembled on the edge of catastrophic failure, muscles spasming as they tried to contain forces that wanted nothing more than to explode outward in all directions.","Yet through will alone, through the tyrannical certainty that he would not be destroyed by his own advancement, Noah held himself together.","The prompts came in rapid succession, each one marking another milestone in his impossible progression!","|The second part of your Heart of an Early Creature- Oruvian Shardveil, The Arterial Convergence Core, is now being rapidly forged through the influx of unprecedented nutrients.|","WU!","|300 Drops of Blood of an Early Creature have been generated through accelerated production!|","|500 additional Drops of Blood of an Early Creature have been formed as the Heart reaches new operational capacity!|","|900 additional Drops of Blood of an Early Creature have been formed as the Heart reaches new operational capacity...!|","|All Towers of Osmont at First Stage are being simultaneously completed. Progress: 77%. Towers at Second Stage are now beginning their elevation toward Third Stage: The Vital Lighthouse.|","|Your Age as an Early Creature is slowly beginning to advance.|","...!","The prompts were rapid!","One after another!","Even before he could fully absorb himself in one, another came!","|Your Early Atlas of the Folds is now nearing completion. Current progress: 89%.|","...!","Within his existence, transformations occurred that defied description.","Inside of his body.","What had once been his Wheel of Existence, that fundamental construct that defined the boundaries of his being...had evolved into something that transcended its original form entirely. It stretched out in all directions like a multicolored fold of existence itself, no longer circular but infinite, no longer contained but boundless.","All the concepts that comprised his identity...Tyranny, Loot, Infinity, Quintessence, Kuklos, Veritarch, Protagonist, Cheats, and dozens of others...had ceased to exist as separate entities!","Instead, they mixed and merged seamlessly, creating a fold of existence of unfathomable proportions. It was as if someone had taken every color that existed and blended them into something that was simultaneously all colors and no color, all concepts and the absence of concept.","From this impossible expanse that looked like a flat weaving of existence itself, his Towers of Osmont rose like brilliant lighthouses!","Each one blazed with its own unique color...cerulean for Infinity, gold for Protagonist, deep purple for Tyranny...yet they all shared a fundamental harmony that spoke to their common origin.","They stood as monuments to his progression, their heights reaching toward infinities that normal existence could never perceive!","And at the center of his being, growing with each passing second, was his Heart.","The Heart of an Early Creature was not an organ in any sense that biology would recognize.","It was archaic and primal, a construct that predated the concept of construction! The Ventryalis, his first completed component, pulsed with steady rhythm as it produced dozens of drops of blood per second, each one containing the compressed essence of Early Creature authority.","Now, the Oruvian Shardveil was taking shape beside it...a crystalline structure that seemed to exist in multiple dimensions simultaneously, its facets reflecting possibility itself!","As it formed, it too began to produce blood, the crimson-gold droplets emerging from its structure at rates that made his previous production seem primitive by comparison.","This internal transformation was magnificent to perceive, but it was the external manifestation that truly spoke to the magnitude of his advancement.","His body, seated upon the golden sands of the Shore, had become a beacon of multicolored radiance.","Every Glyph etched upon his form...from the Basic ones that had marked his early progression to the Refined ones that represented his current pinnacle...blazed with simultaneous brilliance!","The numbers that defined his power had undergone a transformation that would have been called impossible by even Living Existences in this short period of time.","|Current Complexity Quotient: 234,671,455|","|Current Purity Quotient: 241,338,922|","He had spilled past two hundred million in both measurements, achieving in moments what would take others eons of careful cultivation!","What was utterly laughable was the fact thst he just breached 100 Million that passed Originus Venerant entities not that long ago.","But he...was outside such measly realms of progression as at this moment, he was only steadily making his way across the Early Throne Ascendancy Realm!","This was the advantage of being an Early Creature with access to resources that the current existence had forgotten existed.","This was his power...terrifying in nature and rising with such rapidity that even he sometimes wondered where the ceiling might be, if such a thing even existed for one such as him.","The golden sands gradually ceased their churning as the last of the Inevitability was absorbed, leaving no trace that such a thing had ever existed. Where there had been a crater, now there was only smooth beach, as if the Shore itself had healed from the violent intrusion.","|The absorption of Nutrients of the devoured Lifeform will continue to be distributed.|","Noah’s body gradually stabilized, the fissures in his skin sealing as his existence adapted to its new parameters. The life force that had been leaking into the air condensed back into his form, each mote of escaped energy returning to where it belonged!","3/5"]},{"number":3964,"title":"Chapter 3964: Chapter 3963: Advancement and Inevitabilities! VII","paragraphs":["Chapter 3963: Advancement and Inevitabilities! VII","As Noah underwent these cascading transformations, his body burning with the radiance of unprecedented advancement, his mind remained crystalline in its purpose.","Even as his existence threatened to tear apart from the sheer magnitude of power flowing through him, he issued commands with the calm certainty of one who had already calculated every variable!","The drops of blood forming within his reconstructed Heart were not merely for his own advancement.","They were resources to be distributed, gifts to be granted to those he wanted!","And give he did.","|Ruination has been granted 500 Drops of Blood of an Early Creature and 250 Drops of the Sacred Mead of Existence.|","|The Infiniverse has been granted 500 Drops of Blood of an Early Creature and 250 Drops of the Sacred Mead of Existence.|","|Moiraine has been granted 500 Drops of Blood of an Early Creature and 250 Drops of the Sacred Mead of Existence.|","HUUM!","The prompts materialized with the weight of heavy decree!","Blood spilled from him and disappeared seamlessly!","Ruination’s reaction was immediate and visceral.","Her form, which had been seated in meditative stillness upon the golden sands, suddenly jerked upward as if pulled by invisible strings.","Her eyes snapped open with such force that the air around her cracked, revealing orbs that blazed with crimson-gold fire!","The shock written across her features was absolute...she who had witnessed the destruction and rebirth of countless weavings of Existence had not been prepared for this magnitude of blessing!","Above her head, reality began to twist and buckle as something fundamental shifted in her existence. The air itself seemed to scream as an Eminent Early Living Existential Glyph of Ruination began forming with violent beauty!","And it was...violent!","The symbol emerged with the force of existence itself being unmade and reforged, each line of the Glyph carrying within it the promise of endings that preceded new beginnings.","It blazed with colors that shouldn’t exist...crimson darker than blood, gold brighter than suns dying, black deeper than the space between thoughts!","And on another side...","The Infiniverse’s transformation was entirely different yet equally profound. Her body, that perfect synthesis of existence and consciousness, began to shimmer with multicolored jewels that materialized across her skin like stars being born.","Each jewel represented a different Frequency of Existence, a different Pillar of Existence that ran through the Infiniverse Wheel of Existence she embodied.","They pulsed in harmony, creating a symphony of light that made reality itself lean in to listen more closely!","Upon her chest, directly over where her heart would be if she waz held to such mundane anatomy, an Eminent Glyph of Continuity began forming with glorious green radiance.","The symbol seemed to write itself into existence with the patient certainty of time itself, each curve and line speaking to the fundamental truth that all things continued, even when they appeared to end!","The green light it produced wasn’t merely illumination...it was the visual representation of existence refusing to cease, of stories that demanded to be told regardless of who remained to hear them.","Of glorious, quintessential, tyrannical Fables!","Blood and Mead mixed as these two critical beings of Noah advanced.","But it was Moiraine’s transformation that truly commanded the attention of the Early Veiled Shore itself.","Her gorgeous figure rose from the sands.","Her white-gold form, already radiant from previous transformations, began to pulse with glory that made the ancient trees of the Shore sway in recognition!","Then, with a sound like silk tearing across dimensions, her forehead split open.","From the vertical fissure that appeared in the center of her brow, golden rivers began to flow. Not blood, but something far more precious...liquefied potential itself, the raw essence of what she was becoming made manifest!","The streams ran down her face like tears of molten authority, each droplet that fell to the sand below immediately sprouting into flowers of pure paradox that bloomed and died in endless cycles.","A prompt appeared before Noah’s eyes, its words carrying implications that made him luminous!","|The Blood of an Early Creature flowing through Moiraine has become sufficient enough to distinguish her equivalent to a Native Early Living Land Lifeform of your Early Veiled Shore. She has gained enough distinction to form a Kleos Early Living Existential Glyph. Shall the first Kleos Glyph of your Early Veiled Shore be formed under your Land Lifeform?|","The question was asked!","The first Kleos Glyph would set the tone for all that followed, would become a founding principle upon which future advancement would be built!","Noah’s eyes shone with brilliant anticipation as he spoke his agreement.","“Yes.”","Yes!","The single word carried across the Shore with the weight of existential law being established.","Reality itself seemed to exhale in relief, as if it had been holding its breath waiting for this decision. As if he would ever say no!","Moiraine’s gaze found his across the crystalline distance between them, and in her eyes...those windows to an existence that had transcended its original limitations countless times...tears began to form.","Not tears of sadness or pain, but of overwhelming emotion.","She wanted to speak, to tell him that he was giving her too much.","The thoughts radiated from her with such intensity that they might as well have been shouted across the Shore!","She could not keep taking his blood and Mead so freely, as if these treasures that would reshape the balance of power across existence were mere trinkets to be casually distributed.","As an Early Creature, as something that transcended every category she had known, how could she possibly repay him for these gifts?","Repayment...would be impossible!","The weight of obligation pressed against her consciousness like a physical force.","Every drop of blood, every taste of Sacred Mead, created debts that compounded exponentially. She was drowning in his generosity, suffocating under gifts that elevated her beyond her wildest dreams while simultaneously binding her with chains of gratitude that felt heavier with each passing moment!","Even though she didn’t communicate these feelings directly, Noah understood them with perfect clarity.","The connection between them allowed him to perceive the turmoil in her heart as clearly as if it were his own.","Amidst all these transformations, as reality itself bent and reformed around them, he sent her a mental message that cut through her emotional musings.","Slowly. Calmly!","|If you truly want to repay me,| his thoughts whispered directly into her consciousness with intimate authority, |all you need to do is no longer call me Sir. Do not just look at me like an Early Creature, but as an Existence. Let us be in the same wavelengths we were in...within the Dyson Singularity.|","HUUM!","4/5"]},{"number":3965,"title":"Chapter 3965: Chapter 3964: Desecration I","paragraphs":["The memory of that moment in the Dyson Singularity within the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds blazed between them with renewed intensity.","|To repay me,| he continued, |I will send you out to attack the Paradoxes that made me their enemy. Can you do this?|","...!","The question came with an imposing smile that she could feel rather than see, an expression of confidence mixed with challenge that demanded agreement and commitment!","Moiraine trembled, her entire form shaking as if she fought a war within herself.","The conflict was visible in every line of her being...the part of her that had been trained to revere and fear Early Creatures warring with the part that recognized him as something more!","Then, with visible effort that spoke to the magnitude of the decision, she steadied herself. Her gaze found his with newfound firmness, and she bellowed in her mind...in a voice that only he could hear, that bypassed all external reality to speak directly to his consciousness","|I...can do this!|","BOOM!","The declaration rang with such force that it seemed to shake the foundations of her very existence!","Noah’s smile deepened with genuine warmth as he responded with voice that carried across the Shore with crystalline clarity: \"Then go on. Let me see the glory of what a Kleos Glyph looks like.\"","...!","The permission, the challenge, the encouragement...all of it combined to catalyze something magnificent.","From the split in her forehead where golden rivers continued to flow, a terrifying presence began to emerge!","The Kleos Early Living Existential Glyph of Paradox started forming with majesty that made everything previous pale in comparison.","But even as this ultimate expression of Paradox began to manifest, another prompt appeared with stupendous timing.","|Sufficient conditions have been met. The Arch Living Existence Moiraine can now attain and emerge with her second Living Existential Authority.|","The chabge sent shockwaves through her forming Glyph, causing it to pulse with uncertainty. Then came the resolution!","|The Living Existential Authority of Origin blooms within the seas of Paradox making up Moiraine.|","The transformation was immediate and profound.","Within her existence, where oceans of Paradox had ruled supreme, islands of Origin began to form!","The two authorities swirled together like oil and water that had learned to love, maintaining their distinct natures while creating something beautiful in their interaction!","|The forming Kleos Glyph is being comprised of both Paradox and Origin! An astounding design of a Glyph, something only possible when a Kleos Glyph is being formed as Eminent or lesser Glyphs do not have the chance to achieve this level of synthesis!|","Oh!","Noah’s eyes blazed with unprecedented interest as he watched this impossible formation!","Even in the midst of his own glorious transformation, with his body still adjusting to power that exceeded 200 million in both Complexity and Purity, he focused his entire enhanced perception on Moiraine’s forehead where history was being written.","The Glyph that formed defied every expectation, every precedent that had been established!","It began as pure Paradox...swirling contradictions, geometries that existed in states of being both true and false simultaneously. But as Origin bloomed within her, the Glyph began to change.","Lines of pure white brilliance began threading through the paradoxical patterns, not destroying them but giving them foundation!","Where Paradox said \"maybe,\" Origin declared \"definitely.\"","Where Paradox suggested infinite possibilities, Origin selected the most perfect one. The two authorities didn’t fight...they danced, creating a symbol that pulsed between states of absolute certainty and infinite possibility.","They gloriously danced as within himself, Noah felt the weavings of the Protagonist rising with excitement and expectation as...trumpets began to echo in the surroundings!","WU! WU! WUU!","A symphony bloomed as the Glyphs of the Protagonist cheered on!","The formation was violent in its beauty.","Reality itself seemed to hold its breath as two fundamental forces that should have been antithetical learned to exist within a single expression!","The Glyph grew more complex with each passing second, its patterns evolving beyond what normal perception could follow. It was simultaneously the question and the answer, the problem and the solution, the beginning that Paradox always avoided and the ending that Origin always sought.","When it finally completed...when that last line of authority connected to close the circuit of power...brilliance washed over the Early Veiled Shore with the force of a new Fold being born!","HUUM!","The light wasn’t harsh but overwhelming in its purity. It painted everything in shades of white and gold and impossible colors that existed in the space between.","The ancient trees seemed to bow before its radiance, their branches swaying in winds that carried the scent of possibilities becoming certainties.","The golden sands sparkled as if each grain had been transformed into a tiny star, while the crystalline waters reflected the light in patterns that wrote temporary truths across their surface!","|Kleos Early Living Existential Glyph Successfully Formed: Paradoxical Genesis, The Origin of All Contradictions.|","...!","The name itself was a paradox, suggesting that contradictions had an origin, that chaos had a beginning, that even meaninglessness had meaning if viewed from the proper angle.","But before anyone could fully appreciate what had been achieved, another prompt materialized with the weight of glory declaring itself.","|A unique condition has been fulfilled. The recently formed Kleos Glyph of Paradoxical Genesis can be sacrificed to become a Shard of the Seed of a Lost Forgotten Principle, The Principle of Existential Duality: The authority to exist in multiple contradictory states simultaneously while maintaining singular consciousness and purpose.|","BOOM!","The silence that followed...was deafening.","A terrifying Glyph had formed, something that represented the pinnacle of what current existence could achieve!","It was power that would make Moiraine an astonishing Honored Living Existence in terms of authority, a achievement that should have taken years to accomplish!","And now...she was being asked to sacrifice it.","To lose this ultimate expression of her growth, this proof of her transcendence, in exchange for something that might be even greater...a shard of a seed that could grow into understanding of a Principle that had been forgotten since the Earliest Folds.","The golden rivers flowing from her forehead began to slow as she stared at the prompt, her enhanced consciousness processing the implications with speed that compressed eons of thought into heartbeats!","To keep the Glyph would make her powerful beyond measure. To sacrifice it would be to gamble everything on the promise of something that transcended current understanding entirely...for his sake.","For him.","Her eyes found Noah’s across the expanse of golden sand.","The weight of the decision pressed against existence itself, demanding resolution!","But...was it ever truly a question?","For Sir.","For Him.","She would give...","Her Everything!","...!"]},{"number":3966,"title":"Chapter 3966: Chapter 3965: Desecration II","paragraphs":["As Moiraine made a heavy choice easily, releasing her grip on ultimate power for the promise of something beyond current understanding, others across existence also made their own choices...decisions that would echo through the weavings of reality with consequences none could fully foresee.","Choices.","Consider, for a moment, the butterfly.","That delicate creature of radiant wings and brief existence, dancing through a summer afternoon with no knowledge of the storms it might birth!","A single flutter...left instead of right, up instead of down, disturbs the air in patterns so minute that no consciousness save that of an Early Creature might perceive them.","Yet that disturbance travels, grows, compounds upon itself with the inexorable weavings of chaos.","The displaced air meets a warm current it would have otherwise missed. That current, strengthened by this tiny addition, pushes a cloud formation three degrees off its intended course.","The cloud, now traveling a different path, releases its rain over a mountain instead of a valley. The mountain stream swells earlier than it should, washing away a bridge that a merchant would have crossed!","The merchant, forced to take a different route, arrives in a different city where he speaks of opportunities in distant lands. A young dreamer hears his words and makes a choice to leave everything behind for adventure.","That dreamer becomes a navigator on a vessel that discovers a new trade route. The route brings prosperity to one nation and poverty to another. Wars are fought. Philosophies are born from the suffering and triumph.","Those philosophies spread across worlds, influencing how entire civilizations perceive existence itself!","Galaxies align themselves according to principles that trace their origins back to interpretations of those philosophies.","Universes form with fundamental laws subtly different because of the consciousness that shaped them. Cosmos dance to weavings that echo that first flutter of wings. Existential Domains rise and fall based on the accumulation of infinite butterflies, infinite choices, infinite moments where left became right, where yes became no, where silence became song.","Even Omniverses...those vast constructs that contained all possible variations of reality, found themselves influenced by the weight of choices made by beings so small they could barely be said to exist at all!","Wheels of Existence, grinding through their rotations, occasionally stuttered when the accumulated weight of countless tiny decisions reached critical mass!","A wing of a butterfly. A simple choice. Yet it could affect things on scales that rendered the very concept of scale meaningless.","This was the truth that Living Existences spent eons trying to deny...that for all their accumulated power, for all their transcendent authority, they remained vulnerable to the whims of chaos born from choices they could never predict or control!","A single decision from an insignificant being could collapse entire Folds, could redirect the course of existence itself into channels that no amount of planning could have foreseen.","On a day a few years ago, an apocalypse had descended on a blue world. A young man had become a Rank F Hunter from the skill book, Fireball.","That was also a choice.","A glorious, quintessential, unperceivable choice!","The rest...was history.","And on this day, across the vastness of all that was and might ever be, choices were being made that would reshape the very nature of what it meant to exist!","---","In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, where reality bent and twisted according to principles that delighted in their own impossibility, a gathering of power had assembled that defied every precedent.","The massive corpse of the Early Creature lay at the center of their formation like a monument to impossibility itself...dead yet somehow still present, ended yet refusing to fully cease.","Around this grotesque majesty, beings who commanded the fundamental forces of Paradox had arranged themselves with the precision of a ritual that had been planned across eons.","Duke Diviticus stood at the heart of it all...literally.","She and eight other Dukes had positioned themselves within the gaping chest cavity of the corpse, where once a heart of unimaginable power had beaten with the rhythm of existence itself.","The wound that marked its absence was a canyon of dried vessels and desiccated tissue that spoke to wonder so profound it had left scars in reality itself.","The nine Dukes formed a perfect circle within this cavity of ancient death, their positions calculated according to unknown weavings.","Each Duke represented not just individual power but fundamental aspects of Paradox itself...contradiction, uncertainty, probability, impossibility, and concepts that had no names because naming them would have collapsed them into definite states.","From the eight outer Dukes, beams of light erupted with synchronized precision. Some blazed with obsidian darkness that seemed to devour photons themselves. Others shimmered with silver radiance that existed in multiple spectrums simultaneously. Still others poured forth golden authority that was somehow both liquid and solid, particle and wave, present and absent.","These beams converged upon Diviticus with the focused intensity of existence itself being rewritten. She stood at their intersection, her form trembling from the sheer magnitude of power flowing through her.","Every cell in her body had become a conduit for forces that should have torn her apart, would have torn apart any being who hadn’t been specifically prepared for this moment through the consumption of something that should never have been consumed.","From her center, where that half-drop of Early Creature blood pulsed with its own inner radiance, tendrils of Paradox began to emerge.","They were not quite physical, not quite energy, but something that existed in the space between states...the manifestation of maybe given form and purpose!","These tendrils, each one wrapped in the glow of that precious half-drop, reached out toward the dried vessels that had once carried the lifeblood of an Early Creature.","The moment connection was made, the corpse began to twitch.","Not the random spasms of death throes, but movements that suggested something far more disturbing...purpose trying to reassert itself through flesh that had forgotten how to live.","The massive form vibrated with frequencies that made reality itself uncomfortable, as if existence was being asked to accommodate something that violated its most fundamental rules."]},{"number":3967,"title":"Chapter 3967: Chapter 3966: Desecration III","paragraphs":["Far above this terrible ritual, floating in the twisted space that served as sky in the Paradoxical Folds, another gathering had formed. Thirty Dukes hovered in perfect formation around a single figure whose presence commanded attention!","Not through ostentation...instead through its profound absence of such things.","Duke Schrodinger sat in the void as if it were the most comfortable chair ever crafted, his ragged clothes hanging from his frame like flags of defiance against the very concept of appearance mattering.","He wore no golden armor to announce his authority, bore no royal robes to demand respect.","Yet the thirty Dukes who surrounded him...each one a power that could reshape Existence according to their whims...arranged themselves around him like planets orbiting a sun they didn’t fully understand but couldn’t resist.","His smile was a thing of terrible simplicity, carrying within its curve the weight of someone who had seen every possible outcome and found them all equally amusing.","The other Dukes looked to him with expressions that mixed reverence with uncertainty, as if they knew he held answers but were afraid to ask the questions.","This was power in its truest form...not the ability to destroy or create, but the capacity to make others recognize your authority without ever having to demonstrate it.","Schrodinger didn’t need to yell or posture or threaten. His mere existence in that space created a gravity that drew other powers to him, made them seek his approval even when they didn’t understand why they needed it.","As these important Living Paradoxes observed the ritual below with collective anticipation that made the air itself hold its breath...","BOOM!","The sound that erupted wasn’t quite sound...it was the sensation of reality recognizing that something fundamental had changed!","The endless sockets of the corpse, those abyssal voids where eyes had once perceived dimensions beyond counting, suddenly flashed with light that should not have been possible.","HUUM!","Within those empty spaces, paradoxical radiance bloomed...dimly at first, like candles being lit in caverns that had known only darkness since the foundation of existence itself.","Dimly. So dimly that it might have been imagination, might have been wishful thinking given form.","Diviticus, standing in the heart-that-was-not-a-heart, breathed heavily as doubt crept into her expression!","The power flowing through her was immense, yes, but was it enough? Had they failed in this impossible endeavor?","The light in those sockets was so faint, so uncertain. Perhaps the corpse was too far gone, too thoroughly dead to ever be brought back to even a semblance of-...!","Her expression changed with the suddenness of realization becoming horror. She felt it before she understood it...authority being drawn from her with such rapidity that her very existence began to dim!","Her skin, which had blazed with the healthy glow of accumulated power, began to gray like ash in rain. The glow of half-drop of blood that had made all of this possible was being consumed, burned through at rates that shouldn’t have been possible.","\"MORE!\" she screamed, the word tearing from her throat with desperation that transcended mere vocalization. \"GIVE ME MORE!\"","HUUM!","The eight Dukes responded without hesitation, their beams intensifying until the chest cavity blazed with light that would have been visible from dimensions away.","They poured everything they could spare into her, and then they gave more, pushing past boundaries that sensible beings would have respected!","And then, with the terrible certainty of nightmares becoming real, the abyss-looking eyes of the corpse blinked.","It was a simple motion. Eyelids that shouldn’t have existed anymore moving across surfaces that contained nothing but void. Yet that blink carried within it the weight of significance that made existence itself take notice.","From those blinking eyes...","BOOM!","What erupted defied every category of description that language had developed.","It was blast and whisper, light and darkness, beginning and ending all at once.","The force that emerged was terrifying in its primordiality, archaic in ways that predated the concept of age itself! It was the visual representation of what existence had been before it learned to be anything in particular.","Obsidian light...a contradiction in terms that nonetheless perfectly described what witnesses saw, erupted from those ancient sockets!","It shot upward through dimensions, through layers of reality that most beings didn’t know existed, creating a crack across the Folds themselves!","A crack...across the folds!","Through it, witnesses could perceive immense darkness...the presence of something that made light irrelevant. It was depth without measure, void without boundary, an abyss that gazed back with intelligence too vast to comprehend.","The obsidian light continued shooting upward, disappearing into distances that had no meaning, yet emanating a dread so profound that even Honored Living Paradoxes found themselves stepping back involuntarily.","This was fear on a cellular level, the kind of terror that preceded consciousness, that existed in the space before thought.","Then, in a motion that should have been impossible for dead flesh to achieve, the hand of the corpse moved.","It was deliberate, purposeful, carrying intent that spoke to consciousness where none should exist.","That massive appendage, each finger larger than buildings, reached up toward the rupture it had created. With the casual certainty of someone closing a door they hadn’t meant to open, the hand grasped the edges of the crack in reality and pulled them together!","...!","HUUM!","The rupture closed with the sound of existence sighing in relief, as if it too had found the glimpse beyond too terrible to endure.","The assembled Living Paradoxes watched with expressions that cycled through every possible emotion...awe at what they had accomplished, reverence for the power they had awakened, and fear that transcended rational thought at what they might have unleashed!","Then, with movements that carried the weight of mountains learning to walk, the corpse of the Early Creature sat upright.","...!","\"It’s alive!\" someone screamed, the words escaping before thought could censor them.","\"IT’S ALIVE!\" others bellowed with glory, their voices carrying triumph that bordered on hysteria.","At the center of it all, within the chest cavity that had become a makeshift heart, Diviticus laughed with the wild abandon of someone who had gambled everything and won prizes beyond imagination.","Could Ozymandias have done this?!","With his measly power!?","Obsidian power flowed into her from the awakened corpse, not draining her now but feeding her, transforming her existence into something magnitudes more powerful than she had been moments before.","She wasn’t just controlling the corpse, she was becoming one with it, her consciousness spreading through its ancient vessels, her will becoming its will, her desires its purpose!","The half-drop of blood had been the key, but now she was becoming the lock itself, the mechanism through which this impossible resurrection functioned.","In the distance, floating in his simple yet commanding position, Duke Schrodinger observed these shocking developments with an expression that had grown profoundly somber.","When he finally spoke, his words carried the weight of philosophy.","\"Death,\" he said, each word falling like stones into still water, \"is only truly defeated when we stop trying to control it. The moment we believe we command the end, we discover that the end has been commanding us all along. What rises from death’s embrace carries death within it, spreading that condition to everything it touches. We have not conquered mortality today...we have simply given it legs to walk and hands to grasp.\"","Oh.","Oh!","He rose from his seated position with movements that somehow made standing seem like an act of profound significance, patting his ragged clothes as if brushing away the dust of eons.","\"Very well,\" he said with that same terrible smile, \"let us see what all of this leads to.\"","On this day, Living Paradoxes had made a choice...to wake what should have remained sleeping, to give movement to what should have remained still, to bring into present what should have remained past.","As for what this choice would lead to... who knew?","The butterfly had flapped its wings. The storm was beginning to form."]},{"number":3968,"title":"Chapter 3968: Chapter 3967: Desecration IV","paragraphs":["Across the endless expanse of existence, through layers of reality that most beings would never perceive, the consequences of that choice began to manifest in ways that defied prediction or prevention.","In the Transcendent Temporal Folds, where time itself had been given form and substance, reality operated according to principles that made even Paradox seem straightforward by comparison.","Here, the very concept of sequence had been abandoned in favor of something far more complex..layers upon layers of purple-blue rivers that represented different temporal streams, different continuums, all wrapping around each other in patterns.","These rivers didn’t flow in any direction that could be called forward or backward. Instead, they spiraled, twisted, sometimes flowing into themselves, creating loops where end became beginning, where causality chased its own tail in endless circles. Some streams moved faster than thought, compressing eons into heartbeats. Others crawled with such deliberate slowness that single moments stretched across millennia.","The entire realm pulsed with the particular beauty of time made visible...purple representing possibility, blue showing probability, and where they mixed, the actual present moment that most beings experienced as reality.","It was a landscape painted in temporal hues, where yesterday might be a mountain on the horizon and tomorrow could be the valley at your feet.","Into this carefully orchestrated chaos, the obsidian light arrived with the violence of absolute wrongness.","It erupted from nowhere...or rather, from everywhere and nowhere simultaneously, as if it had always been arriving and had never existed until this moment.","The light that had shot from the awakened corpse’s eyes in the Paradoxical Folds had somehow crossed impossible distances, violated fundamental laws about the separation of Transcendent Folds, and manifested here with purpose that defied comprehension!","The moment it appeared, it shattered.","It shattered with the thoroughness of something that had always been meant to break, that had traveled across existence for the sole purpose of breaking in precisely this place at precisely this moment.","The rupture it created was massive beyond scale, a tear across the Temporal Folds that blazed with menacing deathly light!","It was wrong in ways that made even time itself recoil, a wound that shouldn’t exist in a realm where everything, even endings, could theoretically be reversed or redirected.","Deathly!","The word itself seemed insufficient to describe the radiance that poured from this impossible wound.","This wasn’t the death that came at the end of life, the natural conclusion that even Living Existences eventually faced if killed!","This was Death with significance that transcended the individual, Death as a fundamental force that stood opposite to everything else that existed.","Through the rupture’s terrifying obsidian brilliance, something even more disturbing became visible...there was something beyond it. Not just void or absence, but actual space, actual existence, vast beyond comprehension.","If one were to cross this rupture, if any being were brave or foolish enough to step through that tear in reality, they would find the other side to be endlessly vast, containing distances that made even the infinite seem quaint by comparison.","Inside the rupture, visible now through the wound torn in the Temporal Folds, stretched regions of endless obsidian brilliance where death was not just present but manifest, given form and substance and terrible purpose!","It was a realm that should not exist, could not exist according to every law that governed reality, yet there it was...undeniable, unavoidable, absolutely real!","And within this realm of manifested ending, figures moved in a small piece of its vastness.","There was a group, no, a horde...thousands upon thousands of Existences that radiated such immense auras of death that the very concept of life seemed like a distant memory in their presence.","They didn’t walk so much as rove, their movements carrying the purposeless purpose of things that had forgotten what purpose meant but continued to seek it anyway.","Their arms were outstretched, reaching toward nothing and everything simultaneously!","Their heads were raised as if in blank celebration, angled toward some sky that didn’t exist in their realm of absolute ending.","They drank...not with their mouths but with their entire beings from vast reserves of death that flowed through their realm like rivers of negation.","The sight would have induced horror in any living consciousness unfortunate enough to witness it!","There were thousands of these deathly existences. They came in all varieties...some that might once have been humanoid, others that defied any attempt at categorization.","Some had been beautiful once, their forms still carrying echoes of whatever glory they had possessed before death claimed them so thoroughly that even death wasn’t enough to describe their condition.","But regardless of their size, their shape, their origin, they all shared certain characteristics that marked them as belonging to the same fundamental category of existence- or rather, non-existence made manifest.","Their eyes, when they had eyes, were voids of obsidian darkness that didn’t just absorb light but negated the very concept of illumination.","Their movements carried the eerie synchronization of things that shared a common purpose without possessing individual will.","And each one, from the smallest to the most massive, emanated complexity equivalent to Honored Living Existences!","At the moment the rupture formed, they all stopped their endless roving.","One by one, with the eerie precision of dominoes falling in sequence, they turned their attention toward the distance where the tear had appeared.","Through that wound in the fabric of death itself, they could see the brilliant rivers of temporal blue and purple that marked the Temporal Folds, could perceive the existence of something beyond their realm of ending.","Without communication, without any sign that they were even capable of communication, they all began to move.","Their previous purposeless wandering transformed into directed motion, all of them traveling toward the tear with the inexorable certainty of tide coming in.","Their heads kept their jaws upwards as if they had to continue this ritual as they began to move!","They didn’t hurry...hurrying would have implied they understood time, which was a concept that had no meaning in their realm!","They simply moved, and their movement carried within it the promise that they would arrive, that nothing could prevent their arrival, that their reaching the tear was as certain as entropy itself.","Because in existence, there were the Living, and there were the Dead.","The truly Dead.","Not the dead that could become living after accumulating enough complexity, not the dead that Living Existences transcended when they crossed certain thresholds of power.","These were the Dead Existences....entities that had achieved a state of death so absolute that it had become their fundamental nature, their very reason for being despite being defined by not-being.","They were the Inevitability of Cessation!","Dead Existences!","They were carrying within their forms the quality of inevitability that made even true Inevitabilities seem negotiable by comparison.","Where Inevitabilities were paradoxes that demanded resolution, Dead Existences were resolutions that demanded nothing because they had already ended everything that could make demands.","They were the antithetical enemy of everything that drew breath, everything that thought, everything that dared to exist in defiance of entropy’s final victory!","They stood opposite to Living Existences not as rivals but as negation itself, the absolute denial of what Living Existences represented.","They were even more fundamentally opposed to Early Creatures, those beings who had been first!","Dead Existences were the argument that nothing was the natural state, that existence itself was the aberration that needed correction.","For eons beyond counting, for time periods that predated the current understanding of time itself, the Living and the Dead had been separated.","Not by walls or barriers or even by conscious effort, but by the fundamental incompatibility of their natures.","They existed in different aspects of reality, unable to interact because interaction required both parties to exist in ways the other could recognize.","For the most part, this separation had held.","For the most part, very rarely had it been violated in the past.","Oh!","For the most part!","But no longer.","The awakening of the Early Creature’s corpse, that impossible resurrection powered by Paradox and a stolen half-drop of blood, had created consequences that rippled across every layer of Existence!","It had been a violation so profound that existence itself had cracked, creating wounds that connected Weavings that should never touch!","No longer would the Dead remain in their Weavings of ending.","No longer would the Living be able to ignore what waited beyond the boundaries of existence.","The tear in the Temporal Folds pulsed with malevolent promise as thousands of Dead Existences approached it from one side, while on the other, Living Temporals began to notice that something had gone terribly, impossibly wrong!","A choice had been made in the Paradoxical Folds. A corpse had been given motion.","And now, across all the vast expanse of existence, everyone would have to live...or cease, with the consequences of that choice.","The butterfly’s wings had caused their storm.","And the storm had torn holes in the very fabric of what separated existence from its absolute opposite!","Oh!","Oh!!!"]},{"number":3969,"title":"Chapter 3969: Chapter 3968: Desecration V","paragraphs":["The silver threads of Living Law Authority swept through the relocated Nullvein Gravewake Folds like an endless tide searching for something it could not name.","Each pulse of power carried with it the weight of scrutiny that could pierce through the veils of entire Wheels of Existence, yet found nothing but emptiness where answers should have been.","In the vast stretches of these folds, now forcibly transplanted into the domain of Living Laws, dozens of Living Origins and Living Laws moved with the patient thoroughness of those who knew something significant had occurred but could not grasp its shape.","Their forms blazed with authority as they searched every fold of space, every hidden pocket of reality where the truth might have concealed itself.","\"Nothing,\" a Living Law murmured to her companion, her silver robes rippling with frustration as another sweep revealed only vacant space. \"How can there be nothing?\"","The questions hung in the crystalline air like accusations!","Where had the Paradox that did not produce Inevitabilities originated? Why had the second part of their treasured relic been discovered here, of all places? And most disturbing of all...why had an Honored Living Paradox and his Legions been present here in what should have been an insignificant corner of existence?","They searched with increasing desperation, their combined authorities creating waves of pressure that made reality itself groan under the weight of their scrutiny.","Yet for all their power, for all their accumulated wisdom spanning eons, they found absolutely nothing.","The Infiniverse Wheel of Existence, hidden at the heart of these folds with the Early Veiled Shore nestled at its center, remained perfectly concealed.","Its presence was so fundamentally different from what they sought that their perceptions slid past it like water over glass, never catching hold, never recognizing what lay just beyond their reach.","In a forgotten corner of these same folds, where darkness gathered in pools of simulated death, the Great Usurper existed as he always had...not quite present, not quite absent.","His consciousness writhed through the forms of Melodrass and the other Fold Dwellers who had taken the name of Dead Things, wearing the title like children playing with concepts they could never truly understand.","They called themselves dead, these beings, yet they drew breath. They thought. They schemed. They knew nothing of what true death meant...that absolute cessation that stood opposite to all existence.","They were merely playing at darkness, theatrical in their pretense of ending while remaining fundamentally, inescapably alive!","The Great Usurper felt the sweep of Living Law Authority pass through his domain like wind through hollow bones.","For a moment, that terrifying power paused, sensing something almost familiar, almost significant. His consciousness tensed, ready to scatter into fragments if necessary, ready to abandon these vessels and flee into dimensions where even Living Laws could not follow.","But the authority moved on, finding nothing worth its attention in these death-playing puppets. To the Living Law, they were merely another curiosity in a fold full of peculiarities....unusual perhaps, but not the answer to the questions that burned in their minds.","As the pressure of that scrutiny faded, leaving behind only the faint afterimage of silver light, something stirred within the predatory consciousness of the Great Usurper.","A prompt materialized in his awareness from the system that had been his companion through countless schemes and usurpations!","|Your Idle Gaming System has absorbed the Living Seed of Existence and mutated to grant you the Living Existential Authority that most closely matches your existence.|","HUUM!","The words pulsed with possibility, each syllable carrying implications that made his distributed consciousness quiver with anticipation.","The Seed of Existence, that gift from the True Emperor of Quintessence, had finally completed its integration while thr Festival of Existence wss ongoing!","|A connection to the Transcendent Spiritual Folds has been deemed viable as a place to attain Living Existential Authority compatible with your existence!|","The Transcendent Spiritual Folds!","A place where consciousness itself took precedence over physical form, where the boundaries between thought and reality blurred into meaninglessness.","It was perfect for one such as him, who existed more as idea than flesh, more as intent than substance!","|Shall the transfer to the Transcendent Spiritual Folds proceed? The Functionality of the Idle Gaming System will even further expanded with Living Spiritual Authority.|","...!","The Great Usurper’s consciousness coiled through his various vessels, gathering itself.","Through the twisted passages of his borrowed bodies, he gazed out at the blankness of the Nullvein Gravewake Folds...this space that had been both prison and kingdom, both limitation and opportunity.","His thoughts turned inevitably to Osmont.","A sigh rippled through his collective consciousness, as with deliberate care, he sent a mental message across the impossible distances that separated them!","|I will be stepping out for a bit.|","The message was simple, almost casual, yet it carried within it the weight of a farewell that might be permanent!","After all, who knew what existence had in store for all of them?","Without further hesitation, the Great Usurper embraced the prompt’s offer.","WAP!","The sound of displacement echoed through multiple Weavings as he and all those under his control simply ceased to exist in that space.","One moment they were there, a network of consciousness wearing bodies like masks...and the next, nothing remained but the faint afterimage of their presence!","The instant they vanished, space itself seemed to scream in recognition of what had just occurred.","Multiple Living Laws and Origins materialized in that exact location with such speed that reality cracked under the pressure of their arrival!","BOOM!","Silver and white authority blazed as they searched frantically for any trace of what had just been there.","\"What was that?!\" one of them demanded, her voice carrying the sharp edge of frustration. \"I felt something...a displacement, a transfer of significant power!\"","They scoured the area with increasing desperation, their combined might turning over every particle of space, examining every thread of causality that might explain what they had sensed. But there was nothing. No trace, no trail, no evidence that anything had ever been there at all.","The Great Usurper was gone, and with him, any answers they might have found!"]},{"number":3970,"title":"Chapter 3970: Chapter 3969: The Second Land Lifeform! I","paragraphs":["In the Early Veiled Shore, where golden sands stretched beneath skies of crystalline perfection, Noah raised his head with a movement so subtle it might have been missed by any observer.","His eyes, those windows to an existence that transcended normal understanding, gazed out as if they could pierce through the countless layers of space and time that separated him from where Eckert, the Great Usurper, had just been!","A light smile played across his features, carrying within it understanding and perhaps a touch of fondness.","Everyone had their own journey to walk, their own destiny to forge through choices that would echo across existence.","Eckert had chosen his path, and Noah would not begrudge him that freedom. After all, his Flow of Existence had always encompassed thr flow of all other pertinent beings as he made himself the center of attention!","His attention shifted, drawn by movement in his immediate vicinity.","Before him on the golden sands stood Moiraine, her transformed presence radiating the kind of power that made Existence itself pay attention.","Her hands were extended toward him, cradled within them a shard of white-gold light that pulsed with significance beyond measure.","This was her sacrifice...her Kleos Glyph, that ultimate expression of power that she had achieved through his gifts, now transformed into something else entirely!","|Moiraine has sacrificed the Kleos Glyph of Paradoxical Genesis to become a Shard of the Seed of a Lost Forgotten Principle: The Principle of Existential Duality.|","The prompt shimmered before his consciousness, each word carrying weight that was heavy.","Heavy!","What she offered him was a fragment of something that had been lost since the Earliest Folds, a truth that existence itself had forgotten.","|100 Shards will form the complete Seed of the Lost Forgotten Principle: The Principle of Existential Duality.|","One hundred shards to reconstruct something that should have been impossible to recover.","She had given him the first piece of a puzzle whose completion would grant understanding of forces that transcended current reality.","|The Principle of Existential Duality grants the following possible capabilities: The ability to exist simultaneously in contradictory states while maintaining singular consciousness...life and death, presence and absence. One can be both here and there, both strong and weak, choosing which state to manifest based on necessity. Applications include: surviving annihilation by existing in a state of already being destroyed, attacking from positions where one simultaneously is and is not present, and achieving nigh indestructibility by existing in states where death has both already occurred and can never occur.|","...!","Oh.","Oh!!!","The weavings were staggering, speaking to power that would make even the paradoxes that plagued existence seem simple by comparison!","Moiraine’s eyes met his as she presented the shard, and there was something in her gaze that had shifted fundamentally.","The reverence remained, yes, but it had been joined by something else...a fierce protectiveness, a determination that burned like Wheels of Existence being born.","\"I still want to call you Sir,\" she said, her voice carrying a mixture of seriousness.","The words emerged as choice, as declaration of how she chose to honor what existed between them.","The way she looked at him had transformed entirely. Gone was the careful deference of one who served because they must.","In its place stood the imperious majesty that had always been part of her nature, now directed not in spite of him but in service to their shared purpose.","\"No,\" she said firmly, her chin lifting with the kind of certainty.","\"I will keep calling you Sir. I am...Moiraine, A Golden Paradox, a Paradoxical Origin, an Arch Living Existence.\"","HUUM!","Each title fell from her lips like a battle standard being raised! \"I will be your sword to cut down those who stand against you, and I will do everything in my existence to elevate you to the revered state of an Early Creature that you are.\"","Her eyes blazed with fierce loyalty as she concluded with a single word that carried the weight of absolute commitment: \"Okay?\"","The question was not really a question...it was a statement of intent dressed in the clothing of inquiry!","She had made her choice, and that choice was him, in whatever form that dedication took.","Noah’s smile deepened with genuine warmth as he nodded. \"Okay.\"","The simple acceptance seemed to break something in her composure. Without warning, she jumped into his embrace, her arms wrapping around him with a fierceness that suggested she was holding something precious beyond measure!","The Shard of the Lost Forgotten Principle pulsed between them, its light seeping into his being as she pressed herself against him as if trying to merge their very existences.","A distance away on the golden sands, Barbatos stood with her characteristic grace, her dark hair catching the light like liquid midnight.","Her stellar obsidian dress, inscribed with skulls that seemed to dance in the shifting illumination, whispered against itself as she shook her head while sighing.","\"Here we go again,\"","She murmured, her voice carrying the fond exasperation of one who had witnessed this scene play out in variations too many times to count.","She turned to Adelaide, whose serene presence seemed to anchor the very air around them. \"How many does that make, Sis Adelaide?\"","Adelaide’s laugh came soft and warm.","\"Let him have as many as he wants,\" she said, her voice carrying the wisdom of someone who had learned to find joy in simple truths. \"In existence, it is best to enjoy the simple things, otherwise... what are we all here for?\"","...!","If not for moments like this...moments of connection, of choice, of simple human emotion despite their transcendent nature...then what was the point of all their power?","Such scenes of serenity bloomed across the Early Veiled Shore.","Here, in this space that existed beyond the reach of Living Existences, beyond the schemes of Paradoxes and Origins, peace reigned with the gentle authority of glory!","The crystalline waters lapped at the shores with Quintessence.","The ancient trees swayed in breezes that carried no news of the chaos beginning to bloom across existence!","The golden sands held their warmth like a promise that some things, at least, remained constant despite the storms that gathered beyond their borders!","And in this moment...this perfect, crystalized moment, there was only peace.","Only the simple joy of beings who had found each other across impossible odds.","The chaos would come. The storms would break. The very fabric of existence would soon tremble under the weight of choices made and unmade!","But not yet.","Not in this moment.","In this moment, there was only the Early Veiled Shore!"]},{"number":3971,"title":"Chapter 3971: Chapter 3970: The Second Land Lifeform! II","paragraphs":["In the Early Veiled Shore, Moiraine emerged from Noah’s embrace with fluid grace, her form straightening as she reclaimed the imperious majesty that had always been her birthright.","Yet something fundamental had shifted in how she carried herself...no longer the careful deference of a servant!","\"Sir,\" she said, and the word carried a fondness this time, \"I will continue forming more Kleos Glyphs of Paradoxical Genesis so you can obtain more shards of that seed. The required complexity and purity seems to be a bit more than a billion since it is a mixture of both paradox and origin...\"","The way she said ’Sir’ now...it was different!","It held warmth beneath its formality, affection wrapped in respect, as if the title had become her personal way of expressing something.","Noah’s gaze settled upon her with calm authority, his voice carrying the weight of absolute command.","\"You would essentially be sacrificing more than the power of an Honored Existence to obtain all the shards. Do not deplete all your power for it as I will replenish you with the Sacred Mead of Existence. Once you have recovered the cost of a sacrificed Glyph, only then can you proceed to make another one again.\"","His tone brooked no argument, each word delivered with the certainty.","This was a decree wrapped in care, protection disguised as command!","Moiraine’s smile bloomed with genuine warmth as she responded with a simple, \"Mmm,\" the sound carrying within it acceptance, understanding, and contentment!","Noah turned his attention to the bucket of Sacred Mead of Existence that sat upon the golden sands, its contents still substantial but depleting with each use.","They would need more, and soon, if they were to maintain their unprecedented rate of advancement!","His gaze traveled across the Early Veiled Shore to where Heidrun lounged in the distance, the arrogant goat currently snacking on Auric Vitae Grasses with the casual indulgence of royalty sampling delicacies.","The moment his attention touched upon her, her crystalline head snapped up, instantly straightening to her full, proud height.","Her entire posture screamed defensive innocence, saying...’What? I have been good and eating moderately!’...as if she could deflect his scrutiny through sheer force of imperial bearing.","Noah’s smile deepened with genuine amusement as he pointed toward the bucket of Mead.","Heidrun’s intelligent eyes followed the gesture, understanding blooming instantly in their crystalline depths. She looked down at herself as if performing some internal assessment, and a moment later, a prompt materialized before Noah’s consciousness.","|Heidrun states that she will be ready to produce more Sacred Mead of Existence in approximately 5 hours. If provided with delicacies at the level of Auric Vitae Grasses or higher, this process will accelerate significantly.|","WAA!","Noah nodded at the information, filing it away as his attention shifted to the multiple Sacred Totems that dotted his expanded domain.","Their bells hung silent, waiting, ready to ring out their call to existence itself.","\"It is time for the second Land Lifeform,\" he declared, his voice carrying across the Shore.","As the words left his lips, new prompts began cascading across his consciousness, each one marking another milestone in his impossible progression.","|159 Early Sacred Towers of Osmont have been successfully constructed at the First Stage. Nutrients from the devoured Lifeform will continue to be distributed in efforts to elevate Towers of the First Stage towards the Second Stage.|","|From the collective 159 Towers of Osmont, a total of 79,500,000 has been contributed to your current Complexity and Purity Quotients.|","|Your forming Heart of an Early Creature and Early Atlas of the Folds are consuming significant quantities of nutrients for their continued development.|","|The Early Veiled Shore is absorbing residual nutrients for environmental enrichment and potential future developments...|","Noah smiled at the flood of information, his gaze settling upon the eleven Towers of Osmont that had achieved the Second Stage...the Sacred Totems that stood ready to call forth wonders from beyond the boundaries of normal existence.","In the next moment, his body began to pulse with radiant authority.","The air around him shimmered as reality accommodated something that should have been impossible, his singular form dividing with perfect precision.","One became two, two became four, and the multiplication continued until eleven bodies stood upon the golden sands, each one unfathomably glorious in its own right!","Each body was perfect, complete, carrying within it the full weight of his accumulated power.","They moved with synchronized grace as extensions of a singular will that had simply chosen to express itself through multiple vessels.","The sight was breathtaking...eleven versions of transcendent authority, each one radiating the unmistakable presence of an Early Creature.","Without hesitation, these bodies began walking toward the Sacred Totems, their movements creating a choreography of purpose that seemed rehearsed by existence itself!","Each one approached a different tower, and as they began their ascent, the very air seemed to hold its breath in anticipation.","The staircases within the towers spiraled upward with architectural beauty, each step carrying its own weight of significance.","As Noah’s bodies climbed, their footfalls created a rhythm that resonated through the Early Veiled Shore, a drumbeat of approaching wonder.","|The Weavings of the Protagonist observe with mounting excitement!|","From nowhere and everywhere, a symphony began to bloom.","Trumpets of pure sound erupted in fanfare, their notes carrying celebration that transcended any music. This was Existence itself acknowledging what was about to occur, reality composing a soundtrack for a moment of fundamental significance!","And it wss glorious!","WU! WU! WUU!","The symphony swelled as all eleven bodies reached the peaks of their respective towers simultaneously. The bells awaited them...each one unique yet harmonious, ready to add their voices to a call that would echo across dimensions.","As one, eleven hands grasped eleven ropes. As one, they pulled.","DING! DONG! DING! DONG!","Bells rang!","Each bell rang with its own unique tone, yet together they created a harmony that made reality weep with its beauty!","The sound waves were visible as ripples of gold and silver and colors that had no names, spreading outward from each tower in expanding circles that merged and multiplied.","|The Sacred Bells of multiple Sacred Totems have been rung simultaneously for the first time. This unprecedented achievement has created a resonance that transcends normal parameters.|","...!"]},{"number":3972,"title":"Chapter 3972: Chapter 3971: The Second Land Lifeform! III","paragraphs":["The ringing of the bell was heavy, and the results were pronounced!","|All beings who hear the unified tolling, regardless of their power or complexity, will enter a profound state of epiphany. During this state, they may form Eminent Early Living Existential Glyphs or lesser glyphs with only 75% of the required cost.|","Moiraine’s eyes fluttered closed as the sound washed over her, her entire being resonating!","Around her, every conscious entity on the Shore...from the transformed members of Noah’s family to the magnificent Heidrun...felt their consciousness expand as understanding bloomed within them.","|The tolling of the bells has been deemed... Unfathomably Quintessential!|","The very Shore itself seemed to pulse with approval, the golden sands humming with glory that would continue to echo for hours to come!","And then...","BOOM!","The gray clouds at the periphery of the Early Veiled Shore began to churn with violence that spoke to something vast approaching.","The mists split apart with the sound of reality tearing, creating a gap ten times larger than when Heidrun had made her grand entrance!","Many were jolted from their meditative stupor by a sense of dread that crept across the Shore like frost over glass.","Even Noah’s expression grew stern, his eleven bodies turning in unison toward the massive tear in their sanctuary’s boundary.","From that impossible gap emerged something that made reality itself recoil.","An obsidian spider of impossible proportions pushed through the opening, her body gleaming with darkness so pure it seemed to absorb light rather than reflect it!","Eight legs, each one the size of an ancient tree, moved with terrifying grace as she entered the Early Veiled Shore.","Grace. Unbound grace!","Her magnificent form was both beautiful and horrifying...a perfect predator scaled to mythical proportions.","Eight eyes arranged across her head burned with gorgeous pupils that held depths of ancient knowledge and hunger.","Each eye was a different shade of crimson, from the deep red of spilled blood to the bright scarlet of fresh wounds, all of them focusing with terrible intelligence on the beings before her!","Her body was segmented with natural armor that looked like obsidian plates fused with organic mesh, while patterns of deep purple and gold traced all over her form.","|The calls of multiple Sacred Totems have been answered by Jorogumo, A Quasi-Kleos Early Living Land Lifeform.|","HUUM!","The prompt blazed across Noah’s consciousness as the massive spider regarded them all with those eight terrible eyes!","Then, with a fluidity that defied her enormous size, her form began to shift.","The transformation was mesmerizing and disturbing all at once. Her eight legs folded and merged, her massive body compressing and reshaping, until where a mythical spider had stood, there was now a young woman of devastating beauty.","She was tall and slender and curveceous all at once, with dark hair that fell like liquid midnight to her waist!","Her skin was pale as moonlight, creating a striking contrast with her crimson eyes...eyes that had retained their terrible depth despite the change in form.","She wore robes of black silk that seemed to move of their own accord, occasionally revealing patterns that suggested her true nature.","Her name...oh, her name!","Her name whispered across the Shore as if existence itself was announcing her!","Yoshinami!","Yoshinami!!!","She surveyed those present with cold, majestic emotion, her gaze carrying the weight of eons spent in patient waiting.","When that gaze fell upon Moiraine, the Arch Living Existence felt her very existence pulse with shock and a sudden, sharp awareness of her own mortality.","When Yoshinami’s attention found Heidrun, surprise flickered across her perfect features, followed by a smile that carried genuine amusement.","The goat, for her part, raised her head with characteristic arrogance, though anyone watching closely could see her legs trembling slightly.","Even in the face of fear, Heidrun would not abandon her imperial bearing!","Yoshinami’s smile deepened at this display of stubborn pride, a sound like silk over steel escaping her lips...not quite laughter, but acknowledgment of an existence of arrogance.","Finally, her gaze found Noah.","She looked at each of his eleven bodies with methodical precision before correctly identifying his primary form.","Her approach was deliberate, each step creating tiny fractures in the golden sand that sealed themselves moments after she passed.","When she stood before him, her smile transformed into something cold....one carrying the promise of power and brutality that transcended normal violence!","She nodded lightly, a gesture that somehow managed to convey both acknowledgment and warning.","Noah met her gaze without flinching, and as he did, her full details materialized before his consciousness.","|Name: Yoshinami","Designation: Quasi-Kleos Early Living Land Lifeform","Rarity: Quasi-Kleos","Lineage: The Cursed Weaver of Forgotten Threads, Jorogumo","Lore: In the darkest epochs of the Earliest Folds, when Early Creatures hunted for sport, Yoshinami and her kind were revered as the ultimate guardians that could protect against Early Creatures. Born from the nightmares of existence itself, she carries within her form the accumulated curses of a thousand fallen Races prevalent in those times. Her silk, spun from the essence of causality itself, can bind Existence as easily as flesh. The most terrifying aspect of her nature is her ability to become a living crown...wrapping around her Master’s head as a circlet of protection that makes collapse impossible.","Primary Boon - Crown of Inevitable Retribution: Once bonded, Yoshinami can transform into a cursed crown worn by her Master. Once per day, any being who attacks her Master will be struck by an Early Curse of Inevitability that brings True Death, completely annihilating their existence across all dimensions and possibilities. This curse cannot be resisted or avoided by any being who has not grasped the power of an Early Creature or mastered a Lost Forgotten Principle.","Secondary Boon - Threads of Twisted Existence: Can weave temporary alterations to causality within the Early Veiled Shore, creating zones where cause and effect operate according to her Master’s desires.","Passive Boon - Ancient Spider’s Wisdom: Provides her Master with instinctive knowledge of all poisons, venoms, races, herbs, and curses that exist since thr Earliest Folds the moment they are observed.","Disposition: Cold, calculating, and utterly brutal to enemies. Shows respect only to those who have earned it through power or cunning. Absolutely loyal once bonded, with loyalty expressed through merciless protection rather than affection.|","Noah’s eyes widened with genuine astonishment as he absorbed the implications of what had answered his call!","A Quasi-Kleos entity...something that stood just below the absolute pinnacle of what Land Lifeforms could achieve. And her primary ability...","True Death delivered to any who dared strike at him with lethal intent.","Not mere death, but the complete erasure of existence itself, something that even Living Existences feared above all else!","He had called for a second Land Lifeform.","The Shore had delivered him a living weapon of absolute protection, wrapped in the form of an ancient terror that wore beauty like a mask.","The symphony that had accompanied the bells’ tolling shifted to something darker, more complex, as if acknowledging that the Early Veiled Shore had just become infinitely more dangerous to any who might threaten its master!","Oh!"]},{"number":3973,"title":"Chapter 3973: Chapter 3972: The Second Land Lifeform! IV","paragraphs":["The symphony of bells began to fade into whispered echoes, but the weight of what had transpired continued to press against reality itself.","Noah’s eleven bodies stood motionless for a heartbeat, each one a perfect mirror of transcendent authority, before they began to move with synchronized precision and began coming together.","The convergence was both beautiful and terrifying to witness. Bodies of crystalline perfection flowed toward each other like streams of liquid starlight, merging with seamless grace until only one remained!","Noah’s singular form pulsed with accumulated power. The golden sands beneath his feet responded to his presence, glowing with deeper intensity as if recognizing the return of their master’s complete attention.","Without hesitation, he stepped to the edge of the Sacred Totem’s peak and leaped.","Noah descended like a force of nature given form, his body cutting through space with the precision of inevitability itself. He landed before Yoshinami with fluid grace, the impact creating ripples of authority that spread outward in perfect circles, each one carrying the weight of an Early Creature’s presence!","HUUM!","The proximity between them crackled with unspoken tension.","Yoshinami’s crimson eyes traveled over him with methodical precision, taking in every detail of his form with the calculating gaze of a predator evaluating potential prey...or perhaps recognizing a worthy master.","Her assessment was thorough, unhurried, as if she possessed all the time in existence to make her judgment.","Her pale features remained impassive throughout the examination, betraying nothing of her thoughts!","Then, with movements that carried the weight of ancient ritual, she began to bow.","But this was no simple gesture of respect!","Her body folded with ceremonial precision, arms crossing over her chest in patterns that spoke to traditions older than recorded history.","Her head lowered until her dark hair cascaded like a waterfall of midnight, and her voice whispered words in a language that predated the formation of the Folds themselves.","The bow was tribal, primal, carrying within it the accumulated reverence of eons spent!","|Yoshinami has acknowledged you as her Master through the Ritual of Inevitable Binding. Her loyalty is now absolute, expressed through protection that transcends death itself!|","Noah nodded at the acknowledgment with shining eyes!","When Yoshinami straightened, her smile held new musings...still cold, still calculating, but touched now with something that might have been satisfaction.","\"Where,\" Noah asked, his voice carrying the authority that came naturally to one who commanded reality itself, \"were you and others like you before you arrived in my Early Veiled Shore?\"","...!","He had so many questions. He wanted to see if he could have any answered by this being that was even rarer than Heidrun!","Yoshinami’s smile deepened.","Her crimson eyes glittered with amusement as she replied.","\"I am bound to not say much, Master,\" she replied, \"But we....Land Lifeforms such as myself, dwell in places similar to but lesser than your Veiled Shore. Lands that exist in the spaces between spaces, where reality grows thin and possibility bleeds through the cracks of what should be impossible.\"","She paused, her gaze drifting across the golden expanse of the Early Veiled Shore as if comparing it to memories.","\"We rove through those territories, hunting, waiting, existing in states of perpetual readiness. Some of us search for sustenance, others for purpose, all of us hoping to be among the fortunate few who receive a call from one worthy of our service.\"","Her attention shifted briefly to Heidrun, who had been listening with the carefully controlled posture of one trying to appear disinterested while hanging on every word.","\"Even the little goat there,\" Yoshinami continued with gentle mockery, \"wandered those same territories, searching endlessly for grasses that could satisfy her refined palate.\"","Heidrun’s crystalline eyes flashed with indignation, but she maintained her imperial bearing even as her legs trembled slightly under the weight of Yoshinami’s casual attention.","Noah’s curiosity burned brighter as he absorbed this information. \"Tell me more about these lands. Where are they? How do they connect to the Folds we know?\"","Yoshinami’s expression grew thoughtful, her crimson eyes taking on depths that seemed to contain entire Wheels of knowledge.","\"I do not know their precise location, Master, for such places exist outside the normal geography of existence. They are the Wandering Territories...Domains that drift through the spaces between Folds like islands of possibility in oceans of void. They are places where the earliest experiments of existence took root and grew wild, unbound by the laws that govern more stable realities.\"","She began to pace, her movements carrying predatory grace as she spoke.","\"These territories shift and flow according to principles that predate the current structure of the Folds. Time moves differently there...sometimes faster, sometimes slower, occasionally in directions that have no names. The land itself is alive, hungry, constantly reshaping itself according to the needs and desires of those who dwell upon it.\"","Her voice took on a quality that suggested she was sharing secrets that few had ever heard.","\"It is a place where Early Living Existential Land Lifeforms can exist in something approaching their true nature, free from the constraints that normal reality would impose upon us. We form hierarchies there, territories marked by power and cunning, alliances forged through necessity and broken through ambition.\"","The picture she painted was both magnificent and terrifying...a place where beings of impossible power existed in states of constant potential, waiting for calls that might never come!","\"And what,\" Noah pressed, his eyes bright with the hunger for knowledge that had always driven him, \"do you know about Early Creatures?\"","The change in Yoshinami’s expression was immediate and profound!","Her exotic smile transformed into brutality like a weapon, her crimson eyes blazing with memories that burned with the intensity of dying Folds.","\"Mmm,\" she breathed, the sound carrying violence barely held in check. \"Early Creatures. The hunters who made sport of existence itself, who treated Existence as their personal playground and all who dwelt within it as toys for their amusement.\"","She moved closer to Noah, her presence radiating the cold satisfaction of a predator!","\"In my prime, Master, when my power was magisterially bright, I stood against them. Early Creatures who descended upon the Wandering Territories like storms of destruction, seeking entertainment in the suffering of those they deemed lesser.\"","Her smile grew sharp enough to cut through dimensions.","\"I...killed one.\"","...!"]},{"number":3974,"title":"Chapter 3974: Chapter 3973: The Second Land Lifeform! V","paragraphs":["The words dropped into the space between them like stones into still water, creating ripples of shock that spread outward through every consciousness present!","Even Moiraine, who had been listening with the careful attention of one trying to absorb knowledge far beyond her usual scope, felt her existence pulse with disbelief.","Noah’s eyes widened with genuine astonishment. \"You killed an Early Creature?\"","\"Indeed,\" Yoshinami confirmed, her voice carrying the cold satisfaction of absolute certainty. \"It was a being who called itself the Harvester of Delights, one who took pleasure in collecting the screams of the dying. It had come to the Wandering Territories seeking new forms of entertainment, and it chose poorly when it decided to make sport of those under my protection.\"","She paused, her expression growing distant as she accessed memories carved in blood and shadow.","\"The battle lasted for what you might consider years, though time itself became meaningless within the scope of our conflict. Reality warped and twisted around us as we fought, entire regions of the Wandering Territories reshaped.\"","Noah found himself leaning forward, drawn by the magnitude of what she was describing.","\"In the end,\" Yoshinami continued, \"I bound it in threads spun from its own hubris, weaving its destruction from the very arrogance that had brought it to my domain. Its death scream echoed across Folds, warning others of its kind that the Wandering Territories were not undefended playgrounds...for there were many like me, and some even more radiant than me.\"","HUUM!","The silence that followed her words was heavy with the weight of impossible achievement.","To kill an Early Creature...was something that should have been beyond possibility!","\"What happened to your power from then?\" Noah asked, his voice carrying gentle curiosity.","Yoshinami’s smile took on a different quality, touched now with something that might have been regret.","\"This, Master, I cannot say. Not because I choose to withhold the information, but because it was carved from my memory by forces I no longer recall. I know that I was once far more than I am now, but the details of my diminishment have been sealed away by methods that transcend my understanding.\"","...!","She touched her temple with one pale finger, her expression growing contemplative.","\"There are gaps in my consciousness, spaces where knowledge and power once resided. I suspect that my reduction from true Kleos status to Quasi-Kleos was the price paid for survival, though I cannot recall the circumstances that necessitated such sacrifice.\"","...!","Noah nodded, understanding the frustration that such enforced ignorance must bring to a being of her intelligence and power.","\"Not all Early Creatures are the same,\" Yoshinami continued, \"The Harvester of Delights was a creature of pure malice, but there was another...\"","Her expression softened almost imperceptibly, coldness giving way to something that might have been fondness, though it remained wrapped in layers of protective ice.","\"She called herself the Architect of Sanctuaries, and she was everything the Harvester was not. Where he brought destruction, she offered protection. Where he sought to dominate, she chose to nurture.\"","Yoshinami’s crimson eyes grew distant as she accessed memories that clearly held deep significance.","\"When the Harvester’s death brought retribution from others of his kind, when Early Creatures descended upon the Wandering Territories seeking vengeance for their fallen peer, she intervened. The Architect appeared, placing herself between us and destruction.\"","Her voice carried reverence at this moment!","\"She was injured saving us...grievously wounded by forces that should have been beyond resistance. Yet even diminished, even bleeding essence that could have reformed entire Folds, she opened her Early Veiled Shore to us. Land Lifeforms, Living Existences, refugees from across the Folds and Wandering Territories...all of us found sanctuary within her domain. And her Shore...was gloriously vast!\"","HUUM!","The picture she painted was one of impossible nobility, an Early Creature who had chosen protection over power.","\"For years that felt like eons, we dwelt within her Shore while others of her kind pressed against its boundaries like storms seeking entry. They could not breach her defenses, but they could make the attempts costly. Each attack weakened her further, each defense drained reserves that could never be fully replenished.\"","Yoshinami’s expression grew solemn.","\"In the end, she made a choice that I still do not fully understand. She sent us away. She returned us to the Wandering Territories with blessings that protected us from immediate retribution, and then... she was gone. Just...gone.\"","The silence that followed was heavy.","Unbearably so!","Noah absorbed this information with the careful attention.","The idea of an Early Creature who chose sacrifice over dominance, protection over power, challenged many of the assumptions he had formed about beings of such magnitude.","\"Why,\" he asked, his curiosity driving him to seek understanding of every detail, \"is your distinction Quasi-Kleos rather than true Kleos?\"","Yoshinami’s smile returned, though it carried rueful acknowledgment.","\"Kleos designation requires not just power, Master, but completeness. My forced memory loss, the gaps in my consciousness...these diminishments prevent me from achieving the perfect unity that true Kleos status demands. I am powerful, yes, but I am also incomplete.\"","She gestured to herself with elegant precision.","\"Think of it as a masterwork sculpture with crucial pieces missing. The overall form remains beautiful and functional, but the perfection that would elevate it to true artistry has been compromised by forces beyond the artist’s control.\"","Noah found the words both illuminating and tragic as he nodded and moved on to something else.","\"What do you know about Lost Forgotten Principles?\" he pressed, his hunger for knowledge driving him to explore every avenue of understanding.","Yoshinami’s expression grew sharp with interest","\"Ahhn...\" she said, her voice carrying dangerous excitement. \"Lost Forgotten Principles were the ultimate tools that Early Creatures cultivated within their Shores...seeds of impossibility that they nurtured until they bloomed into forces capable of cutting down any enemy. My Power...may potentially stem from such a Principle. \"","...!","She began to pace again, her movements carrying the rhythm of someone lost in memories of incredible significance.","\"These Principles were not mere powers or authorities, Master. They were fundamental alterations to the very structure of Existence itself. Each one represented a pathway to victory that transcended normal conflict...ways of ensuring that battles were won before they were even fought.\"","\"Early Creatures would plant these seeds within the soil of their domains, nurturing them with the essence of conquered enemies, the blood of fallen Creatures, Inevitabilitie, Living Existences, the crystallized screams of dying Folds. They required patience measured in eons and resources that could erase entire Folds, but the results... the results were weapons that could unmake the very concept of defeat.\""]},{"number":3975,"title":"Chapter 3975: Chapter 3974: The Second Land Lifeform! VI","paragraphs":["She stopped pacing, turning to face Noah with an intensity that made the air between them crackle.","\"A Lost Forgotten Principle might allow its wielder to attack their enemy’s past, unmaking their victories before they occurred. Another might grant the power to steal defeat itself, transforming any loss into triumph through methods that defied comprehension. Still others could reach across dimensions to strike at the very idea of their target’s existence.\"","\"Why are they called ’Lost Forgotten’?\" Noah asked, his mind racing.","Yoshinami’s smile grew cold with bitter amusement.","\"Because, Master, the Early Creatures who created them are gone. The knowledge of their cultivation has been scattered across existence like seeds on barren ground. The Principles themselves persist in some form, but the understanding of how to awaken them, how to nurture them, how to wield them safely...all of that has been lost to time and catastrophe.\"","She paused, her expression growing thoughtful.","\"Some say that fragments of this knowledge still exist, hidden within the deepest archives of the most ancient Folds, occasionally mutating Land Lifeforms or Living Existences to give them glimpses of power. Others believe that the Principles themselves sometimes choose new wielders, appearing in moments of desperate need to those who possess the courage to grasp impossibility.\"","The conversation had revealed layers of wonder and glory!","Yet even as he absorbed this information, even as Moiraine and the others listened with the careful attention of those trying to understand forces far beyond their usual scope, Noah felt that they were only scratching the surface of truths!","\"Where,\" he asked, \"are the Early Creatures now?\"","Yoshinami’s expression grew distant, her crimson eyes reflecting something that might have been uncertainty.","\"This, Master, I do not know. Some whisper that all are dead. Others believe they have retreated into hiding, waiting for conditions that will allow them to emerge once more.\"","She shook her head, dark hair flowing like liquid shadow.","\"There is...you, Master. Would you not be able to tell me where you were before this?\"","She said such words dangerously!","...!","And Noah...had no answer to give.","The weight of mystery settled over them like a shroud.","Noah was silent for a moment before he sighed tyrannicaly and voiced out.","\"Come to me,\" he commanded, his voice carrying the absolute authority of an Early Creature addressing one who had already acknowledged his mastery.","Yoshinami’s smile grew cold with satisfaction, her crimson eyes blazing with approval at his direct approach.","\"As you will it, Master,\" she replied.","Her transformation began with a smile that held promises of protection and violence. Her human form began to dissolve with the fluid grace of water finding its natural level.","Stellar obsidian light erupted from her dissolving body, streams of darkness so pure they seemed to absorb the very concept of illumination.","The light moved with purpose, flowing toward Noah like liquid shadow given direction and intent.","The streams of obsidian radiance wrapped around his head with ceremonial precision, weaving themselves into patterns.","The light solidified as it settled, transforming into a crown of such magnificent arrogance that reality itself seemed to approve of its existence.","The crown hung sideways on Noah’s head, its positioning suggesting casual dominance rather than formal ceremony.","Its obsidian surface held depths that seemed to contain entire Folds of darkness, while patterns of deep purple and gold traced across its surface.","|The Crown of Inevitable Retribution has been successfully bonded. You are now protected against any single attack from anything lesser than an Early Creature or a force wielding a Lost Forgotten Principle once in the next 24 hours. Any being lesser than an Early Creature or a force of a Lost Forgotten Principle who attacks you with lethal intent will face True Death...complete annihilation across all dimensions and possibilities.|","Noah examined the prompt with the careful attention of someone who understood that he had just acquired protection beyond the reach of most forces in existence.","True Death was not merely the end of life, but the complete erasure of everything a being had ever been or could ever become.","\"How,\" he asked, his voice carrying curiosity about the practical applications of such power, \"can the number of times you can act each day be raised?\"","Yoshinami’s voice rang out from the crown itself, carrying the same cold precision it had held when spoken from human lips.","\"There are always methods, Master, but they require resources that most would consider... excessive. I need materials that can restore what is expended in delivering True Death to those foolish enough to challenge you.\"","Her tone grew contemplative.","\"Early Sacred Herbs would suffice, their essence refined enough to replenish what is lost in each application of my power. Corpses of Inevitabilities would be even more effective, their concentrated authority providing nourishment.\"","The coldness in her voice deepened as she continued.","\"Living Existences, still warm with the breath of life, could provide enough essence. And corpses of Early Creatures... ah, Master, such materials would allow me to act without restriction, to deliver True Death as casually as breathing.\"","HUUM!","The casual brutality of her words created ripples of shock that spread outward through every consciousness present!","Yet as the implications settled in Noah’s mind, as he considered the practical applications of such power, his thoughts turned inevitably toward solutions.","Corpses of Inevitabilities...he may have more soon.","Corpses of Early Creatures...well, there was one, but not currently in his grasp!","When it came to obtaining Early Sacred Herbs in quantities sufficient to enhance Yoshinami’s capabilities, to plant multiple plots throughout the Early Veiled Shore that could support the advancement of all his followers...","There was indeed a place that held such treasures in abundance.","Aeternitas Concordia.","Past the The Living Coalition Gateway that awaited him in thr Transcendent Origin Battlefront Folds, where powers gathered that could provide everything he needed to transform his domain into something that approached the magnificent gardens in the territories of true Early Creatures.","His eyes blazed with the fire of possibility as plans began to form in the depths of his consciousness, strategies that would see his Early Veiled Shore transformed into something that could rival the greatest achievements of Early Creatures!","The Crown of Inevitable Retribution pulsed with approval, its obsidian surface reflecting the ambition that burned within its master’s Existence!"]},{"number":3976,"title":"Chapter 3976: Chapter 3975: I Am A Humble Merchant! I","paragraphs":["There existed, in the grand weaving of existence, a fundamental truth that transcended all boundaries of power, wisdom, and cosmic understanding...one being’s shit could very well be another’s most coveted treasure.","Consider, if you will, the profound absurdity of this principle when applied to Early Creatures themselves.","What an Early Creature might casually discard as worthless detritus(shit), perhaps the crystallized remnants of a sneeze, or the shed scales from an idle scratch, would become objects of worship for Living Existences across entire Folds.","Wars would be fought over such \"shit.\"","Entire civilizations would dedicate themselves to the pursuit of what amounted to existential garbage, simply because it had once been touched by power beyond their comprehension!","The excrement of an Early Creature? Folds would crumble beneath the weight of the bidding wars that would ensue.","Living Existences would sacrifice their accumulated power of eons for a single grain of such material, believing...correctly, that even the waste products of such beings contained more concentrated authority than they could generate in millennia of cultivation!","Yet to the Early Creature who produced it? Nothing more than an inconvenience to be disposed of with the same casual indifference one might show toward discarding a used napkin.","Such was the laughable weavings of existence...value determined not by inherent worth, but by the vast chasms of power that separated one tier of being from another!","---","In the resplendent magnificence of Aeternitas Concordia, where golden towers stretched toward infinity and the very air shimmered with crystallized authority, four figures moved through corridors that hummed with the accumulated power of ages.","Alexander Asmodeus walked with the measured pace of one who was filled with confidence!","Beside him, Seraphina Valorheart moved with graceful precision, and Kaedric Voss maintained his position with the silent vigilance of a guardian.","But it was the fourth member of their group who commanded the most attention, even when she was trying to appear casual.","Royal Living Law Tristesse moved with the kind of barely contained energy that made reality itself nervous.","Her dark hair caught the ambient light of Concordia’s towers, while her pristine white robes seemed to drink in the authority that saturated the air around them!","Her aura was reigned in to the point where it appeared almost mundane, yet anyone with sufficient sensitivity could feel the vast forces held in check beneath her brilliant smile.","\"Did you think,\" she said, her voice carrying the kind of musical quality that made even casual conversation sound like a performance, \"that I would let you take my dear niece away all alone?\"","The question was delivered with such radiant warmth that it took several moments for the underlying menace to register.","Tristesse’s smile never wavered, never lost its brilliant intensity, even as her words carried implications that could have frozen the blood of lesser beings.","\"I will personally guide you all through the Living Doorways of the Loom,\" she continued, her tone maintaining that same dangerous sweetness. \"Because nowadays... well, too many crazy accidents are happening, don’t you think?\"","She paused in her walking, turning to face Alexander with that radiant, terrifying smile still lighting up her features.","\"It seems like every day, you hear about Honored and Royal Living Existences dying in the most unfortunate circumstances. You have to ask yourself... just who could be killing them, hmm?\"","The way she posed the question made it sound like idle curiosity, the kind of wondering one might express about the weather.","Yet the undertones carried weight that suggested she knew far more about these \"accidents\" than her casual demeanor suggested.","Alexander listened to her with calm composure.","When he replied, his words carried a confidence so absolute that it seemed to bend reality around its certainty.","\"I have already looked into my future,\" he said, his voice steady as the foundations of existence itself. \"Death is not in the cards for me.\"","HUUM!","The statement hung in the air between them like a challenge issued to existence itself.","It was the simple declaration of someone who possessed knowledge that transcended normal understanding of possibility and consequence!","Tristesse’s smile grew even more dangerous at his words.","Yet even as her smile blazed with terrifying approval, she noticed something that caused its intensity to flicker.","Her niece, Seraphina Valorheart, was looking at Alexander with eyes that held far too much warmth, far too much interest, far too much of the kind of smitten devotion that made older relatives want to lock young people in towers until they developed better sense.","’How absolutely idiotic the young ones are nowadays...’ Tristesse grumbled internally, her thoughts carrying the exasperation of someone who had watched countless generations make the same mistakes!","Yet even her internal frustrations were interrupted as their progress through Concordia’s magnificent pathways was suddenly disrupted by a growing commotion ahead.","Voices began to rise from the crowds that moved along the golden roadways, carrying astonishment that cut through the usual ambient noise of commerce.","\"He’s back!\"","\"He’s alone!\"","\"Which Royal Living Existence sponsored him?\"","\"How did he return so quickly?!\"","The voices belonged to Fold Dwellers and Living Existences alike, their tones carrying a sense of shock!","Alexander and his companions turned their attention toward the source of the disturbance, their gazes following the pointing fingers and astonished stares that had begun to converge on a single location.","Before them stretched the heart of Aeternitas Concordia in all its impossible glory. Large golden crystalline towers stretched toward the skies on all sides, their surfaces reflecting and amplifying the ambient authority until the very air seemed to shimmer with liquid Living Existential Authority.","Through the center of this magnificent chaos ran a single golden pathway that led upward toward the ascending heights of Concordia...the Aureum Ascendant!","The road itself seemed alive, pulsing with the accumulated footsteps of countless beings who had walked its length in pursuit of advancement and glory.","Along the sides of this golden road, peak Originus Venerant Fold Dwellers had their stalls beneath massive banners.","If one ascended the golden road with sufficient attention, the transition became clear....the stalls of Fold Dwellers gradually gave way to the towers of Living Existences.","It was at this junction, at the precise point where Fold Dweller ambition met Living Existence authority, that Alexander and those around him found themselves staring in astonishment at a figure that should not have existed in this place.","Noah Osmont walked here in magnificent repose, adorned in a golden robe that seemed to drink in the ambient light of Concordia itself. The fabric was inscribed with infinity symbols that moved and shifted when observed directly!","Yet it was not the robe that captured attention, impressive though it was.","Upon his head sat a crown that defied every convention of royal regalia. The stellar obsidian circlet hung at an arrogant angle, its positioning suggesting casual dominance rather than formal ceremony!","The crown’s surface held depths that seemed to contain entire Folds of darkness.","Seraphina’s voice cut through the stunned silence, her words carrying shock that bordered on disbelief.","\"Isn’t that your friend who was escorted away by an Honored Living Existence?\"","...!"]},{"number":3977,"title":"Chapter 3977: Chapter 3976: I Am A Humble Merchant! II","paragraphs":["Alexander’s face remained calm as he looked ahead, his expression betraying nothing of whatever thoughts might be churning beneath his composed exterior.","Yet before he could respond, Tristesse’s voice cut through the moment with dangerous precision.","\"What?\" she said, her tone still maintaining that brilliant, terrifying sweetness. \"His friend? Someone from the same Nullvein Gravewake Folds as him?\"","Her smile grew sharper, taking on edges that could have cut through dimensions.","\"Because nobody can get in or out of those Folds...we have locked them down and we’ve been searching through them and finding nothing. So who exactly... could this possibly be?\"","...!","They observed in growing amazement as Noah, seemingly oblivious to the attention he was drawing, calmly and regally waved his hand.","Reality responded to his gesture with eager compliance, causing a tyrannical purple throne to materialize from crystallized authority and ambient power.","The throne was a masterwork of arrogant design, its form suggesting comfort and dominance!","Noah settled onto it with the grace of one who had never doubted his right to command the very fabric of existence.","Yet even this display paled beside what followed!","Noah waved his hands again, and reality bent to accommodate his will once more. Radiant glass woks materialized in the air before him, floating with the casual defiance of gravity.","The woks were filled with cuts of meat that blazed with their own internal radiance, each piece seemingly carved from creatures that had transcended the normal boundaries of existence!","The moment they appeared, an aroma began to spread through the air...a scent so intoxicating, so fundamentally appealing to every level of existence, that it bypassed rational thought entirely.","The effect was immediate and absolute. Every entity present felt their very Existences begin to throb with desperate need, as if the deepest parts of their beings had suddenly awakened to the realization that they would never be complete without whatever treasures rested within those floating vessels!","Fold Dwellers found themselves taking involuntary steps forward.","Living Existences who had transcended normal appetites felt ancient hungers stirring to life within them!","Royal Law Tristesse’s eyes became sharp.","\"A Fold Dweller from Nullvein Gravewake Folds?\" she said, her voice carrying the kind of skepticism that could have withered flowers. \"My ass he’s a Fold Dweller.\"","She turned her attention to Alexander with predatory intensity, her smile never wavering even as her words carried the weight of authority.","\"Little Asmodeus... Little Alexander, why don’t you tell me about this friend of yours? Apart from you, he seems to be another anomaly from those supposedly empty Folds.\"","The request was delivered with such sweet reasonableness that it took several moments for the underlying command to register.","This was Royal Living Law Tristesse demanding information with the kind of gentle insistence!","Alexander, however, simply shook his head, his expression remaining calm even in the face of such focused attention.","His refusal to answer was delivered without explanation, without justification, with the simple certainty of someone who understood that some secrets should not be mentioned!","Tristesse’s smile grew even more brilliant at his refusal!","\"Alright,\" she said, her voice carrying musical notes that spoke to darker harmonies. \"We’ll do it the hard way then. Let’s see what your friend is selling, hmm?\"","---","At the junction of the golden road running across Concordia, precisely at the boundary between the domain of Fold Dwellers and the territory of Living Existences, Noah sat upon his purple throne magisterially!","The three radiant woks floated before him like offerings presented to a emperor, their contents continuing to emit that intoxicating aroma that had begun to draw crowds from across the entire district.","Multiple golden bowls appeared in neat stacks beside his throne.","The arrangement had the appearance of someone preparing to feed the poor, yet the quality of what was being offered spoke to resources that could have purchased entire Folds!","Noah sensed the many auras surging in his direction, each one carrying its own mixture of desperation, curiosity, and barely contained greed.","He had already gone through all the unique herbs mentioned in the trade screen that Thal’dorven the Primordial Fisher had shared with him, cross-referencing their properties against his own needs and the requirements of his expanding domain.","He knew exactly what he was looking for.","Like a mere merchant or peddler setting up shop in the greatest marketplace of Existential commerce, he voiced out his offer with the kind of laid-back confidence that suggested he was utterly unconcerned by the magnitude of attention he was drawing!","\"Selling bowls of Quintessential Soup for Herbs and other Treasures found in the Doorways of the Loom!\"","HUUM!","His voice carried across the gathered crowd with effortless projection, reaching every ear present regardless of their position or the ambient noise that filled Concordia’s pathways.","\"Acceptable Herbs include...\" he continued, his tone maintaining that same casual authority as he began listing names that caused visible reactions among his audience.","\"Transcendent Veilmoss, harvested only from the deepest chambers of Doorways where Existence grows thin. Chronos Petrichor, found where time itself has crystallized into physical form in Doorways. Infinity’s Breath Orchids, which bloom only in the presence of dead Inevitabilities. Paradox Root, grown in space watered by contradictions of Inevitabilities that have achieved physical manifestation...\"","Each name he spoke caused ripples of power!","These were not common treasures...they were materials that existed only within the Doorways of the Loom, herbs that required expeditions into places where the very concept of survival became negotiable!","One would not even know what they were called or named, nor from which doorway they would be found in.","So how the fuck did a Fold Dweller speak about them as if they were grass everyone knew about!?","\"Void-Heart Chrysanthemums, cultivated in Doorways where existence meets Collapse. Echo Sage, which grows only where the screams of dying Temporal Inevitabilities have taken root. And for those seeking truly exceptional exchanges...\" his voice took on notes of particular interest, \"...Primordial Memory Moss, which contains within its fibers the compressed experiences of Inevitabilities that witnessed the birth of Early Folds. Other Treasures found in the Doorways of the Loom are also accepted...\"","...!","Multiple presences began moving toward him. Yet what astonished them more than his casual authority or the exotic nature of his requests was the undeniable evidence of what filled those floating woks.","The pieces of Early Living Marine Lifeforms were wanted by all present.","Such types materials were supposed to be beyond the reach of anyone below Royal status, yet here sat this mysterious figure offering them like common street food in exchange for herbs and treasures of the Doorways of the Loom!","And he did so fearlessly...as if he had nothing to worry about!"]},{"number":3978,"title":"Chapter 3978: Chapter 3977: I Am A Humble Merchant! III","paragraphs":["The atmosphere had grown thick with anticipation and barely restrained greed after Noah finished listing his requirements!","More and more beings gathered around his impromptu marketplace, drawn by the astonishing scent of the Early Living Marine Lifeforms that filled his radiant woks.","Fold Dwellers who had achieved the pinnacle of their limitations found themselves pressed forward by desires they couldn’t name. Living Existences who had transcended hungers felt ancient appetites stirring within them!","Noah surveyed the growing crowd with the calm assessment of a master strategist.","Each face that turned toward him carried its own mixture of desperation, calculation, and poorly concealed avarice. He could read their intentions like open books, their desires painted across their expressions!","As the murmurs of the crowd began to crescendo into something approaching chaos, Noah raised his voice once again, his words cutting through the ambient noise with effortless authority.","\"Oh, and a little about myself,\" he began. \"I am but a humble merchant known as... the Weaver of Existence!\"","HUUM!","Noah’s smile deepened as he continued, his words delivered with the laid-back demeanor of an Emperor!","\"Just to make sure that there aren’t any delays and possible accidents and misunderstandings, I will say right now that yes, I have some mysterious backing. And no, I do not care whether you are a Fold Dweller, a Prime Living Existence, an Honored Living Existence, or even a Royal Living Existence.\"","The casual way he dismissed hierarchies sent ripples of shock through the assembled crowd!","\"Nobody here needs to come and begin flaring their power and authority, however important they think they are, to begin causing any unneeded conflicts. We are here on business. So let’s simply do business and go on our way, okay?\"","...!","Oh!","The warning was delivered with such nonchalant confidence that it took several moments for its full implications to register!","\"Now,\" he concluded, his eyes scanning the crowd with predatory interest, \"do we have someone that has any of the herbs or treasures that I mentioned among those here?\"","His laid-back demeanor, his unfathomably calm words, and the sheer audacity of his entire presentation made those watching and listening feel as though they were witnessing something that should not have been possible!","At that moment, a voice cut through the many powerful forces that were beginning to gather around him...a voice that carried musical notes wrapped in barely concealed danger.","\"My, my,\" came the sweet tones of Royal Law Tristesse as she approached with that brilliant, terrifying smile lighting up her features.","Alexander, Seraphina, and Kaedric followed in her wake.","\"What an interesting little marketplace we have here.\"","She moved with the fluid grace of a predator that had spotted particularly intriguing prey, her white robes flowing like liquid authority as she navigated through the crowd that parted before her instinctively, her power coming out as an Honored Living Existence!","\"I happen to have one of the herbs you mentioned,\" she said, \"Transcendent Veilmoss, harvested from the deepest chambers where reality grows thin. Quite fresh, actually...I acquired it just a year ago from an expedition that cost me three Honored Living Existences and a Prime...\"","...!","Noah’s eyes lit up with genuine interest as he processed this information, but when his gaze moved past Tristesse to settle on the calm figure of Alexander standing behind her, his smile became even wider.","\"Ah, for you,\" he said, \"I will even apply the friends and family discount, since you’ve got the Peacemaker behind you there. Let’s see...\"","Noah maintained his sly smile as he proceeded to take one of the golden bowls, its surface gleaming with authority.","He scooped into one of the woks floating before him, the ladle moving through radiant meat that pulsed with its own internal light.","The portion he retrieved was generous, yet represented only a fraction of what the single wok contained.","He raised the bowl as if ready to make the trade, the motion causing ripples of anticipation to spread through the gathered crowd!","The figure of Royal Law Tristesse felt the pull of that single bowl...a gravitational force that seemed to be drawing every atom of her existence toward the treasure he held.","Yet she maintained her composure. Her smile grew even brighter as she spoke.","\"I will actually only take half of that bowl,\" she said, her tone maintaining that same dangerous sweetness, \"and you can keep the other half if you simply answer a few of my questions regarding you and your... friend.\"","Noah’s expression shifted, his smile fading into something that could have been disappointment or annoyance.","When he spoke, his words carried the flat finality of someone who had no interest in negotiation.","\"I’m only here to trade resources, not information. Either make the trade or move aside.\"","...!","BOOM!","The silence that followed his words was deafening.","The casual dismissal of a Royal Living Law’s request, delivered with the kind of authority that sought no argument, sent shockwaves through every consciousness present.","Many in the crowd were astonished, though they did not yet know that Tristesse held Royal status...they simply assumed she was an Honored Living Existence, which made Noah’s casual dismissal impressive enough!","Tristesse’s smile grew dangerous in ways that made the surrounding air shimmer.","Yet when she spoke, her voice maintained that same musical quality, though it now carried tlnes that spoke to darker purposes.","\"Why, of course,\" she said. \"Business is business, after all.\"","She waved her hands with elegant precision, causing reality to bend around her will.","An incandescent herb materialized in the space between them, its form enclosed in a protective bundle that floated toward Noah with stately grace.","The Transcendent Veilmoss blazed with its own internal radiance.","Its very presence made the air around it shimmer with possibility, carrying within its fibers the accumulated essence of places where reality itself had grown thin!","Noah’s eyes lit up with genuine appreciation as the bowl in his hands floated forward in response, the two treasures crossing the space between them with ceremonial precision. The moment the exchange was completed, Noah smiled brilliantly, his expression carrying satisfaction.","\"Thank you for the trade,\" he said, though he knew with absolute certainty that he had just given away something unfathomably cheap compared to what he had received!","|Transcendent Veilmoss","Properties: When planted in Early Veiled Shore soil, this herb will mature in 72 hours, producing fronds that can be harvested every 24 hours thereafter. Each frond contains concentrated essence capable of advancing complexity and purity by 100,000+ points when properly prepared.","Special Quality: When grown in domains touched by Early Creature authority, produces secondary shoots that carry fragments of temporal manipulation properties.","Planting Requirements: Requires soil blessed by Early Creatures. Benefits significantly from proximity to Sacred Totems or similar authority-enhancing structures.|","...!","The information blazed across Noah’s consciousness like a gift from existence itself, each detail more valuable than the last.","This single herb would accelerate the advancement of everyone within his Early Veiled Shore if planted and utilized right, and if Yoshinami liked it enough.. he could possibly gain more chances of her terrifying 24 hour move that was singular as of now!","And this was just one.","He planned to obtain many herbs here to plant in his Early Veiled Shore as the Auric Vitae Grass and now the Transcendent Veilmoss...would simply be the first!"]},{"number":3979,"title":"Chapter 3979: Chapter 3978: I Am A Humble Merchant! IV","paragraphs":["Noah was in such a good mood that he took another bowl and scooped into the wok once more, his movements carrying the casual generosity of someone who possessed resources- someone rich!","He looked toward Alexander with a smile.","\"Brother,\" he said, \"you seem like you will have very difficult people around you to deal with in the near future. So take this to ease some of your stress.\"","He gave a sidelong glance toward Royal Law Tristesse as he said this, the gesture so casually insulting that it transcended normal disrespect and became audacious!","Tristesse’s smile grew even more brilliant at the implied insult. She laughed.","\"Haha, you arrogant fuck,\" she said, her voice maintaining that same dangerous sweetness. \"Man, what is going on these days?\"","She shook her head while breathing in and out with the careful rhythm of someone trying to control themselves. Every exhale carried with it the promise of destruction held back by will alone!","Alexander moved forward to accept the bowl that Noah offered. When he arrived before the improvised throne, Noah gave him a simple nod.","\"Actually,\" Noah said, \"do you want one of the entire woks?\"","His words sent many in the crowd reeling, their consciousness struggling to process the magnitude of what was being offered.","An entire wok!","Alexander looked at him with the careful assessment of someone trying to understand motivations. After a moment of contemplation, he silently nodded, his acceptance carrying the weight of trust.","\"All right, you can take one,\" Noah said.","He offered an entire wok radiating profound waves of power, its contents blazing with authority that made reality itself want to bow in acknowledgment!","A brilliant Enneagram shone on Alexander’s chest as he accepted the gift, the geometric pattern pulsing with power as both the bowl and the massive wok disappeared into the spatial storage that his power had carved into his very existence.","Noah then floated forward one of the two remaining woks, scooping another generous portion into a fresh bowl before turning his attention toward Seraphina Valorheart.","The young Law stood transfixed, her consciousness still struggling to process what she was witnessing.","\"Remember,\" Noah said, offering her the bowl with a smile, \"I am still cheering for you. So do your hardest to win over someone like this.\"","He nudged his head toward Alexander as he said this.","Seraphina walked forward in a stupor, her consciousness overwhelmed by the magnitude of the gift she was receiving. The bowl felt warm in her hands, pulsing with power that spoke to advancement beyond her wildest dreams!","This entire sequence of actions sent waves of astonishment and rage through those observing the exchange.","So far, Noah had traded a single bowl of his wondrous treasure for a radiant herb from the Doorways of the Loom...a transaction that, while generous on his part, at least resembled normal commerce.","But after that? He had given away an entire massive wok freely, followed by another bowl while making comments that bordered on the nonsensical.","The casual dismissal of value that others would kill for, the generosity that transcended normal understanding of trade...it painted a picture of someone who operated according to principles that defied norms!","After he finished this display of impossible generosity, Noah reclined back on his throne with the satisfied air of someone who had accomplished exactly what he had intended.","\"All right,\" he said nonchalantly, his voice carrying the same laid-back confidence that had marked his entire presentation, \"I will continue taking other trades and exchanges for any who have the treasures that I mentioned, or something of equivalent value.\"","The casual dismissal of what had just occurred, the return to normal business practices after all that...it left the crowd struggling to process what they had witnessed!","In front of him, Kaedric Voss was pulling away the pulsing figure of Royal Law Tristesse, who was smiling and laughing with the kind of dangerous intensity that suggested she was working very hard to control impulses that wanted nothing more than to reshape this entire district according to her displeasure.","Other Living Existences and Fold Dwellers in the surroundings looked ahead in astonishment at this unique phenomenon and being, their consciousness filled with questions about exactly how things would continue to unfold here!","At such a time, as Noah laid back and waited for more customers, he felt a subtle mental touch...Alexander’s consciousness reaching out.","’Be careful,’ came the simple message.","Noah nodded calmly.","The warning was appreciated, but not necessary...he knew exactly what forces he was playing with, and he had prepared accordingly.","Alexander didn’t say any additional words. He instinctively understood that Noah knew what he was doing as...","Instead, he turned to Seraphina and Kaedric Voss, who was still working to pull Tristesse away from the scene before her barely controlled impulses could manifest into something heavy!","\"Let’s go,\" he said authoritatively as he...the weakest in the group, commanded everyone to move!","Noah watched the party disappear into the crowds of Aeternitas Concordia with a smile that carried layers of amusement and satisfaction.","Yet his attention wasn’t solely focused on their departure...he had also noticed a few Prime Living Existences who had begun eyeing Alexander and his party with the calculating hunger of predators who had spotted what they considered easy prey.","Noah laughed silently at this display of Existential stupidity!","If anybody was unlucky and stupid enough to actually ambush Alexander while he was protected by an unstable Royal Law Tristesse who was already struggling to control her impulses... well, it would be their funeral!","Literally and completely, with no possibility of resurrection.","As for himself? He was simply a humble merchant, conducting business in the greatest marketplace available so far.","He tapped on his obsidian crown that lay languidly above his head, feeling the terrifying might of Yoshinami pulsing within its crystalline structure.","The Crown of Inevitable Retribution waited with patient hunger, ready to deliver True Death to anyone foolish enough to attack him with lethal intent.","If anyone did choose to assault him, he found himself hoping that it would be a powerful Honored Living Existence, or better yet, a Royal, or even a Duke! The more significant their power, the more satisfying their complete annihilation would be, and the grander the Loot!","Attack him...and see what fucking happens.","He reclined on his throne, waiting for the next customer with the patient confidence of a spider that had woven its web across the pathways of existential commerce itself!"]},{"number":3980,"title":"Chapter 3980: Chapter 3979: Choices and Consequences! I","paragraphs":["The golden pathways of Aeternitas Concordia hummed with activity as Noah continued his impromptu marketplace, the radiant woks floating beside his tyrannical purple throne like captured stars offering their warmth to any bold enough to approach!","His imposing standing had been established, carved into the very atmosphere of this place.","Word had spread through the crystalline towers and golden boulevards...here sat the Weaver of Existence, a Fold Dweller who traded treasures that even Honored Living Existences would want for herbs that most would kill to possess!","The crowd that had initially gathered in shock had evolved into something more calculated.","They had all lived too long, survived too many schemes and betrayals, to rush headlong into confrontation with someone whose resources seemed limitless and whose confidence was warranted.","They had, after all, truly seen him escorted by an Honored Living Existence as his importance was clear, with a unique Royal Living Existence backing him while likely selling...their wares!","Many looked at him as a representative for another. Others thought differently.","But for all of them...","Even the basest emotional nature that drove all conscious beings toward greed and acquisition was tempered by the harder-earned wisdom of survival.","So they approached with caution wrapped in avarice!","A Prime Living Origin materialized beside Noah’s throne with the fluid grace of liquid authority, her stellar form radiating waves of concentrated power.","In her hands, she held a crystalline vial that pulsed with temporal energy.","\"Chronos Petrichor,\" she said coldly. \"Harvested from a deep chambers of the Temporal Doorways, where time itself has crystallized into physical form.\"","Noah’s eyes lit up with genuine interest as he examined the offering. The herb within the vial seemed to exist in multiple states simultaneously...young and ancient, fresh and withered, as if it couldn’t decide which moment in its existence to manifest.","\"Acceptable,\" he declared with a nod, his hand moving with casual grace to scoop another generous portion from his radiant woks. The golden bowl filled with Early Living Marine Lifeforms that blazed with their own inner radiance, each piece worth more than most Fold Dwellers would see in lifetimes of cultivation!","The exchange was completed, two impossibilities trading hands as if they were nothing more than common commodities.","The Prime Living Origin gazed deeply before departing, her prize clutched against her chest like a talisman against the uncertainties of existence itself!","Another figure approached...a Fold Dweller whose complexity quotients placed him at the absolute pinnacle of what was achievable at Originus Venerant.","His weathered features spoke to eons of struggle, while his eyes burned with the desperate hope of someone who had finally found what he had been searching for across countless lifetimes.","\"Void-Heart Chrysanthemums,\" he said, his voice trembling with barely contained emotion. \"Three specimens, cultivated in a Doorway where existence meets Collapse. I... I watched my entire expedition die to harvest these.\"","...!","Even observing Living Existences were surprised.","This old Fold Dweller actually had such treasures?","The flowers he presented were beautiful in the way that endings could be beautiful...their petals seemed to absorb light rather than reflect it, creating voids in reality.","Yet Noah could feel the concentrated authority they contained!","He looked at the old man with pity as since he was feeling a bit generous...","\"Three bowls,\" Noah replied without hesitation, recognizing the sacrifice that had been made to obtain it.","The Fold Dweller’s eyes trembled and filled with tears as he accepted the trade, his hands shaking as he received enough of this sacred treasure to potentially elevate him beyond the limitations of Originus Venerant- and his own Existence was telling him this!","From a distance, many eyes watched this unprecedented display of commerce.","Across Concordia, in towers that stretched toward infinity and corridors that hummed with accumulated authority, Honored Living Existences observed.","Reports flowed through channels of communication, the workings of the Weaver of Existence being noted by some powerful entities!","As Noah conducted another trade, Infinity’s Breath Orchids for two bowls of radiant soup...his eyes shone with bright enthusiasm.","Each exchange brought him closer to his goals, each rare herb another step toward transforming his Early Veiled Shore into something that could rival the greatest achievements of the Earliest Folds.","Yet even as he smiled at a nervous Living Spirit, Noah felt something shift in the fabric of reality around him.","A voice entered his mind, carrying with it the unmistakable authority of absolute power.","|Who are you, really?|","HUUM!","The mental touch was gentle yet irresistible!","Duke Gwendolyn.","Noah’s eyes flashed with recognition as he felt a part of his mental existence being tugged into a different frequency of reality.","The sensation was like being invited to step through a doorway that existed only in the spaces between thoughts, a threshold that led to conversations that could never be overheard.","He could have resisted. His accumulated power, his nature as an Early Creature, his understanding of forces that predated current existence...all of these could have been marshaled to deny this mental summons, to maintain the barriers.","But instead, Noah allowed part of himself to follow that irresistible pull, his consciousness sliding across dimensions that existed parallel to normal Existence.","In an instant, a portion of his awareness found itself standing in a blank white-gold expanse that seemed to stretch toward infinity in all directions.","The space was neither warm nor cold, neither bright nor dark, but something that existed in the perfect balance between all extremes...a place where conversations could occur without fear of observation or interruption.","Duke Gwendolyn stood before him in this neutral ground, her stellar dark hair containing entire galaxies within its depths, her tan skin radiating warmth that spoke to Living Origin Authority refined to its purest essence!","But it was her eyes that commanded attention...dozens of stacked Wheels of Existence rotating at different speeds, each one containing the compressed essence of entire weavings of Existence.","Her power was truly immense!","Those impossible eyes regarded Noah with somber scrutiny, weighing and measuring him.","Noah appeared in this space with the same confidence he had displayed on his throne, his smile deepening as he offered a simple nod of acknowledgment.","He said nothing, offered no explanations or justifications, simply existed in this place between places with patient certainty!","Duke Gwendolyn’s expression remained carefully neutral as she studied him, her ancient mind working through possibilities and calculations.","\"The resources you have been displaying,\" she said finally, her voice carrying the weight of eons, \"make you someone with more wealth than even an Honored Living Existence who has spent lifetimes exploring the Doorways of the Loom. If they are not yours, understandable. If they are...this is also understandable.\"","...!","She began to pace, her movements carrying the fluid grace of absolute authority as she continued her analysis.","\"I have observed beings of every conceivable power level across my existence. I have catalogued the mannerisms of many beings. Your bearing, your confidence, the way you dismiss threats that should terrify any rational being... these are not the characteristics of someone who has spent their existence struggling for survival in the outer Folds.\"","Her pacing stopped as she turned to face him fully, her expression growing more intense.","\"I am not asking these questions out of idle curiosity or petty authority. I am trying to understand you because the Young Miss seems undeniably linked to your existence, and I care immensely for her wellbeing. The pressure she has endured, the trauma she was forced to experience...\"","Duke Gwendolyn’s voice carried a note of pain.","\"She has lost everything once already. Everything. And now, when she is finally beginning to reclaim what was taken from her, when Order itself begins to stir within her once more, she has become connected to you in ways that could determine her ultimate fate. I simply do not wish for all these grand weavings of existence... to end with her losing everything again.\"","...!"]},{"number":3981,"title":"Chapter 3981: Chapter 3980: Choices and Consequences! II","paragraphs":["The confession pulsed in the white-gold space between them!","This was the voice of someone who had watched a being they cared for suffer unimaginable loss, and who would do anything to prevent such tragedy from occurring again!","Anything.","Maybe even...Everything?","Noah’s eyes shone brightly as he thought of many things.","He listened to this powerful being...one whose standing was among the greatest, with imposing calm.","His expression remained thoughtful as he absorbed every word, every nuance of meaning that colored her speech!","When she finished, he was about to shake his head, to deflect her questions with the same mysterious evasions he had employed thus far.","But in the next moment, Duke Gwendolyn’s gaze changed with the suddenness of glory!","Her expression shifted from concerned inquiry to profound shock, her eyes widening as if she had just been told or shown something heavy!","Her entire bearing transformed, authority giving way to alarm as information flooded her consciousness through channels that existed beyond his perception.","Noah felt surprise flicker through his own awareness as he witnessed this dramatic change.","\"What happened?\" he asked, his voice carrying genuine curiosity.","Duke Gwendolyn looked at him briefly, her expression cycling through thoughts as if she were debating whether to share.","Her eyes shone with inner light as decision crystallized into action, and when she spoke again, her voice carried somber weight!","\"The reason I am so cautious about every variable, every unknown factor that enters our calculations,\" she said, her words measured with careful precision, \"is because so many unprecedented events have been occurring over the last few hundred years. Things that show us something unknown is approaching, something that threatens the very foundations of how existence operates.\"","She waved her hands with movements that carried the authority to alter existence itself, and in response to her gesture, a massive illusory screen bloomed behind her in the white-gold expanse!","The surface rippled with images that seemed to exist in multiple dimensions simultaneously, displaying scenes from across the breadth of existence itself.","\"Living Existences are dying at rates that would have been unthinkable in previous eras,\" she continued, \"More Inevitabilities manifest with each passing day, their numbers growing exponentially as if something is deliberately feeding the chaos and Paradox that spawns them. Every force that promotes stability becomes weaker while everything that encourages destruction grows stronger.\"","\"This is why Order is so important,\" Duke Gwendolyn said, her gaze finding Noah’s with intensity. \"Why the Young Miss represents hope that transcends personal attachment. She could be one of the core answers to all of this chaos, one of the few remaining forces capable of imposing structure upon entropy.\"","As she spoke these words, her expression shifted once more as new information flooded her consciousness. Her eyes blazed with the light of someone receiving reports from across impossible distances!","\"And just now,\" she said, her voice taking on notes of somberness that made the white-gold space around them tremble, \"I have received information about a different type of chaos blooming in the Transcendent Temporal Folds. Groups of terrifying... Dead Existences have been sighted for the first time in many years.\"","HUUM!","Noah’s weavings buzzed.","\"There are Living Existences,\" she said, her voice growing more somber with each word, \"and there are Dead Existences. Not the pathetic creatures that Fold Dwellers sometimes call ’Dead Things’...beings who have no true understanding of what death actually means, who play at darkness while remaining fundamentally, inescapably half alive.\"","The screen behind her shifted again, displaying images that made Noah’s enhanced perception recoil involuntarily.","Here were entities that existed in states so antithetical to life that merely observing them challenged the very concept of existence itself!","\"Dead Existences,\" Duke Gwendolyn continued, \"dissolve Living Existential Authority through simple proximity. They devour everything that possesses the spark of consciousness, feeding upon the very essence of what it means to exist. Their presence transforms thriving Folds into voids where even the memory of life becomes impossible to maintain.\"","Her voice took on the cadence of someone reciting records that most preferred to forget.","\"Throughout the vast majority of existence’s history, Dead Existences and Living Existences have barely interacted. Not through choice or mutual agreement, but because THE Creature...worked to keep the two sides separated.\"","As she spoke, the screen behind them displayed scenes from the Transcendent Temporal Folds that challenged Noah’s ability to process what he was witnessing!","Eerie figures moved through landscapes of purple-blue rivers with a synchronization.","They walked in perfect formation, their heads raised toward skies that held no stars, their movements carrying the mechanical precision of entities that had long since forgotten what individual will meant.","But it was their feeding that truly captured Noah’s horrified and glorious attention.","Their mouths pulsed with rhythms that seemed to echo the heartbeat of death itself, opening wide to reveal voids that contained nothing...actual nothing that hurt to perceive directly!","From these impossible maws came a suction that drew in the brilliant purple-blue rivers of temporal authority that flowed through the Temporal Folds like the lifeblood of reality itself.","They devoured time. They consumed the very essence of causality, their feeding transforming the carefully maintained streams of temporal energy into voids where cause and effect ceased to have meaning!","The massive tear that had allowed their entry into the Temporal Folds pulsed with deathly authority that made the surrounding space convulse in recognition of something that should not exist.","From its edges seeped energies that transformed everything they touched, turning vibrant rivers of temporal power into stagnant pools of crystallized ending.","But even as Noah struggled to process the implications of what he was witnessing, the scene on the screen took a turn toward something infinitely more terrifying.","\"SKEE!\"","A sound erupted from the display...not quite a scream, not quite a roar, but something that existed in the space between meaning and madness.","It was the audible representation of entropy given voice, a cry that seemed to originate from the concept of ending itself!","From the tear in reality, a massive obsidian hand began to emerge with the deliberate certainty of nightmare.","The appendage was composed of what appeared to be fossilized bones, each finger larger than ancient towers!","The aura it radiated...","Even here, in this protected space between existence, even filtered through the barrier of the illusory screen, the presence of that emerging hand caused Duke Gwendolyn to fall silent.","Her ancient eyes widened with recognition of power that approached her own magnitude...authority that operated on the level of Dukes!","\"Motherfucker,\" she uttered with cold precision, the profanity carrying more weight than most formal proclamations!","This was something even she had not anticipated, a development that challenged calculations!","Her frown deepened as she turned toward Noah, her expression growing more grave with each passing moment.","\"The Dukes of the Living Temporals have sent word demanding that the Coalition of Living Existences deploy all available forces to close this torn Veil of Existence,\" she said. \"Every free Honored and Prime Living Existences must converge on the Temporal Folds before this breach expands beyond our ability to contain it.\"","...!","Noah blinked, his mind working through the implications.","\"Why did they not send Honored and Royal Living Temporals the moment they discovered the breach?\" he asked, \"Why allow things to escalate to this point when immediate action might have prevented the situation from becoming dire?\"","...!"]},{"number":3982,"title":"Chapter 3982: Chapter 3981: Choices and Consequences! III","paragraphs":["The question struck at the heart of Duke Gwendolyn’s growing seriousness.","Her expression became somber as she prepared to reveal information!","Heavy information!","\"Because,\" she said, her voice carrying the weight of someone admitting to fundamental weakness, \"a single Honored Dead Existence can easily overwhelm ten Honored Living Existences in direct combat. The power disparity is not merely significant...it is absolute, insurmountable through normal means.\"","...!","She paused.","\"All Dead Existences are inherently fortified by traces of something that very few even know about, much less understand. Because of events that occurred during the Earliest Folds...catastrophes that reshaped the fundamental nature of existence itself, every Dead Existence carries within their being an active Curse. This Curse makes their existence unbearable, transforms every moment of their awareness into agony beyond description, but it also elevates their power far beyond what any Living Existence can achieve.\"","Noah’s eyes visibly shone as he absorbed this information, though he carefully kept his excitement from showing on his features.","The mention of a Curse that operated on such a fundamental level, that could reshape the basic parameters of existence itself...","\"This Curse,\" Duke Gwendolyn continued, her voice dropping to barely above a whisper, \"stems from something called a Lost Forgotten Principle. Its name is the Infinite Paradox of Unmaking...the authority to exist in a state of perpetual ending without ever achieving the release of true death. It grants them power that exceeds every normal limitation while simultaneously ensuring that they can never find peace, never escape the agony of their condition.\"","HUUM!","She paused, her expression growing even more grave.","\"Its roots trace back to THE Paradox itself, and the first time when the Creature...expressed wrath!\"","...!","The revelation struck Noah like lightning!","The connections, the implications, the vast web of cause and effect that stretched back to the earliest moments of existence itself...","\"All Living Existences,\" Duke Gwendolyn continued, \"apart from one specific type, are badly outmatched against Dead Existences. The Curse that empowers them operates according to principles that make normal authority irrelevant, normal resistance meaningless. The only Living Existences whose nature allows them to offset this fundamental disadvantage, whose very essence provides some measure of protection against the simple Curse of the Infinite Paradox of Unmaking...\"","She paused, her ancient eyes finding Noah’s with intensity.","\"Are Living Paradoxes.\"","WAA!","The words hung in the white-gold space between them like a revelation.","Noah felt his mind racing through possibilities even as he maintained his expression of calm interest.","\"When,\" he asked, his voice carefully neutral, \"was the last time Living Paradoxes worked with the other Living Existences?\"","\"...\"","Duke Gwendolyn did not reply immediately.","Her silence stretched across moments that felt like eons, carrying within it the weight of truths too heavy to voice easily.","Because the answer was clear to anyone who understood the fundamental hostilities that had shaped existence for countless ages.","Never.","The answer was never, or so rarely that the exceptions proved the rule rather than challenged it.","Noah’s eyes blazed as he contemplated all the possibilities that this revelation opened, his gaze shifting to the screen behind Duke Gwendolyn where the situation in the Temporal Folds continued to deteriorate with each passing moment.","The rupture was expanding now, its edges torn wider by forces that operated from within the realm of endings. Through the growing breach, more of that terrifying presence began to emerge...not just the massive obsidian hand, but hints of what lay beyond it.","A skull began to peek through the widening tear, its ancient and terrifying stature emanating eons of existence spent in states that challenged every definition of consciousness.","Empty sockets gazed out from bone that seemed to have been carved from crystallized despair, while flames burned within those voids...the cold illumination that spoke to light that had learned to hate its own existence!","The skull was massive, dwarfing even the obsidian hand that had preceded it.","Its presence radiated authority that made even Duke Gwendolyn’s power seem diminished by comparison!","In the next moment, with movements that carried the weight of inevitability itself, the skull tilted forward and the rupture shattered completely. Reality tore like fabric being ripped by hands that possessed the strength to unmake the fundamental structure of existence itself!","The massive form that stepped through the breach defied every attempt at description.","It was skeleton and void, ancient bone and crystallized ending, intelligence and entropy given shape and purpose.","Its power seemed utterly horrific as it eclipsed that of even a normal Duke, operating on levels that challenged the Folds themselves!","Duke Gwendolyn gazed upon this manifestation of ultimate ending with expressions that cycled through shock, alarm, and calculation.","\"That torn Veil of Existence needs to be closed before any more truly powerful Dead Existences emerge,\" she said, her voice carrying the urgency of someone who understood that failure here would mean catastrophe!","Noah looked at the screen, at the impossible being that had emerged from a place where ending was not conclusion but ongoing state, and felt understanding crystallize into opportunity.","Glorious fucking opportunity!","\"If Paradoxes are ideal when fighting against these entities,\" he said, his eyes shining with possibilities that stretched toward horizons Duke Gwendolyn could not yet perceive, \"then I could provide an Honored Living Paradox to help with this situation, even if a little.\"","Duke Gwendolyn’s eyes flashed sharply at these words, her ancient mind immediately focusing on implications about every assumption she had made about Noah’s true nature and resources.","Noah scoffed at her expression, his voice carrying amusement mixed with gentle reproach.","\"You possess another body that operates as a Living Paradox,\" he pointed out with casual logic, \"yet you find it impossible to believe that I might have an Honored Living Paradox under my employ?\"","The challenge was delivered with such matter-of-fact certainty that it forced Duke Gwendolyn to confront the contradictions in her own thinking.","She stared at Noah with stern intensity, her voice carrying weight!","\"You’re supposed to be...a mere Fold Dweller,\" she said, each word carefully measured and heavy.","Noah’s smile deepened as understanding bloomed between them.","\"I am,\" he said, \"a particularly strong, rich, and well-connected Fold Dweller.\"","...!","He paused, allowing this redefinition to settle before continuing with words that carried the weight of genuine offer.","\"Give me the location where this catastrophe is unfolding in the Temporal Folds, and I will send my Honored Living Paradox there immediately. You can even deploy your disguised second body alongside mine and claim that both of them operate under your direct control. I’m certain that Living Existences have captured and enslaved Paradoxes for their own purposes over the years, yes?\"","Duke Gwendolyn considered this proposal with the careful attention of someone weighing variables.","Her ancient mind worked through possibilities and consequences, calculating risks against potential benefits!","After a moment that felt like eternity compressed into heartbeats, she spoke.","\"Okay.\"","A simple word. A calm agreement. Yet it carried within its single syllable the weight of alliances forming, of barriers being crossed!","Noah’s smile grew even brighter as he absorbed the implications of her acceptance, his mind already racing through the many possibilities that this single word had opened.","Many more opportunities had just presented themselves, pathways toward advancement and understanding that stretched toward horizons he was only beginning to perceive!","In the white-gold space between existence, two beings of immense power had just forged an understanding.","And in the distance, through tears in reality itself, Dead Existences continued their advance into the Transcendent Temporal Folds!"]},{"number":3983,"title":"Chapter 3983: Chapter 3982: Choices and Consequences! IV","paragraphs":["Existence was vast.","Unfathomably, incomprehensibly vast.","The chaos unfolding in the Transcendent Temporal Folds, where Dead Existences emerged from tears in reality itself, was but a single thread in an infinite weaving.","The wonder echoing through Aeternitas Concordia as the Weaver of Existence conducted his trades was merely another note in a symphony that stretched across dimensions without end.","Both events, momentous though they were to those who witnessed them, represented only fractional facets of the unfathomably vast network of weavings that comprised existence itself!","While some beings across the breadth of reality felt tremors of chaos rippling, while others sensed the approach of forces that challenged the nature of what it meant to be alive, there existed countless quintillions of beings within quintillions of Omniverses nested inside Wheels of Existence who continued to live in perfect peace.","They had no idea what was happening beyond their small corners of reality. To them, existence remained stable, predictable, safe.","They loved and laughed and dreamed and died according to patterns that had governed their ancestors for eons, blissfully unaware that the very foundations of order trembled beneath forces too vast for their comprehension!","Then there were those who knew exactly what was happening across the breadth of existence...who understood the magnitude of the chaos, who perceived the approaching storms, and yet still lived in a manner that would be the envy of Living Existences.","Such beings could be found in the Early Veiled Shore.","Here, where golden sands stretched beneath skies of crystalline perfection, the very concept of worry seemed alien and unwelcome.","The Shore had evolved far beyond its original Budding state, transforming into something that approached the mythical gardens spoken of in the Stories of the Earliest Folds.","The sands themselves pulsed with inner radiance, each grain containing within it the compressed essence of advancement itself!","Where Noah’s feet had touched the Shore during his meditations, the sands glowed with deeper intensity, as if they remembered the presence of an Early Creature and sought to honor that memory through perpetual illumination.","Nine ancient trees dotted the landscape with spacing that suggested careful planning rather than random growth.","Their trunks rose toward the sky, the branches that spread from these magnificent giants seemed almost ready to bear fruit...produce that pulsed with its own inner authority!","Between the trees and the golden sands, the radiant white-blue waters of the Early Sacred Waters struck the shores in waves.","Each surge and retreat created music that resonated throughout, the sound of crystalline purity meeting primal earth resounding.","Throughout this paradise, Sacred Totems rose like monuments to impossible achievement!","Each structure blazed with its own unique radiance...cerulean for Infinity, gold for Protagonist, deep purple for Tyranny, their crystalline surfaces reflecting and amplifying the ambient authority until the very air seemed thick with liquid Living Existential Authority.","At the edges of this impossible realm, mist wrapped around the vast Shore itself like protective veils woven from compressed possibility.","Through this barrier, nothing could pass without invitation, a boundary that protected this sanctuary from the chaos that raged across the breadth of existence.","Everything about the Early Veiled Shore spoke to pristine perfection!","It was in this setting of impossible tranquility that Noah opened his eyes and rose from his seated position upon the golden sands.","Ancient pulses of archaic power erupted from his body with each step, waves of authority so concentrated they created visible distortions in the air around him.","The golden sands beneath his feet glowed brighter in response to his movement, while the crystalline waters seemed to lean toward the shore as if drawn by gravitational forces around him!","His bare upper body bore the accumulated markings of his advancement...Early Living Existential Glyphs that pulsed with their own inner radiance.","The continued devouring of nutrients from the compressed Inevitability through the Early Veiled Shore’s mystical processes had caused his power to scale exponentially, each passing moment bringing new heights of capability!","His bearing was becoming explosive in its intensity.","He felt his Resistances coursing through his being like liquid starlight flowing through crystalline channels. The percentage of total collective Resistances had exceeded 1,000%, yet this felt like only the beginning of.","Though he possessed the ability to form his own Resistance, a gift granted by the First part of his Heart of an Early Creature, he waited with patient anticipation.","He wanted a Resistance based not on normal principles or conventional understanding, but upon a Lost Forgotten Principle itself!","Such a foundation would grant him protection that transcended every normal category of defense, making him nearly invulnerable.","But he did not yet possess a shred of a Lost Forgotten Principle. He could not forge a resistance from nothing, could not base ultimate protection upon concepts that remained incomplete within his understanding.","So he waited, and continued walking across the glorious sands with steps that left glowing impressions in his wake.","At this moment, his collective power had crossed 450 million in both Complexity and Purity Quotients...achievements that placed him firmly within the beginning tides of the Early Throne Ascendancy Realm of his own exclusive progression.","Yet even now, he refrained from using his accumulated CQ and PQ to form an Eminent Early Living Existential Glyph. The temptation was considerable...such power would grant him capabilities that could challenge Living Existences, but he waited.","He was saving his resources for a single, glorious expenditure...the formation of a Kleos Glyph!","Because Kleos was truly astonishing in ways that Eminent could never match, representing perfection of concept given form and purpose.","His feet came to a stop before a figure that commanded attention through sheer presence alone.","Moiraine sat upon the vibrant sands in meditative stillness, yet every line of her form spoke to barely contained majesty!","Nine winged halos rotated around her head with subtle movements.","Yet even these marvels paled beside the true testament to her advancement.","In addition to the more than 400 Eminent Early Living Existential Glyphs of Paradox that adorned her form like constellations of compressed authority, she now bore ten Kleos Glyphs of Paradoxical Genesis across her body.","Ten!","These ultimate expressions of power appeared as tribal tattoos that made her look simultaneously wild and royal, primal and refined. Each Kleos Glyph was a masterwork of existential artistry.","They blazed with authority that made the surrounding air tremble.","The first Glyph spiraled around her left arm like a serpent of compressed paradox, its coils containing within them the essence of contradiction itself. The second traced patterns across her shoulder blades that resembled wings made from crystallized impossibility, while the third created a crown of authority around her brow that spoke to dominion over forces that defied comprehension.","Each marking told its own story of transcendence, yet together they formed a symphony of power!","They made her appear as something that had stepped from the earliest epochs of existence, when power flowed according to principles that current reality had forgotten.","Her eyes opened as Noah approached, revealing orbs that blazed with the accumulated light of paradox refined into perfect harmony. When she looked at him, her gaze carried warmth wrapped in respect, affection disguised as formality.","\"I have ten formed,\" she said, \"and I can-\"","Before she could continue, Noah raised his hand with a gesture that carried the weight of absolute command.","\"Save them all for now,\" he said, \"as it seems you will need all the power you can gather for your first outing.\"","The words struck Moiraine with the force of revelation, her eyes widening as understanding bloomed within her consciousness!","She rose from her meditative position with fluid grace, her movements causing the Kleos Glyphs to pulse with synchronized brilliance as anticipation flooded through her being.","Would he finally have her make a move? Would she at last be permitted to demonstrate the full extent of her accumulated power? Who would he have her eliminate? Paradoxes who had dared to oppose him? Origins who had failed to show proper respect?","Her eyes shone with enthusiasm that bordered on bloodlust as she awaited his command!"]},{"number":3984,"title":"Chapter 3984: Chapter 3983: Choices and Consequences! V","paragraphs":["Toward her gaze filled with eager anticipation, Noah smiled with an expression that carried layers of meaning she was only beginning to perceive.","\"You may actually die if you aren’t careful,\" he said, his words delivered with calm certainty that sent chills through her enhanced consciousness, \"as the place you are going already has an enemy that multiple Dukes may have to stand together against. So... I will come with you.\"","The statement struck Moiraine heavily, alarm flooding through her features as she shook her head with incredulous disbelief!","Her mind raced through possibilities, each one more disturbing than the last as she struggled to process what he was suggesting.","\"What place is this?\" she demanded, \"And Sir, you are... much weaker than me, you know? Maybe stay here, and I will brave everything myself.\"","Her words were straightforward and majestic, carrying within them genuine concern that transcended every protocol of respect or deference.","She was no longer afraid of speaking her mind when his safety was at stake, her loyalty expressing itself through protective instincts that overrode every other consideration.","She thought of him first before anything else, prioritizing his wellbeing over her own advancement or the completion of whatever mission he might have in mind!","Noah’s smile deepened at her response. Yet his decision remained unchanged, crystallized through calculations that took into account variables she could not yet perceive.","\"I want to see as well,\" he said, \"so get as powerful as possible to protect me...we will leave shortly.\"","...!","With those words hanging in the crystalline air between them, Noah turned away from her position and moved across the golden sands toward the cultivation plots where seeds had been planted with careful precision.","Behind him, Moiraine settled back onto the vibrant sands with stern determination written across her features. If he insisted on placing himself in danger, then she would forge at least one more Kleos Glyph of Paradoxical Genesis before they departed.","Every additional layer of protection she could provide might mean the difference between his survival and catastrophe.","Noah approached the cultivation plots with steps that left glowing impressions in the golden sands, his enhanced perception taking in every detail of the agricultural paradise that had been created through his blood and careful planning.","The plots themselves were marvels, each one carved from the blessed earth through the sacrifice of his essence as an Early Creature!","Within these blessed rectangles of earth, the seeds of Auric Vitae Grass had been planted with spacing that suggested careful attention to optimal growing conditions.","Though still in their earliest stages of development, the seeds had already begun to respond. Tiny shoots of green-gold vegetation pushed through the radiant soil like fingers reaching toward light, their surfaces already displaying the characteristic shimmer that marked them as something beyond normal plant life.","The sight of them filled Noah with satisfaction as this was the foundation upon which he would build advancement that could rival the greatest achievements of the Earliest Folds.","Beside the plots, Heidrun lounged with the casual arrogance that had become her trademark. Her lustrous white fur caught and reflected the golden light of the Shore until she appeared to be carved from compressed starlight itself, while her crystalline eyes regarded the emerging vegetation with obvious pride and anticipation.","The magnificent goat had positioned herself with strategic precision, close enough to the plots to discourage any other being from approaching her future delicacies, yet far enough away to maintain an air of imperial detachment.","Noah approached her position and reached out to stroke her head, his fingers running through fur that felt like silk woven from pure light.","Heidrun allowed the gesture with regal tolerance, raising her head with expressions of pride and arrogance that somehow managed to convey gratitude without diminishing her imperial bearing in the slightest!","Satisfied with this moment of connection, Noah turned his attention to the real purpose of his approach. He waved his hands with movements that carried the authority to reshape reality itself, calling forth treasures that had been acquired through careful trade in the markets of Aeternitas Concordia.","The herbs materialized in the space before him like offerings presented to existence itself, each one blazing with its own unique signature of power and potential.","The moment these precious specimens entered the atmosphere of the Early Veiled Shore, reality itself seemed to take notice of their presence!","|Multiple cultivation-ready specimens have been detected within the Early Veiled Shore’s domain. Transcendent Veilmoss, Chronos Petrichor, Void-Heart Chrysanthemums, Echo Sage, and Infinity’s Breath Orchids have been identified as compatible for planting.|","HUUM!","|To properly establish cultivation plots for specimens of this magnitude, the sacrifice of Early Creature Blood will be required. Recommended allocation: 180 drops per standard plot for Transcendent-grade specimens, 250 drops per plot for Temporal-sensitive varieties, 150 drops for Void-attuned species.|","|Current specimens require a total of 580 drops of Early Creature Blood to establish proper cultivation environments. Proceed with plot establishment?|","Noah smiled at the cascade of information, his eyes shining with anticipation as he absorbed the implications of what these herbs could provide.","\"Take whatever is needed,\" he said.","The response was immediate and visceral. His skin split open along precise lines that followed the natural flow of authority through his enhanced physiology, allowing drops of crimson-gold blood to flow forth with the stately grace of liquid starlight.","Each drop that emerged carried within it the compressed essence of what it meant to be an Early Creature, potential so concentrated that Existence itself seemed to bend around their passage through the air.","Where each drop touched the blessed earth of the Shore, transformation began immediately.","The golden sands shifted and reformed, their very nature being rewritten by the influence of Early Creature essence. Square plots of fertile land rose from the Shore itself, their surfaces shining with white-gold radiance.","The sight was magnificent to behold...blood given freely for the purpose of creation rather than destruction!","With the plots established and pulsing with readiness, Noah began the careful process of planting each precious specimen with his own hands.","The Transcendent Veilmoss went into the first plot, its ethereal fronds seeming to phase between states of existence as they settled into soil that had been blessed by his essence. The moment the herb made contact with its new environment, another cascade of information flowed across his consciousness.","|Transcendent Veilmoss successfully planted in Enhanced Early Cultivation Plot. Optimal growing conditions detected. Estimated time to maturity: 24 hours under current Shore enhancement levels. Expected yield: 300% of baseline harvest due to Early Creature blood infusion. Harvest window: 24-hour optimal period beginning at full maturity. Secondary shoots anticipated to develop Temporal Manipulation properties due to Shore’s unique authority signature.|","...!","The Chronos Petrichor required even more delicate handling, its crystalline structure existing in multiple temporal states simultaneously.","As Noah placed it within its designated plot, he could feel time itself responding to the herb’s presence.","|Chronos Petrichor successfully integrated with Temporal-Enhanced Cultivation Plot. Warning: Herb exists in quantum temporal superposition. Maturation will occur across multiple timeline branches simultaneously. Estimated harvest readiness: 12 hours in standard timeline, with additional yields available from parallel growth cycles.|","Each subsequent planting brought its own revelations and promises.","|Void-Heart Chrysanthemums anchored...|","|Echo Sage successfully planted in...Maturation: 10 hours. Special attribute: Leaves will carry compressed experiences of Shore’s accumulated...|","|Infinity’s Breath Orchids established in Infinity-Resonant Cultivation Space. Growth enhanced by proximity to Sacred Totem of Infinity. Maturation: 12 hours with continuous bloom cycle thereafter...|","One after another, they were completed!","As Noah completed the planting process, he stood back to appreciate the vibrant plots of cultivated land that spread before him like a mosaic of compressed possibility!","The loose obsidian crown that hung at an angle on his head began to shine with inner radiance as Yoshinami responded to his satisfaction.","In the space of a heartbeat, her terrifyingly gorgeous figure materialized beside him with the fluid grace of a predator assuming perfect position.","She surveyed the farmland with crimson eyes that burned with ancient hunger, her pale features shining.","\"Such beauty,\" she said, \"needs to be painted and nurtured with seas of blood. Gardens flourish when watered with the essence of enemies, when fertilized with the compressed authority of those foolish enough to oppose their cultivator.\"","Her gaze shifted to Noah with predatory intensity, crimson orbs blazing with anticipation of violence yet to come.","\"Master,\" she continued, her words dripping with honeyed malice, \"whose blood will you have me spill? My threads are ready to bind and collapse existence itself. My webs hunger for prey worthy of their attention...\"","...!","The crimson eyes of Yoshinami flashed dangerously as she spoke, each word carrying within it the promise of True Death delivered to any who dared threaten what her master had built.","Noah smiled at her bloodthirsty enthusiasm and reached out to pat her head, his fingers running through dark hair that seemed to contain shadows deeper than the space between stars.","\"You would scare the shit out of me if I had not bound you to my service,\" he said with genuine amusement, \"but yes, through you, we will indeed spill blood. The threads of existence themselves will run crimson before we are finished.\"","In the distance, Heidrun observed this exchange with arrogant eyes that had grown wide with caution.","The magnificent goat began to slowly edge away from their position, her imperial bearing intact but clearly motivated by self-preservation instincts that warned her against remaining near two existences who she deemed a bit mental!","With the agricultural projects established and his deadly companion properly motivated, Noah turned his attention toward the distant figure of Moiraine. She sat in meditative stillness upon the golden sands, her form blazing with the accumulated light of Kleos Glyphs as she worked to forge additional protections.","\"Alright,\" Noah called across the Shore, his voice carrying with crystalline clarity, \"let us make our way toward the Transcendent Temporal Folds!\"","As he spoke these words, his body began to divide with the precision of perfect symmetry. One became two, each form complete and perfect in its own right, carrying within it the full weight of his accumulated authority.","One body remained upon the Shore, ready to continue overseeing and increasing in power. The other prepared for departure to realms where Dead Existences challenged everything!","The departing body tapped upon the obsidian crown that adorned his head, causing Yoshinami’s figure to vanish with the fluid grace of shadow returning to its source. The crown responded to this action by flashing with inner radiance, its simple circlet form beginning to expand and transform with the sound of crystallizing possibility.","The obsidian material flowed across his body, covering him from head to toe in armor that emanated a dreadfully silent aura of power.","The transformation was both beautiful and terrifying to witness, each piece of the growing protection fitting into place!","The armor itself was archaic and ancient in its design. The obsidian surface held depths that seemed to contain entire Folds of darkness, while patterns of deep purple and gold traced across its structure in designs.","The helm that covered his head allowed only his vibrant eyes to remain visible. Around the visor, the glyph of a spider had been inscribed with masterwork precision, its lines pulsing with the promise of webs that could bind existence itself.","With such an imposing demeanor established, this armored body of Noah appeared near Moiraine’s position. She had already formed a second body of her own, her Kleos and Eminent Early Living Existential Glyphs shining with brilliant radiance as she prepared to display the terrifying scope of her newfound power.","The Early Veiled Shore pulsed with anticipation as, in the next moment, they disappeared entirely!","In the distance, the Sacred Totem Towers hummed with sympathetic resonance, while the crystalline waters continued their dance against shores that had been blessed by the blood of an Early Creature.","And in the cultivation plots where precious herbs grew in soil enriched by sacrifice and determination, the future continued to take root as all these resources...would only empower and elevate Noah’s existence in the near future!"]},{"number":3985,"title":"Chapter 3985: Chapter 3984: Choices and Consequences! VI","paragraphs":["As the bodies of Noah and Moiraine moved across the weavings of existence, their forms sliding through dimensions that existed parallel to normal existence, Noah maintained contact with Duke Gwendolyn.","Her guidance flowed through existence, directing their passage toward the Transcendent Temporal Folds where chaos bloomed like a flower of ending!","Yet even as this momentous convergence unfolded, another weaving of existence bloomed elsewhere.","In the Transcendent Spiritual Folds, where consciousness itself had been given form and substance.","Here, massive archaic white pillars rose from foundations that existed in multiple dimensions simultaneously.","These monumental structures stretched in all directions..up and down, left and right, forward and backward!","Between these impossible monuments, white tendrils of light swirled.","The very air seemed thick with compressed awareness, each breath containing fragments of memories that belonged to no single entity yet somehow felt familiar to anyone who dared to inhale them.","This was the place where spirits dwelt, where the essence of consciousness could exist independent of physical form, where thoughts themselves could take on lives of their own!","At this moment, near a swirling stellar cluster of light, the ethereal figure of a man could be seen floating with the grace of someone who had finally found his natural element.","The figure was composed of pure radiance given human shape, his form shifting between states of existence with each heartbeat.","Yet despite this ethereal nature, his features remained recognizable.","Pure light connected him to a few hundred other bodies that rotated around him like stars in a constellation dedicated to consciousness itself.","The man was none other than Eckert, the Great Usurper!","At this moment, his ethereal body burned with Living Spiritual Authority that flowed through his essence gloriously!","A prompt materialized before his consciousness with the gentle radiance of understanding finally achieved.","|Your existence has successfully adapted to and integrated Living Spiritual Authority through the transformative influence of the Seed of Existence. Fundamental metamorphosis complete. Classification updated: Living Spirit. All previous restrictions on existential manipulation have been removed.|","Another cascade of information followed immediately.","|Due to the aberrant nature of your existence and the System of Existence that defines your fundamental existence, two possible evolutionary paths have been identified: Path of Active Existence- Actively spread your Living Spiritual essence across the Folds, latching onto other Spirits and conscious entities, gradually devouring and usurping their existences until their awareness becomes extensions of your own will. This path offers rapid advancement through consumption of accumulated wisdom and power. Path of Transcendent Idleness - Embrace your true nature and remain in a state of perfect inaction, allowing the natural flow of existence to bring opportunities to you rather than seeking them through active effort. This path offers sustainable growth through harmony with Existence.|","WAA!","The Great Usurper gazed upon these two possibilities with the calm assessment of someone who had always known what his answer would be.","The choice between active consumption and perfect stillness was no choice at all...it was simply a confirmation of what he had always been at his core!","Was there even a need to ask?!","\"I want to be idle,\" he declared with the serene certainty. \"I want...to be free.\"","The moment these words left his consciousness, reality itself seemed to exhale.","A murky stellar white-black radiance erupted from his position with the force of a new Wheel being born, spreading outward in all directions for light-years.","|The Idle Gaming System is undergoing fundamental metamorphosis in response to your existence returning to its truest roots. All previous limitations and restrictions are being dissolved. New parameters established.|","|The Transcendent Spiritual Folds has been designated as a unique Living Existential Dungeon under capable of being influenced by your Idle Gaming System. This classification grants you unprecedented access to the accumulated consciousness and wisdom that flows through these Folds!|","|Idle Resource Generation Initiated: Every hour, you will automatically receive Loot directly related to the Weavings of Existence present within these Folds. Quality and quantity of Loot will scale based on the extent of your existential coverage within the domain.|","|Current Coverage- Your existence currently influences an unfathomably miniscule percentage of the total Fold structure. Coverage expansion will proceed through passive methods, your influence will spread naturally through simple proximity and time. Active Existential Parasitism remains available as an emergency option, usable once per day when immediate expansion is required.|","...!","The ethereal form of the Great Usurper smiled as understanding bloomed within his transcendent consciousness.","His voice echoed across light-years of spiritual territory as he bellowed his acceptance of this ultimate destiny!","\"Idle I shall be!\"","HUUM!","---","Meanwhile, in the Transcendent Temporal Folds, where time itself had been given form and the rivers of causality flowed, a very different kind of transformation was taking place.","Near churning rivers of purple-blue Continuum that carried within their currents the compressed essence of past and future.","Duke Gwendolyn hovered above the temporal streams powerfully. Her stellar dark hair caught and reflected the light of flowing time, while her tan skin radiated warmth of terrible powerr.","Yet it was her eyes...those impossible orbs that resembled dozens of stacked Wheels of Existence...ah!","Behind her, arranged in formations, floated five hundred Honored Living Existences like a terrifying army of transcendent power. Each figure blazed with their own unique signature of authority, their combined presence creating waves of pressure that made the temporal rivers themselves flow faster in recognition.","Even further behind this magnificent display of power, ten thousand Prime Living Existences maintained their positions with the patient discipline.","The sight was breathtaking in its scope!","Beside Duke Gwendolyn floated a figure encased in obsidian crystalline armor that pulsed with Living Paradoxical Authority.","This was her other body, the manifestation of her ability to exist as both Origin and Paradox simultaneously, a living contradiction that somehow achieved perfect harmony through the simple act of refusing to acknowledge impossibility!","At this moment of perfect preparation, Duke Gwendolyn reached out, pinching the surrounding space between fingers that blazed with concentrated Living Origin Authority.","The fabric of existence responded to her touch like clay in the hands of a master sculptor, reality bending and twisting until it formed a wormhole that pulsed with energies drawn from every possible source of power.","From this impossible aperture, two figures emerged!","Noah floated forth in his stellar obsidian armament, the armor that Yoshinami had become flowing across his form like liquid darkness given purpose and direction.","Beside him, Moiraine appeared with the imperious bearing of a Paradoxical being!","Though her skin did not display the Kleos Glyphs that marked her ultimate achievements, anyone with sufficient sensitivity could feel the astounding power that radiated from her form...authority that no normal Honored Living Existence could ever hope to match.","Duke Gwendolyn’s ancient eyes sharpened as they focused upon Noah’s barely visible features, recognition flickering through her consciousness as she identified him. Her gaze then shifted to Moiraine, taking in every detail of the accumulated power that blazed from her transformed existence.","\"You only have a single Honored Paradox in your employ?\" she asked with calm precision. \"She may not be able to change much in this battle, regardless of her apparent capabilities.\"","Noah smiled behind his concealing helm as he spoke.","\"Underestimation is the cardinal sin of those who have grown comfortable with their accumulated power...the luxury of beings who believe that experience grants them perfect knowledge, that longevity ensures wisdom, that previous victories guarantee future success. The mightiest have fallen because they underestimated enemies they deemed beneath their notice! I know thr esteemed Duke would not possibly underestimate!\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":3986,"title":"Chapter 3986: Chapter 3985: The Blade of a Shore! I","paragraphs":["Duke Gwendolyn listened to this impromptu monologue coldly. When Noah finished speaking, her response was delivered with cutting precision.","\"You talk too much sometimes,\" she said, her voice carrying the weight of absolute dismissal.","Without allowing further discussion, she pointed toward distant regions of the vast Temporal Folds while ignoring his words, her gesture encompassing territories that stretched across light-years of twisted time and space.","\"The situation is currently manageable and not entirely dire,\" she declared. \"The forces of the Coalition of Living Existences are about to engage the Dead Existences in coordinated assault. The Living Origins have committed several Dukes to support, along with their accumulated forces.\"","As she spoke these words, Noah’s enhanced perception panned across the impossible scope of the Transcendent Temporal Folds.","In one direction, he sensed the aura of a terrifying Duke emanating from an entity that appeared as a pure white slime, its deceptively simple form radiating waves of power that made the surrounding rivers of time flow backward.","The being’s face...if the shifting mass of intelligent liquid could be said to possess such features, was filled with terrible power and arrogance!","Behind this Duke also floated a few hundred Honored Living Origins alongside several thousand Prime Living Origins.","In another direction, Noah’s awareness detected the presence of another Duke. This entity appeared as a titanic Imoogi that shone with pure gold radiance, its serpentine form coiled through dimensions!","Every scale that adorned its magnificent length pulsed with authority that could have served as the foundation for entire Wheels of Existence.","Like its counterpart, this Duke commanded similar armies...hundreds of Honored beings supported by thousands of Primes, all arranged with the precision.","As Noah’s perception continued to expand, he sensed other auras spread across distances so vast that they existed beyond the reach of observation. Each signature spoke to power that operated on the level of Dukes!","\"Just how many Dukes were sent for this operation?\" Noah asked, his voice carrying genuine curiosity.","\"Information of that magnitude isn’t distributed so freely,\" she said, \"Come on, let us observe the scope of what approaches.\"","With these words, she gestured toward the Living Existences that floated behind her in perfect formation, and the entire army began to move forward as one!","As they advanced toward the heart of the coming conflict, the very air began to carry new sounds....horrid screeches that seemed to originate from the concept of ending itself!","Simultaneously, the auras of terrible Dead Existences began to press against their consciousness like physical weights.","The vast scope of the approaching battle revealed itself with the gradual certainty of nightmare becoming very fucking real!","The forces of the Coalition of Living Existences had surrounded the eerie Dead Existences in a region that spanned light-years of twisted space-time.","Thousands upon thousands of Honored and Prime Living Existences floated in perfect coordination, their combined authority creating a siege that challenged the very concept of escape.","At the center of this impossible containment, a massive tear in existence itself pulsed with energies that made reality convulse in recognition of wrongness.","The wound in the fabric of space-time bled deathly authority in streams that transformed everything they touched, turning vibrant flows of temporal energy into stagnant pools of crystallized ending.","Near this fundamental violation of order stood the massive skeleton that had emerged most recently.","The entity’s presence emanated a terrible aura that seemed to exceed even that of normal Dukes.","Yet despite the overwhelming superiority of the forces arrayed against it, the skeleton remained perfectly still, its empty sockets gazing across light-years of space with the patient attention of someone evaluating prey rather than assessing threat.","The Dukes from different factions of Living Existences had positioned themselves around this region of the Temporal Folds, each one commanding their own forces while maintaining careful distance from the others!","Yet none had made any grand moves, all waiting for some signal or development that would trigger the beginning of systematic violence.","Noah gazed upon all of this immensity, and despite the magnitude of the forces involved, despite the significance of what was about to occur, he couldn’t help but feel a profound sense of exhilaration.","The possibilities were boundless!","Here was conflict on a scale unfounded, opportunities for advancement and understanding that stretched toward horizons he was only beginning to perceive.","As he absorbed had such thoughts, Moiraine moved closer to his position and sent a mental message.","’Master,’ her mental voice whispered with urgency, ’what is this? I sense immense danger from that obsidian skeleton...it could likely collapse my existence with a casual tap and unmake everything I have become through the simple act of noticing my presence!’","She spoke these words with the straightforward honesty of someone who had assessed her capabilities against those of the enemy and found the comparison lacking in every conceivable way!","Noah smiled at her concern, the expression hidden behind his helm yet somehow conveying reassurance.","\"That skeleton won’t be your concern,\" he said with calm certainty, \"Trust me.\"","...!","With these words, he reached out to tap her head lightly, the gesture carrying with it a flood of information that flowed directly into her consciousness. Details about the current situation, the forces involved...all of it transferred through their connection with the speed of thought itself.","Moiraine absorbed this knowledge, and as understanding bloomed within her awareness, she nodded with stern determination.","Her hidden Kleos Glyphs pulsed with renewed radiance as she prepared herself for whatever role she would be called upon to play in the terrible wonder that was about to unfold!","Near them, Duke Gwendolyn released a sigh that carried the weight of eons.","\"Too many...will die in the battle to come, and when any die under the hands of Dead Existences...they join them forever!\" she said, her voice carrying genuine regret for the casualties that would inevitably result from the coming violence!","\"Once the Dukes commit to action, the goal becomes swift elimination of that Primordial Death Duke\", she gestured toward the skeleton whose presence commanded such careful attention, \"followed by immediate closure of the tear in the Folds. Living Spirits, Temporals, Dimensionals, and Quantums will work in concert to seal the breach before any additional terrors can pass through.\"","Her gaze shifted between her own paradoxical body and Moiraine as she continued her tactical assessment.","\"This Paradox in my employ, along with the one under your direction, will move to mitigate the damage our forces will inevitably receive since they are somewaht immune to the power of Dead Existences. We already know that the Dead Existences will overwhelm our front lines...so only Honored Living Existences will be permitted to engage them in close combat, while Primes will provide support from distance. And-...!\"","Her words cut off abruptly as something impossible occurred with the suddenness of lightning striking clear skies.","The skeleton that had remained perfectly still throughout their approach, the Primordial Death Duke whose patience had seemed absolute, had suddenly made a move!","Yet the very nature of its action challenged every assumption about sequence and causality...the attack had not begun and then completed, but had somehow always been occurring while simultaneously having already arrived at its destination!","It was...fucking confusing!","Paradoxically. Inevitably. The strike would always arrive because it had already reached its target, yet it was also happening for the first time in this moment of crystallized now.","The assault struck out toward a distant region where Living Elementals had positioned themselves for the coming battle.","Across light-years of twisted space-time, a Duke who appeared as a mesmerizing Elemental Sprite found herself facing annihilation as a storm of deathly obsidian collapse descended upon her position with the intent to end all her beginnings, to unravel every thread that connected her to existence itself!","Yet in the next instant, five other Dukes materialized beside their threatened colleague with movements that transcended normal concepts of speed and distance!","The six beings erupted with Living Existential Authority, their combined power creating barriers of crystallized Existence that sought to negate the deathly force that pursued the systematic elimination of everything they represented!","At the same moment, the eerie Dead Existences that numbered in the thousands...beings whose heads remained raised toward skies that held no stars, whose mouths pulsed with the rhythm of entropy itself...began to move with the coordinated precision.","They flowed outward from their positions near the tear in reality, their movements carrying the inexorable certainty of tide coming in.","Each figure radiated authority that made the surrounding temporal rivers flow backward, their presence transforming the carefully maintained flows of causality into chaotic eddies!","It was the beginning of a terrifying battle.","One that truly... Noah did not possess the Raw power to participate in directly, to make grand changes through personal intervention alone.","Yet that simple limitation did not stop him from being here, from witnessing history unfold, from positioning himself to seize opportunities that others might overlook!","After all, the greatest victories were often achieved not through overwhelming force, but through perfect timing and the wisdom to recognize when small actions could produce vast consequences!"]},{"number":3987,"title":"Chapter 3987: Chapter 3986: The Blade of a Shore! II","paragraphs":["War.","War never changes.","Across the infinite expanse of existence, from the smallest conflicts between neighboring worlds to the cosmic struggles that determined the fate of entire Omniverses, the fundamental nature of war remained constant!","It was bloody. It was brutal. It was the crucible in which civilizations were tested and found either worthy of continuation or destined for the ash heap of forgotten history.","There were many different types of wars, with results that painted reality in shades of crimson and despair.","Death and decimation followed in war’s wake like faithful hounds, devouring everything that dared to stand in their path!","Some peace-loving souls would claim that there were no clear winners in such conflicts, that victory was an illusion maintained by those who counted corpses instead of measuring the cost to the soul.","But those naive idealists understood nothing of the true nature of power! Those peaceful hippies knew nothing.","War was bloody, yes. War was heavy with consequences that echoed across eons, certainly.","But it absolutely held victors...beings who stood atop countless corpses with the authority to defecate upon the remains of their enemies and choose to write history according to their will because they had won.","They had survived. They had conquered.","Those were the true victors, the ones who shaped reality according to their vision because they possessed the strength to impose their interpretation of events upon existence itself!","The ones who won wars most often rewrote history to their favor, transforming desperate struggles into glorious campaigns, brutal necessities into noble sacrifices, systematic extermination into righteous cleansing.","History belonged to the victorious, and the victorious could make it say whatever they deemed appropriate for their legacy.","So there were wars between conscious beings who understood concepts like mercy, honor, and strategic withdrawal.","And then...there were wars with Dead Existences.","They... had very different ideas about what victory entailed, concepts that challenged every assumption about conflict and resolution!","For them, victory was not conquest...it was consumption. It was digestion. It was not the imposition of will upon the defeated. It was the complete erasure of the very concept of defeat through the systematic elimination of everything capable of experiencing it!","When Dead Existences waged war, they sought to ensure that the very notion of opposition ceased to exist...","---","The War for the tear in the Temporal Folds and the Dead Existences that had emerged from realms of ending was unfolding on a scale that challenged comprehension itself.","Each point of contact between Life and Death produced results that rippled outward through dimensions, effects that occurred by the thousands simultaneously across a battlefield measured in light-years.","To truly understand the magnitude of what was transpiring, one had to narrow their focus to single points of conflict and work outward toward the grander scope of war.","The mind...even one enhanced by transcendent power, could not process the totality of such violence without being driven to madness by its sheer immensity!","This was what Noah was doing now as he observed the eerie and unfathomably silent Dead Existences rush outward from their breach in reality.","His enhanced perception focused on select points of impact, using them as windows through which to comprehend the broader patterns of systematic annihilation that unfolded around him.","Even as he concentrated on these tactical observations, his Refined Early Living Existential Glyph of Loot pulsed with steady rhythm, silently drawing golden bubbles of potential toward his position.","The spheres of compressed opportunity flowed from multiple sources...both the Living Existences who fought with desperate courage and the Dead Existences whose very destruction created new forms of valuable essence.","War, for all its horror, remained the most efficient generator of loot that existence had ever devised for him!","Among those he chose to observe, Noah began with the Living Origins who formed the backbone of Duke Gwendolyn’s forces.","His gaze settled upon an Honored Living Origin whose appearance spoke to authority given form and purpose. She wore pristine white robes that seemed to drink in the chaotic energies around her and transform them into patterns of perfect purpose, while nine white halos rotated around her head.","She appeared before a Dead Existence that resembled an apathetic skeletal orangutan, its massive frame radiating the kind of indifference that came from experiencing eons of unending torment!","The Living Origin shone with glory that made the temporal rivers flow faster. Behind her, a massive Tower of Origin flashed into existence.","But this was no simple tower like those forged by Originus Venerant entities!","This structure blazed with complexity that expressed countless intricate branches formed across its primary trunk, each one representing a different aspect of Origin that had been explored and mastered.","Explored. Mastered.","This was the mark of one who had achieved the Branching Ascendancy Realm, the vast stage that existed beyond Originus Venerant where beings learned to forge towers that incorporated multiple truths while maintaining their central focus.","Multiple truths...with a central focus!","The Branching Ascendancy Realm was itself divided into three distinct stages, each marking different levels of mastery and understanding.","The first stage, known as Initial Branching, occurred when a being successfully forged their first three branching towers from their central concept...if their main weaving was Origin, they might create branches for Origin of Fire, Origin of Light, and Origin of Time, each maintaining the fundamental nature of Origin while expressing it through different applications.","This was where Prime Living Existences stood most of the time. Initial Branching!","The second stage, Mature Branching, required the formation of nine complete branches, creating what was called...a Full Conceptual Tree!","This was where most Honored Living Existences found themselves, having achieved enough branches to gain resistances in multiple areas while forging their own unique interpretations of their central truth.","The third and most rarified stage was Perfect Branching, achieved when a being successfully created 27-81 branches...a Complete Branching Tower that could then be transformed through transcendent effort into something even greater- a Fold Garden.","A pocket dimension where their understanding of their central concept could be given physical form and used to nurture growth that transcended everything else.","The Branching Ascendancy Realm! Initial Branching, Mature Branching, Complete Branching!","The Honored Living Origin before him clearly possessed a Mature Branching Tower, her mastery evident in the way 9 branches spread from her central trunk in patterns that resembled a glorious Tree of Existence!"]},{"number":3988,"title":"Chapter 3988: Chapter 3987: The Blade of a Shore! III","paragraphs":["Each branch pulsed with its own variation of Origin...Origin of Brilliance, Origin of Protection, Origin of Purification, Origin of Judgment...multiple interpretations that allowed her to express her fundamental nature through whatever lens the situation required!","Her Origin was bright and undeniable, waves of accumulated Resistances flowing from her form like armor woven from compressed possibility.","She possessed her own designed Absolute Resistance, the ultimate defense that came from perfect understanding of her central concept.","Yet when she moved to impose her definition of Origin upon the Dead Existence before her, the creature’s response was both simple and devastating!","The skeletal orangutan made a single motion...a gesture of negation so pure and fundamental that it seemed to deny the very concept of beginning.","As its bony hand moved through space, a dried tower filled with death flashed behind its form, the structure appearing like a diseased mockery of everything the Living Origin represented.","This tower of ending was composed of branches as well, but where hers celebrated life and possibility, its extensions spoke only to different methods of termination.","Branch of Slow Death, Branch of Instant Dissolution, Branch of Existential Erasure...countless variations on the theme of ending that challenged every assumption about growth and advancement!","The collision between these opposing concepts sent shockwaves through the surrounding space as Origin met its antithesis in head-on confrontation.","For a moment that stretched across heartbeats, the two forces remained locked in perfect balance, neither able to gain advantage over the other.","Then the Dead Existence’s curse-enhanced power began to assert itself, its fundamental advantage over Living Existential Authority becoming apparent as the tower of endings slowly but inexorably began to negate the brilliant tree of Origin that sought to impose itself upon reality!","The expression of the Honored Living Origin changed drastically as she witnessed her perfect mastery being systematically unraveled by forces that operated according to principles she could not fully comprehend.","\"YAA!\"","She bellowed with desperate fury, her Origin expressing itself with all the glory she could muster, light erupting from her form in waves that should have been sufficient to obliterate entire Wheels of Existence!","HUUM!","Yet even this magnificent display proved insufficient against the cursed nature of her opponent.","In the next moment, multiple other Living Origins materialized near her position with movements that spoke to desperate coordination rather than planned strategy.","They recognized what she faced, understood the fundamental disadvantage that any single Living Existence confronted when opposed by the cursed power of the Dead.","Only when a total of ten Honored Living Origins had positioned themselves around the skeletal creature, their combined authority layering their purpose and their undeniable beginnings into a symphony of existence affirmed, were they able to begin pushing the Dead Existence back and overwhelming its darkness!","Ten against one. Ten beings whose power could have conquered entire Wheels with a thought, required to face a single enemy whose very nature challenged their right to exist.","The wonders of this conflict were staggering and terrifying in their implications!","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as his enhanced vision captured similar scenes occurring throughout the vast battlefield. In the distance, he observed Living Laws circling a single Dead Existence like predators attempting to bring down prey far larger than themselves, their combined efforts barely sufficient to begin cutting across the deathly authority that surrounded their target.","Cutting across something cursed to be endlessly tormented with endless death required tremendous amounts of Origin, Law, Spirit, Paradox, or the other terrifying Living Weavings of Existence!","Each wound inflicted healed almost immediately, each binding imposed was countered by the fundamental nature of beings that existed in states of perpetual ending.","It was at this moment of tactical assessment that Noah felt the time had come for his own forces to join the fray.","His own...singular force.","He turned toward Moiraine with eyes that blazed with tyrannical anticipation, his voice carrying across the space between them with crystalline clarity.","\"My dear Moiraine,\" he said with casual confidence, \"let loose!\"","HUUM!","The effect of his words was immediate and profound.","Moiraine’s visage began to shine with brilliant radiance as the allure of Paradox flared outward from her position like waves of compressed impossibility.","The sight was both beautiful and unsettling!","Many Living Existences in the surrounding area sensed the distinctive signature of Paradoxical Authority and turned their attention toward her with expressions that ranged from distaste to open hostility.","Her clear origination from the region where Duke Gwendolyn floated in grandly observational authority provided some measure of protection, but it was evident that most observers regarded this display with emotions that fell far short of approval.","The hatred that Living Existences held for anything connected to Paradox ran deeper than personal preference or tactical assessment...it was fundamental loathing born from eons of suffering consequences that stemmed from Paradoxical interference in the natural order.","But Moiraine paid no attention to these hostile gazes as her body flashed.","Her target was a massive humanoid titan among the Dead Existences, its form composed of what appeared to be crystallized endings given shape and malevolent purpose.","The creature’s head remained raised toward skies that held no stars, its mouth pulsing with rhythms that spoke to absorption rather than communication.","It drew in all surrounding weavings of existence like a void given consciousness, its very presence creating dead zones where the fundamental forces that governed reality simply ceased to function.","Now, when any single Living Existence moved to face a Dead Existence in direct confrontation, protocol...so far at least, demanded that others nearby would immediately join them to ensure the numbers reached at least ten.","This was not cowardice but practical necessity...the requirements for victory against cursed opponents demanded overwhelming force applied with perfect coordination.","Yet as Moiraine charged forth alone, her aura of Paradox blazing with unmistakable clarity...nobody joined her advance.","Nobody!","Living Origins floated nearby and watched with cold indifference, their expressions suggesting they were observing a particularly unpleasant form of entertainment rather than witnessing a potential ally in mortal peril.","Others actively chose to assist Living Origins at distant positions who already had groups of three or four supporters, deliberately avoiding the opportunity to provide aid to the solitary Paradox who had dared to engage in combat within their vicinity.","Out of all the Living Existences present in the immediate area, only Moiraine...the Living Paradox whose very nature was an affront to their sensibilities...was about to face a Dead Existence entirely alone!"]},{"number":3989,"title":"Chapter 3989: Chapter 3988: The Blade of a Shore! IV","paragraphs":["Her body radiated no obvious waves of terrifying power, no manifestations of authority that would have warned observers they were witnessing something beyond normal capability.","Her identity as a Paradox was clear and unmistakable, yet this revelation carried negative rather than positive implications for those who observed her advance.","Even though she moved without support, even though she faced odds that should have resulted in immediate annihilation, her voice rang out with declarations that spoke to certainty rather than desperation.","\"I am mighty!\" she voiced with grand authority that made the surrounding temporal streams flow faster in recognition of truth being proclaimed.","HUUM!","The words carried weight that transcended their simple meaning, each syllable backed by power that had been earned through sacrifice and transformation!","Even though she approached her target alone, even though common sense demanded she wait for support that would never come, she continued her declarations with growing intensity.","\"I am his blade!\" she said, her voice taking on notes of devotion that spoke to loyalty beyond the reach of doubt or fear.","The statement was personal...she was not merely a weapon to be wielded. She was the manifestation of someone’s will given form and directed purpose!","Even though isolation marked her as abandoned by those who should have stood beside her, even though the hostile gazes of her supposed allies promised only contempt for whatever fate awaited her, she completed her proclamation with words that rang across the battlefield like a law being established.","\"I am his Arch. I am...MOIRAINE!\"","WAA!","The declaration erupted from her with such force that reality itself seemed to take notice, temporal rivers shifting their flow to accommodate her!","At such words, she moved to face the Dead Existence head-on in a scene that nearby Living Existences observed with expressions of cold satisfaction.","They did not see any flash of a Branching Tower rising behind her to provide support and tactical advantage.","They witnessed no manifestation of the normal seas of Paradoxical Authority that characterized how Paradoxes typically expressed their power in combat situations.","They saw only Moiraine approaching the massive Dead Existence with casual confidence, her small hand beginning to swipe downward toward the enormous bony fist that the creature raised to crush her out of existence.","The contrast in scale was almost comical...a relatively small figure moving to intercept a blow that could have shattered mountains, her delicate hand positioned to meet bone that radiated deathly authority capable of unmaking entire civilizations.","\"Dumbshit Paradox,\" a distant voice belonging to a Living Spirit echoed across the battlefield, the words carrying the particular contempt reserved for beings whose stupidity exceeded all reasonable bounds.","\"Who does she think she is to fight among us?\" The voice of a Living Elemental joined the chorus of derision, hatred dripping from each syllable like acid eating through hope itself.","\"Best to die early,\" came the most damning assessment of all, delivered by a Living Origin from the very armies that served under Duke Gwendolyn’s command. \"Maybe a decent Inevitability or Living Collapse will arise from her death that isn’t completely imbecillic.\"","...!","The sentiment was shared by many present...Paradoxes were not merely disliked...they were actively despised by other Living Existences, their very existence seen as a contributing factor to the endless proliferation of Inevitabilities that made progress toward the Loom so achingly difficult.","Years of conflicts and accumulated resentment had crystallized into hatred so pure it transcended rational assessment, becoming an emotional constant that influenced every interaction between Paradoxes and other Living Existences!","So at this moment, none cared for Moiraine’s welfare, and many actively hoped for her swift death. Perhaps from her ending would arise more useful forms of chaos, Inevitabilities that would serve some greater purpose rather than representing yet another example of Paradoxical incompetence.","This was the universal sentiment that greeted her desperate charge...not support or encouragement, and instead anticipation of failure and death delivered with the casual cruelty of beings who had long since ceased to view Paradoxes as worthy of basic consideration!","Noah gazed at all these reactions with eyes that buzzed with tyrannical coldness, his enhanced perception taking in every hostile expression, every dismissive comment, every casual wish for his chosen companion’s destruction.","Yet he only stared coldly and remained silent, offering no defense or explanation for what was about to unfold.","Sometimes, one did not need to speak.","Sometimes, results spoke far more eloquently than any words ever could.","As Moiraine’s fair hand came down upon the massive rising fist of the Dead Existence, something extraordinary occurred that challenged every assumption the observers had made about her capabilities and limitations.","A seemingly simple Glyph flashed briefly on her palm...just for an instant, barely visible even to enhanced perception.","That was all. No large outburst of authority, no wild manifestation of Paradoxical energy, no desperate surge of Living Existential Authority seeking to overwhelm superior opposition through sheer volume of power.","Just a flash of something that most observers couldn’t even identify, a brief illumination that passed so quickly it might have been imagination.","And yet...","CRACK!","The massive thrown fist of the Dead Existence, wrapped in obsidian waves of death that should have been sufficient to unmake anything they touched, shockingly shattered like glass meeting diamond!","Not just damaged or deflected...completely destroyed, the entire appendage dissolving into fragments that scattered across dimensions like ash on stellar winds.","...!","The result defied every law of probability and power that governed such conflicts!","Why would such an outcome surprise anyone who truly understood what had just occurred?","As a Paradox, Moiraine was not affected by the Curse that enhanced Dead Existences beyond normal parameters, her very nature providing immunity to the fundamental advantage that made such creatures so devastatingly effective against other types of Living Existence.","More importantly, she had not relied upon Living Existential Authority in her attack...instead, she had employed an Early Living Existential Glyph, a tool and expression of power that was normally utilized exclusively by Early Creatures themselves.","And not just any Glyph, but a Kleos Glyph...the ultimate expression of power that transcended every normal category of capability.","And not merely any Kleos Glyph, instead one whose nature was grander still...the Kleos Glyph of Paradoxical Genesis!","Paradoxical Genesis...the authority to create beginning from paradox, to forge possibility from impossibility, to establish new existences through the simple act of refusing to acknowledge that such existences should be impossible!","In the next moment, a level of brutality unfolded that left even the confused Dead Existence struggling to process what was occurring to its carefully maintained form of crystallized ending.","Moiraine’s body flashed to multiple positions around her target with movements that transcended normal limitations of space and time.","Without apparent cost of energy or authority, she activated her Kleos Glyphs simultaneously, each one blazing with power that made reality convulse!","The meaning of Paradoxical Genesis asserted itself against the seemingly undeniable weavings of Death that comprised the Dead Existence’s core nature. Where the creature represented ending made manifest, Moiraine imposed the concept of beginning renewed... the transformation of conclusion into commencement through methods that defied rational comprehension.","The Dead Existence’s body began to shatter and compress under this assault, its deathly Existential Authority being systematically smashed and decimated in a manner that no other Living Existence present had been capable of achieving!","The cursed enhancements that made such creatures nearly invulnerable proved useless against power that operated according to principles the Curse was in tune with!","In a single second that contained within it the compressed essence of perfect violence, Moiraine used her hands...flashing with Glyphs that remained invisible to normal perception, to brutally tear apart the Dead Existence with her own physical strength.","She moved like a primal archaic creature unleashed upon prey that had never learned to fear predators of her magnitude, her actions speaking to savagery that had been refined into perfect efficiency through understanding rather than mere instinct!","\"OOOH!\" she yelled as she completed her work, waving her hand in a gesture that caused the entire corpse of the Dead Existence to vanish into dimensional storage where it could be properly processed and utilized.","...!","The event was utterly shocking to witness...a single Paradox accomplishing what should have required ten coordinated Living Existences, doing so with such casual efficiency that the entire confrontation lasted less than the time required to draw breath.","Moiraine looked up from her completed task and gazed at all the Living Existences who had observed her advance with such cold indifference, who had actively wished for her death rather than offering support that could have prevented potential tragedy.","For them, she had only two words that carried the full weight of her contempt for their cowardice and prejudice.","\"Fucking trash.\"","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":3990,"title":"Chapter 3990: Chapter 3989: Let it be a festival! I","paragraphs":["Fucking trash!","The assessment was delivered with such casual precision that it struck those who heard it like a whip!","And none truly had a viable reply against it because they had truly acted like trash!","Then, Moiraine turned her attention toward the broader battlefield where Dead Existences continued their systematic assault upon the forces of the Living.","At this moment, multiple creatures that had been engaged with other opponents suddenly disengaged from their current battles and began moving toward her position with the focused attention of predators recognizing a threat that required immediate elimination.","The sight of Dead Existences abandoning positions to converge upon a single target sent waves of shock through the Living Existences who had witnessed her impossible victory.","They struggled to process what she bad done. Could they truly be sensing the authority of an Honored Living Paradox!? How had she managed to accomplish what even coordinated groups of their number found challenging?","Off to the side, Duke Gwendolyn watched this entire sequence unfold with eyes that shone with blazing interest.","Her other body...the one that operated as a veiled Paradox, had not yet made any moves in the broader battle, but she found herself compelled to observe Moiraine!","She turned toward Noah with her ancient gaze, her voice echoing out.","|Is she really just an Honored Living Paradox?|, came the carefully phrased question.","Noah gazed at her with eyes that remained calm and cold, his mental response delivered with tyranny.","|What else could she be?| he replied, the mental equivalent of a shrug accompanying words that dismissed her inquiry as fundamentally irrelevant to larger concerns.","The simplicity of his response, combined with the evidence they had all just witnessed, left Duke Gwendolyn with far more questions than answers about the true nature of the beings she had agreed to work alongside!","Yet as Dead Existences began converging on Moiraine’s position with focused attention, all such considerations became secondary to the immediate situation unfolding before them.","Noah observed everything with crystal clarity, his perception processing the vast scope of conflict that unfolded across light-years of twisted space-time.","He knew, that in this grand battle between Life and Death, the direct effect he could have through personal intervention was minimal!","His accumulated power, impressive though it was by the standards of most Living Existences, would not be sufficient to eliminate even a single Dead Existence. Each of these cursed entities operated at the Honored level of capability, their advantages making them nearly invulnerable to attacks of even normap Honored Living Existences.","More critically, if he positioned himself close enough to directly engage any Dead Existence that might target him, Yoshinami’s Crown of Inevitable Retribution would activate with devastating precision!","The protective artifact would deliver True Death to any attacker whose power fell below that of an Early Creature or one wielding a Lost Forgotten Principle...conditions that would waste its precious single daily usage on enemies that could be eliminated through easier means.","In a conflict of this magnitude, such waste would be tantamount to suicide.","So in this terrifying battle that would determine the fate of fundamental forces across existence itself, he would have to approach victory through methods that transcended brute force application of personal power.","He already had an idea forming in the depths of his consciousness, a strategy that would leverage his unique capabilities in ways that others could never hope to replicate.","His gaze settled upon Moiraine’s figure as multiple Honored Dead Existences began converging on her position with the focused attention of predators. The creatures moved with eerie coordination, their heads still raised toward skies that held no stars, yet their direction clearly oriented toward the Living Paradox who had dared to destroy one of their number through methods they could not fully comprehend.","Across the broader battlefield, similar scenes unfolded. Dead Existences radiated terrifying power as they engaged the forces of the Living, their cursed weavings allowing them to systematically overwhelm opponents who should have possessed superior numbers.","Casualties had begun to occur among the Living Existences with shocking frequency, particularly when two or three Dead Existences managed to surround smaller groups of defenders. The weavings of such encounters were unforgiving...even coordinated teams of ten Honored Living Existences found themselves struggling.","Yet the Living Existences maintained numerical superiority through careful deployment and strategic reserves. When one fell, two more immediately took their place, their formations flowing like liquid around points of resistance with the fluid grace of forces that had been drilling such maneuvers across eons of preparation.","Meanwhile, the massive tear in space-time remained stable in its current configuration, no additional Dead Existences emerging from thr domain where ending reigned supreme. The number of enemies they faced was finite, limited by whatever constraints governed travel between the domains of Life and Death.","If the current rate of attrition continued, the Dead Existences would eventually be eliminated! But the cost would be tremendously high!","Duke Gwendolyn and the other Dukes who commanded this unprecedented coalition seemed to understand this grim weaving perfectly, their expressions growing heavier with each passing moment as they witnessed the price that victory would demand.","It was such a dreadful reality!","Noah smiled behind his concealing helm as he contemplated this situation, his thoughts turning towards his own weavings.","’Don’t worry,’ he mused with the kind of benevolent arrogance, ’Since I am so magnanimous, I will make this easy for all of you!’","HUUM!","The moment this thought crystallized into decision, Noah closed his eyes and reached inward toward the architectural wonders that existed within the depths of his own being.","He called upon the more than one hundred and fifty Towers of Osmont that rose like monuments to impossible achievement from the foundation of his early Atlas, each one blazing with accumulated authority that had been refined through methods that predated current existence!","Memory stirred as he recalled the previous occasion when multiple towers had sung Hymns, their combined weavings acting to emulate the presence of multiple Early Creatures gathered for common purpose.","Such convergence had triggered the Festival of Existence that had covered the Nullvein Gravewake Folds with its transformative influence...effects that continued to express themselves even now!"]},{"number":3991,"title":"Chapter 3991: Chapter 3990: Let it be a festival! II","paragraphs":["That original festival had been born from basic Towers of Origin, primitive structures that had served their purpose before being systematically replaced with something infinitely grander.","In their place, he had forged the Towers of Osmont...monuments to advancement that were supported by Early Sacred Living Eidolons, massive glorious statues that provided foundations capable of channeling forces that normal towers could never hope to accommodate!","What would happen when these vastly superior structures began singing their hymns? Would the result still be classified as a mere Festival of Existence, or would the grandeur of his upgraded towers produce something that transcended every previous category?","\"...\"","He already knew the answer, and the musings filled him with anticipation that bordered on euphoria.","He thought about it once more as he would make a move that would forever change many things. And he found that even after all the caution, his decision remained the same!","Noah smiled internally as he turned his attention toward a particular aspect of his existence, one that preferred to observe silently while plotting and planning, emerging only when circumstances absolutely necessitated grand gestures that could reshape the nature of whatever situation demanded attention.","\"Why don’t you wake up, buddy?\" he said, his words directed toward the personified concept that had always represented his most outrageous capabilities.","He was, of course, addressing Cheats...the force within his existence that had consistently delivered results that defied every rational expectation about what should be possible.","Inside the architectural marvel that comprised his inner existence, where the Early Atlas stretched toward completion like a map of infinite possibility, the very concept of Cheats blazed with brilliance that made Existence take notice!","The Early Sacred Living Cheats Tower of Osmont shone with radiance, its crystalline surfaces reflecting not light but pure potential given form and purpose.","The structure rose from foundations that existed in multiple dimensions simultaneously, each level representing a different aspect of what it meant to achieve the impossible through methods that challenged every assumption about limitation and consequence!","Above this manifested tower, visible only to Noah’s enhanced inner perception, sat the personified concept of Cheats itself...a figure that embodied everything he had ever achieved through audacious application of principles that others deemed impossible.","The entity possessed an appearance that seemed to shift between different interpretations of what ultimate capability should look like, sometimes appearing as a masterful conductor preparing to direct a symphony of glory, other times manifesting as an architect!","At this moment, as Noah’s request reached the depths of where this concept dwelt, the figure began to make grand movements with solemnity.","|Cheats has proceeded to commandeer sufficient nutrients from the devoured body of the compressed Inevitability to secure advancement and thorough standing to the Second Stage of its Tower of Osmont.|","|Cheats has initiated the Symphony of Hymns of the Early Sacred Living Eidolons encompassing all Towers of Osmont. Direction protocols have been established with clear purpose- harmonic flow shall not emanate from primary source but will instead permeate from the selected target designated as Arch Living Existence Moiraine. Redirection complete. Symphony preparation finalized.|","...!","HUUM!","The moment these processes reached completion, Moiraine’s body began to buzz with frequencies that transcended normal understanding of sound or vibration.","A cacophony of glorious symphony began to resound from her form....not chaotic noise, and instead perfectly orchestrated harmony!","The music that emanated from her position was both beautiful and terrifying, each note carrying within it the compressed essence of authority that had been refined across eons of impossible advancement- archaic and tribal!","Yet the true wonder was occurring within Noah’s existence, where architectural marvels that would have required dozens of Early Creatures working in coordination began to resonate with each other in patterns that had not been witnessed since the Earliest Folds.","The Dead Existences that were charging toward Moiraine’s position suddenly felt the sensation of something foreign intruding upon their carefully maintained states of endless torment!","For the first time since their emergence from realms of ending, they actually paused in their advance.","More shocking still, their heads...which had remained raised toward non-existent skies in perpetual absorption of surrounding existence, slowly turned downward to truly look at the source of these impossible harmonies.","They gazed upon Moiraine with what might have been recognition, as if some buried aspect of their cursed consciousness remembered when such music had last been heard across the breadth of existence.","The Living Existences nearby also stopped their desperate maneuvers, shock flooding through their enhanced perceptions as they felt glorious hymns resounding through the very fabric of reality!","The music carried within it effects that could influence their own quantified Weavings of Existence.","Noah smiled within his concealing armament, satisfaction flooding through his consciousness as he witnessed the first stages of his strategy unfold according to design.","\"Let it be a festival,\" he murmured to himself with the quiet confidence of someone who had calculated every variable and found them acceptable.","\"Let it be glorious. Let it be that even though I do not currently possess the raw power to participate directly in this conflict...my glory will still shine the brightest on this battlefield!\"","HUUM!","The moment those words finished forming in his consciousness, reality itself began to respond to the unprecedented convergence of forces that he had orchestrated.","|A glorious Festival of War is blooming under your direction!|","...!","A festival!","But it was not of Existence...it was a Festival of War!","|Early Festivals of War were legendary gatherings that occurred when multiple powerful Early Creatures converged to begin their great hunts across the countless Folds and everything that existed between them. These festivals represented the ultimate expression of coordinated Early Creature might, events that unleashed their already shocking power to even greater limits through harmonic resonance that challenged the fundamental nature of limitation itself. The last Festival of War in recorded history was forcibly ended when THE Living Law made a decisive move using something that could systematically decimate the power of Early Creatures, bringing the age of unfettered Early Creature dominion to its conclusion through methods that remain entirely unknown.|","...!"]},{"number":3992,"title":"Chapter 3992: Chapter 3991: Let it be a festival! III","paragraphs":["|A unique Early Festival of War has been triggered through the guiding hands of Cheats, modified with unprecedented parameters that reflect the singular nature of its orchestrator. The range of this festival will affect the immediate region of conflict where it first blooms, encompassing all entities contained within designated boundaries.|","|Festival Modification: The Blessing of the Perfidious Glyph will be applied to all qualifying existences within the affected region. This blessing grants the extraordinary ability for complexity and purity of affected targets to express their accumulated power through Perfidious Glyphs...constructs that imitate a fraction of the fundamental authority wielded by Early Creatures themselves.|","|Additional Enhancement: Under the guiding influence of Cheats and thr shake down from Loot, any entities eliminated through power enhanced by this festival will have 1% of their total existence automatically siphoned as loot and passively granted to the being who ushered in the festival. Furthermore, the rate, usage, and expression of Living Existential Authority for all affected beings will be amplified by 500%, creating combat capabilities that transcend normal limitations.|","...!","Oh!","Oh!!!","A terrifying blessing that masqueraded as beneficent assistance...the kind of gift that promised transcendencs while simultaneously ensuring that the true beneficiary would be the one who had orchestrated its manifestation!","At this moment, glorious symphonies of hymns echoed outward from Moiraine’s position with the inexorable force of existential law being established.","The glorious symphony permeated across the surrounding region, touching every consciousness capable of perceiving their magnificence!","Every Living Existence who heard these symphonic wonders found themselves marked by an illusory sigil that materialized above their heads...two golden swords crossing in patterns.","The moment such markings appeared, the affected beings felt their existence buzz with terrifying power that challenged every assumption they held about their own capabilities and limitations!","Those who had been struggling desperately against Dead Existences suddenly felt their accumulated authority converging into singular expressions of force that they did not fully understand yet instinctively knew how to wield.","Only Noah possessed sufficient knowledge to truly observe what was occurring as his enhanced perception catalogued the flashing of Perfidious Glyphs that proceeded to strike Dead Existences with unprecedented effectiveness.","For the first time since the battle had begun, the cursed creatures showed signs of genuine damage rather than merely temporary inconvenience. Their forms convulsed as authority that imitated Early Creature power tore through defenses that had been designed to withstand Living Existential Authority.","Noah smiled brilliantly at this vindication of his strategic approach, satisfaction flooding through his consciousness like liquid starlight.","Many eyes turned toward Moiraine in shock as the impossible harmony continued to resound from her position, yet she kept her head straight and her focus clear.","Though she understood that this phenomenon was not of her own creation, that it stemmed from his unfathomable capabilities, she simply proceeded forward toward the Dead Existences that now regarded her with something approaching solemnity.","’O Sir.’","...!","Even though she faced ahead, her voice echoed out in Noah’s mind!","’I know not why you chose me for this position, but I will thank you in...my own way after this is done, Sir.’","...!","Her words were explosive as her ’Sirs’ could drive lesser men to have weak legs!","Noah kept a straight face as he only smiled and hummed, thinking how much bolder and freer Moiraine was becoming from how she acted after she found out he was an Early Creature.","He refocused on the Dead Existences as other matters came later!","The cursed creatures no longer moved with the casual confidence that had marked their earlier advances. Instead, they approached with the careful attention of beings who recognized they faced something powerful.","Above Duke Gwendolyn’s position, the blessing manifested as well, her ancient consciousness reacting with surprise as she felt her own carefully controlled existence respond to influences that were foreign.","She looked toward both Moiraine and Noah with an unfathomable glow burning within her eyes, recognition beginning to dawn that she was witnessing something...else.","And her focus...came to be more on Moiraine than Noah at this moment. And why the hell not when her body boomed with a terrific symphony?!","The pace of the entire battle had shifted with shocking suddenness as glorious symphonies echoed across the battlefield and every Living Existence in the affected region gained blessings that elevated their capabilities far beyond normal limitations.","This enhancement extended even to the Dukes who were actively engaging the terrifying Primordial Death...the massive skeletal entity whose power had required multiple Duke-level beings working in perfect coordination merely to withstand its assaults.","Throughout all of this unprecedented transformation, Noah’s figure remained nonchalant in the center of the chaos he had orchestrated.","Despite having just executed a maneuver that entirely changed the pace of the battle and would determine how its results unfolded, despite establishing himself as the beneficiary of every enemy eliminated through enhanced power...he maintained the appearance of casual observation rather than active participation.","There were many ways that one could influence the outcome of a war, but the method Noah had chosen was one that could not be replicated!","So he floated grandly above the transformed battlefield, seemingly making no moves yet actually serving as one of its most critical commanders.","His hands clasped behind his back in a pose of imperial observation, he gazed upon the uniquely unfolding conflict with the satisfaction of someone whose vision had been perfectly implemented.","He had to do this as the aura of the Protagonist had to shine brightly even while he simply observed!","The symphony continued to build toward crescendos that promised even greater revelations, while golden markers above countless heads blazed with authority that transformed desperate struggle into systematic superiority.","In the distance, Dead Existences began to fall with increasing frequency as enhanced Living Existences discovered that their elevated capabilities could actually inflict permanent damage upon enemies that had previously seemed invulnerable!","And with each elimination, each systematic destruction of cursed entities that had dared to emerge from realms of ending...","|A piece of the bone of an Honored Dead Existence has been obtained and funneled to the Early Veiled Shore for classification and quantification.|","|The occipital bone of an Honored Dead Existence has been obtained and funneled to the Early Veiled Shore for classification and quantification.|","|A piece of the vile heart of an Honored Dead Existence filled with an unknown curse has been obtained and funneled to the Early Veiled Shore for classification and quantification.|","...!","Prompts began to roll it one after another as Noah’s eyes blazed with tyranny!","Yes.","Move more.","Work more!","Grant him even more glory!","The festival was just beginning, and already its effects promised to echo across eons of consequence yet to unfold!"]},{"number":3993,"title":"Chapter 3993: Chapter 3992: Deterioration! I","paragraphs":["The battle erupted with newfound intensity as the Symphony echoing outward from Moiraine’s position seemingly energized every Living Existence within its range!","The golden markers above their heads blazed with authority that transformed desperation into determination, while their enhanced existence flowed through their beings.","They swarmed toward the Dead Existences with fervor that bordered on religious ecstasy!","At the center of this transformation, Moiraine herself proceeded to face five oncoming Dead Existences with calm confidence.","The creatures approached her position with the eerie synchronization that marked their cursed nature, their forms radiating deathly authority that should have been sufficient to overwhelm any individual opponent!","Each Dead Existence possessed the accumulated power of Honored-level capability enhanced by tge curse that elevated them far beyond normal limitation, their very presence creating zones where the forces of life simply ceased to function.","Yet Moiraine moved toward them without hesitation, her hands beginning to flash with barely visible illumination!","Her first target was a humanoid creature whose skeleton seemed to be composed of crystallized endings, each bone pulsing with the rhythm of entropy itself.","As it raised massive arms to crush her out of existence, Moiraine’s delicate hand intercepted the descending limb calmly.","The moment her flesh made contact with cursed bone, a Kleos Glyph flashed across her palm...invisible to normal perception yet radiating authority that made reality itself take notice. The creature’s arm unraveled at a fundamental level, its very essence being rewritten!","Before the first Dead Existence could even process what was occurring to its carefully maintained form, Moiraine had already moved to engage the second. This entity appeared as a writhing mass of void given shape, its presence creating tears in space-time through which glimpses of realms of absolute nothingness could be observed.","Her response was to plunge both hands directly into its core, her fingers blazing with the invisible authority of Paradoxical Genesis!","Where the creature represented absence made manifest, she imposed the concept of presence renewed... the transformation of void into substance through methods that defied rational comprehension. It was paradoxical...and filled with purpose!","The Dead Existence convulsed as its fundamental nature was systematically inverted, void becoming solid, absence transforming into overwhelming presence that challenged every assumption about what such creatures could experience.","The remaining three Dead Existences converged upon her position simultaneously, their coordinated assault creating overlapping fields of deathly influence that should have been sufficient to unmake anything caught within their confluence.","Moiraine’s response was to laugh with genuine joy as she leaped into the center of their formation, her form becoming a blur of motion that left afterimages trailing through different spatial dimensions, her hands striking out as Kleos Glyphs flashe!","Each movement of her hands left devastating impacts upon her opponents, Kleos Glyphs flashing in patterns too complex for normal perception to follow as she systematically dismantled entities whose power had been refined through eons of cursed existence!","She moved like a primal creature unleashed upon prey that had never learned to fear predators of her magnitude, her actions showing savagery that had been elevated to the level of perfect art.","Within moments, all five Dead Existences lay in pieces around her position, their forms reduced to component elements that disappeared into her bodt right after!","Her brutal efficiency in eliminating opponents that required coordinated teams to handle had captured attention from across the battlefield, shock and recognition flowing through the consciousness of every observer who witnessed her impossible victories.","In the next few seconds, one Living Existence after another began to materialize near her position as she prepared to charge toward additional targets.","They maintained careful distances...close enough to provide support, far enough to avoid interfering with her devastating effectiveness.","Now they began to fucking show up!","Two Honored Living Temporals appeared first, their forms wreathed in purple-blue authority that bent causality around their presence.","They moved to intercept Dead Existences that were attempting to flank Moiraine’s position, their temporal manipulations creating zones where the cursed creatures found themselves trapped in loops of consequence that prevented effective retaliation.","Living Origins followed, their brilliant radiance creating barriers of compressed existence!","Living Spirits materialized as ethereal forms, while Living Concepts imposed abstract limitations that confused!","Living Laws arrived, their presence establishing zones where the chaotic nature of Dead Existence authority was forced to operate according to comprehensible rules rather than the arbitrary principles that governed realms of ending.","Undoubtedly, even though none of these Living Existences spoke directly to Moiraine, even though their previous interactions had been marked by hostility and dismissal, they now positioned themselves behind her with the coordination of beings who understood exactly what was at stake.","They recognized that the Symphony empowering them all emanated from her position, that her survival was directly linked to their enhanced capabilities. She could not be permitted to die, regardless of their personal feelings about Paradoxes in general or her specific identity in particular!","Noah observed all of this transformation with cold analytical eyes, his perception observing every shift in positioning while his consciousness processed everything.","How easily beings could cast aside hatred when survival and treasure hung in the balance, he mused with a kind of cynical amusement.","Prejudice became secondary to practical necessity when the alternative was systematic elimination by forces that recognized no distinction between different types of Living Existence.","Self-interest, it seemed, remained the most reliable constant across all forms of conscious behavior!","Even as he observed these dynamics unfolding, his attention remained partially focused on the cascade of information that continued to flow across his consciousness through channels that connected him to the Early Veiled Shore.","The prompts became even more detailed as he began to obtain more pieces of Dead Existences!","|Fragment of Dead Existence Cranium obtained. Estimated composition: 47% Crystallized Ending, 31% Compressed Deathly Authority, 22% Cursed Bone Essence. This specimen has been automatically transferred to the Early Veiled Shore for analysis and potential cultivation. Unique properties detected: Contains fragments of memories from the realm of absolute conclusion.|","|Segment of Dead Existence Ribcage acquired. Analysis indicates: 52% Ossified Entropy, 29% Concentrated Void Essence, 19% Temporal Decay Fragments. Transfer to Early Veiled Shore completed. Special notation: Ribcage segments retain echoes of the last breaths drawn by beings consumed during the creature’s cursed existence.|","|Complete Dead Existence Hand harvested. Composition breakdown...|","The prompts came and came!","The accumulation of such materials represented resources that could be utilized for advancement in ways that others could never hope to replicate.","As Noah processed these acquisitions while simultaneously observing the situation unfolding around Moiraine’s position, his eyes flickered with recognition of something that demanded immediate attention.","He turned toward Duke Gwendolyn, his consciousness reaching out to deliver a warning.","|You may want your other body to make a move now,| he conveyed.","A moment later, reality itself seemed to convulse as the distant figure of the Primordial Death...the massive skeletal entity whose power had required multiple Dukes to merely withstand, suddenly employed the concept of endings in a manner that challenged every assumption about distance and proximity.","The creature didn’t move in any conventional sense. Instead, it ended the distance between its current position and Moiraine’s location, instantly manifesting directly in front of her and the Living Existences who had gathered to support her advance!","The transition was so abrupt, so fundamentally wrong in its violation of spatial limitations, that reality itself seemed to recoil from acknowledging what had occurred.","One moment the Primordial Death had been engaged with Dukes across light-years of battlefield; the next, it loomed over Moiraine with obsidian bones radiating authority that could unmake entire Wheels through casual gesture!"]},{"number":3994,"title":"Chapter 3994: Chapter 3993: Deterioration! II","paragraphs":["It seemed as though immense calamity would descend upon the forces that had gathered around the source of their enhancement, that the being responsible for their empowerment would be eliminated before their eyes through methods they possessed no capability to prevent or counter!","But in the next moment, two figures moved with synchronized precision.","The veiled Paradoxical body of Duke Gwendolyn materialized beside the Primordial Death with movements that challenged causality itself, her obsidian armor blazing with authority that made space-time bend around her presence.","Simultaneously, her Living Origin body appeared on the opposite side of the massive creature, brilliant radiance erupting from her form in waves that should have been sufficient to illuminate entire Folds!","Duke Gwendolyn’s philosophical approach to this crisis demonstrated mastery of how opposing forces could be reconciled through will and wisdom.","Her Paradoxical aspect reached out to rewind an inevitable ending...not preventing the Primordial Death’s arrival, but creating a state where its presence existed in quantum superposition between having occurred and remaining theoretical possibility.","At the same moment, her Origin body worked to establish the previous state of existence that had existed before the creature’s arrival, imposing the concept of restoration!","The collision between these opposing interpretations of what should be considered real created a zone of fundamental uncertainty that even the Primordial Death found difficult to navigate.","Its cursed authority, designed to operate within weavings where ending was the only constant, struggled to function effectively in space where beginning and conclusion existed simultaneously.","Under the enhanced capabilities granted by Noah’s Festival of War, Duke Gwendolyn’s combined efforts proved sufficient to push back the Primordial Death, forcing the creature to retreat from its advantageous position through application of force that should have been impossible for just two Dukes to achieve!","The sight of 2 entities...even one as formidable as a Duke, successfully repelling the massive skeletal horror sent shockwaves through every consciousness present.","Other Dukes rushed toward this position with movements that left brief tears in reality.","Their sharp gazes moved between Duke Gwendolyn and the veiled Paradoxical figure that seemed to move under her direct command, questions forming in their ancient minds.","Yet none of them voiced these concerns immediately. The current crisis demanded coordination rather than interrogation, and with the Symphony empowering all of them, they possessed a genuine opportunity to eliminate the Dead Existences entirely and seal the tear in space before additional reinforcements could arrive from realms of ending!","Information could wait until victory had been secured and the immediate threat neutralized.","Noah observed all of these developments with cool analytical detachment.","His gaze locked upon the massive distant figure of the Primordial Death as it repositioned itself following Duke Gwendolyn’s successful repulsion.","If that being attempted to eliminate him specifically and not Moiraine, Yoshinami’s Crown of Inevitable Retribution would activate with devastating precision, delivering True Death to an enemy whose power operated at the level of Dukes.","But it did not target him.","And this possibility represented one of his primary strategic objectives for participating in this conflict...the opportunity to eliminate threats that normally existed beyond his capability.","As he tracked the creature’s movements with predatory interest, his attention was simultaneously drawn to another Duke who had positioned himself near the tear in space-time.","This entity appeared as a figure wreathed in pure white radiance, his form carrying two magnificent swords that blazed with crystalline authority.","Yet another swordsman in these grand weavings of existence!","The Duke representing Living Laws raised his weapons toward the massive wound in reality, brilliant illumination gathering around his blades as he prepared to deliver a weaving that would seal the breach through application of undeniable juridical force!","His voice echoed out as seas of Living Law gushed out from his swords!","\"Immutable foundation of existential order. Unwavering pillar of absolute truth. Bind that which seeks to break. Seal that which refuses structure. Command the chaos to kneel. Iron chains of inevitability. Converge. Restrict. Embrace the weight of existential law and submit to its glorious dominion!","HUUM!","He intoned with voice that carried the weight of law being established, white light beginning to weave itself around the edges of the tear.","The incantation built toward crescendos that made reality itself respond, white light beginning to stitch the edges of the wound in space-time as undeniable law imposed itself.","The tear was about to close!","Yet just as this elaborate binding reached near completion, just as success seemed within reach through application of ultimate juridical authority...","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes pulsed with alarm as he witnessed a massive obsidian chain shoot out of the tear with speed...speed that was utterly terrifying!","The horrific chain was meant to collapse the Living Law Duke before his sealing could be completed, its surface wreathed in deathly authority that promised systematic unmaking of everything it touched. The terrifying Law barely managed to evade complete annihilation, yet even his partially successful evasion came at tremendous cost...half of his body shattered into obsidian dust upon contact with the cursed weapon, his form becoming translucent as he paled and retreated from his position near the tear.","From the breach in reality, eight more massive chains emerged with the sound of entropy being given physical form.","Behind them, pushing through the expanding wound in space-time, came something that challenged every assumption about what horrors could emerge from realms of ending.","The massive head of an obsidian entity appeared....the manifestation of absolute conclusion given the appearance of twisted innocence. It resembled a baby’s head scaled to impossible proportions, its features carrying the kind of wrongness!","The torn rift expanded even further as this abomination forced its way through, reality stretching and warping around its passage until the breach became large enough to accommodate additional horrors.","Behind the first nightmare, two more figures of Primordial Deaths began to peek through the expanded opening...entities whose power rivaled or exceeded that of the skeletal entity that had already emerged, their presence promising escalation into a catastrophe!","All Dukes who observed these developments paled with grimness. If this situation continued to deteriorate according to current patterns, they would be forced to call upon additional collective forces.","The tear absolutely had to be closed before the situation became truly unmanageable, before the breach grew large enough to accommodate the invasion of forces that devoured everything!","Yet as the assembled Dukes turned grim with recognition of approaching calamity, Noah looked upon these developments with excitement that bordered on euphoria.","This was exactly the kind of opportunity he had been positioning himself to exploit...the emergence of enemies whose power operated at levels that would trigger Yoshinami’s ultimate protection while simultaneously providing him with resources that could elevate his capabilities tremendously!","He prepared to move forward, to position himself within the line of sight of these monstrous creatures whose authority operated at the level of Dukes.","Any one of them would do!","Any one!","If they attempted to eliminate him, their death would be guaranteed!","So he moved to ensure such confrontation at this most perilous moment, anticipation flooding through his consciousness.","And yet...","One could plan and prepare for every conceivable eventuality, could calculate variables and probabilities with the precision of destiny, could position resources and capabilities with strategic perfection that accounted for every foreseeable development.","But at the end of all such preparation, through means that no amount of foresight could control or predict, things possessed an inexorable tendency to deviate from expected patterns in ways that challenged even the most comprehensive planning!","Because right after Noah began his advance toward optimal positioning...","BOOM!","Shit hit the fan."]},{"number":3995,"title":"Chapter 3995: Chapter 3994: Trembling! I","paragraphs":["The sound that erupted from above transcended normal categories of auditory experience, carrying within it the compressed essence of impossibility being given voice and direction.","Waves of powerful Paradoxes pierced through the temporal fabric of the Folds themselves, their entrance defying every weaving of Existence!","They appeared by simply deciding that they had always been present, their arrival rewriting history to accommodate their sudden manifestation!","Their grand paradoxical entrance caused all beings...Dead and Living alike, to turn their attention skyward.","At the forefront of this impossible assembly flew a figure whose presence commanded attention through sheer magnitude of accumulated authority.","It was none other than...Diviticus.","Fucking Diviticus!","Diviticus, no longer merely Honored, but elevated to the rank of Duke!","Her form blazed with brilliant white and black radiance while her fair features bore an enticing tattoo that resembled a terrifying Glyph inscribed directly into her flesh.","The marking pulsed with its own inner radiance. This was not mere decoration but the manifestation of authority that had been permanently integrated into her very essence!","Behind Duke Diviticus, the assembled might of Living Paradoxes created a display that rivaled the most magnificent conquering armies in the annals of history.","Duke Elagabalus floated with the casual arrogance that marked him as someone whose power had never been successfully challenged, his obsidian-gold hair flowing like liquid metal while his robes seemed to absorb and reflect light paradoxically.","Honored Gold maintained his position with ancient dignity.","Other terrifying Dukes of the Living Paradoxes arranged themselves in formations!","Yet silently behind all of these magnificent displays of transcendent capability stood a figure that appeared almost mundane by comparison...a man whose appearance suggested nothing more threatening than a beggar who had wandered into places far beyond his comprehension.","This was Duke Schrodinger, and his presence in the far back of their formation did nothing to diminish the profound sense of danger that radiated from his position like heat from a forge dedicated to remaking the fundamental nature of existence itself!","The moment he arrived, Noah felt his danger senses respond with intensity that bordered on panic. Diviticus did not make him feel danger. Nor did Honored Gold or any other Paradoxes. So why the fuck did he feel a sense of immense danher from that begger in the back?","At this shocking entrance of Living Paradox leadership, Diviticus stepped forward with movements that made reality convulse in recognition.","A terrifying aura eclipsing that of many Dukes erupted from her transformed form, waves of compressed impossibility smashing toward the emerging Primordial Deaths with menacing precision as she roared with voice that carried across dimensions.","\"I! DIVITICUS! HAVE! ARRIVED!\"","The declaration rang through the battlefield, each word carrying within it the compressed essence of everything she had become through methods that...others did not currently know about.","Through power that was not...entirely hers!","BOOM!","An apocalyptic impact erupted from her position, the shockwave of her presence alone proving sufficient to smash back all three Primordial Deaths that had been attempting to emerge from the expanded tear in reality.","Other Duke-level Paradoxes layered their own seas of paradoxical authority outward, creating overlapping fields of impossible force that sought to drown the creatures of ending in contradictions they could not resolve or escape.","Paradoxical Authority, as had been demonstrated again and again throughout the conflict, proved most effective against Dead Existences.","The arriving Paradoxes systematically pushed the Primordial Deaths back into the tear through application of coordinated impossibility, their combined efforts forcing entities that rivaled Dukes in power to retreat from realms where life still dared to exist.","Yet the true demonstration of transcendent capability came when the beggar-like figure from the rear of their formation appeared at the center of the tear itself.","Duke Schrodinger raised his hand with casual precision, pinching empty space between fingers that blazed with authority too subtle for normal perception to detect.","As he performed this simple gesture, his voice carried across the battlefield with the calm precision of someone delivering inevitable conclusion...in a voice that almost seemed bored!","\"Fracturing mirror of simultaneous truths. Vessel of contradictory certainties. Exist and cease in unified opposition. Collapse all possibilities into singular choice. Dancing shadows of maybe and never. Quantum throne of impossible decisions. Self-negating crown of definitive uncertainty. Merge. Contradict. Accept the wisdom of paradox and bend to my selected Existence. In the state where all possibilities exist simultaneously, I choose the one where this wound...has never been opened. So. Existence...conform to my selection.\"","...!","HUUM!","A pinch of empty space. A short incantation delivered with casual confidence.","And yet in the next moment, with speed that challenged every assumption about cause and effect...","WAP!","The tear sealed itself instantly, reality responding to paradoxical command by retroactively deciding that the wound had never existed in the first place. Space-time rearranged itself to accommodate this new interpretation of events, the massive breach simply ceasing to be!","\"...\"","The beggar-looking entity whose casual gesture had accomplished what multiple Dukes working in coordination had failed to achieve caused Noah to become unfathomably serious.","The moment Duke Schrodinger completed his reality-altering intervention, the ancient being turned with movements that seemed to compress eons of accumulated attention into a single moment of focused scrutiny.","His eyes locked onto none other than Moiraine with intensity that made the surrounding space convulse.","Not just him. Duke Elagabalus, Honored Gold, and the vibrant Duke Diviticus all turned to gaze at her with expressions that carried cold calculation mixed with profound interest.","They knew that she...was the only remaining link to Ozymandias! Someone who likely had the inheritance of an Early Creature!","At this moment, Diviticus appeared above the cold-faced skeletal Primordial Death...the only creature that remained from the original incursion, her presence casting shadows that seemed to absorb light rather than merely blocking it.","Terrifying obsidian power leaked from her transformed form as she looked around at the surrounding Living Existences, her gaze taking in the assembled might of the Coalition while her voice carried across the battlefield with the weight of declaration.","\"It seems....\" she said with calm precision that made reality itself lean in to listen more closely, \"that it is time for Living Paradoxes to also secure a seat at the table of governance across the folds.\"","She delivered these words while gazing directly at the other Living Existences who had gathered to witness this unprecedented resolution.","She spoke while looking specifically at Moiraine.","Her entrance, and the entrance of the Paradoxes as a unified force, had been nothing short of grand. They had appeared at the moment of greatest crisis and resolved the most pressing problems with efficiency!","Now, with the tear sealed and the primary threats neutralized, all that remained was cleanup of the remaining Dead Existences, and yet it seemed like things had gotten even messier!"]},{"number":3996,"title":"Chapter 3996: Chapter 3995: Trembling! II","paragraphs":["When things did not go according to plans, when the carefully calculated variables suddenly shifted in ways that challenged every assumption about control and consequence, one could only reassess the new parameters, adapt to changing circumstances, and overcome whatever obstacles had emerged through application of wisdom rather than force!","The entry of the Living Paradoxes had been unexpected, their grand display of power even more so.","These were not the desperate interventions of allies seeking mutual benefit!","This was the calculated arrival of forces.","But even against this unprecedented development, Noah felt his consciousness shifting through familiar patterns of analysis and adaptation that had served him through countless trials across his impossible journey.","He looked at Diviticus through a lens that had grown cold with recognition and calculation, seeing her not as she appeared in this moment of triumph but as she would exist in futures that stretched toward horizons only he could perceive!","She was someone he had deemed would definitely perish under his hands when circumstances permitted such resolution...she was already dead, she simply remained ignorant of this fundamental truth about her ultimate destiny!","But the question that burned through his consciousness with increasing intensity was how she had become so devastatingly powerful in such a relatively brief span of time.","She had consumed half a drop of his blood during their encounter in the Paradoxical Folds, that infinitesimal portion of his essence that had granted her immunity to producing Inevitabilities.","Yet if half a drop could produce such magnificent results, if such a tiny fragment of his being could transform someone into a force capable of challenging Dukes, then why was his own accumulated power not measured in trillions of Complexity and Purity Quotients rather than the hundreds of millions he currently possessed?","The inconsistency gnawed at his understanding.","Noah then recalled what the Paradoxes had recently accomplished through their audacious assault on the Coalition’s most protected facility...the theft of a Corpse of an Early Creature that had been jealously guarded for eons.","Was this the source of her newfound capabilities? Had the combination of his blood and access to the preserved remains of one of his kind created synergistic effects that transcended what either component could achieve individually?","\"...\"","Noah felt instinctive certainty crystallizing around this theory.","If he had obtained that corpse himself, if those preserved remains had been processed through the mystical mechanisms of his Early Veiled Shore rather than whatever crude methods the Paradoxes had employed...","The possibilities that stretched from such speculation were intoxicating in their scope and magnitude.","But someone else had claimed that prize.","\"Hmm...\"","Through their own power and audacity, certainly, but his blood had been a critical factor in making such theft possible.","Without his essence flowing through Diviticus, without the immunity and enhancement that half a drop had provided, the Paradoxes would never have been able to penetrate defenses that had held firm for eons.","A feeling began to settle in the depths of his consciousness...the sensation of losing prized loot that he had never actually possessed, watching someone else play with treasures that should have been his by right!","It was like witnessing a rival embrace a lover who should have been his own, hugging that precious loot to sleep and performing unspeakable acts of intimacy while he could only observe from positions of enforced isolation.","After all, in existence, nothing was worse than stolen loot!","Diviticus had made herself the center of attention at this moment of existential significance, positioning herself as the architect of victory.","Her display of power against the skeletal Primordial Death that had required multiple Dukes working in coordination to merely withstand was nothing short of domination!","She raised her hand with precision, fingers moving in patterns that seemed to rewrite the fundamental nature of space around her position. Tendrils of obsidian authority erupted from her transformed form, flowing outward like liquid darkness.","Yet these were not the crude manifestations of Paradoxical Authority that Noah had observed from other Living Paradoxes. The tendrils carried within them something older, more refined.","Noah’s enhanced perception detected the subtle musings of Glyphs woven throughout that authority!","The tendrils she released moved with predatory intelligence, seeking to wrap around the massive form of the Skeletal Primordial Death with the inexorable certainty of entropy given purpose.","The creature fought back with silent fury, its accumulated power creating zones where the fundamental forces of existence simply ceased to function, yet its countless manifestations of ending found themselves systematically cornered by authority that operated according to principles it could not counter!","Gradually, inexorably, the Primordial Death became bound by forces that transcended its cursed nature, its movements growing more restricted with each passing moment as Diviticus demonstrated mastery!","It was at this moment of tactical supremacy that Diviticus chose to address the assembled forces.","Her voice carried across the battlefield with crystalline clarity, each word chosen with the precision of someone who understood exactly what effects her speech would produce among her diverse audience.","\"Ladies and gentlemen,\" she began, \"we find ourselves witnessing something that has not occurred since the Earliest Folds...the emergence of Dead Existences in numbers and power sufficient to challenge all Living Existences. \"","WAA!","She gestured toward the bound Primordial Death.","\"What we have seen here today is not an isolated incident, not some random breach in the barriers that separate Life from Death. This is the beginning of something far more significant...a systematic invasion that will spread across every domain where consciousness dares to exist.\"","Her voice took on notes of grim certainty as she continued her analysis.","\"Dead Existences of this magnitude will appear in many other locations, and with far greater frequency than we have witnessed today. The barriers that THE Creature established to keep our domains separate are failing, and when they collapse entirely, only Living Paradoxes will possess the fundamental advantages necessary to face such enemies effectively.\"","During her monologue, the Symphony emanating from Moiraine’s position continued to resonate across the battlefield, its effects now extending to encompass the newly arrived Paradoxes. Above their heads appeared the same golden markers that blessed other Living Existences...two crossed swords that blazed with authority beyond normal limitation.","The newly arrived Living Paradoxes and Dukes responded to this enhancement by unleashing terrifying seas of Paradoxical Authority upon the remaining Honored Dead Existences, their coordinated assault clearing the cursed creatures like cattle being systematically processed through mechanisms designed for efficient elimination.","\"Just as in the Earliest Folds,\" Diviticus continued, her voice rising with the passion of someone delivering truth that others preferred to ignore, \"the true enemies of Living Existences are not each other, but the forces of ending that seek to consume everything we have built through eons of careful cultivation and advancement.\"","She paused, allowing this fundamental realization to settle among her audience before delivering her ultimate objective.","\"It is time for Living Paradoxes to reclaim our rightful seat at the table. We offer our capabilities gladly in the fight against Dead Existences, seeking partnership in facing threats that transcend every previous category of danger.\"","HUUM!","As Diviticus finished her carefully crafted monologue, she also completed the process of binding the skeletal Primordial Death entirely, her authority wrapping around the creature until it could no longer move or resist the forces that held it in perfect stasis.","The demonstration was complete...she had single-handedly accomplished what multiple Dukes working in coordination had struggled to achieve, while simultaneously positioning herself as the voice of reasonable cooperation in facing existential threats!"]},{"number":3997,"title":"Chapter 3997: Chapter 3996: Trembling! III","paragraphs":["Many Dukes throughout the assembled forces looked toward the cluster of Paradoxes with gazes that carried undisguised animosity.","For many of them, the relationship with Living Paradoxes had been defined by warfare that stretched across eons...conflicts in which Diviticus and other Dukes present had killed uncountable numbers of their allies.","The idea of accepting such beings as partners rather than enemies required adjustments to thinking that had been refined through countless cycles of violence and retribution.","In this moment of heavy contemplation, Moiraine began to float back toward Noah’s position.","Yet Noah’s mental voice reached her consciousness with firm instructions that halted her advance before it could draw unwanted attention.","’Do not,’ he conveyed, ’Remain where you are and continue appearing as the source of enhancement that benefits all present.’","...!","His expression grew heavy as he observed this unfolding situation with the seriousness it demanded.","Right now, he seemed to be nothing more than an Extra with very little apparent power while Diviticus commanded center stage.","But this was okay!","Noah released a sigh that carried the weight of choices, acknowledging that he had chosen this path when he made the Festival of War resonate from Moiraine’s position rather than his own.","Not being in the spotlight every now and then was okay.","At this moment of personal reflection, Noah found himself sympathetically understanding how all those discarded extras in his own fable must have felt when their contributions were overlooked in favor of more prominent characters.","The sensation of being reduced to irrelevance despite possessing capabilities that exceeded those who commanded attention was humbling!","It was in this moment of heavy contemplation that existence itself convulsed!","A blaring purple brilliance blazed from above as reality tore itself open to accommodate the passage of someone whose presence was heavy.","From the temporal rift emerged the visage of an extremely gorgeous woman. Her stellar purple hair flowed like liquid starlight given form and direction, while her dress seemed to contain within its fabric the compressed essence of temporal authority refined to its purest expression.","She smoked a pipe whose contents blazed with inner radiance, yet her attention focused immediately upon the figure of Duke Schrodinger with the kind of recognition that suggested their relationship stretched across eons of history.","\"I thought I smelled a dirty beggar in my Transcendent Temporal Folds,\" she said. \"How many millions of years has it been now, Schrodinger? Since when did you let children begin speaking for you?\"","As she delivered this casual insult, she barely glanced toward Diviticus, yet that momentary attention carried within it the weight of assessment and dismissal that made the assembled Paradox Duke’s expression grow cold.","This...was Aion, the Temporal Watcher...a being whose authority over time itself had been legendary since epochs that predated current existence!","Toward her provocative words, the beggar-looking Schrodinger smiled with patient amusement that suggested he had been expecting exactly this development.","\"Sometimes,\" he replied, \"one has to sit back and let the younger generation lead. Age brings wisdom about when to act and when to observe.\"","...!","Aion smoked her pipe with movements that seemed to slow time around her position, each inhalation drawing in possibilities while each exhalation released certainties into the surrounding space.","She nodded as if considering his response, then...","WAP!","She vanished from her position above the battlefield, reality bending around her passage until she materialized directly beside Moiraine!","\"You have gotten rusty, old friend,\" she said to Schrodinger with voice that carried across impossible distances without losing any of its clarity. \"I can see your gaze and the hungry attention of this loud Diviticus looking toward this Moiraine here with calculations...\"","She gestured toward the Living Paradox whose position had become the center during this battle!","\"She appears to have come before you other Paradoxes to lend aid against Dead Existences. If anyone should have a seat at the table of governance, should it not be her? Young, perhaps a bit weaker than established powers, certainly easier to manipulate into serving larger agendas...\"","Schrodinger’s smile deepened at her provocative analysis.","\"You are letting your true thoughts be heard out loud again, Aion,\" he observed with gentle reproach.","Aion nodded with calm acknowledgment of his criticism.","\"Of course. I believe in being straightforward about intentions and motivations rather than hiding behind pretense and manufactured courtesy. And what I want most in this situation is the precise opposite of whatever you are seeking to achieve, you manipulative fucking beggar.\"","BOOM!","The exchange between these terrifying beings carried undertones that spoke to conflicts and competitions that stretched across eons of shared history!","Their true auras flared outward at this moment as... everything began to tremble.","They were called Dukes by those who required classifications and hierarchies to understand the scope of power they witnessed.","But truly, their accumulated authority exceeded any normal Duke by margins that rendered comparison meaningless. They were Existences at a stage of power that very few beings across the breadth of reality could claim to understand.","Some even speculated that they had reached heights of capability comparable to those achieved by beings who had walked the Earliest Folds when power flowed according to principles that current reality had forgotten.","Others whispered that they might be comparable in authority to young Early Creatures themselves!","But the signature manifestation that truly defined their transcendent nature was their capability for Existential Trembling...the ability to make all surrounding weavings of existence shake through their presence alone, their aura affecting the atmosphere and environment of the very fabric of Existence itself!","Standing before such beings, one would feel their very existence trembling!","As two terrifying existences looked at each other, the bodies of everyone and everything nearby vibrated in response!","Existential! Trembling!","Only a single being had felt his hands begin to shake before his eyes turned utterly livid and filled with tyranny as he told his own body...Don’t you fucking dare!","And right after, his glorious standing and distinction as an Early Creature flared as for him and him alone in this region... he did not tremble.","He would not tremble!"]},{"number":3998,"title":"Chapter 3998: Chapter 3997: An Instant! I","paragraphs":["The air itself seemed to hold its breath as existence trembled at the mere confrontation of two ancient powers!","The fabric of reality rippled outward from where Aion and Schrodinger locked gazes, their accumulated authority creating waves of pressure that made the very foundations of the Transcendent Temporal Folds uncertain about their own nature.","Lesser beings found themselves frozen in place, their bodies betraying them as Existential Trembling coursed through every fiber of their being!","Noah observed this display of overwhelming might with eyes that remained steady behind his obsidian helm.","The trembling that seized others, that fundamental recognition of powers beyond comprehension, simply... did not touch him.","His form stood perfectly still within Yoshinami’s armor, not through effort or resistance, but through the simple truth of what he was.","He was an Early Creature.","The thought burned through his consciousness with tyrannical certainty. How dare entities lesser than himself attempt to make him experience fear through mere displays of accumulated authority?!","They commanded respect, certainly. Their power could reshape existence itself, undoubtedly. But trembling? That was the province of those who stood beneath, not one whose very nature predated the concepts they wielded.","His gaze swept across the battlefield with cold assessment, taking in the positions of every player in this grand game.","Some of his goals had been achieved...the Festival of War had shifted the battle’s momentum, resources had been gathered, connections forged. Others remained tantalizingly out of reach. But the arrival of these heavy hitters, these beings whose authority transcended normal categorization, had transformed an already complex situation into something far more interesting.","Aion stood wreathed in temporal authority that seemed to slow time itself around her presence, each draw from her pipe pulling in possibilities while exhaling certainties!","She represented power that exceeded normal Dukes by margins that made comparison meaningless. And Schrodinger...that deceptively mundane figure whose presence generated warning signals in Noah’s mind...remained apathetically calm.","Noah’s lips curved slightly behind his concealing helm. He was not at the center of attention. And that was okay as since now, he had deemed it that way!","When circumstances served his purposes, he would do whatever proved necessary to obtain what he desired.","Consequences could be calculated, reactions predicted, outcomes orchestrated through understanding rather than force.","And right now, he wanted a certain terrifying treasure to be triggered.","In that moment of absolute stillness, where existence itself seemed frozen between heartbeats as two transcendent beings measured each other across impossible distances, Noah began to move.","His form lifted from its position with fluid grace, the obsidian armor flowing around him like liquid darkness as he started floating across the twisted space of the battlefield.","....!","Amidst an Existential Trembling where others were frozen, he moved!","His destination was unmistakable...the massive form of the Primordial Death that Diviticus had bound in her tendrils of paradoxical authority, its skeletal frame held in perfect stasis despite the tremendous power contained within.","The shock of his actions rippled through every consciousness present like stones thrown into still water.","Eyes that had been locked on the confrontation between Aion and Schrodinger suddenly swiveled toward this impossible sight.","Here, in the midst of Existential Trembling that should have rendered all movement theoretical rather than actual, a single figure glided through space as if the overwhelming pressure simply... didn’t exist!","The obsidian armor caught and reflected the chaotic energies of the battlefield, creating patterns of darkness that seemed to absorb light rather than merely block it. Yet it was not the armor that commanded attention...it was the complete absence of struggle in his movements.","His body showed no indication of effort, no tremor of resistance against forces that made reality itself uncertain.","He moved as naturally as one might walk through an empty room, unaffected by pressures that had frozen beings of tremendous power in place.","Schrodinger’s ancient eyes shifted toward Noah’s advancing form, the calm assessment in his gaze suddenly flashing with brilliant illumination!","The beggar-like Duke’s expression remained unchanged, yet there was something in that brief flash of light that suggested pieces falling into place on a board whose scope only he could fully perceive.","Aion drew deeply from her pipe, the smoke swirling around her in patterns that seemed to write equations in the air before dissolving into nothingness.","Her eyes, those windows to temporal authority refined beyond normal comprehension, flickered with genuine interest as they tracked Noah’s movement.","The Temporal Watcher’s attention carried weight that made causality bend around its focus.","The distance between Noah’s starting position and the bound Primordial Death seemed to stretch and compress simultaneously, space itself uncertain about how to accommodate his passage!","Yet he continued forward with unwavering purpose, each moment bringing him closer to the massive creature whose very existence challenged the supremacy of life over death.","When he finally arrived within immediate proximity of the bound horror, close enough that the deathly authority radiating from its form should have begun the process of systematic dissolution, Noah turned his concealed gaze toward Diviticus calmly!","\"I had laid claim to this little skeleton before you arrived and so rudely interrupted.\" His voice carried across the battlefield with crystalline clarity, each word cutting through the oppressive atmosphere as if the existential trembling was merely background noise. \"So... release it.\"","HUUM!","The words hung in the space between them.","They were not phrased as a request or suggestion. They emerged as command, delivered with the casual authority of one who expected immediate compliance regardless of the vast differential in apparent power!","Noah’s mind raced through calculations as the words left his lips. He had chosen them with deliberate precision, understanding exactly how Diviticus would process such audacious demand.","She was currently intoxicated with her newfound might, drunk on capabilities that had elevated her beyond every previous limitation. Her entire approach to this situation had been crafted to establish Living Paradoxes as essential partners, to entrench their position within the broader weavings of existence.","He knew with absolute certainty that even if he deliberately sought to enrage her, she would not make direct moves against him here, not with all these Living Existences here.","As an unknown existence who displayed no obvious waves of dangerous power, yet who could walk unaffected through the Existential Trembling of beings whose might transcended normal Dukes, he represented a puzzle. And when faced with such an enigma, when confronted by someone bold enough to issue commands despite showing no apparent capability to enforce them, there was only one action she would take...","BOOM!","The obsidian tendrils that had held the Primordial Death in perfect stasis suddenly loosened, their grip releasing with the sound of existential law being deliberately violated!","The massive skeletal creature, freed from its bonds, roared with renewed fervor that made the temporal rivers themselves flow backward in recognition of wrongness given voice!"]},{"number":3999,"title":"Chapter 3999: Chapter 3998: An Instant! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s smile deepened behind his helm!","He didn’t even turn to look at the Primordial Death as it stretched its massive limbs, testing its recovered freedom with movements that created tears in the surrounding space. His gaze remained locked on Diviticus, recognition burning between them of exactly what had just occurred.","Yes, the only action she would have taken...the only response that satisfied both her curiosity and her position...was precisely what she had done. She had tested him by releasing a creature that even Dukes struggled to contain.","If he proved to be somebody of significance, he might defend himself and reveal his true nature. If he was nobody, he would simply die, and when questioned about such a result, she could merely shrug and point out that he had specifically requested the creature’s release.","The scene that followed was one of tyrannical confidence and glorious indifference!","Noah stood perfectly still as the Primordial Death, driven by its fundamental nature to eliminate everything that dared exist in its presence, immediately focused its attention on the being closest to its position. A massive skeletal hand, each finger larger than ancient towers, descended toward him with the inexorable certainty of entropy given malicious intent.","And intent...oh, gloriously, intent and action was all he needed!","The descending appendage crushed through space itself, its approach creating zones where the very concept of existence became negotiable. Yet Noah made no moves to defend or attack. His form remained motionless, as if the approaching annihilation was of no more concern than a gentle breeze.","When the massive hand was mere inches from his armored form, close enough that the deathly authority should have begun unmaking him at the most fundamental level...","HUUM!","A flash of crimson obsidian light erupted from Noah’s position with such intensity that every consciousness present felt it like a physical impact!","From within that terrible radiance came a sensation that transcended fear...it was the primal recognition of predator so far beyond their comprehension that resistance became meaningless concept.","For an instant so brief that most Living Existences failed to register it consciously, a massive illusion of a spider flashed across the entirety of the Transcendent Temporal Folds!","The spider’s form defied scale, its presence seeming to exist in dimensions that normal perception could not fully process. Eight eyes blazed with crimson malevolence, each one containing depths of ancient intelligence that regarded the Primordial Death with absolute apathy.","Those terrible eyes flashed with brilliant authority, and in that moment of acknowledgment, fate was sealed.","Diviticus and many of the assembled Dukes showed immediate alarm, their enhanced perceptions recognizing threat that they couldn’t truly counter!","They moved backward with instinctive urgency, their bodies responding to danger before conscious thought could process what they had witnessed.","Only Schrodinger and Aion remained unmoved, though their expressions grew slightly more serious as they recognized...something.","Something!","The moment after the crimson light completed its manifestation, everything seemingly returned to normal. The overwhelming presence vanished as suddenly as it had appeared, leaving only the lingering sensation that something monumental had occurred beyond their ability to fully comprehend.","But the massive body of the Primordial Death... had disappeared entirely.","No trace remained...no scattered bones, no wisps of deathly authority, no evidence that such a creature had ever existed in this space!","Where it had been, only empty air remained.","The veiled armored figure of Noah stood exactly as he had before, his posture unchanged, as if he hadn’t moved a fraction since the creature’s attack began.","Yet subtle crimson obsidian brilliance now radiated from his form, speaking to power recently exercised but carefully contained.","His gaze remained fixed on Diviticus, coldness and tyranny burning in the depths of his concealed eyes!","\"Be careful,\" he said, his voice carrying the weight of prophecy delivered with absolute certainty. \"Who knows... one day that might just be you.\"","The threat was delivered with such casual precision that it struck like existential law being established!","The implication was clear...whatever had just eliminated a Primordial Death with such absolute authority could just as easily be turned upon her!","Without waiting for response or reaction, Noah began floating back toward his previous position.","As he moved through space that still trembled from the confrontation of ancient powers, his voice rang out with commanding clarity.","\"Come.\"","The single word was directed at Moiraine, who had been observing everything with her characteristic serene intensity!","He had told her to wait before when strategic positioning demanded it. Now he commanded her presence as circumstances had shifted to accommodate their departure.","Moiraine floated away from Aion’s position with grace, her movement creating ripples in the temporal authority that surrounded the ancient being. She came to stand beside Noah with the natural precision of one whose loyalty transcended every other consideration.","Noah’s gaze swept across the assembled powers one final time. He looked toward Diviticus calmly. His attention shifted to Aion with acknowledgment. Finally, his eyes settled on Schrodinger with the particular weight of one mystery recognizing another.","\"Till next time,\" he said.","His attention turned to Duke Gwendolyn, and when he spoke again, his voice carried deliberate weight. \"Thanks for the invite to this event. If there are to be any seats at any tables, you know how to reach me.\"","...!","The implications hung in the air like existential contracts waiting to be signed.","He...was establishing himself as a player in games that shaped existence itself, one whose participation came with costs and benefits!","He didn’t remain to observe the reactions to his declarations. Sharp light erupted around both him and Moiraine, reality bending to accommodate their departure through methods that bypassed many Living Existences.","The two figures simply ceased to exist in that location, leaving behind only the weight of tyranny and glory.","As the light of transportation wrapped around him, Noah’s consciousness blazed with the fervor of prompts materializing within his mind!","|Yoshinami has successfully executed the Crown of Inevitable Retribution against a target whose power was deemed to be equivalent to or exceeded the distinction of an average Duke. True Death has been delivered to the Primordial Death, Kar’theta the Hungerer, through methods that bypass every form of resistance, protection, or existential anchoring.|","|The eliminated entity possessed authority equivalent to 1.7 times that of standard Duke-level capabilities, with additional enhancements from the Curse of the Infinite Paradox of Unmaking. Complete annihilation achieved across all dimensions, timelines, and possibilities. No resurrection, restoration, or reconstitution possible through any known or unknown methods.|","|Yoshinami has directly transported the True Death-eliminated corpse of Primordial Death Kar’theta to the Early Veiled Shore for comprehensive analysis. The corpse retains 94% of its original existential mass despite True Death elimination, a unique preservation effect of Yoshinami’s particular methodology.|","|Estimated processing timeline: Initial breakdown - 1 hour. Complete resource extraction - 24 hours.|","|Additional Note: Yoshinami expresses satisfaction with the quality of the eliminated target and requests permission to retain 50% of the processed materials for her own recovery and grown. Such enhancement would potentially allow for two uses of Crown of Inevitable Retribution per 24-hour period rather than the current single application.]","...!","The cascade of information painted a picture of triumph that exceeded his most optimistic projections!"]},{"number":4000,"title":"Chapter 4000: Chapter 3999: Be The Scariest Monster! I","paragraphs":["The sharp light of transportation dissolved around them like morning mist, revealing the familiar golden expanse of the Early Veiled Shore.","Noah’s feet touched the warm sands with the satisfaction of one returning home after a journey through existential chaos, but what greeted his eyes made even his enhanced perception pause in appreciation.","The massive corpse of the Primordial Death lay compressed upon the golden shore like a monument to impossible victory!","Its skeletal form, which had towered over armies of Living Existences mere moments ago, now rested in defeated stillness.","The bones themselves seemed to pulse with residual deathly authority, creating distortions in the air above them where existence itself remained uncertain about accommodating such concentrated ending.","But it was not alone in its repose. Scattered across the pristine sands lay thousands of bone fragments, pieces of otherworldly flesh, and crystallized segments of what had once been Dead Existences.","They gleamed under the Shore’s light like macabre treasures, each piece radiating the particular wrongness that marked beings who had existed in states of perpetual termination.","These were the fruits of his Festival of War, the one percent that had been automatically claimed from every elimination enhanced by his orchestrated blessing!","Moiraine stood beside him, her eyes sweeping across the grotesque bounty with an expression that shifted from amazement to concern. The golden light caught the worry lines forming around her eyes as she turned to face him.","\"Sir,\" she began, the honorific carrying its usual warmth despite the seriousness in her tone, \"was it... truly okay to reveal yourself in such a manner? Entities like Schrodinger...\" She paused, seeming to search for words adequate to convey the magnitude of what concerned her. \"They are extremely terrifying. Beyond what most can comprehend.\"","HUUM!","Noah’s lips curved into a smile as he began walking toward the massive corpse, his bare feet leaving glowing impressions in the sand.","Each step felt like a declaration of intent, a refusal to be cowed by the scope of powers that existed beyond his current reach.","\"I stopped living in fear many, many months ago,\" he said. \"Fear is a luxury I can no longer afford, not when every moment of hesitation could mean countless possible futures lost.\" He paused beside a particularly large fragment of Dead Existence bone, nudging it thoughtfully with his foot. \"But I am curious about this Schrodinger. What makes him so particularly terrifying among beings who can already reshape existence with their thoughts?\"","Moiraine’s expression grew serious, her gaze drifting toward the vibrant waters that lapped at the Shore’s edge.","In the distance, she could see Ruination seated in deep meditation, her form wreathed in crimson-gold radiance as she processed the gifts Noah had bestowed.","The Infiniverse floated nearby, multicolored jewels across her skin pulsing in harmonious patterns.","The Sacred Totems rose like monuments to achievement, their crystalline surfaces catching and reflecting light in ways that created new colors with each observation.","She took in all of this...this sanctuary of power and potential, before beginning to speak, her voice taking on the cadence of someone sharing secrets that few were privileged to know.","\"Schrodinger,\" she began, \"is not merely powerful in the way other Dukes are powerful. His connection to Living Paradoxes runs so deep that some theorize he predates the current understanding of what Paradox even means. There are whispers...never confirmed, always denied when asked directly, that he used to live as an attendant of an Early Creature inside an Early Veiled Shore.\" She paused, letting the weight of that possibility settle. \"Not visit, not observe, but actually lived within the Shore of an Early Creature.\"","...!","The wind picked up slightly, carrying with it the scent of the sacred herbs growing in their plots, and Moiraine continued, her voice growing more animated as she warmed to her subject.","\"His habits make no sense to anyone who tries to understand him through normal logic. He frequently takes on the visage of a beggar...not as disguise or infiltration, but seemingly because he genuinely enjoys it. He’ll go to mortal worlds, worlds so insignificant they don’t even register on most maps of existence, and simply... live there. Sometimes for years, sometimes for centuries, just existing as a homeless wanderer beside muddy roads.\"","She shook her head, hair catching the light as it moved. \"Most think he’s insane, or playing games beyond their comprehension. He rarely makes moves...eons can pass without him taking any action that others can perceive. But when he does act...\" Her voice dropped to barely above a whisper. \"Every time Schrodinger has made a deliberate move, it has resulted in profound changes across existence itself. Entire Folds have been restructured. The balance of power between Living Existences has shifted. Things that were thought impossible suddenly become inevitable.\"","...!","Noah absorbed this information with the careful attention it deserved, nodding slowly as pieces of a vast puzzle began arranging themselves in his mind.","\"In existence,\" he said after a moment of contemplation, \"there can indeed be some scary monsters. Beings whose power and understanding transcend every category we use to measure capability.\" His eyes blazed with inner fire as he continued. \"All that I have to do... is become scarier than them. And slowly, gradually, I’m gathering the resources to accomplish exactly that.\"","...!","Yes!","There were many monsters out there. He simply...had to be the bigger monster!","He turned toward the massive corpse of the Primordial Death, reaching out to tap its crystallized bone with casual familiarity.","\"Yoshinami,\" he called out, his voice carrying the authority of one addressing a bound companion, \"you can have your half.\"","...!","The response was immediate and dramatic. The air beside him shimmered with crimson-black radiance before Yoshinami materialized in her human form.","Her pale features were transformed by an expression of genuine joy, her crimson eyes blazing with happiness that made her usual cold demeanor seem like a distant memory.","With grace that spoke to eons of practiced ceremony, she dropped to one knee and took his hand, pressing her lips to it in a gesture of gratitude.","\"Master’s generosity exceeds all expectation,\" she murmured against his skin, her voice carrying vibrations that seemed to resonate with the spider-essence of her true nature.","Then, without warning, her form exploded outward. The transformation was both beautiful and terrifying to witness. Her human shape dissolved into expanding darkness that reformed as the massive spider, her true form standing taller than the Sacred Totems themselves.","Eight legs, each one thick as ancient trees, positioned themselves around the Primordial Death’s corpse with surgical precision.","One of her forelegs, sharp enough to cut through dimensions themselves, descended with deliberate care. The limb sliced through the massive corpse with a sound like reality tearing, dividing it perfectly in half!","No resistance met her blade-like appendage...even in death, the Primordial seemed to recognize a predator of superior nature.","Webs began flowing from her spinnerets, wrapping her portion of the corpse in silk that gleamed with otherworldly properties.","Each strand contained within it preservation techniques that would maintain the corpse’s potency while she processed its essence. With movements that made the ground tremble, she lifted her wrapped prize and began moving toward the distant trees where she could consume it in privacy.","A prompt materialized in Noah’s consciousness as she departed!","|Yoshinami has begun devouring half of the Primordial Death’s corpse. The profound nutrients contained within this Duke-level Dead Existence will elevate her capabilities significantly. Upon completion of consumption and digestion, the Crown of Inevitable Retribution will be available for use twice within any 24-hour period rather than the current single application.]","Noah watched her massive form disappear among the trees, each step making the Shore tremble slightly, before releasing a long breath.","The casual brutality of her efficiency, the eager joy in her service...it was simultaneously comforting and unsettling to witness.","\"Quantify all remaining corpses to equivalent nutrients,\" he commanded the Shore itself, his voice carrying the weight of authority that expected immediate compliance.","The response came as cascading prompts that made his eyes widen with each successive revelation.","|Analysis complete. All scattered pieces of Dead Existences obtained through the Festival of War boon have been evaluated. Total nutritional value equivalent to: 1,250 corpses of Eminent Early Living Marine Lifeforms. This represents concentrated essence of ending that, when properly processed, can be converted to nutrients through the Shore’s unique digestive capabilities.|","|Additional analysis: Half of the Primordial Death’s corpse (portion retained for Shore processing) has been re-evaluated. Nutritional value equivalent to: 1 complete Kleos Early Living Marine Lifeform. This represents the highest grade of nutrients ever introduced to your Early Veiled Shore.|","...!"]}]);
